ls to increase competition and reform taxes have the potential to transform the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/opinion/mexicos-ambitious-economic-agenda.html', 'snippet': 'Proposals to increase competition and reform taxes have the potential to transform the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mexico’s new president, Enrique Peña Nieto, has  proposed  reforms that could make monopolistic industries like telecommunications more competitive, bolster oil production and improve the government’s finances. The proposals are commendable and could transform Mexico’s economy. But success is far from guaranteed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico’s Ambitious Economic Agenda', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico’s Ambitious Economic Agenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena Nieto, Enrique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T00:42:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/94c10575-d178-5cf7-8cc9-df0aadac342c', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94c10575-d178-5cf7-8cc9-df0aadac342c'}, {'abstract': 'After watching their teammate Kevin Ware break his right leg in the first half, the top-seeded Cardinals regrouped