name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T01:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da72d99c-4ef3-56dc-9bfb-ee398bde43ba', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da72d99c-4ef3-56dc-9bfb-ee398bde43ba'}, {'abstract': 'The 21-year-old had been a member of the class of 2013 but was on leave and visiting friends, a university spokesman said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/nyregion/woman-21-is-found-dead-in-columbia-dorm.html', 'snippet': 'The 21-year-old had been a member of the class of 2013 but was on leave and visiting friends, a university spokesman said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A young woman was found dead, possibly from a drug overdose, in a Columbia University dormitory room on Sunday morning, the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Found Dead in Columbia Dorm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woman Found Dead in Columbia Dorm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T01:10:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf6e72c-8faf-539a-a100-0e60811a72ff', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf6e72c-8faf-539a-a100-0e60811a72ff'}, {'abstract': 'Winning numbers for March 31, 2013, for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Winning numbers for March 31, 2013, for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'March 31, 2013', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T01:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/04e61845-3e27-507d-ae0b-99fe92e9af39', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04e61845-3e27-507d-ae0b-99fe92e9af39'}, {'abstract': 'There are major benefits and big risks in what some Republican-led states want to do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/opinion/using-medicaid-dollars-for-private-insurance.html', 'snippet': 'There are major benefits and big risks in what some Republican-led states want to do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration and Republican officials in several states are exploring ways to redirect federal money intended to expand Medicaid, the main public insurance program for the poor, and use it instead to buy private health insurance for Medicaid recipients. The approach could have important benefits for beneficiaries and for the future of health care reform. But the idea also carries big risks. Federal officials will need to enforce strict conditions before agreeing to any redirection of Medicaid dollars that were originally intended to enlarge the Medicaid rolls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Medicaid Dollars for Private Insurance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Using Medicaid Dollars for Private Insurance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T01:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac9c05a0-6a70-5290-a5e5-643cdc4b5ffc', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac9c05a0-6a70-5290-a5e5-643cdc4b5ffc'}, {'abstract': 'A breakthrough agreement on guest workers raises hopes for a broader deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/opinion/the-immigration-spring.html', 'snippet': 'A breakthrough agreement on guest workers raises hopes for a broader deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been amazing this year to watch immigration reform, that perennial train wreck of an issue, keep rolling forward without losing steam or blowing up. A bipartisan band of senators called the Gang of Eight has been working steadily for months on a bill; a similar group in the House is doing the same; diverse outside forces are lining up to urge all of them on, and every week seems to bring new reason for optimism. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Immigration Spring', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Immigration Spring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T01:14:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ecd1631-970a-5ca2-a6da-416bb10531a5', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ecd1631-970a-5ca2-a6da-416bb10531a5'}, {'abstract': 'The gun bills that the Senate is about to consider offer a new example of the skill with which its leader, Harry Reid of Nevada, evolves on issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/us/politics/harry-reid-draws-on-political-calculus-as-he-leads-senate.html', 'snippet': 'The gun bills that the Senate is about to consider offer a new example of the skill with which its leader, Harry Reid of Nevada, evolves on issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It was, Senator Harry Reid of Nevada ebulliently proclaimed, a “happy day for me” as he stood with Wayne LaPierre, the head of the National Rifle Association, in 2010 at a new shooting range in Las Vegas made possible by federal money secured by Mr. Reid. “People who criticize this probably would criticize baseball,” Mr. Reid said before firing off a few rounds.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/us/REID/REID-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/01/us/REID/REID-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/us/REID/REID-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/us/REID/REID-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1433, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/us/REID/REID-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/01/us/REID/REID-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/us/REID/REID-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Views Shift on Guns, Reid Corrals Senate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Views Shift On Guns, Reid Corrals Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject'