 nations in the world, but that reputation has taken a beating. The government’s latest move has only added to the criticism.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/canadas-latest-climate-change/', 'snippet': 'Canada was long seen as among the most environmentally consciousness nations in the world, but that reputation has taken a beating. The government’s latest move has only added to the criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just days after World Water Day, the Canadian government quietly acknowledged last week that it had dropped out of the United Nations anti-drought convention. The move reportedly makes Canada the only nation in the world not party to United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification, or Unccd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/01rdv-canada-drought/01rdv-canada-drought-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/01rdv-canada-drought/01rdv-canada-drought-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/01rdv-canada-drought/01rdv-canada-drought-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/01rdv-canada-drought/01rdv-canada-drought-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/01rdv-canada-drought/01rdv-canada-drought-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/01rdv-canada-drought/01rdv-canada-drought-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/01rdv-canada-drought/01rdv-canada-drought-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s Latest Climate Change', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harper, Stephen J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b75bdcff-b647-5498-a8c5-3fad8f71889d', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b75bdcff-b647-5498-a8c5-3fad8f71889d'}, {'abstract': 'With Stephen, there were lung collapses and hospital visits that stacked up like rush-hour cars. But strangely, I slept well then.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/the-ways-ive-worried/', 'snippet': 'With Stephen, there were lung collapses and hospital visits that stacked up like rush-hour cars. But strangely, I slept well then.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, I found myself lying in bed, trying to sleep, a common occurrence. I had forgotten to call my mom back earlier, and I now pictured her standing in her kitchen. Then the next secon