hattan, in a 161-page decision, has given the multinational banks being investigated for manipulating the London interbank offered rate, or Libor, a dose of good news for once. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Libor Ruling, a Big Win for the Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buchwald, Naomi Reice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charles Schwab Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS AG', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T11:44:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2376637c-054b-507c-a1fb-8094f7d3afad', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2376637c-054b-507c-a1fb-8094f7d3afad'}, {'abstract': 'A strategic neighborhood of Aleppo falls to the rebels after Kurdish fighters join them against the Assad regime. Where next?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/could-syrias-kurds-change-the-course-of-the-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'A strategic neighborhood of Aleppo falls to the rebels after Kurdish fighters join them against the Assad regime. Where next?', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALEPPO, Syria — On Saturday I trudged across the grassy ravine that separates Sheikh Maksoud, a majority-Kurdish neighborhood on a hilltop, from the rebel-held portions of the city. Beside me were rebel fighters carrying weapons and ammunition. Civilians were coming the opposite way, whole families laden with the few possessions they could carry on their backs. Everyone was jogging across the open ground, fearful of snipers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kurdish Factor', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Kurdistan Workers' Party", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T11:50:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthieu Aikins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthieu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aikins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cbf0631-55ed-56fe-8c51-605176736909', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cbf0631-55ed-56fe-8c51-605176736909'}, {'abstract': 'Some mail programs and third-party services offer notification when someone opens a message 