ck-to-school shopping season earlier each year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Madison Avenue Springs April Fool’s Pranks Early', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "APRIL FOOL'S DAY", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Eagle Outfitters Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mother', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Procter & Gamble Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T12:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/387e920f-05d9-579c-86ec-b4ee93a8867a', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/387e920f-05d9-579c-86ec-b4ee93a8867a'}, {'abstract': 'It will feature two events with a local hook: tributes to the landmark book “Blues People” and to the nightclub owner Lorraine Gordon.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/james-moody-jazz-festival-announces-its-lineup/', 'snippet': 'It will feature two events with a local hook: tributes to the landmark book “Blues People” and to the nightclub owner Lorraine Gordon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Jersey Performing Arts Center, in Newark, has announced a lineup for the second annual TD James Moody Democracy of Jazz Festival, in November. Presented in partnership with WBGO 88.3 FM, it will feature two marquee events with a local hook: a 50th-anniversary words-and-music tribute to “Blues People,” the landmark book by the lifelong Newark resident Amiri Baraka (Nov. 5); and a concert tribute to the nightclub proprietor Lorraine Gordon, who spent her childhood there (Nov. 7).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'James Moody Jazz Festival Announces Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Rivera, Paquito", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Lorraine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McBride, Christian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moody, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Performing Arts Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T12:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5c7a217-ea89-51d8-9c68-2821f046fb0c', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5c7a217-ea89-51d8-9c68-2821f046fb0c'}, {'abstract': 'There is one job on Wall Street for which pay has continued to rise since the financial crisis: board member. | Michael S. Steinberg is the most senior SAC Capital Advisors employee to be ensnared in the government’s insider trading investigation. | A Dell proxy statement sheds light on the process of fielding interest from bidders. | Efforts to replace corporate directors rarely succeed.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/on-wall-street-its-good-to-be-a-director/', 'snippet': 'There is one job on Wall Street for which pay has continued to rise since the financial crisis: board member. | Michael S. Steinberg is the most senior SAC Capital Advisors employee to be ensnared in the government’s insider trading investigation....', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is one job on Wall Street for which pay has continued to rise since the financial crisis: board member. Compensation for directors at the nation’s biggest banks has ticked up even as the banks themselves have reined in salaries and bonuses, DealBook’s Susanne Craig reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Wall Street, It’s Good to Be a Director', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T12:03:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afaf8475-6929-5690-9fce-a8623506ed75', 'word_count': 1733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afaf8475-6929-5690-9fce-a8623506ed75'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/opinion-report-the-immigration-debate/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: The Immigration Debate', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T12:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40df4815-a5a6-5d70-af16-20f97dca87a7', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40df4815-a5a6-5d70-af16-20f97dca87a7'}, {'abstract': 'Some would argue that the earliest recorded adjudication regarding copyright was in sixth-century Ireland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/opinion/global/to-every-book-its-copy.html', 'snippet': 'Some would argue that the earliest recorded adjudication regarding copyright was in sixth-century Ireland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regarding “Court strikes blow against publishers” (March 28): Eduardo Porto states that the first copyright laws were enacted in England in the 18th century. Some would argue that the earliest recorded adjudication regarding copyright was in sixth-century Ireland, when St. Columba copied a book of psalms while studying under St. Finnian. The latter took him to court and King Diarmait offered this adjudication: “To every cow its calf; to every book its copy.” The copy was returned to Finnian and is now housed at the Royal Irish Academy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Every Book its Copy', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T12:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d538c43-3b28-5ea5-91b8-ea99f6d2fbc4', 'word_count': 91