y-selling-direct/', 'snippet': 'A wave of e-commerce companies are trying to build premium brands at discount prices by cutting out middlemen and going straight to manufacturers, Claire Cain Miller and Stephanie Clifford report Monday in The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A wave of e-commerce companies are trying to build premium brands at discount prices by cutting out middlemen and going straight to manufacturers, Claire Cain Miller and Stephanie Clifford report Monday in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Start-Ups Aim to Build Brands by Selling Direct', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T14:59:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/008ae0af-e519-569e-ab64-287c90b6d1dd', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/008ae0af-e519-569e-ab64-287c90b6d1dd'}, {'abstract': 'For YogaFit, the next step is search engine optimization. “It’s not a guaranteed science,” the owner acknowledged.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/releasing-new-web-sites-and-trying-to-manage-s-e-o/', 'snippet': 'For YogaFit, the next step is search engine optimization. “It’s not a guaranteed science,” the owner acknowledged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last few months She Owns It business group members Beth Shaw, who owns YogaFit, and Alexandra Mayzler, who owns Thinking Caps Group, have overseen the redesign of their company Web sites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Releasing New Web Sites and Trying to Manage S.E.O.', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YogaFit Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T15:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4b886a7-15ea-57c9-8edc-0474e55f9691', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4b886a7-15ea-57c9-8edc-0474e55f9691'}, {'abstract': 'Jasper Conran reinvents the family business.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/not-his-fathers-conran-shop/', 'snippet': 'Jasper Conran reinvents the family business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since taking over his father’s venerable stores last year, the designer Jasper Conran has been quietly revolutionizing the brand. At the flagship Chelsea location in London, shelves brim with Marie Daâge Limoges porcelain, vintage Blodwen Welsh blankets and linens as crisp as Granny Smith apples. There are edgier home pieces by Maison Martin Margiela, chic-beyond-chic stainless steel kitchens by Alpes Inox and divine cloud sculptures that the artist Benedetta Mori Ubaldini makes out of chicken wire. Conran has also added an entire section dedicated to the sort of children’s goodies — pink roller skates, giant buttons, paper pompoms — that you want to buy regardless of age. In May, he will reopen the Conran Shop’s location in Marylebone, complete with a Penthouse apartment, fully decorated and shoppable, and a roof terrace. “I love the idea of the store as a magazine,” Conran says. “It’s about highlighting different things, and discovering and showcasing new talent.” 81 Fulham Road, London; 011-44-20-7589-7401.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not His Father’s Conran Shop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conran Shop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T15:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rita Konig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Konig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8342c38-3935-5115-a9ff-aea81e9d3e1c', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8342c38-3935-5115-a9ff-aea81e9d3e1c'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama pulled an April Fools’ joke Monday with the help of another, funnier politician: Kid President.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/and-now-a-special-message-from/', 'snippet': 'President Obama pulled an April Fools’ joke Monday with the help of another, funnier politician: Kid President.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama pulled an April Fools’ joke Monday with the help of another, funnier politician: Kid President.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And Now to Washington, for a Message From . . .', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "APRIL FOOL'S DAY", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T15:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84d0dc58-90c6-5973-95be-32114c77b759', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84d0dc58-90c6-5973-95be-32114c77b759'}, {'abstract': 'Carl Richards discusses why we fail to budget, even though spending money in a way that’s aligned with what we value will bring us more happiness.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/why-budgeting-will-lead-to-more-awareness/', 'snippet': 'Carl Richards discusses why we fail to budget, even though spending money in a way that’s aligned with what we value will bring us more happiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah, and is the director of investor education at The BAM Alliance. His book, “The Behavior Gap,” was published this year. His sketches are archived\xa0on the Bucks blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Budgeting Will Lead to More Awareness', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T15:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10d88860-54ac-58c0-bfc4-f21c106cae8b', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10d88860-54ac-58c0-bfc4-f21c106cae8b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Norris, who will be supervising producer of “Fuse News,” is the latest former employee of MTV to join that program, whose on-air talent also includes Alexa Chung and Jack Osbourne.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/mtv-veteran-john-norris-joins-fuse-news/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Norris, who will be supervising producer of “Fuse News,” is the latest former employee of MTV to join that program, whose on-air talent also includes Alexa Chung and Jack Osbourne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With each new employee hired, the news division at Fuse is increasingly coming to resemble a cable rival that once put the M in music television. On Monday, Fuse said that it had hired John Norris, a veteran producer and on-air personality at MTV, as supervising producer of “Fuse News,” its daily music-news program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MTV Veteran John Norris Joins ‘Fuse News’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chung, Alexa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osbourne, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fuse Networks LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T15:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff0cd9aa-36c7-5c70-a1cc-95afcd8dbdc9', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff0cd9aa-36c7-5c70-a1cc-95afcd8dbdc9'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement between the musicians and management has yet to be ratified, but performances will resume immediately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/san-francisco-symphony-strike-ends/', 'snippet': 'The agreement between the musicians and management has yet to be ratified, but performances will resume immediately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The musicians of the San Francisco Symphony and its management have settled a strike and performances will resume on Tuesday, the orchestra said. The agreement, for a 26-month contract, ends the strike called on March 13 that forced the cancellation of orchestra appearances at Carnegie Hall and the Kennedy Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco Symphony Strike Ends', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Symphony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T15:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ba7ac5c-0e9b-546c-bbf7-82c8040a3896', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ba7ac5c-0e9b-546c-bbf7-82c8040a3896'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for James E. Holmes had tried to bargain for their client to plead guilty in exchange for life in prison with no chance of parole.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/us/prosecutors-seek-death-penalty-against-james-holmes.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for James E. Holmes had tried to bargain for their client to plead guilty in exchange for life in prison with no chance of parole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CENTENNIAL, Colo. — James E. Holmes deserves to die for killing 12 people in a storm of bullets inside a packed Colorado movie theater last July, prosecutors said in a hearing here on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'hea