e to outlaw abortion for fetal conditions like Down syndrome. I’m not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My daughter, like all kids, is a delight and a lot of work. Now 4, she talks nonstop, although her speech isn’t always comprehensible. She reads. She performs class conversations for me: “What does a cow say? Moo. Great work, Maybelle!” This evening she sang me “I’m Just a Girl Who Can’t Say No” from “Oklahoma!” (a song that, in my daughter’s case, is clearly untrue because she excels at saying no).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Outlawing Abortion Won’t Help Children with Down Syndrome', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Down Syndrome', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T16:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Piepmeier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepmeier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3fd0268-a02f-52b8-818e-f7918702c260', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3fd0268-a02f-52b8-818e-f7918702c260'}, {'abstract': 'The suit contends that a flawed drainage system allowed water to enter the passenger compartment where it sometimes damaged a crucial part of the electronic stability control, causing it to malfunction.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/suit-over-volvo-sunroofs-can-move-forward-judge-rules/', 'snippet': 'The suit contends that a flawed drainage system allowed water to enter the passenger compartment where it sometimes damaged a crucial part of the electronic stability control, causing it to malfunction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in New Jersey has allowed to move forward a class-action suit that asserts sunroofs in thousands of Volvos were prone to water leaks,\xa0which could compromise a crucial safety system. The suit contends that the company concealed the problem from consumers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suit Over Volvo Sunroofs Can Move Forward, Judge Rules', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cavanaugh, Dennis M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volvo Car Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T16:13:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4b80de0-6511-5190-b876-60b3422e3709', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4b80de0-6511-5190-b876-60b3422e3709'}, {'abstract': 'The chairwoman of the Georgia G.O.P. said same-sex unions could lead to fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/a-new-argument-against-marriage-equality/', 'snippet': 'The chairwoman of the Georgia G.O.P. said same-sex unions could lead to fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adding to the annals of things that make no sense, the chairwoman of the Georgia Republican Party argued over the weekend that legalizing same-sex marriage would create new opportunities for swindling the U.S. government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Argument Against Marriage Equality', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T16:14:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5577b31d-0e5c-5389-8116-3481caa505a8', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5577b31d-0e5c-5389-8116-3481caa505a8'}, {'abstract': 'The animosity of couples going through divorce can easily complicate a marital home’s sale, but the clients also represent a niche opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/nyregion/divorce-as-a-niche-for-realty-agents.html', 'snippet': 'The animosity of couples going through divorce can easily complicate a marital home’s sale, but the clients also represent a niche opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lucky are the few who move out of their houses simply because they have tired of the view or suddenly possess the means to trade up. More often, it is a change in life circumstances that pushes people out into the housing market, something like a new job, a new husband or a new baby.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/nyregion/02APPRAISAL/02APPRAISAL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/02/nyregion/02APPRAISAL/02APPRAISAL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/nyregion/02APPRAISAL/02APPRAISAL-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/nyregion/02APPRAISAL/02APPRAISAL-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/nyregion/02APPRAISAL/02APPRAISAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/02/nyregion/02APPRAISAL/02APPRAISAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/nyregion/02APPRAISAL/02APPRAISAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Breakup, They Help Sell the House', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Breakup, They Help Sell the House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':