t had extended the contract of its signature star, Conan O’Brien, until November 2015.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TBS Extends Conan O’Brien’s Contract Until November 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TBS Network', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Conan", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T17:59:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3295fc2b-e023-57b6-b110-6a6499b1a275', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3295fc2b-e023-57b6-b110-6a6499b1a275'}, {'abstract': 'A 135-year tradition at the White House was marked by the president’s dismal basketball performance, while families affected by gun violence joined thousands of revelers.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/missed-shots-and-quiet-messaging-at-easter-egg-roll/', 'snippet': 'A 135-year tradition at the White House was marked by the president’s dismal basketball performance, while families affected by gun violence joined thousands of revelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man in a bunny suit, a YouTube sensation and a dismal free throw performance by the president got all the laughs at the White House Easter Egg Roll on Monday morning. But along with the more than 30,000 children who frolicked across the South Lawn of the White House in ruffle socks and pastel-colored neckties, families of the victims of gun violence served as reminders of the children who could not be there. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missed Shots and Quiet Messaging at Easter Egg Roll', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Easter and Holy Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T18:04:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94c1eabe-50a0-5948-a5ca-cf7deea7f2a5', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94c1eabe-50a0-5948-a5ca-cf7deea7f2a5'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/dining-calendar-11/', 'snippet': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn Flea will extend its Manhattan presence on Monday with the opening of Smorgasburg Snack Bar on the second floor of the Whole Foods Market Bowery, at 95 East Houston Street on the Lower East Side. Unlike the pop-up Smorgasburg Bowery, which features a rotating cast of restaurants, the snack bar will feature vendors offering everything from doughnuts to kitchen aprons. The hours are 8 a.m. to 11 p.m. daily. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dining Calendar', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '