eadline': {'main': 'The Most ‘Upsetting’ Tournament Ever?', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Gulf Coast University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Louisville', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wichita State University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T19:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Bergen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e22aaf3-0ce4-5504-8a5d-8d0c6ed2dfa5', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e22aaf3-0ce4-5504-8a5d-8d0c6ed2dfa5'}, {'abstract': 'A boutique restoration company based in Glendale, Calif., brings 35-year-old sedans, coupes and wagons back to life.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/the-benz-whisperers/', 'snippet': 'A boutique restoration company based in Glendale, Calif., brings 35-year-old sedans, coupes and wagons back to life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not unusual to see a hipster tooling around Silver Lake or Williamsburg in a beat-up old Mercedes. What’s rarer is to find those 35-year-old sedans, coupes and wagons restored to mint condition. That’s the particular obsession of J. G. Francis (above right), who with the help of Sean Johnstun, founded Mercedes Motoring, a boutique restoration company based in Glendale, Calif.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Benz Whisperers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T19:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Delavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bbfcf2e-dd60-5ebc-9990-4e680c5f868a', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bbfcf2e-dd60-5ebc-9990-4e680c5f868a'}, {'abstract': 'Small coastal fisheries are having an outsize impact on sea turtle populations, a new study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/postcard-from-a-loggerhead-turtle-dying-ground/', 'snippet': 'Small coastal fisheries are having an outsize impact on sea turtle populations, a new study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New research is confirming that small coastal fishing efforts, including along the Pacific coast of Mexico’s Baja peninsula, pose a substantial threat to several endangered sea turtle species. There’s much that can be done to cut turtle losses, as you’ll be learning later this spring when Pace University students making this year’s spring documentary (for a course I co-teach) wrap their short film in early May. (The previous films are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/dotloggerhead/dotloggerhead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/01/blogs/dotloggerhead/dotloggerh