to grow, but the number of participants is the subject of a dispute between the military and lawyers for the detainees. Capt. Robert Durand, a military spokesman, said Monday that by the military’s count, 39 of the 166 detainees have been deemed hunger strikers. That is up from 28 a week ago and 37 on Friday. Lawyers for detainees, however, say their clients have told them that the majority of prisoners in Camp Six and Camp Five — the disciplinary wing where detainees live in individual cells — are participating in the strike. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Detainees on Hunger Strike', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Military', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Detainees On Hunger Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-01T23:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/394e0113-10ff-54fa-9855-519ea2ddd075', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/394e0113-10ff-54fa-9855-519ea2ddd075'}, {'abstract': 'It is easy to slow down Internet servers by harnessing thousands of computers to simultaneously send streams of data to a single address, but careful monitoring by Web services can protect against such attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/science/distributed-denial-of-service.html', 'snippet': 'It is easy to slow down Internet servers by harnessing thousands of computers to simultaneously send streams of data to a single address, but careful monitoring by Web services can protect against such attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, a dispute between an antispam enforcer and a spam provider escalated into one of the largest Internet attacks in history — what specialists call a DDoS, for distributed denial of service, in which a service like the ability to visit a Web site or use a network is denied because of deliberate congestion. In this case, a powerful stream of data, peaking at 300 billion bits per second, made some sites unavailable and slowed networks around the world. In some cases the slowdown lasted for as long as nine days.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/science/02after-_BRF/02after-_BRF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 192, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/02/science/02after-_BRF/02after-_BRF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 192}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/science/02after-_BRF/02after-_BRF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 192, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/science/02after-_BRF/02after-_BRF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 192, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':