rl': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/business/american-airlines-settles-suit-against-orbitz.html', 'snippet': 'The airline has battled Orbitz and other companies over the right to provide flight and price information to travel agents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT WORTH (AP) — American Airlines said Monday that it had settled lawsuits with the online travel agency Orbitz over the agency’s display of information about American flights and fares.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Airlines Settles Suit Against Orbitz', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Airlines Settles Suit Against Orbitz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel Agencies and Agents', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sabre Holdings Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Travelport Ltd', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orbitz Worldwide Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Expedia Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T00:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82645eab-fae3-512e-8f22-5d036528de8f', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82645eab-fae3-512e-8f22-5d036528de8f'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge’s ruling could halt the resale of digital music as well as other digital good like e-books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/business/media/redigi-loses-suit-over-reselling-of-digital-music.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge’s ruling could halt the resale of digital music as well as other digital good like e-books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in New York has dealt a blow to the nascent business of reselling digital goods like music and e-books, ruling that a small company’s secondary market for digital music infringes on the copyrights controlled by record companies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/business/Resale/Resale-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 851, 'width': 589, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/business/Resale/Resale-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 851, 'width': 589, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/business/Resale/Resale-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/02/business/Resale/Resale-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/business/Resale/Resale-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Setback for Resellers of Digital Products', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Setback For Resellers Of Digital Products', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ReDigi Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Richard J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T00:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/705eaf97-e080-575e-866c-1b8d6bbf171a', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/705eaf97-e080-575e-866c-1b8d6bbf171a'}, {'abstract': 'A new book suggests that the growing number of interfaith couples don’t know exactly what they’re getting into.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/marrying-out-of-the-faith/', 'snippet': 'A new book suggests that the growing number of interfaith couples don’t know exactly what they’re getting into.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 1963, my brother Ron was going out with (that was the phrase then) an Irish Catholic girl named Ann who was attending the University of Rhode Island. One day, she was sitting in class and suddenly through the window she saw my father, who, it turned out, had tracked her down by finding out from the university administration what classes she was taking and at what times. He took her to dinner and then proceeded to tell her that it would ruin his son’s life if he were to marry a non-Jewish girl. He then asked if she would be willing to have no contact with Ron for a year; in return, he offered to pay all her expenses during that time. She refused.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marrying Out of the Faith', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T01:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cd6452e-6e6e-5dc6-83bc-a77afd6767ea', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cd6452e-6e6e-5dc6-83bc-a77afd6767ea'}, {'abstract': 'For many recent superwealthy foreign buyers, London is just a stop in a peripatetic international existence that might also include New York, Moscow and Monaco.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/world/europe/a-slice-of-london-so-exclusive-even-the-owners-are-visitors.html', 'snippet': 'For many recent superwealthy foreign buyers, London is just a stop in a peripatetic international existence that might also include New York, Moscow and Monaco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — An odd thing was happening, or rather not happening, as dusk fell the other day across Belgravia, home to some of the world’s most valuable real estate: almost no one seemed to be coming home. Perhaps half the windows were dark.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/world/JP-LONDON/JP-LONDON-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/02/world/JP-LONDON