dce5b7c-56db-52ef-95ef-5a9dbb4785a3', 'word_count': 1581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdce5b7c-56db-52ef-95ef-5a9dbb4785a3'}, {'abstract': 'Trey Anastasio, a composer of the show, accompanies Allison Case and Jay Armstrong Johnson in “I’m Gone.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/in-performance-hands-on-a-hardbody/', 'snippet': 'Trey Anastasio, a composer of the show, accompanies Allison Case and Jay Armstrong Johnson in “I’m Gone.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hands on a Hardbody,” a new Broadway musical at the Brooks Atkinson Theater, concerns a group of Texans vying to win a truck in an endurance test. The country-rock score was written by Trey Anastasio, of the jam-band Phish, and Amanda Green, who also wrote the lyrics. (Doug Wright wrote the book.) In this excerpt Mr. Anastasio, on guitar, accompanies the actors Allison Case and Jay Armstrong Johnson in “I’m Gone.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: ‘Hands on a Hardbody’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANASTASIO, TREY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Case, Allison', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jay Armstrong', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phish', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T12:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b6c4236-21a7-5452-b641-0cc92007907d', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b6c4236-21a7-5452-b641-0cc92007907d'}, {'abstract': 'Promoting women’s labor-force participation without curbing their career achievements will require addressing another issue: why family-friendly policies aren’t being used by men.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/incentives-for-men-to-help-women-to-work/', 'snippet': 'Promoting women’s labor-force participation without curbing their career achievements will require addressing another issue: why family-friendly policies aren’t being used by men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I wrote in an article appearing this week in The New York Times Magazine, if you want women to be bigger participants in the labor force, some expansion of work-life accommodations (parental leave, flex work, telecommuting, etc.) is probably desirable, particularly relative to the barren landscape of work-life policies in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Incentives for Men, to Help Women to Work', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T12:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'org