nd marriage at Princeton and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Reducing Sodium in Your Diet', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T12:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab08268-4e49-5155-9248-8b0dfd5512bd', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab08268-4e49-5155-9248-8b0dfd5512bd'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/opinion-report-medical-devices/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Medical Devices', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T12:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f2fff1b-33f6-5c01-9259-f26498d42c26', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f2fff1b-33f6-5c01-9259-f26498d42c26'}, {'abstract': 'In a wide-ranging presentation that cited films including “Citizen Kane,” “Vertigo,” “The Red Shoes” and “The Day the Earth Stood Still,” Mr. Scorsese said “we have to treat every last moving image as reverently and respectfully as the oldest book in the Library of Congress.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/martin-scorsese-argues-for-film-preservation-in-2013-jefferson-lecture/', 'snippet': 'In a wide-ranging presentation that cited films including “Citizen Kane,” “Vertigo,” “The Red Shoes” and “The Day the Earth Stood Still,” Mr. Scorsese said “we have to treat every last moving image as reverently and respectfully as the oldest book...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Drawing upon films that included Orson Welles’s “Citizen Kane,” Alfred Hitchcock’s “Vertigo” and Thomas Edison’s short of two cats engaged in a boxing match, Martin Scorsese made the case on Monday evening that Americans “need to take pride in our cinema, our great American art form” and that all films need to be preserved, regardless of their box-office performance or apparent cultural merit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/scorsese/scorsese-articleLarge.png', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/scorsese/scorsese-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/scorsese/scorsese-jumbo.png', 'height': 361, 'width': 635, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/scorsese/scorsese-superJumbo.png', 'height': 361, 'width': 635, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/scorsese/scorsese-thumbSt