sion that the fund’s Sigma Capital unit illegally traded in shares of technology companies after a former analyst there obtained secret information about the companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/14-million-sac-settlement-is-approved/', 'snippet': 'Judge Harold Baer approved a pact in which SAC agreed to pay $14 million to settle accusations by the Securities and Exchange Commission that the fund’s Sigma Capital unit illegally traded in shares of technology companies after a former analyst t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the same day prosecutors announced insider trading charges against a former portfolio manager at the hedge fund SAC Capital Advisors, a judge signed off on a civil settlement between the fund and regulators related to the same set of facts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$14 Million SAC Settlement Is Approved', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baer, Harold Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horvath, Jon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marrero, Victor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinberg, Michael Saren', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T12:51:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/149a61b5-ed1d-5d62-b81e-5bf625594404', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/149a61b5-ed1d-5d62-b81e-5bf625594404'}, {'abstract': 'The government quickly appointed Harris Georgiades, the deputy finance minister, to replace Michalis Sarris, who negotiated the nation’s bailout agreement with international creditors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/business/global/cypriot-finance-minister-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'The government quickly appointed Harris Georgiades, the deputy finance minister, to replace Michalis Sarris, who negotiated the nation’s bailout agreement with international creditors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michalis Sarris, the Cypriot finance minister who negotiated Cyprus’s bailout agreement with international creditors, resigned on Tuesday, citing the beginning of a government inquiry into the collapse of the country’s banking industry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/world/03cyprus_cnd/03cyprus_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/world/03cyprus_cnd/03cyprus_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/world/03cyprus_cnd/03cyprus_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/world/03cyprus_cnd/03cyprus_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/world/03cyprus_cnd/03cyprus_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/03/world/03cyprus_cnd/03cyprus_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/world/03cyprus_cnd/03cyprus_cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyprus Chief of Finance Quits Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finance Minister Resigns in Cyprus, Citing an Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarris, Michalis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kanter, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T12:51:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman and James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48d6e91e-9bb2-57e2-b25e-37367c36a994', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48d6e91e-9bb2-57e2-b25e-37367c36a994'}, {'abstract': 'An Australian studio combines digital design and casting to make hard-to-resist bowls, plates and cups.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/good-enough-to-eat-pieces-of-porcelain/', 'snippet': 'An Australian studio combines digital design and casting to make hard-to-resist bowls, plates and cups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just in time for all things springlike, the latest collection in the Pieces of Porcelain line from the Australian studio Mod Collective is available from Gretel Home. Mod Collective’s founder, the ceramicist Valissa Butterworth, combines digital design and hand-molding and casting to make these hard-to-resist bowls, plates and cups. She colors them with raw pigment, a process that allows her to use bold hues as well as delicate ones, and which ensures that even if a piece chips, you still see color all the way through. The exteriors are left unglazed, while a clear gloss glaze is used on the inside of the pieces to make them safe for food. Prices for the collection range from $32 to $149.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Enough to Eat | Pieces of Porcelain', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T13:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18e3b6c0-30e5-58a0-852f-05fb98b3fa7b', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18e3b6c0-30e5-58a0-852f-05fb98b3fa7b'}, {'abstract': 'Rather than hiring an advertising agency to create a campaign, the state will rely on a team of professional copywriters, graphic designers and creative technologists who live there. Residents will be asked to critique the work the professionals produce.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/colorado-looks-to-its-own-people-to-burnish-its-image/', 'snippet': 'Rather than hiring an advertising agency to create a campaign, the state will rely on a team of professional copywriters, graphic designers and creative technologists who live there. Residents will be asked to critique the work the professionals p...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Colorado is taking a nontraditional approach to the usual efforts of creating ads that are meant to help burnish the brand image of a state. With an initiative — Making Colorado — to be announced on Tuesday, the state will ask its residents for advice that will shape the development of a campaign that is to be introduced in August. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorado Looks to Its Own People to Burnish Its Image', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hickenlooper, John W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiff, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac30a5c6-0f14-5503-86da-4e61768cff08', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac30a5c6-0f14-5503-86da-4e61768cff08'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: An air traveler learns that no matter how good Carnegie Deli’s mustard is, he cannot take eight ounces through the security checkpoint.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/mustard-fails-security-test-at-the-airport/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: An air traveler learns that no matter how good Carnegie Deli’s mustard is, he cannot take eight ounces through the security checkpoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary,', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mustard Fails Security Test at the Airport', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condiments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delicatessens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mustard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T13:03:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b966ba7-eb46-59f0-b27c-575b0ac60ef5', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b966ba7-eb46-59f0-b27c-575b0ac60ef5'}, {'abstract': 'Verizon is working with its main rival, AT&T, about a joint bid for Vodafone, The Financial Times’s Alphaville blog reports. If true, a successful deal could solve issues at both Verizon and Vodafone.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/could-verizons-best-friend-be-its-biggest-rival/', 'snippet': 'Verizon is working with its main rival, AT&T, about a joint bid for Vodafone, The Financial Times’s Alphaville blog reports. If true, a successful deal could solve issues at both Verizon and Vodafone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Verizon and Vodafone have confronted a problem: what to do with Verizon Wireless, which they both own nearly equally?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Could Verizon’s Best Friend Be Its Biggest Rival?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T13:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8670742b-638f-5ec8-a616-8d415db246fc', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8670742b-638f-5ec8-a616-8d415db246fc'}, {'abstract': 'A strengthening housing market and low interest rates spurred consumers and businesses to replace aging models.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/business/car-sales-keep-up-their-streak.html', 'snippet': 'A strengthening housing market and low interest rates spurred consumers and businesses to replace aging models.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Automakers reported on Tuesday that March sales of new cars and trucks were the highest monthly total in five years, providing more evidence of a sustained turnaround in the industry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'March Auto Sales Increased 3.4% for Highest Total Since 2007', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'March Auto Sales Increased 3.4% for Highest Total Since 2007', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T13:36:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c196e6ec-c284-5904-9edf-2f14f2cb8f86', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c196e6ec-c284-5904-9edf-2f14f2cb8f86'}, {'abstract': 'Nick Zinner, guitarist for the Yeah Yeah Yeahs, shares with us some of his behind-the-scenes photography of the band.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/who-has-the-most-exclusive-backstage-pass/', 'snippet': 'Nick Zinner, guitarist for the Yeah Yeah Yeahs, shares with us some of his behind-the-scenes photography of the band.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past weekend’s article about the Yeah Yeah Yeahs features portraits by Robert Maxwell. But for a more candid look at the band, we asked the guitarist Nick Zinner to send us some of his most recent pictures of the group’s performances and travels. Zinner’s photography has been exhibited in art galleries and collected in four monographs. I asked him a few questions about his work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/magazine/29-karen-o-1/29-karen-o-1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/29/magazine/29-karen-o-1/29-karen-o-1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/magazine/29-karen-o-1/29-karen-o-1-jumbo.png', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/magazine/29-karen-o-1/29-karen-o-1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 996, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/magazine/29-karen-o-1/29-karen-o-1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/29/magazine/29-karen-o-1/29-karen-o-1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/magazine/29-karen-o-1/29-karen-o-1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Has the Most Exclusive Backstage Pass?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T1