nsion from the Yankees before spring training, he was still being represented by Scott Boras, baseball’s most formidable and challenging negotiator. It is Boras, after all, who consistently takes big-name players to free agency so they can obtain every last penny possible in a new contract.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1096, 'width': 1611, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cano Fires Agent and Signs With Jay-Z’s Agency', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hired Fired', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boras, Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roc Nation Sports', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGENTS (BUSINESS)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T16:46:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcd79520-a20f-5c72-81d9-c8a10d572a44', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcd79520-a20f-5c72-81d9-c8a10d572a44'}, {'abstract': 'After being a dedicated college applicant for more than a year, I might be expected to understand the admissions process better. Ironically, I am only more baffled by it.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/envelope-please-sush-krishnamoorthy-9/', 'snippet': 'After being a dedicated college applicant for more than a year, I might be expected to understand the admissions process better. Ironically, I am only more baffled by it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in the college application process, I classified colleges as “dream” schools and “reach” schools based on their acceptance rates. It is popular advice to do so. Also, the terms “selectivity” and “acceptance rate” are often used interchangeably, and this indicated to me that the higher the acceptance rate of a college, the easier it is to get in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Acceptance Rates, Apparently, Are Poor Predictors of Getting In', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bryn Mawr College', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Institute of Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wellesley College', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T16:54:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sush Krishnamoorthy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sush', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krishnamoorthy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b4fdbce-0a96-573d-81b2-8f5f840d95e7', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b4fdbce-0a96-573d-81b2-8f5f840d95e7'}, {'abstract': 'A chat with NASA experts on rising seas in a warming world.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/a-nasa-hangout-on-rising-seas-and-global-warming/', 'snippet': 'A chat with NASA experts on rising seas in a warming world.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:11 p.m. | Updated |Earlier today, I participated in a NASA Google+ Hangout on Air on these questions and more:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A NASA Hangout on Rising Seas and Global Warming', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coast Erosion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watkins, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google+', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T16:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/341fed56-ce86-591c-ab99-7abc5fd06abf', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/341fed56-ce86-591c-ab99-7abc5fd06abf'}, {'abstract': 'In relation to other wealthy countries, the United States is doing a relatively good job of getting women into high-achieving jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/comparing-the-worlds-glass-ceilings/', 'snippet': 'In relation to other wealthy countries, the United States is doing a relatively good job of getting women into high-achieving jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the more surprising things I learned in my research for an article in The New York Times Magazine is that despite all the complaints about the glass ceiling, the United States is actually doing a relatively good job of getting women into high-achieving jobs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing the World’s Glass Ceilings', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T16:58:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d0c11eb-368b-5bfe-8216-722c128f248d', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d0c11eb-368b-5bfe-8216-722c128f248d'}, {'abstract': 'How was I going to find the right people with the right skills to build the lines of code I needed if I didn’t understand what I was looking for?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/finding-a-coder-when-you-dont-know-how-to-code/', 'snippet': 'How was I going to find the right people with the right skills to build the lines of code I needed if I didn’t understand what I was looking for?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I first entered the start-up world, I found the landscape tricky to navigate —\xa0especially as a nontechnical founder of a technology company. How could the founder of a tech start-up not know anything more than HTML? How was I going to hire the right people with the right skills to build the lines of code I needed if I didn’t understand what I was looking for?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding a Coder When You Don’t Know How to Code', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T17:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Herrera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herrera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b24cdba6-3259-5f73-b6c0-cc78a45d0e5e', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b24cdba6-3259-5f73-b6c0-cc78a45d0e5e'}, {'abstract': 'Officers and a bomb-sniffing dog were on hand as the rifle association unveiled its plan to train and arm security guards at every school in the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/us/nra-details-plan-for-armed-school-guards.html', 'snippet': 'Officers and a bomb-sniffing dog were on hand as the rifle association unveiled its plan to train and arm security guards at every school in the nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With the Senate set to debate gun control this month, a National Rifle Association task force released a 225-page report on Tuesday that called for armed police officers, security guards or staff members in every American school, and urged states to loosen gun restrictions to allow trained teachers and administrators to carry weapons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Sees Guns as Path to Safety in Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Sees Guns as Path To Safety In Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hutchinson, Asa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T17:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7644c821-90b3-596f-9a41-0cddf3f7d786', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7644c821-90b3-596f-9a41-0cddf3f7d786'}, {'abstract': 'The London-based designer Marianna Kennedy’s new resin lamps are a great way to add eye-popping color to any room.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/feeling-for-bright-lights/', 'snippet': 'The London-based designer Marianna Kennedy’s new resin lamps are a great way to add eye-popping color to any room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m just mad for these candylicious resin lamps by the London-based designer Marianna Kennedy. They come in eye-popping colors like deep sea green or chrome yellow, and at about $600 each (with shade) are relatively affordable, unlike the lacquered gueridon tables and gilded mercury mirrors in Kennedy’s gallery-quality collection. The conical shades are made from antique book cloth, most of which Kennedy sources from Paris. “Isn’t it funny,” she says, “you just have to say it comes from Paris and it sounds irresistible.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Bright Lights', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bright Lights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T17:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rita Konig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Konig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7698eb50-ccb2-58c9-b755-7bc257ac578f', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7698eb50-ccb2-58c9-b755-7bc257ac578f'}, {'abstract': 'U.S. Soccer this week is celebrating its founding 100 years ago, on April 5, 1913 in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/u-s-soccer-celebrates-100-years/', 'snippet': 'U.S. Soccer this week is celebrating its founding 100 years ago, on April 5, 1913 in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'U.S. Soccer is coming home — to New York — to celebrate the 100th anniversary of its founding on April 5, 1913.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/sports/soccer/usloggo/usloggo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image