'snippet': 'Yasmine Mousa, a former interpreter for The New York Times in Baghdad, says that Iraq remains hostage to an ill-fated decision and wonders whether there is room for repair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I first set foot at Baghdad International Airport in March 2010 to work for The New York Times, I was no stranger to Iraq. Until 2003, Baghdad had been my home. I still had family and friends here, and they remained dear to me, and I to them. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unfamiliar Feelings in a Familiar Land', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussein, Saddam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T17:29:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yasmine Mousa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yasmine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mousa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/952cf4c9-d660-5f94-88a3-483f279c8c36', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952cf4c9-d660-5f94-88a3-483f279c8c36'}, {'abstract': 'The roster of faculty members who have helped shape white-collar crime as an important field of legal study is made up largely of women.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/women-lead-the-way-in-white-collar-law/', 'snippet': 'The roster of faculty members who have helped shape white-collar crime as an important field of legal study is made up largely of women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s still a man’s world in many sectors of the legal profession, as it is in much of corporate America. It’s true for prosecutors, for white-collar defense partners at major firms and in executive suites. But when it comes to researching and being an authoritative voice of study about white-collar crime, women are taking the lead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Lead the Way in White-Collar Law', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T17:29:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ff57ead-1fbd-5be7-bccc-6ffd87b9fd0f', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ff57ead-1fbd-5be7-bccc-6ffd87b9fd0f'}, {'abstract': 'After taking charge in the second set, Serena Williams dominated Maria Sharapova to win her sixth Sony Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/breaking-it-down-williams-vs-sharapova/', 'snippet': 'After taking charge in the second set, Serena Williams dominated Maria Sharapova to win her sixth Sony Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KEY BISCAYNE, Fla. — Serena Williams is from another planet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/sports/tennis/03serena/03serena-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/spor