fone, whether alone or in conjunction with others,” following a report that it was working with AT&T on a joint bid.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/verizon-says-its-not-currently-planning-to-bid-for-vodafone/', 'snippet': 'Verizon said on Tuesday that it did not “currently have any intention to merge with or make an offer for Vodafone, whether alone or in conjunction with others,” following a report that it was working with AT&T on a joint bid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investors hoping for a giant trans-Atlantic telecommunications deal will have to cool their heels for a bit longer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verizon Says It’s Not ‘Currently’ Planning to Bid for Vodafone', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T21:26:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/772b9725-68f0-5376-88dc-1295ab9f0e24', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/772b9725-68f0-5376-88dc-1295ab9f0e24'}, {'abstract': 'The Pan Asian Repertory Theater’s production of “Three Trees” looks at the life of Alberto Giacometti.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/theater/reviews/three-trees-a-play-about-giacometti-by-alvin-eng.html', 'snippet': 'The Pan Asian Repertory Theater’s production of “Three Trees” looks at the life of Alberto Giacometti.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Three Trees” is inspired by the life of the 20th-century artist Alberto Giacometti and his unusual relationship with his muse, the Japanese philosophy professor Isaku Yanaihara. Unusual not only because the muse was male, but also because he happened to be sleeping with Giacometti’s wife, with the artist’s full knowledge and consent.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/sub2three/sub2three-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/sub2three/sub2three-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/sub2three/sub2three-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/sub2three/sub2three-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1225, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/sub2three/sub2three-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/sub2three/sub2three-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/sub2three/sub2three-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Artist’s Muse Loves the Artist’s Wife', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Artist’s Muse Loves the Artist’s Wife', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pan Asian Repertory Theatre', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eng, Alvin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giacometti, Alberto', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T21:27:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f23987e2-aa74-547f-83e4-0d05bab7e409', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f23987e2-aa74-547f-83e4-0d05bab7e409'}, {'abstract': 'When an arts building, like the planned hub at ground zero, is designed to be adaptable to everything, it can wind up being not especially good for anything.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/arts/music/questions-on-ground-zero-arts-center-left-unanswered.html', 'snippet': 'When an arts building, like the planned hub at ground zero, is designed to be adaptable to everything, it can wind up being not especially good for anything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The visionary architect Frank Gehry remains committed to designing the performing arts center at the site of the former World Trade Center. But what exactly has Mr. Gehry been asked to design? What is it for? Which institutions, ensembles or companies will perform in the complex? Who wil