d_paragraph': 'With ECMAScript 6 inching closer and closer to becoming an accepted standard, it’s a perfect time to look at some of the incredibly useful changes in the last big ES release. ECMAScript 5, published in 2009, gave JavaScript developers some great new options. One of its most powerful additions was Object.defineProperty. This method allows you to make better use of the browser’s internals. John Resig explains:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using ECMAScript 5 Objects and Properties', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T22:07:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trevor Landau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trevor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b77f1628-1c7e-577d-a18e-296d8981108d', 'word_count': 1143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b77f1628-1c7e-577d-a18e-296d8981108d'}, {'abstract': 'Cindy Kleine’s gripping documentary about her husband, the theater director André Gregory, feels almost like a sequel to “My Dinner With André.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/movies/andre-gregory-before-and-after-dinner-by-cindy-kleine.html', 'snippet': 'Cindy Kleine’s gripping documentary about her husband, the theater director André Gregory, feels almost like a sequel to “My Dinner With André.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s the art of being, not the act of performing,” the experimental-theater director André Gregory muses in “André Gregory: Before and After Dinner,” an indelible, gripping documentary portrait by his wife, Cindy Kleine. “Even emotion can be a mask.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/andre/andre-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/andre/andre-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/andre/andre-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/andre/andre-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 1392, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/andre/andre-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/andre/andre-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/andre/andre-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Dessert, After That Meal With Wally', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Dessert, After That Meal With Wally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gregory, Andre', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T22:08:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffcfa0d7-95e7-5937-bc36-b34f6363d8b3', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffcfa0d7-95e7-5937-bc36-b34f6363d8b3'}, {'abstract': 'Just in time for the Tribeca Film Festival, moviegoers can keep track of screenings with a limited-edition watch.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/movie-time/', 'snippet': 'Just in time for the Tribeca Film Festival, moviegoers can keep track of screenings with a limited-edition watch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To help moviegoers keep on track for a week’s worth of screening indie titles during this year’s Tribeca Film Festival, which takes place in New York later this month, IWC Schaffhausen created a limited-edition “Tribeca Film Festival 2013″ watch. Produced in stainless steel and a batch of only 100, the watch will set you back $13,600 and is available today at the watchmaker’s flagship store on Madison Avenue, just in time to map out your viewing schedule. For those truly wanting to commemorate the event, a single platinum version will be up for auction at Antiquorum on April 10.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Movie Time', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tribeca Film Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IWC Schaffhausen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T22:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0c7b214-aaf6-588e-a1c0-ca45cc6c3211', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0c7b214-aaf6-588e-a1c0-ca45cc6c3211'}, {'abstract': 'Fargo, N.D., is preparing for its fourth flood in the last five years, but plans are under way to wall off the city from the Red River’s spring rages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/us/fargo-nd-seeks-flood-protection.html', 'snippet': 'Fargo, N.D., is preparing for its fourth flood in the last five years, but plans are under way to wall off the city from the Red River’s spring rages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FARGO, N.D. — Just last fall, the reservoirs and rivers here in the Red River Valley were so low from drought that Mayor Dennis R. Walaker of Fargo was concerned that the faucets and shower heads in his city would run dry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/us/FLOOD-1/FLOOD-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/us/FLOOD-1/FLOOD-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/us/FLOOD-1/FLOOD-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/us/FLOOD-1/FLOOD-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/us/FLOOD-1/FLOOD-1-thumbSt