in Mr. Redford’s latest film, “The Company You Keep.” Click on the image above to watch the event, which was moderated by the Times media columnist David Carr.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Streaming: TimesTalks With Robert Redford and Shia LaBeouf', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaBeouf, Shia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redford, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-02T22:28:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5e4f75c-a9cf-5f09-a3a5-fdd7b1ee681d', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5e4f75c-a9cf-5f09-a3a5-fdd7b1ee681d'}, {'abstract': 'Hedge funds are promising to pay their director candidates millions of dollars if they can improve a company’s performance.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/02/upping-the-ante-in-a-play-for-a-stronger-board/', 'snippet': 'Hedge funds are promising to pay their director candidates millions of dollars if they can improve a company’s performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Would you pay a director tens of millions for fantastic performance? Welcome to the newest trend in activist investing: hedge funds paying their nominees to a company’s board as if they were chief executives.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upping the Ante in a Play for a Stronger Board', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Upping the Ante in a Play for a Stronger Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exec