', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53738f1f-e582-56f3-ab74-fe4b6f9389d3', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53738f1f-e582-56f3-ab74-fe4b6f9389d3'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin signed a law on Tuesday that could roll back a reform, pushed by his predecessor, that allows the direct election of regional governors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/world/europe/russia-new-law-allows-governors-to-be-appointed-undoing-reform.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin signed a law on Tuesday that could roll back a reform, pushed by his predecessor, that allows the direct election of regional governors.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Vladimir V. Putin signed a law on Tuesday that could roll back a reform pushed by his predecessor allowing the direct election of regional governors. The new law allows regional legislatures to forgo elections and appoint governors from a list of candidates approved by Mr. Putin. He abolished direct elections for governors in 2004, during his second term as president, but President Dmitri A. Medvedev pushed a law through Parliament last year to restore them in what was seen as a major concession to a growing political opposition movement. Mr. Putin, now serving his third term as president, has said that the new law is needed to protect minorities in regions where elections could be combustible. Critics said the law would allow the pro-Kremlin United Russia Party to avoid election defeats by using its control of regional legislatures to bypass popular voting. The law was the latest unwinding of Mr. Medvedev’s initiatives since Mr. Putin returned to the presidency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: New Law Allows Governors to Be Appointed, Undoing Reform', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: New Law Allows Governors To Be Appointed, Undoing Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T01:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cabce551-7020-5619-8c57-f4d6262ffd7e', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cabce551-7020-5619-8c57-f4d6262ffd7e'}, {'abstract': 'Jay-Z has long been in the inner circle of A-list athletes, and now he is making a move to turn those relationships into big business in a more formal way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/sports/new-jay-z-lyrics-for-athletes-please-let-me-represent-you.html', 'snippet': 'Jay-Z has long been in the inner circle of A-list athletes, and now he is making a move to turn those relationships into big business in a more formal way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'His social circle includes the biggest names in sports. His celebrity cachet is unmatched. He has informally advised athletes on everything from housing choices to contract extensions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarg