nt_headline': 'Public Housing as a &#8216;Penal Colony&#8217;', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T01:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/042200c6-12d3-59e0-9ce1-645aa7688f23', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/042200c6-12d3-59e0-9ce1-645aa7688f23'}, {'abstract': 'Malcolm A. Smith, who was part of an unusual two-party alliance controlling the State Senate, faced immediate repercussions after he was charged in a bribery plot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/nyregion/corruption-case-reaches-coalition-leading-state-senate.html', 'snippet': 'Malcolm A. Smith, who was part of an unusual two-party alliance controlling the State Senate, faced immediate repercussions after he was charged in a bribery plot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last fall, as a group of breakaway Democrats was preparing to join forces with Republicans to take control of the State Senate, they recruited Malcolm A. Smith, a Queens Democrat, to join their caucus. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/nyregion/ALBANY/ALBANY-article