e a boost to the court when the State Department offers a reward for information on fugitives in atrocity cases and issues a list of names that will include the court’s most-wanted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — When a fugitive African warlord, Gen. Bosco Ntaganda, gave himself up in March to the United States Embassy in Rwanda and asked to be sent to the International Criminal Court here, American diplomats publicized the episode and swiftly brokered the transfer. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Grows More Helpful to International Criminal Court, a Body It First Scorned', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Grows More Helpful to International Criminal Court, a Body It First Scorned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Marlise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapp, Stephen J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hague (Netherlands)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T01:38:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3e23bcf-139a-5ab1-93e5-80a84fabcd17', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3e23bcf-139a-5a