article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/803c1900-f3de-5000-8eb7-a2569bed9e10', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/803c1900-f3de-5000-8eb7-a2569bed9e10'}, {'abstract': 'Second Stage Theater’s revival of “The Last Five Years” confirms memories of this musical by Jason Robert Brown as a series of pleasant, but not distinctive, show tunes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/theater/reviews/the-last-five-years-a-musical-at-second-stage-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Second Stage Theater’s revival of “The Last Five Years” confirms memories of this musical by Jason Robert Brown as a series of pleasant, but not distinctive, show tunes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the more than 10 years since “The Last Five Years” was first produced, this two-character musical by Jason Robert Brown about the life and death of young love has been embraced by new generations of musical-theater lovers. Watching the revival that opened at Second Stage Theater on Tuesday night, I fancifully imagined I could hear all the fans in the audience singing along in their heads. They greeted almost every number with fervent applause, as if each were the guest of honor arriving at a birthday party. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/03LASTFIVEjp/03LASTFIVEjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/03LASTFIVEjp/03LASTFIVEjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 312}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/arts/03LASTFIVEjp/03LASTFIVEjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam