erbia’s aspirations to join the European Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/world/europe/kosovo-talks-end-without-agreement.html', 'snippet': 'Talks aimed at overcoming ethnic divisions in Kosovo ended without an agreement Wednesday, a potential blow to Serbia’s aspirations to join the European Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Marathon talks aimed at overcoming ethnic divisions in Kosovo ended without an agreement on Wednesday, dealing a potential blow to Serbia’s aspirations to join the European Union and undermining hopes of improved stability in the Balkans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/europe/04kosovo/04kosovo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/04/world/europe/04kosovo/04kosovo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/europe/04kosovo/04kosovo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/europe/04kosovo/04kosovo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/europe/04kosovo/04kosovo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/04/world/europe/04kosovo/04kosovo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/europe/04kosovo/04kosovo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lack of Accord May Hurt Serbia’s Aim to Join European Bloc', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lack of Accord May Hurt Serbia Aim to Join European Bloc', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Balkan States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T13:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b003d41-c9de-5a63-afa5-700e31e0c6b6', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b003d41-c9de-5a63-afa5-700e31e0c6b6'}, {'abstract': 'Danforth W. Toan, who died on Jan. 16 at 94, was among the first architects to wrestle seriously with the challenges of creating long-term living quarters in space.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/this-architect-was-aboard-the-space-station-45-years-ago/', 'snippet': 'Danforth W. Toan, who died on Jan. 16 at 94, was among the first architects to wrestle seriously with the challenges of creating long-term living quarters in space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the International Space Station flew over New York on March 23 (yielding this dazzling nighttime cityscape), it’s safe to say that crew members were not thinking about Danforth W. Toan. But 45 years earlier, before some of the crew members were even born, he was thinking about them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/blogs/20130403SpaceEmbed2/20130403SpaceEmbed2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/02/blogs/20130403SpaceEmbed2/20130403SpaceEmbed2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/blogs/20130403SpaceEmbed2/20130403SpaceEmbed2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/blogs/20130403SpaceEmbed2/20130403SpaceEmbed2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/blogs/20130403SpaceEmbed2/20130403SpaceEmbed2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/02/blogs/20130403SpaceEmbed2/20130403SpaceEmbed2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/blogs/20130403SpaceEmbed2/20130403SpaceEmbed2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Architect Was Aboard the Space Station 45 Years Ago', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Space Station', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space Stations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T13:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7512233-4bb4-5a86-a555-f3818afc4107', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7512233-4bb4-5a86-a555-f3818afc4107'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the hurdles — complicated real estate interests, a nearly complete billion dollar renovation of the current Madison Square Garden, and more — there have been numerous calls for taking the time to get it right.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/municipal-art-society-challenges-architects-for-new-penn-station-vision/', 'snippet': 'Despite the hurdles — complicated real estate interests, a nearly complete billion dollar renovation of the current Madison Square Garden, and more — there have been numerous calls for taking the time to get it right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a way, it’s every architect’s dream – to re-envision Penn Station and Madison Square Garden in New York. The Municipal Art Society of New York is giving four design firms that chance with a challenge to be announced Thursday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Municipal Art Society Challenges Architects for New Penn Station Vision', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Architectural Challenge For Penn Station Vision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pennsylvania Station (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T13:47:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41c588e1-0929-534f-a61d-ca7df0e5b9cb', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41c588e1-0929-534f-a61d-ca7df0e5b9cb'}, {'abstract': 'After an online fundraising campaign, the New York Shakespeare Exchange is filming 154 actors reciting Shakespeare’s sonnets at locations around New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/taking-shakespeares-sonnets-to-the-streets-of-new-york/', 'snippet': 'After an online fundraising campaign, the New York Shakespeare Exchange is filming 154 actors reciting Shakespeare’s sonnets at locations around New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Urie, Lynn Cohen, Joanna Gleason, Austin Pendleton and Chris Sarandon are a handful of the 154 actors who will speak the speech in the yearlong Sonnet Project, an undertaking of the New York Shakespeare Exchange. The company, after raising almost $50,000 in a Kickstarter campaign, will film all of Shakespeare’s sonnets, each performed by a different actor in a New York City location – hence the overall cast of 154. Over the course of the next year, videos will be released singly or in small groups on the Web site SonnetProjectNYC.com, and through a soon-to-be-released mobile app.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/02artsbeat-shakespeare/02artsbeat-shakespeare-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/02artsbeat-shakespeare/02artsbeat-shakespeare-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/02artsbeat-shakespeare/02artsbeat-shakespeare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/02artsbeat-shakespeare/02artsbeat-shakespeare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/02/arts/02artsbeat-shakespeare/02artsbeat-shakespeare-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Shakespeare’s Sonnets to the Streets of New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e9c50cf-8ac0-5969-9e1e-89210d1ac541', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e9c50cf-8ac0-5969-9e1e-89210d1ac541'}, {'abstract': 'The pro-choice side is usually on the defensive. But active attempts to protect reproductive freedom are not unheard of.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/affirming-abortion-rights/', 'snippet': 'The pro-choice side is usually on the defensive. But active attempts to protect reproductive freedom are not unheard of.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anti-abortion activists are nothing if not inventive. State legislatures sympathetic to the cause are constantly finding new ways to restrict the legality or availability of the procedure, passing bans on so-called “partial-birth” abortion, parental consent requirements, and, more recently, “fetal heartbeat” laws. Choking off money is also wildly popular. According to the Guttmacher Institute, 32 states and the District of Columbia prohibit the use of state funds except in cases where the woman’s life is at risk or the pregnancy is the result of rape or incest. Another eight states limit coverage in private insurance plans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Affirming Abortion Rights', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guttmacher Institute', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T14:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c028c4a-b57b-5a1e-b2e0-e2d6757cb7d1', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c028c4a-b57b-5a1e-b2e0-e2d6757cb7d1'}, {'abstract': 'A preview of Wednesday’s matches in the quarterfinals of the UEFA Champions League.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/champions-league-quarterfinals-matchday-2/', 