'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/046efa5e-ef5a-510c-ba5a-bb7fa8b57435'}, {'abstract': 'A new survey finds a strong majority of Republicans and conservative independent voters seek action on climate and non-polluting energy sources.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/survey-finds-most-republicans-seek-action-on-climate-change/', 'snippet': 'A new survey finds a strong majority of Republicans and conservative independent voters seek action on climate and non-polluting energy sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s time for that national “listening tour” on energy and climate, President Obama. Some evidence comes in a new survey from the Center for Climate Change Communication at George Mason University (seen via Tom Yulsman on Facebook). Here’s an excerpt from the news release:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Survey Finds Most Republicans Seek Action on Climate Change', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'George Mason University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T14:43:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28ddb7b1-3bc5-5f6e-bb93-3adb528b082c', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28ddb7b1-3bc5-5f6e-bb93-3adb528b082c'}, {'abstract': 'Rutgers’s initial reaction to video of Mike Rice’s abuse of basketball players drew a firestorm of criticism, on a day when Mark Cuban openly contemplated drafting Brittney Griner for the Mavericks and Texas’ Yu Darvish just missed a perfect game.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/leading-off-rutgers-runs-off-the-rails/', 'snippet': 'Rutgers’s initial reaction to video of Mike Rice’s abuse of basketball players drew a firestorm of criticism, on a day when Mark Cuban openly contemplated drafting Brittney Griner for the Mavericks and Texas’ Yu Darvish just missed a perfect game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news Tuesday could have revolved around Carmelo Anthony’s 50 points against the Heat, Yu Darvish’s almost no-hitter for the Rangers or the idea that the Mavericks owner Mark Cuban might draft Brittney Griner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: Rutgers Runs Off the Rails', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuban, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griner, Brittney', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Sean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdock, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pernetti, Tim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Mike Jr (1969- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific-12 Conference', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T14:44:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Reddicliffe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reddicliffe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/680186d9-84e7-5978-888a-991e927459b4', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/680186d9-84e7-5978-888a-991e927459b4'}, {'abstract': 'Concerned about finding the right summer camp experience for your children? Here’s what to ask.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/finding-the-right-summer-day-camp/', 'snippet': 'Concerned about finding the right summer camp experience for your children? Here’s what to ask.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now is the time to get your kids into summer day camp, if you haven’t already. Parents of children returning to camp, or of younger siblings following their elders, have it easy (and are probably already signed up). But if this will be your child’s first summer of day camp, the choice may feel more difficult.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding the Right Summer Day Camp', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ninety-Second Street Y', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T14:44:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f9798aa-3b83-5af1-bdc2-a3a0aa1271ca', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f9798aa-3b83-5af1-bdc2-a3a0aa1271ca'}, {'abstract': 'A Consumer Reports analysis of five generic drugs found Costco offered the lowest prices.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/want-the-lowest-drug-price-make-sure-to-ask/', 'snippet': 'A Consumer Reports analysis of five generic drugs found Costco offered the lowest prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its latest analysis of prescription drug prices, Consumer Reports comes up with some advice that sounds almost retro: when shopping for medicine, ask for the lowest possible price.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Want the Lowest Drug Price? Make Sure to Ask', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Generic Brands and Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Reports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T14:50:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39a790c9-040c-51aa-9d4c-70062057b871', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39a790c9-040c-51aa-9d4c-70062057b871'}, {'abstract': 'The InterContinental Hotels Group is offering free Internet to its 71 million loyalty program members over the next year.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/free-internet-access/', 'snippet': 'The InterContinental Hotels Group is offering free Internet to its 71 million loyalty program members over the next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Free hotel Internet service may be reaching a tipping point. The InterContinental Hotels Group (IHG) is offering free Internet to its 71 million loyalty program members over the next year. Elite members of the IHG Rewards Club will get free Internet access beginning in July when staying at any of the company’s nine hotel brands, including InterContinental Hotels & Resorts, Hotel Indigo, Crowne Plaza, Staybridge Suites and Holiday Inn. The rest of the program’s members will get the free service starting in early 2014.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Internet Access', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hotels: Free Internet Access', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'InterContinental Hotels Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Stellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33802890-b529-5036-8152-230ff2b7caa3', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33802890-b529-5036-8152-230ff2b7caa3'}, {'abstract': 'A classic French slip-on shoe gets electrified.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/kickstarters/', 'snippet': 'A classic French slip-on shoe gets electrified.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The architect Rafael de Cárdenas has electrified Rivieras, the classic French slip-on, with a sharp new pattern available in four color combos. De Cárdenas says the shoe brand was a natural fit for him. “I like their form and shape as well as their nod to the ’60s and ’70s French Riviera summer culture,” he says. “I also like that they are called a ‘leisure shoe,’ almost as though wearing them might relax you regardless of whether you’re leisurely or not.” $100; Opening Ceremony, (212) 219-2688.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kickstarters', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T15:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/236bd83d-3f5e-5e4b-ba27-f7a99d8be338', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/236bd83d-3f5e-5e4b-ba27-f7a99d8be338'}, {'abstract': 'About 1.7 million vehicles – both Hyundais and Kias – are involved in separate recalls for a malfunctioning stop-lamp switch.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/kia-and-hyundai-are-recalling-1-9-million-vehicles-in-three-actions/', 'snippet': 'About 1.7 million vehicles – both Hyundais and Kias – are involved in separate recalls for a malfunctioning stop-lamp switch.', '