huck Hagel called for a need to rebalance missions and money available for the Pentagon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel, facing inevitable steep cuts in military spending even as global threats remain high, said Wednesday that he is being forced to consider fundamental changes in how the Pentagon defends American interests and conducts its daily business. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Budget Constraints Forcing an Overhaul in Military Operations, Hagel Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Constraints Forcing an Overhaul in Military Operations, Hagel Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanker, Thom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T19:35:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc354db3-e431-5863-acda-3d37ebbf668b', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc354db3-e431-5863-acda-3d37ebbf668b'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama announced that he would return 5 percent of his salary to the Treasury, in solidarity with public servants affected by the sequester.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/look-whos-taking-a-pay-cut/', 'snippet': 'President Obama announced that he would return 5 percent of his salary to the Treasury, in solidarity with public servants affected by the sequester.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday I wrote that the lucky ducks in Congress are exempt from the sequester. Head Start programs are cutting back; the White House furloughed 480 people; but Congressional salaries will remain intact, because they’re not appropriated by Congress or included in presidential budgets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look Who’s Taking a Pay Cut', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T19:36:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/805a0bc8-ab8a-5d97-935e-a47c45fea761', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/805a0bc8-ab8a-5d97-935e-a47c45fea761'}, {'abstract': 'The recent spurt in bank business lending is starting to flash some warning signs. The concern is that banks are making loans to businesses at rates that are so low that they may end up being unprofitable for the lenders.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/as-banks-increase-business-lending-concerns-emerge/', 'snippet': 'The recent spurt in bank business lending is starting to flash some warning signs. The concern is that banks are making loans to businesses at rates that are so low that they may end up being unprofitable for the lenders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the economic scene, it would seem heartening to see a surge in loans that banks are making to corporations of all sizes. The loans help finance business expansion, which may lead to jobs growth. And it shows that banks don’t have to pile back into real estate loans, recently the source of crippling losses, to grow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Business Lending Rises, Concerns Emerge About Profit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huntington Bancshares Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T19:37:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3cf6cc7-bd76-5e2f-84fb-8677c2a2cc09', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3cf6cc7-bd76-5e2f-84fb-8677c2a2cc09'}, {'abstract': 'Carbon Motors employees packed up a moving truck last month and left no forwarding address.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/company-with-aspirations-to-make-police-cars-abandons-its-indiana-offices/', 'snippet': 'Carbon Motors employees packed up a moving truck last month and left no forwarding address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The small town of Connersville, Ind., has closed the books on the Carbon Motors Corporation, an Indiana start-up that had moved to town in 2009 to manufacture and sell police vehicles, but was turned down last year for an Energy Department loan.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Company With Aspirations to Make Police Cars Abandons Its Indiana Offices', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Car Company\r\nAbandons Offices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T19:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tudor Van Hampton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tudor', 'middlename': 'Van', 'lastname': 'Hampton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/343d21b3-5ba4-5740-aed7-a3d6c665f347', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/343d21b3-5ba4-5740-aed7-a3d6c665f347'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said that trains would arrive in time for the morning rush on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/subway-service-is-returning-to-old-south-ferry-station/', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said that trains would arrive in time for the morning rush on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than five months after Hurricane Sandy battered South Ferry station, blowing a hole in the subway map in Lower Manhattan, service will return to the stop on Thursday for the first time since the storm, officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/ny