Women's Wear Daily", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T21:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/03f49953-bc63-51dc-9e35-fe0d745967e1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/03f49953-bc63-51dc-9e35-fe0d745967e1'}, {'abstract': 'With $130 million-worth of needed renovations looming, the Corcoran Gallery of Art looks to the University of Maryland to help with its budget problems.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/corcoran-announces-proposed-partnership-with-university-of-maryland/', 'snippet': 'With $130 million-worth of needed renovations looming, the Corcoran Gallery of Art looks to the University of Maryland to help with its budget problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With $130 million-worth of needed renovations looming, the Corcoran Gallery of Art in Washington was in need of help. On Wednesday, the board of trustees announced that a memorandum of understanding to pursue a partnership with the University of Maryland. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corcoran Announces Proposed Partnership With University of Maryland', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corcoran Gallery of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Maryland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T21:29:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ceb1ab81-0c81-5c73-9f68-eef7f488140a', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ceb1ab81-0c81-5c73-9f68-eef7f488140a'}, {'abstract': 'Images of city and country collide in “MIRROR,” Doug Aitken’s latest video art project.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/a-love-letter-to-seattle-doug-aitkens-mirror/', 'snippet': 'Images of city and country collide in “MIRROR,” Doug Aitken’s latest video art project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mountain ranges. Airplane hangars. Trains and lakes. In Doug Aitken’s latest video art project, “MIRROR,” images of city and country dissolve into graphic patterns. The work, Aitken’s first permanent installation, is displayed on a giant LED screen that’s wrapped around the facade of the Seattle Art Museum. It’s part video, part light display: columns of light brighten the building in time with the film, which highlights the beauty of Seattle and Washington State. The video feed is said to respond to conditions outside the museum — weather, traffic and the like. On March 24, Terry Riley and the Seattle Symphony were on hand to inaugurate Aitken’s first-ever permanent installation for a public museum with a live performance of Riley’s “In C.” The video above features highlights from the event.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Love Letter to Seattle | Doug Aitken’s ‘MIRROR’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Art Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T21:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvia Rupani-Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rupani-Smith', 'qualifier': None, '