, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T21:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f73d9085-2e0c-533c-82ac-926469e9d867', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f73d9085-2e0c-533c-82ac-926469e9d867'}, {'abstract': 'The tangoists Gabriel Missé and Analía Centurión gave one of their late-night performances on Tuesday in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/arts/dance/gabriel-misse-and-analia-centurion-tango-at-dardo-galletto.html', 'snippet': 'The tangoists Gabriel Missé and Analía Centurión gave one of their late-night performances on Tuesday in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The performances that the superlative Argentine tangoists Gabriel Missé and Analía Centurión give in New York are late-night affairs, with the result that a working dance critic usually comes to them after another performance. Over the past 13 months I’ve therefore seen them within an hour or two of superb performances by American Ballet Theater, the Paul Taylor Dance Company and, on Tuesday, Lil Buck. Each time, as I’ve arrived, I’ve feared that the tangoists will pale by comparison. Each time the opposite has proved true.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/submisse/submisse-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/submisse/submisse-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600,