.com/2013/04/04/arts/television/mads-mikkelsen-in-hannibal-on-nbc.html', 'snippet': 'NBC’s “Hannibal,” with Mads Mikkelsen, brings a younger version of Thomas Harris’s infamous psychiatrist Hannibal Lecter to prime-time television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is one reason, and only one reason, that the name Hannibal has become synonymous with gleefully stomach-churning horror: Anthony Hopkins’s tour-de-force performance, both chilling and hilarious, in Jonathan Demme’s 1991 film, “The Silence of the Lambs.” Everything before and since — the four Hannibal Lecter novels by Thomas Harris, the four other films with or without Mr. Hopkins — has gone to the bank because of the way he wrapped his lips around “Good evening, Clarice.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/04HANNIBAL/04HANNIBAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/04HANNIBAL/04HANNIBAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/04HANNIBAL/04HANNIBAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/04HANNIBAL/04HANNIBAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1226, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/04HANNIBAL/04HANNIBAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/04/arts/04HANNIBAL/04HANNIBAL-thumbStandar