c', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APNEA (SLEEP DISORDER)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T22:58:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/78699ff2-7b77-5a2f-bc33-57b31011c1c8', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78699ff2-7b77-5a2f-bc33-57b31011c1c8'}, {'abstract': 'Lisa Wagner, from the blog Rug Chick, offers advice on buying and maintaining carpets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/garden/cleaning-advice-from-a-rug-specialist.html', 'snippet': 'Lisa Wagner, from the blog Rug Chick, offers advice on buying and maintaining carpets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is this rug worth cleaning? If it’s wall-to-wall, hire a professional in-home carpet cleaner. But for wool, silk, cotton, Navajo, Turkish, Afghani, Berber, Chinese or other woven rugs, the answer can often be found on the blog Rug Chick. Lisa Wagner, Rug Chick herself, is an owner with her mother of K. Blatchford’s Rug Cleaning in San Diego. Ms. Wagner teaches rug cleaning to professionals; her next workshop, in McKeesport, Pa., is April 24 through 26. “I share our mistakes over the decades,” she said. Ms. Wagner was born into the business; her father, Don Blatchford — her parents are long divorced — is a rug broker. Her mother, Kate Blatchford, is a weaver and rug-repair specialist. Ms. Wagner is, in other words, a rug geek. “I’m part of a Facebook group,” she said, “that posts pictures daily asking, ‘What’s my rug and where’s it’s from?’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/garden/04QNA_SPAN/04QNA_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/04/garden/04QNA_SPAN/04QNA_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 637}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/garden/04QNA_SPAN/04QNA_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 964, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/garden/04QNA_SPAN/04QNA_SPAN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1928, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/garden/04QNA_SPAN/04QNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/04/garden/04QNA_SPAN/04QNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/garden/04QNA_SPAN/04QNA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rug Expert Keeps Her Eyes on the Floor', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping Her Eyes On the Floor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carpets and Rugs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Linda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleansers, Detergents and Soaps', 'rank': 3, 'major': '