s to a column by David Brooks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Marriage and Freedom', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gay Marriage and Freedom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T23:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/e594add4-202c-56d9-bd23-be4c873cacfb', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e594add4-202c-56d9-bd23-be4c873cacfb'}, {'abstract': 'What spending $638,412 on Gucci clothing means to Buzz Bissinger, the Pulitzer Prize winner, and to a few observers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/fashion/buzz-bissingers-expensive-pursuit-of-a-new-self.html', 'snippet': 'What spending $638,412 on Gucci clothing means to Buzz Bissinger, the Pulitzer Prize winner, and to a few observers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Internet came alive last week with frenzied commentary about the confessional by the Pulitzer Prize winner Buzz Bissinger in the April issue of GQ, an epic tale of a writer stoking a compulsive-shopping disorder with huge doses of Gucci. The article was a classic in glossy magazine moralism, well timed both to lure and shock readers still attempting to stagger out of the slough of an inert economy. What do you mean Buzz Bissinger spent $638,412.97 on clothing? That’s 9,388 pairs of Dockers, or enough to outfit almost 400 of the high school football teams Mr. Bissinger came to fame writing about.', 'print_section': 'E',