wareness System with the New York Police Department, says it is actively negotiating with a number of prospective buyers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/nyregion/new-york-citys-police-surveillance-technology-could-bring-in-money.html', 'snippet': 'Microsoft, which developed the Domain Awareness System with the New York Police Department, says it is actively negotiating with a number of prospective buyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A unique public-private partnership that joined gut-level police acumen with advanced computer algorithms is proceeding toward two goals that rarely coincide: The policing system is making New York safer and it will also make money for the city, which is marketing it to other jurisdictions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Surveillance May Earn Money for City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Surveillance May Earn Money for City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daddario, Richard', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-03T23:56:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25bbc29d-bb3b-55f2-aa3c-06138239a6c0', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25bbc29d-bb3b-55f2-aa3c-06138239a6c0'}, {'abstract': 'It’s money we owe to ourselves. Really.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/03/debt-and-david-stockman/', 'snippet': 'It’s money we owe to ourselves. Really.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: I forgot to explain that the chart shows the ratio of financial-sector debt to GDP.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt and David Stockman', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T00:08:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bed234a-9875-5d02-bd78-d2b943f518e6', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bed234a-9875-5d02-bd78-d2b943f518e6'}, {'abstract': 'The 35 Atlanta public school employees charged in a testing scandal have been released from jail and are awaiting their first appearance in court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/education/georgia-defendants-in-cheating-scandal-released.html', 'snippet': 'The 35 Atlanta public school employees charged in a testing scandal have been released from jail and are awaiting their first appearance in court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 35 Atlanta public school employees charged in a testing scandal have been released from jail and are awaiting their first appearance in court. They are accused of running a conspiracy in which they changed students’ answers on standardized tests in order to be paid performance bonuses. By Wednesday evening, a day after they were ordered to surrender at the Fulton County Jail, all the defendants had posted bond and been released. Defense lawyers said they are asking the district attorney, Paul L. Howard Jr., to hold trials before multiple juries. They said there is no courtroom in the county large enough to accommodate 35 defendants, lawyers and family members. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Defendants in Cheating Scandal Released', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Defendants In Cheating Scandal Released', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Robbie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T00:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/96a91353-e177-5c68-9172-6f5a48dd56fa', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96a91353-e177-5c68-9172-6f5a48dd56fa'}, {'abstract': 'The Archbishop of Milwaukee, Jerome E. Listeki, announced on Wednesday that he has authorized the release of thousands of pages of documents on sexual abuse by Catholic priests, including cases that date back 80 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/us/wisconsin-church-will-release-files-on-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'The Archbishop of Milwaukee, Jerome E. Listeki, announced on Wednesday that he has authorized the release of thousands of pages of documents on sexual abuse by Catholic priests, including cases that date back 80 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Archbishop of Milwaukee, Jerome E. Listeki, announced on Wednesday that he has authorized the release of thousands of pages of documents on sexual abuse by Catholic priests, including cases that date back 80 years. His announcement came one day before a judge was scheduled to hear a motion from abuse victims asking for the documents to be released. \xa0The files, which will be posted on the archdiocesan Web site by July 1, include the legal depositions of former Archbishop Rembert Weakland and Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan, now the archbishop of New York. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin: Church Will Release Files on Abuse', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wisconsin: Church Will Release Files On Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, Timothy M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weakland, Rembert', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T00:28:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd39b000-111d-5fc3-929e-f4f759205b2c', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd39b000-111d-5fc3-929e-f4f759205b2c'}, {'abstract': 'A conversation that cannot have lasted more than 10 minutes changed the way I thought about my life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/opinion/my-dinner-with-martin-luther-king-jr.html', 'snippet': 'A conversation that cannot have lasted more than 10 minutes changed the way I thought about my life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORTY-FIVE years ago, the Rev. Dr. and Mrs. Martin Luther King Jr. went to a small dinner party in Atlanta, not far from the campus of Emory University. It was a quiet January night in 1968. I was one of the guests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Dinner With Dr. King', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Dinner With Dr. King', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T00:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Hood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a58a854e-5de4-5c51-a21b-55e6e18802fe', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a58a854e-5de4-5c51-a21b-55e6e18802fe'}, {'abstract': 'With only months to go in his last presidential term, Mahmoud Ahmadinejad has surprised many of his critics by challenging a coalition of traditionalists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/world/middleeast/ahmadinejad-of-iran-reshapes-image-ahead-of-june-vote.html', 'snippet': 'With only months to go in his last presidential term, Mahmoud Ahmadinejad has surprised many of his critics by challenging a coalition of traditionalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — PresidentMahmoud Ahmadinejad is not going quietly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/IRAN/IRAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/04/world/IRAN/IRAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/IRAN/IRAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/IRAN/IRAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/IRAN/IRAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/04/world/IRAN/IRAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/IRAN/IRAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legac