 {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/407c4d32-971b-51d1-a86b-cf4d5dcbcd74', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/407c4d32-971b-51d1-a86b-cf4d5dcbcd74'}, {'abstract': 'A Greek court on Wednesday handed down 50-year prison sentences to three leading members of the guerrilla group Revolutionary Struggle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/world/europe/greece-court-sentences-guerrillas.html', 'snippet': 'A Greek court on Wednesday handed down 50-year prison sentences to three leading members of the guerrilla group Revolutionary Struggle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Greek court on Wednesday handed down 50-year prison sentences to three leading members of the guerrilla group Revolutionary Struggle, which is best known for firing a rocket-propelled grenade at the United States Embassy in Athens in January 2007, and imposed shorter terms on two others suspected of being members. The verdict was issued in absentia for the organization’s self-professed leader, Nikos Maziotis, and his partner Panagiota Roupa, who have been on the run since last June when they were released from prison after completing the maximum permitted period of 18 months in pretrial custody. The third person sentenced was Costas Gournas. The group has claimed responsibility for a string of bombings and shootings targeting the police and others between 2003 and 2010, causing some injuries but no deaths. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: Court Sentences Guerrillas', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: Court Sentences Guerrillas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, 