/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:30 A.M. (Flix) THE APOSTLE (1997) Robert Duvall, above, wrote, directed and stars in this movie about Sonny Dewey, an evangelical preacher who trades in his church and his cheating wife (Farrah Fawcett) for life on the lam in the rural South. The supporting cast includes Miranda Richardson as the married focus of Sonny’s charm; Billy Bob Thornton as a racist who proves that Sonny can achieve almost anything through his words; and a singing June Carter Cash, as Sonny’s mother. Mr. Duvall received an Oscar nomination for best actor for his portrayal of Sonny in what Janet Maslin, writing in The New York Times, called a “lovely, heartfelt film.” She added, “The actors are first rate, but much screen time in ‘The Apostle’ is given to nonactors who give the film a sweetly believable tone and fill its churchgoing scenes with blazing heart and soul.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T05:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/220f825a-20a6-5d9d-a815-6d6ffb4f13db', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/220f825a-20a6-5d9d-a815-6d6ffb4f13db'}, {'abstract': 'As some in Hong Kong deal with growing dissatisfaction over the city’s restrictive political arrangements under China, others are planning for a more aggressive Occupy movement to push for full democracy by 2017.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/occupy-hong-kong-for-universal-suffrage/', 'snippet': 'As some in Hong Kong deal with growing dissatisfaction over the city’s restrictive political arrangements under China, others are planning for a more aggressive Occupy movement to push for full democracy by 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A civil disobedience movement to push for democratic elections of Hong Kong’s leader in 2017 was launched last week, dubbed the “Let Love and Peace Occupy Central” movement. (Central is the core downtown district of Hong Kong.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/asia/04Occupy2RDV/04Occupy2RDV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/04/world/asia/04Occupy2RDV/04Occupy2RDV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/asia/04Occupy2RDV/04Occupy2RDV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/asia/04Occupy2RDV/04Occupy2RDV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1320, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/world/asia/04Occupy2RDV/04Occupy2RDV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/04/world/asia/04Occupy2RDV/04Occupy2RDV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credi