 gritty realism under the name Iain Banks, and visionary science fiction as Iain M Banks. The latter are just amazing — try starting with Use of Weapons, but every one of the Culture novels is a gem, and it’s terribly sad to think that there will be no more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iain Banks Is Dying', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T11:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5f634f1-a00b-5d57-ac7c-640ccac92ddf', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5f634f1-a00b-5d57-ac7c-640ccac92ddf'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook is expected to introduce a Facebook-centric phone on Thursday that is intended to help increase its profit overseas.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/the-arrival-of-facebooks-phone/', 'snippet': 'Facebook is expected to introduce a Facebook-centric phone on Thursday that is intended to help increase its profit overseas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook is expected to introduce a Facebook-centric phone on Thursday that is intended to help increase its profit overseas, Somini Sengupta writes in Thursday’s New York Times. Read more. »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Arrival of Facebook’s Phone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T11:13:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5eec5ab-79f9-5291-91f3-aa9b43919e33', 'word_count': 30, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5eec5ab-79f9-5291-91f3-aa9b43919e33'}, {'abstract': 'Japan’s central bank said that it would aggressively buy bonds, doubling the amount of money in circulation over two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/business/global/japan-initiates-a-bold-bid-to-end-years-of-falling-prices.html', 'snippet': 'Japan’s central bank said that it would aggressively buy bonds, doubling the amount of money in circulation over two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Haruhiko Kuroda, the new governor of the Bank of Japan, delivered on his promise to drastically change Japan’s economic policy to end a long, debilitating era of deflation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Initiates Bold Bid to End Years of Tumbling Prices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Tries New Tactics To Revive Its Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuroda, Haruhiko', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deflation (Economics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T11:29:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/498da53e-5ef9-5f18-9a49-ed80349c8e85', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/498da53e-5ef9-5f18-9a49-ed80349c8e85'}, {'abstract': 'Now that the free preview edition of Microsoft’s Windows 8 has expired, it is time to upgrade to the final version or reinstall a previous version of Windows.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/qa-moving-on-from-the-windows-8-preview/', 'snippet': 'Now that the free preview edition of Microsoft’s Windows 8 has expired, it is time to upgrade to the final version or reinstall a previous version of Windows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Moving On From the Windows 8 Preview', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows (Operating System)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T11:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ad44726-a95a-541f-a141-c4a97b55f3ab', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ad44726-a95a-541f-a141-c4a97b55f3ab'}, {'abstract': 'With a hit FX series, an HBO special and Woody Allen and David O. Russell movies in the pipeline, the comedian’s moment grows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/arts/for-louis-c-k-the-jokes-on-him.html', 'snippet': 'With a hit FX series, an HBO special and Woody Allen and David O. Russell movies in the pipeline, the comedian’s moment grows.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I don’t necessarily agree with you, but I appreciate it very much,” Louis C. K. says to an applauding crowd at the start of his new stand-up special, “Oh My God.” It’s a quintessential act of belittling himself — a refusal to believe that he deserves the gratitude of the hundreds of fans surrounding him at the Celebrity Theater in Phoenix and the thousands more who will see this comedy special when it makes its HBO debut next Saturday. It’s emblematic of the defeatist charm of Louis C. K., who at 45 finds himself a performer of the moment whose moment keeps getting bigger and bigger. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN/07LOUIS-CK-SPAN-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joke’s on Louis C.K.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Joke’s on Him', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T12:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b2c507a-c4d4-5f77-8227-238a128f794a', 'word_count': 2366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b2c507a-c4d4-5f77-8227-238a128f794a'}, {'abstract': 'Colm Toibin describes how he tried to recognize the humanity as well as the exalted status of Jesus’ mother in his play “The Testament of Mary.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/theater/colm-toibin-on-the-genesis-of-his-testament-of-mary.html', 'snippet': 'Colm Toibin describes how he tried to recognize the humanity as well as the exalted status of Jesus’ mother in his play “The Testament of Mary.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every night from as early as I can remember the family knelt in the evening and said the rosary. Each mystery, as they were called, had 10 Hail Marys; the first part of each Hail Mary was recited by a single voice, and then the second part — “Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of our death. Amen” — by the rest of the family in unison. At the end my mother would recite some extra prayers, including the “Memorare,” which began, “Remember, O most gracious Virgin Mary, that never was it known that anyone who sought thy aid or implored thy intercession was left unaided.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07TOIBIN2_SPAN/07TOIBIN2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07TOIBIN2_SPAN/07TOIBIN2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07TOIBIN2_SPAN/07TOIBIN2_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07TOIBIN2_SPAN/07TOIBIN2_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07TOIBIN2_SPAN/07TOIBIN2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07TOIBIN2_SPAN/07TOIBIN2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/arts/07TOIBIN2_SPAN/07TOIBIN2_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Lady of the Fragile Humanity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Lady of the Fragile Humanity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'v