yprus or any other country might give up the euro or be better off if it did.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.C.B. Chief Says Cyprus Shows Commitment to Euro', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Central Banker Dismisses Any Move to Drop Euro', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draghi, Mario', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T12:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy and Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1e35992-f98b-52a4-998d-a20a3786aa6f', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1e35992-f98b-52a4-998d-a20a3786aa6f'}, {'abstract': 'While the public’s increase in support for same-sex marriage has been exceptionally linear and steady, the number of senators endorsing it has increased at exponential rates. Can this be explained in a mathematical model?', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/explaining-the-senates-surge-in-support-for-same-sex-marriage/', 'snippet': 'While the public’s increase in support for same-sex marriage has been exceptionally linear and steady, the number of senators endorsing it has increased at exponential rates. Can this be explained in a mathematical model?', 'lead_paragraph': 'So many senators are declaring their support for same-sex marriage that I’ve regularly had to check my Twitter feed while working on this article, lest I miss any announcements. As Dylan Matthews of The Washington Post has detailed, 50 senators have now stated their backing for same-sex marriage, up from only 16 in 2010 and eight in 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Explaining the Senate’s Surge in Support for Same-Sex Marriage', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T12:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cdf35f3-ef9a-5c44-bac4-64f8adf694d7', 'word_count': 2146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cdf35f3-ef9a-5c44-bac4-64f8adf694d7'}, {'abstract': 'It has been a controversial European tour for Justin Bieber, the Canadian superstar singer. Is there something new about the youth culture phenomenon he represents, or was it al