ame': 'persons', 'value': 'Irwin, Neil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Mervyn A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trichet, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T14:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0319f6a3-5590-5139-8be0-f1ed09afd366', 'word_count': 1550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0319f6a3-5590-5139-8be0-f1ed09afd366'}, {'abstract': 'Whether you’re downing fish tacos and craft beers or getting your hair blown back by a roller coaster, you’ll find that San Diego delivers more than sunny vibes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/travel/36-hours-in-san-diego.html', 'snippet': 'Whether you’re downing fish tacos and craft beers or getting your hair blown back by a roller coaster, you’ll find that San Diego delivers more than sunny vibes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like its urban rival Los Angeles, San Diego is not so much a city as a loose collection of overlapping (and sometimes colliding) communities bound by arterial, life-giving freeways: it’s a military town in Coronado; a surf town in funky, eclectic Ocean Beach; and a border town in the historic Mexican-American neighborhood of Barrio Logan. If San Diego has a cohesive identity at all, it’s a shared embrace of an easy, breezy Southern California casualness. With its lack of pretension, the city is often seen by outsiders as a kind of Pleasantville — a bland, happy place with an exceptional amount of sunshine. Depending on how deep you look, that may be all you see. But there are, after all, worse things than Spanish tiles, palm trees, tropical blooms, year-round flip-flops, fresh fish tacos and bonfires on the beach.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/travel/07HOURS_SPAN-sf/07-HOURS-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 524, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/travel/07HOURS_SPAN-sf/07-HOURS-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 524}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/travel/07HOURS_SPAN-sf/07-HOURS-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/travel/07HOURS_SPAN-sf/07-HOURS-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1788, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/travel/07HOURS_SPAN-sf/07HOURS_SPAN-sf-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/travel/07HOURS_SPAN-sf/07HOURS_SPAN-sf-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cred