ce situation at Rutgers, there is some recognition, even in the coaching ranks, that fiery motivation can lead to personal attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago Mike Rice sat in Terry Henderson’s living room and asked him to entrust his son to the basketball program at Rutgers. At the time, Terry Jr. was a talented player at Neuse Christian Academy in Raleigh, N.C., with scholarship options, and his father was trying to decide which college coach would get “the keys to my son.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/ncaabasketball/05coach-pic2/05coach-pic2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/ncaabasketball/05coach-pic2/05coach-pic2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/ncaabasketball/05coach-pic2/05coach-pic2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/ncaabasketball/05coach-pic2/05coach-pic2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1414, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/ncaabasketball/05coach-pic2/05coach-pic2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/ncaabasketball/05coach-pic2/05coach-pic2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N