 to change? If you’re Portuguese, you do resistance art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LISBON — “O Povo É Quem Mais Ordena” (“It’s the People Who Call the Shots”) read the banner a middle-aged protester unfurled in a plaza in the upscale commercial neighborhood of Chiado. Under the present circumstances, she told me wistfully, “There’s almost a utopian ring to it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If You Can’t Fix It, Art It', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lisbon (Portugal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T15:49:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/557ad5c1-927a-5617-a22a-c87bfa57e142', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/557ad5c1-927a-5617-a22a-c87bfa57e142'}, {'abstract': 'In food photography, you dress your plates the way you would dress yourself.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/props-help-tell-the-story-of-food/', 'snippet': 'In food photography, you dress your plates the way you would dress yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Scrivani (@AndrewScrivani on Twitter and Instagram) is a freelance photographer and a regular contributor to The New York Times. He writes the blog making SundaySauce.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Props Help Tell the Story of Food', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T16:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Scrivani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scrivani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2554fb1c-0e38-5bcc-8108-cd029ad32268', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2554fb1c-0e38-5bcc-8108-cd029ad32268'}, {'abstract': 'In the last article of the series, a reflection on childhood visits to New York.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/this-city-that-i-love/', 'snippet': 'In the last article of the series, a reflection on childhood visits to New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My father used to talk about the alligators in New York City’s sewage tunnels. He would talk about them full of certainty. They were there as certainly as there were bums in Grand Central. That was his New York: kind of fantastical, kind of dangerous. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This City That I Love', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This City That I Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T16:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandy Soohoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soohoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6161af7b-c72d-5f53-a7de-dfd40ad377a6', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6161af7b-c72d-5f53-a7de-dfd40ad377a6'}, {'abstract': 'Barbra Streisand’s vast underground display of collectibles makes a delicious target for satire in Jonathan Tolins’s “Buyer & Cellar,” a one-man show starring Michael Urie.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/theater/reviews/buyer-cellar-with-michael-urie-at-rattlestick.html', 'snippet': 'Barbra Streisand’s vast underground display of collectibles makes a delicious target for satire in Jonathan Tolins’s “Buyer & Cellar,” a one-man show starring Michael Urie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the dawn of time — well O.K., since the mid-’60s — gay men have been fiercely divided into love-her or hate-her camps by their feelings for Barbra Streisand. The intensity of those relationships is perhaps equaled by the subject’s self-regard, at least based on the evidence of her hilariously unnecessary 2010 coffee-table book, “My Passion for Design.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Underground Passion for a Star’s Stuff ', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Underground Passion for a Star’s Stuff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rooney, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rattlestick Playwrights Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urie, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Buyer & Cellar (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolins, Jonathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brackett, Stephen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T16:01:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4035266-98d2-5524-bb5a-ee8a3c76aaad', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4035266-98d2-5524-bb5a-ee8a3c76aaad'}, {'abstract': 'With Vodafone valued at nearly $50 billion below the breakup value of its assets, the potential for a huge payoff for its shareholders in the form of an acquisition is mouth-watering, the authors say.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/unlocking-vodafones-value/', 'snippet': 'With Vodafone valued at nearly $50 billion below the breakup value of its assets, the potential for a huge payoff for its shareholders in the form of an acquisition is mouth-watering, the authors say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deal prospects make Vodafone look cheap. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unlocking Vodafone’s Value', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T16:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Webb and Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ffe94d0-3099-50cd-a30f-a42d7ed7faf5', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ffe94d0-3099-50cd-a30f-a42d7ed7faf5'}, {'abstract': 'A longtime political leader describes what went wrong with the American effort in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/the-road-to-failure-in-iraq/', 'snippet': 'A longtime political leader describes what went wrong with the American effort in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adnan Pachachi is a Sunni Arab political leader who has long played a prominent role in Iraq — as a foreign minister before Saddam Hussein’s rule, as a president of the Iraqi Governing Council set up by the West after Hussein’s ouster, and as a leading figure in the secular Iraqiya coalition. Ten years after the invasion, he wrote to At War to give his perspective on the miscalculations of the war. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Road to Failure in Iraq', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussein, Saddam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T16:15:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adnan Pachachi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adnan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pachachi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc50765a-9503-575e-8d1c-d7e312bf8f62', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc50765a-9503-575e-8d1c-d7e312bf8f62'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama laid bare the political dilemma he faced on environmental issues, including the fate of the controversial Keystone XL pipeline from Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/us/politics/obama-donors-keystone-pipeline.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama laid bare the political dilemma he faced on environmental issues, including the fate of the controversial Keystone XL pipeline from Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Appearing at the home of an outspoken critic of the Keystone XL pipeline, President Obama on Wednesday night told a group of high-dollar donors that the politics of the environment “are tough.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/us/0405OBAMA/0405OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/us/0405OBAMA/0405OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/us/0405OBAMA/0405OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/us/0405OBAMA/0405OBAMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1225, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/us/0