/04/04/bridgestone-investing-in-potential-north-american-source-for-rubber/', 'snippet': 'Bridgestone is investing millions of dollars to determine if a plant that is native to the North American desert might provide a new source of rubber..', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Bill Niaura jokes that his title is director of new business development because his employer, Bridgestone Americas, does not include “guayule farmer” among its corporate job descriptions. Nonetheless, the company is investing millions of dollars to determine if a plant that is native to the North American desert may provide a new source of the natural rubber needed for tires.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bridgestone Investing in Potential North American Source for Rubber', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BRIDGESTONE Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T16:29:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edsall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/750d6ae1-9628-58fe-b16e-db60f361e665', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/750d6ae1-9628-58fe-b16e-db60f361e665'}, {'abstract': 'Apple has been introducing new versions of its products for so long that it’s a question of which month, not whether, it will introduce new iPads and iPhones. Best Buy on Wednesday took its best guess that the latest iPads are coming soon from Apple by slas