ial intelligence to assess student papers and short written answers, freeing instructors for other tasks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/science/new-test-for-computers-grading-essays-at-college-level.html', 'snippet': 'A system developed by a joint venture between Harvard and M.I.T. uses artificial intelligence to assess student papers and short written answers, freeing instructors for other tasks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine taking a college exam, and, instead of handing in a blue book and getting a grade from a professor a few weeks later, clicking the “send” button when you are done and receiving a grade back instantly, your essay scored by a software program.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/science/05edx/05edx-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/science/05edx/05edx-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/science/05edx/05edx-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/science/05edx/05edx-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/science/05edx/05edx-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/science/05edx/05edx-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/science/05edx/05edx-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Essay-Grading Software Offers Professors a Break', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Software Seen Giving Grades On Essay Tests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EdX', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markoff, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T16:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bf947ac-3085-5452-ae4d-f2b049bccae5', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bf947ac-3085-5452-ae4d-f2b049bccae5'}, {'abstract': 'Filippo Grandi, head of the United Nations Relief and Works Agency, predicted that by the end of 2013, the flow of refugees would swamp humanitarian resources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/world/middleeast/syrias-refugees-overwhelming-relief-efforts-and-host-countries-un-official-says.html', 'snippet': 'Filippo Grandi, head of the United Nations Relief and Works Agency, predicted that by the end of 2013, the flow of refugees would swamp humanitarian resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The head of a United Nations refugee agency said Thursday that refugees from Syria’s war were on the verge of overwhelming the United Nations and the countries bordering Syria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria’s Refugees Overwhelming Relief Efforts and Host Countries, U.N. Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T17:05:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thanassis Cambanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thanassis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cambanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/773ab51a-cdb5-5f64-aca6-1a504f93efab', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/773ab51a-cdb5-5f64-aca6-1a504f93efab'}, {'abstract': 'A thoughtless act profoundly alters a community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/books/review/fellow-mortals-by-dennis-mahoney.html', 'snippet': 'A thoughtless act profoundly alters a community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When middle-aged Henry Cooper is only a few months into his new route as a postal carrier on Arcadia Street, he lights a cigar, tosses the match into the bushes and causes a fire that kills a young wife, fells several houses and sets in motion the events of Dennis Mahoney’s moving first novel, “Fellow Mortals.” Beginning after the disaster and circling back to it, Mahoney shifts among multiple perspectives to examine the fire’s effect on the people whose lives it sears. We meet two elderly sisters who, left homeless by the fire, move in with Henry and his wife. We meet a sculptor, the widower of the woman who died, who buys 30 acres and retreats to the woods. We meet Billy, a man wrecked even before the fire, and his abused wife, and a brittle, frightened real estate agent who repels apologies and refuses to absolve Henry.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/0407-Graver/0407-Graver-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/0407-Graver/0407-Graver-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/0407-Graver/0407-Graver-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/0407-Graver/0407-Graver-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/