k': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T18:43:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peggy Post', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peggy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Post', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff936d9-384a-5b41-922e-51ef1005e87c', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff936d9-384a-5b41-922e-51ef1005e87c'}, {'abstract': 'Studies of selective colleges — which have more resources and higher graduation rates than others — are often based on 200 to 250 institutions based on categories chosen by Barron’s.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/what-makes-a-college-selective-and-why-it-matters/', 'snippet': 'Studies of selective colleges — which have more resources and higher graduation rates than others — are often based on 200 to 250 institutions based on categories chosen by Barron’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When researchers study selective colleges, they often use a group of 200 to 250 colleges, based on categories chosen by Barron’s, which publishes a popular college guide. I have cited such research in several recent articles and wanted to provide the list of those colleges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Makes a College ‘Selective’ — and Why It Matters', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Barron's (Newspaper)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T18:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e6c150-cd04-5113-9576-871773fbdbd7', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e6c150-cd04-5113-9576-871773fbdbd7'}, {'abstract': 'The Plain Dealer, owned by Advance Publications, will trim home delivery to three days a week and lay off 53 newsroom employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/business/media/cleveland-paper-to-curtail-delivery-and-cut-staff.html', 'snippet': 'The Plain Dealer, owned by Advance Publications, will trim home delivery to three days a week and lay off 53 newsroom employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Plain Dealer in Cleveland, whose reporters organized one of the industry’s most active opposition movements against its parent company’s plans for cutbacks, will trim home delivery to three days a week and create a new digital company, the owner, Advance Publications, said on Thursday. The paper is also expected to cut more than a third of its newsroom staff.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleveland Paper to Trim Delivery and Cut Staff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cleveland Paper to Trim Delivery and Cut Staff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haughney, Christine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Plain Dealer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T18:51:59+0000', 'document_type'