th the Dining section. We’ll publish a few standout recipes from a new cookbook for you to try. The next week, the book’s author will join Julia Moskin and readers in a live video chat. This month’s book is Deborah Madison’s “Vegetable Literacy.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking Asparagus and an Onion Tart With Deborah Madison', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Onion Tart From the Queen of Greens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T19:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b8001d6-4546-52fc-bc06-8394951d5aee', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b8001d6-4546-52fc-bc06-8394951d5aee'}, {'abstract': 'The slow pace of the game that some  younger viewers find off- putting may be the very thing that keeps older fans hooked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/booming/why-do-boomers-love-baseball.html', 'snippet': 'The slow pace of the game that some  younger viewers find off- putting may be the very thing that keeps older fans hooked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you think about, is one stretch really enough? And why must we wait until the seventh inning? These aging bones and muscles could use a break — to say nothing about these bladders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/04/booming/04question-booming-baseball/04question-booming-baseball-articleLarge-v3.jpg', '