oach takes a rollicking and ruminative journey through the digestive tract, with side trips to meet its bodily cousins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We should have seen this coming. When Mary Roach wrote “Packing for Mars,” her 2010 book about the bodily experiences of astronauts in space, she seemed especially excited by the feeding, digestive and excremental issues with which NASA had to deal. She has now advanced from the exoticism of space-shuttle toilet training to the universality of the digestive tract. And at last Ms. Roach has a subject that doesn’t make her (insert constipation joke, possibly about Elvis Presley) strain. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/04BOOKROACH_SPAN/04BOOKROACH_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/04BOOKROACH_SPAN/04BOOKROACH_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/04BOOKROACH_SPAN/04BOOKROACH_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/04BOOKROACH_SPAN/04BOOKROACH_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1092, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/04BOOKROACH_SPAN/04BOOKROACH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/04BOOKROACH_SPAN/04BOOKROACH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/04BOOKROACH_SPAN/04BOOKROACH_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Food and You, From One End to the Other', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food and You, From One End to the Other', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roach, Mary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T20:38:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9834a068-e4dc-5220-b025-33eeccb1f41e', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9834a068-e4dc-5220-b025-33eeccb1f41e'}, {'abstract': 'Mexico’s growth prospects are attracting investment banks and investors hunting for ways to gain greater exposure to international markets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/after-stagnation-a-revival-for-mexicos-financial-sector/', 'snippet': 'Mexico’s growth prospects are attracting investment banks and investors hunting for ways to gain greater exposure to international markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — When Banco Santander held the $4.13 billion public stock offering of its Mexico subsidiary here last September, a mariachi band and Mexican folk dancers set the festive mood for a media breakfast in a sun-filled dining room atop the stock exchange’s skyscraper.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Stagnation, a Revival for Mexico’s Financial Sector', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Stagnation, a Revival for Mexico’s Financial Sector', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena Nieto, Enrique', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T20:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f29ee08-6f4a-59dd-9b85-c1745a79a7de', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f29ee08-6f4a-59dd-9b85-c1745a79a7de'}, {'abstract': 'In “Upstream Color,” a man and a woman find each other as part of a plot where little is straightforward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/movies/upstream-color-directed-by-shane-carruth.html', 'snippet': 'In “Upstream Color,” a man and a woman find each other as part of a plot where little is straightforward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shane Carruth’s “Upstream Color,” a deeply sincere, elliptical movie about being and nature, men and women, self and other, worms and pigs, opens with two scenes: Two teenage boys biking around a leafy suburb, and elsewhere, a man harvesting little white worms from orchid root balls. The teenagers slowly tracing circles on the pavement are so attractively framed by the soft, shimmery light and blurred background that they look as if they could have biked out of a Terrence Malick movie. The teenagers join the man, who does nasty things with worms and could be a concerned florist, an experimental entomologist, a budding serial killer or just a run-of-the-mill science-fiction freak.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Worms, a Botanist and Pigs. Sounds Like a Love Story.', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Worms, a Botanist And Pigs. Sounds Like a Love Story.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carruth, Shane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seimetz, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T20:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/38983651-6b8e-59e8-8660-8a7324c71b63', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38983651-6b8e-59e8-8660-8a7324c71b63'}, {'abstract': 'Maimuna Abdi Yussuf, a Somali student at African Leadership Academy in Johannesburg, is "ecstatic" about being accepted to Duke University.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/education/100000002155290/the-envelope-please-maimuna-abdi-yussuf.html', 'snippet': 'Maimuna Abdi Yussuf, a Somali student at African Leadership Academy in Johannesburg, is "ecstatic" about being accepted to Duke University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maimuna Abdi Yussuf, a Somali student at African Leadership Academy in Johannesburg, is "ecstatic" about being accepted to Duke University.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'x