x', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Laskey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/783a5981-d1b0-5544-adc1-0a49ac236c57', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/783a5981-d1b0-5544-adc1-0a49ac236c57'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Friday, selections include speculation about Sheryl Sandberg leaving Facebook and where she might go, a Web site that may have been one of the Facebook chief’s early efforts and investors giving Zynga a vote of confidence when it starts hosting online gambling in Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/todays-scuttlebot-not-so-private-messages-and-facebooks-new-phone/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Friday, selections include speculation about Sheryl Sandberg leaving Facebook and where she might go, a Web site that may have been one ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Not-So-Private Messages, and Facebook’s New Phone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T20:52:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3ec0cf3-d5bb-5069-9775-5114cc1a1bf8', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3ec0cf3-d5bb-5069-9775-5114cc1a1bf8'}, {'abstract': 'While in Scotland, the duchess celebrates tradition in a tartan coat.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/look-of-the-moment-catherine-the-duchess-of-cambridge-3/', 'snippet': 'While in Scotland, the duchess celebrates tradition in a tartan coat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Girl: The royal visits the Donald Dewar Leisure Center in Glasgow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of the Moment | Catherine, the Duchess of Cambridge', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T20:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40a1d763-dc42-5c06-a1cc-04383b275e16', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40a1d763-dc42-5c06-a1cc-04383b275e16'}, {'abstract': 'In “Between Man and Beast,” Monte Reel tells the story of the 19th-century explorer Paul Du Chaillu, who returned from Africa with evidence that a creature of myth — the gorilla — actually existed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/books/review/between-man-and-beast-by-monte-reel.html', 'snippet': 'In “Between Man and Beast,” Monte Reel tells the story of the 19th-century explorer Paul Du Chaillu, who returned from Africa with evidence that a creature of myth — the gorilla — actually existed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our planet nowadays is a well-explored place, where major zoological discoveries are exceedingly rare. True, there are countless kinds of insects and other tiny fauna still undescribed and unnamed in the Amazon and elsewhere; but a new large-bodied animal, a new vertebrate, comes to light seldom. If a previously unknown species of monkey is found (as the lesula was, in the eastern Congo basin, in 2007), the revelation makes news, even if the creature doesn’t happen to have (as the lesula does) a very long nose, a blue tush and the wide, dreamy eyes of Gene Wilder. So it’s hard for us to imagine how sensibilities were affected, in Europe and America, just two and three centuries ago, by the discovery of certain prodigious, unexpected beasts.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/07COVER/07COVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/07COVER/07COVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/07COVER/07COVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/07COVER/07COVER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1301, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/07COVER/07COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/07COVER/07COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/books/review/07COVER/07COVER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Planet of the Ape', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Planet of the Ape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quammen, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reel, Monte', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T20:56:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Quammen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quammen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/923a3634-88d8-513c-abed-25d7704b934c', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/923a3634-88d8-513c-abed-25d7704b934c'}, {'abstract': 'Supporters of a soccer team in the German city of Hamburg unfurled banners against homophobia at the start of a match this week.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/04/german-soccer-fans-fight-homophobia/', 'snippet': 'Supporters of a soccer team in the German city of Hamburg unfurled banners against homophobia at the start of a match this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the terraces of European soccer stadiums are well-known bastions of xenophobia, racism and even fascist salutes, supporters of a team in Hamburg, Germany, displayed a very different sort of politics this week, unfurling banners against homophobia at the start of a match.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'German Soccer Fans Fight Homophobia', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamburg (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-04T20:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccd2480d-3f49-5651-8393-dce64e7b2213', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccd2480d-3f49-5651-8393-dce64e7b2213'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Charles E. Schumer is not only an envoy to the White House but also the Democratic majority’s most important bipartisan bridge builder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/us/politics/schumer-reaches-across