 tent behind the ninth hole at Mission Hills Country Club on Thursday, one spectator turned to another and said, “Isn’t she the one that’s the youngest player?” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/lpga/lpga-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/lpga/lpga-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/lpga/lpga-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/lpga/lpga-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/lpga/lpga-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/lpga/lpga-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/lpga/lpga-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wie, Now a Veteran at 23, Learns to Shrug Off Her Critics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wie, Now a Veteran at 23, Learns to Shrug Off Her Critics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wie, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ko, Lydia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T01:40:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b1d74bb-42eb-5dc6-985f-1fb3daa741cd', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b1d74bb-42eb-5dc6-985f-1fb3daa741cd'}, {'abstract': 'There is plenty of blame to go around for the neurological damage caused by toxic fumes at Royale Comfort Seating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/opinion/saving-money-poisoning-workers-in-taylorsville-nc.html', 'snippet': 'There is plenty of blame to go around for the neurological damage caused by toxic fumes at Royale Comfort Seating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The workers at Royale Comfort Seating in Taylorsville, N.C., had a simple but grueling job. For 10 hours at a stretch they spray-glued pieces of polyurethane foam into shapes that became the spongy filling of cushions sold to many top furniture brands. Unfortunately, the glue contained a dangerous chemical known as n-propyl bromide, or nPB, and the spray guns left a yellowish fog in the air that coated everything in sight. Exposure to the toxic fumes left some workers so dizzy at the end of the day that they walked as if drunk.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Money, Poisoning Workers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving Money, Poisoning Workers ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royale Comfort Seating Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'n-Propyl Bromide (nPB)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupational Safety and Health Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T01:41:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e399e8e2-ae4a-59e7-a62b-ad201942ed0c', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e399e8e2-ae4a-59e7-a62b-ad201942ed0c'}, {'abstract': 'The family of Michael Jackson is suing Anschutz Entertainment Group for wrongful death, claiming it hired the doctor who administered the drugs that led to his death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/business/media/jury-selection-continues-in-trial-on-jacksons-death.html', 'snippet': 'The family of Michael Jackson is suing Anschutz Entertainment Group for wrongful death, claiming it hired the doctor who administered the drugs that led to his death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A global corporation accused of pushing a beloved entertainer to his death. A family whose internal squabbles have been tabloid catnip for decades. A courtroom crowded with lawyers, but off limits to television cameras.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/business/Jackson/Jackson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'arti