 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Generic Brands and Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court of India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T01:44:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/74ccb844-1612-5715-97e1-bee714f1ba22', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74ccb844-1612-5715-97e1-bee714f1ba22'}, {'abstract': 'Alexandra McGuinness’s “Lotus Eaters” are pretty, rich and aimless, but they sure have nice digs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/movies/lotus-eaters-directed-by-alexandra-mcguinness.html', 'snippet': 'Alexandra McGuinness’s “Lotus Eaters” are pretty, rich and aimless, but they sure have nice digs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pity the\xa0young, affluent and tragically beautiful, if we are to believe\xa0 “Lotus Eaters.” The film, from Alexandra McGuinness, throws you into a hazy nonstop Saturnalia in elegant British surroundings as decadent 20-somethings drink, smoke, copulate, dress up, take drugs and flail with their aspirations and arbitrary passions. Its heroine, Alice (Antonia Campbell-Hughes), wants to leave modeling to be an actress; her ex-boyfriend, Charlie (Johnny Flynn), is giving rehab another shot; Marlon (Alex Wyndham) chases Alice; Suzie (Amber Anderson) frets that she is losing Felix (Benn Northover) to Alice; the somewhat older Orna (a good Cynthia Fortune Ryan) pursues Felix while manipulating Alice; and the hapless Benedict (Liam Browne) is just trying to bed whomever he can.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_LOTUS_