bType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_BERT_SPAN/05RDP_BERT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_BERT_SPAN/05RDP_BERT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_BERT_SPAN/05RDP_BERT_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Photographer Is Uneasy in Front of the Camera', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bert Stern:\r\nOriginal Mad Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, Bert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T02:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/86ae50a2-cdc7-582e-94d5-9adedb4800c6', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86ae50a2-cdc7-582e-94d5-9adedb4800c6'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ Andy Pettitte went eight strong innings, scattering eight hits while allowing one run, and Mariano Rivera, in his first appearance of the year, got the save.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/sports/baseball/andy-pettitte-and-mariano-rivera-lift-yankees-over-red-sox.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ Andy Pettitte went eight strong innings, scattering eight hits while allowing one run, and Mariano Rivera, in his first appearance of the year, got the save.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Girardi is not the type of manager who goes around giving fire-and-brimstone speeches to his players, or to members of the news media. The Girardi way is to be steady to the point of being dispassionate, never too high and never too low. In the Yankees’ black-and-white pinstripe world, Girardi is a muted shade of gray.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 537}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1834, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Like Old Times, It’s Pettitte, Rivera, Victory', 'kicker': 'Yankees 4, Red Sox 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Just Like Old Times, It’s Pettitte, Rivera, Victory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T02:39:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45a4286-efd7-5b61-93b9-1cfce5e08507', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45a4286-efd7-5b61-93b9-1cfce5e08507'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Story of Luke” a high-functioning autistic man faces enormous changes to his sheltered life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/movies/the-story-of-luke-by-alonso-mayo.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Story of Luke” a high-functioning autistic man faces enormous changes to his sheltered life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Movies about autism have come a long way since Dustin Hoffman created a sensation in “Rain Man,” playing a savant whose astounding mathematical skills made him a threat to Las Vegas casinos. Whatever its other merits, “The Story of Luke,” a slice-of-life tale of a high-functioning autistic man-child faced with enormous changes to his sheltered existence, explains early on that, no, Luke (Lou Taylor Pucci) does not have any special powers. He’s just like any 20-something trying to find his footing, only more so. (He can, however, make pancakes and 23 other meals he’s learned by watching his favorite cooking show.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_STORY_SPAN/STORY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_STORY_SPAN/STORY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_STORY_SPAN/STORY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_STORY_SPAN/STORY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1081, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_STORY_SPAN/STORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_STORY_SPAN/STORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_STORY_SPAN/STORY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Man’s Wobbly Steps to Independence', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Story of Luke', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pucci, Lou Taylor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayo, Alonso', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T02:44:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/383717a9-c4fe-5823-8abb-1d76cc6f2513', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/383717a9-c4fe-5823-8abb-1d76cc6f2513'}, {'abstract': '“Eddie: The Sleepwalking Carnival,” a horror comedy from Boris Rodriguez, centers on a once-famous artist whose creative fires are stoked by his houseguest’s very strange habits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/movies/eddie-the-sleepwalking-cannibal-from-boris-rodriguez.html', 'snippet': '“Eddie: The Sleepwalking Carnival,” a horror comedy from Boris Rodriguez, centers on a once-famous artist whose creative fires are stoked by his houseguest’s very strange habits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The slaughter begins with a dead deer, but by the time “Eddie: The Sleepwalking Cannibal” skids to a close the body count will have crossed the species line several times over.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_EDDIE_SPAN/05RDP_EDDIE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/05RDP_EDDIE_SPAN/05RDP_EDDIE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'ca