, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spears', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2e11f4f-6e3d-5c3d-9c89-aa033751fd96', 'word_count': 1667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2e11f4f-6e3d-5c3d-9c89-aa033751fd96'}, {'abstract': 'The process behind our cover for the Food & Drink issue.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/making-the-impossible-veggie-burger/', 'snippet': 'The process behind our cover for the Food & Drink issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s cover article by Mark Bittman is about a new crop of restaurant chains selling healthful, vegan or vegetarian versions of traditional fast-food items like burgers and buffalo wings. To convey the idea that these vegetable-based products may be the future of fast food, we decided to make an over-the-top vegan “burger” by squeezing different vegetables inside a multigrain bun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/magazine/03gail1/03gail1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 828, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/03/magazine/03gail1/03gail1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 828}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/magazine/03gail1/03gail1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/magazine/03gail1/03gail1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1254, 'width': 909, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima