il', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/artsspecial/20130406KAFKA-slide-8T19/20130406KAFKA-slide-8T19-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/artsspecial/20130406KAFKA-slide-8T19/20130406KAFKA-slide-8T19-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/arts/artsspecial/20130406KAFKA-slide-8T19/20130406KAFKA-slide-8T19-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Kafka’s Monkey’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Kafka's Monkey (Play)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Kathryn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baryshnikov Arts Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T16:25:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/720b0799-5531-5445-9627-6b2a5550ba49', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/720b0799-5531-5445-9627-6b2a5550ba49'}, {'abstract': 'When my son wet his pants every day at nursery school, the teachers thought I’d lied when I said he was potty trained. He was — he just wasn’t trained to be with anyone but me.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/separation-anxiety/', 'snippet': 'When my son wet his pants every day at nursery school, the teachers thought I’d lied when I said he was potty trained. He was — he just wasn’t trained to be with anyone but me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When babies are born, they lie on their mothers’ breasts, wild heartbeat to wild heartbeat, and start the long introduction that winds itself around to their eventual separation. When my son Jacob was born, I didn’t know that I was ever supposed to put him down. He napped on my chest, and when his eyes opened, they were always greeted by my own. I nursed, rocked and changed his diapers until his eyelids grew heavy again, then I settled him back down on me, rubbing the two-square-inch patch of his tiny back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Separation Anxiety', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T16:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jaime Franchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jaime', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Franchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a65732e-19ae-5b1f-b88d-1a4f8b4517ba', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a65732e-19ae-5b1f-b88d-1a4f8b4517ba'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Sharks, part of the Women’s Football Alliance, begin their season this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/with-little-fanfare-a-womens-team-takes-the-field/', 'snippet': 'The New York Sharks, part of the Women’s Football Alliance, begin their season this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The players on the offensive line, wearing helmets and shoulder pads, were crouched down on the field in Brooklyn. “Green 20! Green 20! 10 hut!’’ shouted the quarterback. The football was handed off to a running back who rushed up the middle before being tackled by several defenders. The whistle blew. Soon practice was over and the team’s coach, Richard Harrigan, offered words of praise, “Good job, ladies, bring it home. Sharks on three. One. Two. Three. Sharks!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/nyregion/05-SHARKS-02/05-SHARKS-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/nyregion/05-SHARKS-02/05-SHARKS-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/nyregion/05-SHARKS-02/05-SHARKS-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/nyregion/05-SHARKS-02/05-SHARKS-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/nyregion/05-SHARKS-02/05-SHARKS-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/nyregion/05-SHARKS-02/05-SHARKS-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/nyregion/05-SHARKS-02/05-SHARKS-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Little Fanfare, a Women’s Team Takes the Field', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'nam