, Jack P (1936-2013)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Bear', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T19:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e53d8a48-38de-5032-94f2-d56d90b9b981', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e53d8a48-38de-5032-94f2-d56d90b9b981'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers share their experiences in working overseas.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/05/financial-lessons-for-american-expatriates/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers share their experiences in working overseas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan, in his Wealth Matters column this week, writes about the tax rules in the United States that can trip up Americans living abroad. The rules have become tougher as the United States tries to find secret overseas accounts. And the rules are also affecting more people as more Americans find job opportunities far from home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Lessons for American Expatriates', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T19:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', '