ndors in the floating market of Amphawa, Thailand, display a recent catch of seafood from their small boats. Amphawa is located about an hour west of Bangkok, in the Samut Songkhram province. The picturesque village is known for canals that feed off the Mae Khlong River, where visitors can dine from the boats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Catch of the Day in Amphawa', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T20:43:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8a52754-a790-5de0-8280-428f2e698e78', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8a52754-a790-5de0-8280-428f2e698e78'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Aviation Administration said Friday that it would halt the closings, part of a $637 million spending reduction at the agency, until June to allow for safety analyses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/06/us/politics/faa-will-delay-closings-of-airport-towers-forced-by-sequestration.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Aviation Administration said Friday that it would halt the closings, part of a $637 million spending reduction at the agency, until June to allow for safety analyses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LEESBURG, Va. — The Federal Aviation Administration said Friday that it would delay closing control towers at 149 airports until June to allow for safety analyses and “to attempt to resolve multiple legal challenges.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/us/FAA/FAA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarg