n-the-bustle/', 'snippet': 'A time-lapse video and behind-the-scenes pictures of our photo shoot of the restaurant’s staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s Food & Drink Issue, you’ll find something you might never otherwise see: nearly 130 employees of Marcus Samuelsson’s Harlem restaurant, Red Rooster, gathered in one place, and standing still. Stephen Wilkes photographed the group around 10 a.m. on a Saturday, and everyone — from the line cooks to the dishwashers to the chef himself — wore their work outfits. You can watch a time-lapse video of the shoot above, and see some behind-the-scenes photos of the day below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Outside the Red Rooster, a Rare Break in the Bustle', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuelsson, Marcus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilkes, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Rooster (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-05T20:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Plucknette', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plucknette', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e986ed9-1f04-570d-ae9d-028793870b12', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e986ed9-1f04-570d-ae9d-028793870b12'}, {'abstract': 'The study of driver workload management is progressing alongside the efforts of the planners who dream up new generations of infotainment features.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/04/07/automobiles/07work-slides.html', 'snippet': 'The study of driver workload management is progressing alongside