eam behind the pioneering Zuppa, just around the corner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On our first visit to Guapo Cocina Mexicana, two of my guests stood outside and peered through the plate-glass window while I fed the parking meter. By the time I joined them, they wore big grins: the manager of the restaurant, sensing an opportunity, had come out into the cold and handed them coupons for free margaritas. It was this mix of hustle and charm offensive — and lively, well-priced, authentic Mexican dishes — that had us developing a little crush on Guapo.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/nyregion/07SUBSUBDINEWE3/07SUBSUBDINEWE3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/nyregion/07SUBSUBDINEWE3/07SUBSUBDINEWE3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 610}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/nyregion/07SUBSUBDINEWE3/07SUBSUBDINEWE3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/nyregion/07SUBSUBDINEWE3/07SUBSUBDINEWE3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1996, 'width': 1963, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/nyregion/07SUBSUBDINEWE3/07SUBSUBDINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/nyregion/07SUBSUBDINEWE3/07SUBSUBDINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarg