clocks were, too. Rick Pitino was a first-time head coach who possessed the energy of an uncoiled spring, and to change what he considered a culture of losing at B.U., he needed his players to run and run and run — two, three, sometimes even four times a day. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/YLOUISVILLE/YLOUISVILLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/YLOUISVILLE/YLOUISVILLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/YLOUISVILLE/YLOUISVILLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/YLOUISVILLE/YLOUISVILLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 1952, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/YLOUISVILLE/YLOUISVILLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/YLOUISVILLE/YLOUISVILLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/YLOUISVILLE/YLOUISVILLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Programs Change, but Pitino’s Methods Do Not', 'kicker': 'Louisville vs. Wichita State', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Programs Change, but Pitino’s Methods Do Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Louisville', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitino, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-06T04:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64a71c00-cbe3-5237-ab43-c852013c00db', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64a71c00-cbe3-5237-ab43-c852013c00db'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/06/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Cinemax) DARK SHADOWS (2012) Johnny Depp, above, summons the spirit of the romantic vampire hero Barnabas Collins in Tim Burton’s revisiting of a 1960s daytime soap opera. Eva Green plays the maid Angelique, who paws at Barnabas’s body. Bella Heathcote is Josette, who runs off with his heart. Three’s a crowd, and the witchy Angelique casts a spell that leaves Josette dead and Barnabas bereft — and leads to a timeout in a deep grave, where, after 200 years of entombment, he awakes in 1972, like a thirstier Rip Van Winkle. “Barnabas’s liberation does the same for Mr. Depp’s performance, and it’s delightful to watch how the actor handles the vampire’s readjustment to the world of the living, which, after he has thrown back some invigorating human Slurpees and faced down a ‘demon’ (a car), he does with both lofty entitlement and abject bewilderment,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “\xa0‘Dark Shadows’ isn’t among Mr. Burton’s most richly realized works, but it’s very enjoyable, visually sumptuous and, despite its lugubrious source material and a sporadic tremor of violence, surprisingly effervescent,” she added. “And while there may not be any deeper resonance lurking in his ‘Dark Shadows’ — the show first surfaced in the middle of the Vietnam War, when real horror was playing out daily in the news — Mr. Burton’s gift for deviant beauty and laughter has its own liberating power.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-06T05:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeb3c6ff-716b-5086-8af7-f679af72ceda', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeb3c6ff-716b-5086-8af7-f679af72ceda'}, {'abstract': 'Bacari Alexander, an assistant coach for Michigan, has used props, like potato chips, as well as stunts to inspire the Wolverines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/06/sports/ncaabasketball/michigan-assistant-a-showman-too.html', 'snippet': 'Bacari Alexander, an assistant coach for Michigan, has used props, like potato chips, as well as stunts to inspire the Wolverines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Somehow, they all work, the varied elements of Bacari Alexander’s story. Somehow, it all ties together, from the streets of Detroit to the Harlem Globetrotters to the Michigan Wolverines, from nutcrackers to construction hard hats to sledgehammers, from custom suits to Magic Circles to basketballs that spin forever on his index fingers.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/2MICHIGAN/2MICHIGAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/2MICHIGAN/2MICHIGAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/2MICHIGAN/2MICHIGAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/2MICHIGAN/2MICHIGAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/2MICHIGAN/2MICHIGAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/2MICHIGAN/2MICHIGAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/sports/2MICHIGAN/2MICHIGAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan Assistant a Showman, Too', 'kicker': 'Michigan vs. Syracuse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he