grief from some trees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMEONE asked me the other day how I had gotten over the sudden death of someone I loved. What I wanted to say but found myself unable to explain (for it would have sounded too strange) was that I learned a good deal about moving through grief from some trees I once knew. They were not my trees. I didn’t plant them. I lived in an apartment surrounded by them. The only tending done was to give them my full attention over the course of four seasons. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07TREE/07TREE-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07TREE/07TREE-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07TREE/07TREE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07TREE/07TREE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07TREE/07TREE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07TREE/07TREE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07TREE/07TREE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year in Trees', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Year in Trees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayes, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-06T17:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Hayes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hayes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/54618ad0-350d-50fb-9135-55a4acebe720', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54618ad0-350d-50fb-9135-55a4acebe720'}, {'abstract': 'Bee colonies have been dying in increasing numbers, and the latest suspect is a pesticide used to protect common agricultural seeds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/opinion/sunday/calamity-for-our-most-beneficent-insect.html', 'snippet': 'Bee colonies have been dying in increasing numbers, and the latest suspect is a pesticide used to protect common agricultural seeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every beekeeper, small or large, hobbyist or commercial, knows that honeybees are in trouble. Over the past decade, bee colonies have been dying in increasing numbers. Last year was especially bad. Perhaps as many as half the hives kept by commercial beekeepers died in 2012. The loss has created a crisis among fruit and vegetable growers, who depend on bees to pollinate their crops. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calamity for Our Most Beneficent Insect', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calamity for Our Most Beneficent Insect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syngenta AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayer CropScience', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pesticides', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-06T17:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/29d68466-398b-5c34-83ee-0be88842b9e8', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29d68466-398b-5c34-83ee-0be88842b9e8'}, {'abstract': 'The glamour of “Mad Men” hides the truth of the drudgery and pressure experienced by the working men who supported families in that era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/opinion/sunday/pity-the-men-on-top.html', 'snippet': 'The glamour of “Mad Men” hides the truth of the drudgery and pressure experienced by the working men who supported families in that era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I dream about my father, as I do even though he has been dead for more than a quarter of a century, I always wake up when I hear the crunch of tires rolling over rock salt — an unmistakable sound evoking the winters of my Michigan childhood in the 1950s and early ’60s. Dad, an accountant, would pull his car out of our icy driveway and head for his office long before first light. This was tax season, and he could keep his business and our family financially afloat only by working 80-hour weeks. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07JACOBY/07JACOBY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07JACOBY/07JACOBY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 577}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07JACOBY/07JACOBY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 985, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07JACOBY/07JACOBY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1970, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07JACOBY/07JACOBY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07JACOBY/07JACOBY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/sunday-review/07JACOBY/07JACOBY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pity the Men on Top', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pity The Men On Top', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacoby, Susan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Sixties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mad Men (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-06T17:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Jacoby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacoby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d8a3a0e-ae50-53cb-8539-840b87e46e81', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d8a3a0e-ae50-53cb-8539-840b87e46e81'}, {'abstract': 'For the last five years, the world has had a break from major conflict. That may be about to end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/opinion/sunday/friedman-weve-wasted-our-timeout.html', 'snippet': 'For the last five years, the world has had a break from major conflict. That may be about to end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YES, it’s true — a crisis is a terrible thing to waste. But a “timeout” is also a terrible thing to waste, and as I look at the world today I wonder if that’s exactly what we’ve just done. We’ve wasted a five-year timeout from geopolitics, and if we don’t wake up and get our act together as a country — and if the Chinese, Russians and Europeans don’t do the same — we’re all really going to regret it.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-fri