ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greuel, Wendy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcetti, Eric', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-06T21:47:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/52de7bbc-6381-51cd-a679-63890115f293', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/52de7bbc-6381-51cd-a679-63890115f293'}, {'abstract': 'Two Democratic candidates struggle to court the city’s powerful labor unions and show independence from them at the same time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/07/us/unions-loom-large-in-los-angeles-mayors-race.html', 'snippet': 'Two Democratic candidates struggle to court the city’s powerful labor unions and show independence from them at the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — They are both Democrats with years of experience at City Hall, who have both chided and courted labor unions over the years. Now, in a race with little separating them ideologically, the two candidates for mayor face the challenge of simultaneously fighting over this powerful force in Los Angeles politics while trying to convince weary voters that they will be independent enough to force unions to accept cutbacks needed to solve the city’s looming budget problems.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/07/us/MAYOR-2/MAYOR-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 