ucation/graduate-school-applications-from-abroad-rise-just-barely.html', 'snippet': 'The number of international students applying to graduate schools in the United States increased just 1 percent this year, the smallest increase in eight years, according to a report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of international students applying to graduate schools in the United States increased just 1 percent this year, after a 9 percent rise last year and an 11 percent gain in 2011, according to a report from the Council of Graduate Schools. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graduate School Applications From Abroad Rise Just Barely', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Graduate School Applications From Abroad Rise Just Barely', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Graduate Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T04:10:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09660a53-dd0d-5694-ba37-53621c9bba07', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09660a53-dd0d-5694-ba37-53621c9bba07'}, {'abstract': 'As states cut back financing, the gap between the pay scales at private and public universities is getting larger, according to the American Association of University Professors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/education/gap-in-university-faculty-pay-continues-to-grow-report-finds.html', 'snippet': 'As states cut back financing, the gap between the pay scales at private and public universities is getting larger, according to the American Association of University Professors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the academic elite — tenured professors at private research universities — average pay this year is $167,118, while at public research universities such professors earn $123,393, according to the annual report by the American Association of University Professors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gap Widens for Faculty at Colleges, Report Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gap Widens For Faculty At Colleges, Report Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tenure', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Assn of University Professors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN COUNCIL ON EDUCATION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T04:10:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8c36c2e-c096-5aee-b614-195ddd02c35a', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8c36c2e-c096-5aee-b614-195ddd02c35a'}, {'abstract': 'A ne