mage', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/europe/THATCHER/THATCHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/09/world/europe/THATCHER/THATCHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/europe/THATCHER/THATCHER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Margaret Thatcher, ‘Iron Lady’ Who Set Britain on New Course, Dies at 87', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Iron Lady’ Who Set Britain on a New Course', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gregory, Joseph R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T12:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph R. Gregory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gregory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7917c358-49bc-5442-a664-3e0dfc4f6fdb', 'word_count': 5382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7917c358-49bc-5442-a664-3e0dfc4f6fdb'}, {'abstract': 'JPMorgan Chase board members are trying to make the case that the bank’s chief executive should remain chairman as well. | Last year was all about perks for chief executives. | Marissa Mayer has bought six start-ups since taking the reins of Yahoo. | Once considered out of fashion, the study of capitalism has a new status in academic circles.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/jpmorgan-works-to-shore-up-support-for-dimon/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan Chase board members are trying to make the case that the bank’s chief executive should remain chairman as well. | Last year was all about perks for chief executives. | Marissa Mayer has bought six start-ups since taking the reins of Yahoo...', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase board members plan to meet with some big shareholders to make their case that Jamie Dimon, the bank’s chief executive, should remain its chairman as well, Susanne Craig and Jessica Silver-Greenberg report in DealBook. The campaigning is unusually proactive this year, shareholders say, reflecting fears within JPMorgan that investors may be dissatisfied with management after last year’s multibillion-dollar trading debacle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Works to Shore Up Support for Dimon', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T12:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1bb633a-fa0b-517a-aa40-bd22c7b2ad27', 'word_count': 2024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1bb633a-fa0b-517a-aa40-bd22c7b2ad27'}, {'abstract': 'Markets are right, except when they aren’t.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/the-intellectual-contradictions-of-sado-monetarism/', 'snippet': 'Markets are right, except when they aren’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still convalescing from This Week; but it helped focus my thoughts a bit more on the jihad against low interest rates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Intellectual Contradictions of Sado-Monetarism', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T12:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16b300b3-1039-5152-b033-777bc41e0dfd', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16b300b3-1039-5152-b033-777bc41e0dfd'}, {'abstract': 'For all practical purposes.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/france-has-its-own-currency-again/', 'snippet': 'For all practical purposes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Weisenthal draws our attention to a development that may surprise many people: French borrowing costs are plunging. (Don’t tell George Osborne — he thinks that low British rates are a unique personal achievement). Here’s the chart for French 10-years:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Has Its Own Currency Again', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T12:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/864c7f5f-bafc-5395-ac0f-a91a8308c3ec', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/864c7f5f-bafc-5395-ac0f-a91a8308c3ec'}, {'abstract': 'Four influential veterans of the fashion industry have teamed up to create a new print publication — and they’re already stirring up controversy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/lets-make-a-magazine/', 'snippet': 'Four influential veterans of the fashion industry have teamed up to create a new print publication — and they’re already stirring up controversy.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Everybody thinks it’s crazy to start a magazine today,” said Alexia Niedzielski, who is starting her third at the age of 30. We are sitting, on the morning of March 5, at Le Mini Palais, a fashionable restaurant in the same building as the Chanel show that has just ended, which is so overbooked with wealthy Chanel customers that Niedzielski has had to persuade the maître d’ to set her up with a wobbly table with no linens in what appears to be the storage room. You do not say “pas possible” to Niedzielski and her friends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Let’s Make a Magazine', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f19e4b-d575-5957-a8de-48daa9c56168', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f19e4b-d575-5957-a8de-48daa9c56168'}, {'abstract': 'Jen Silverman will receive $10,000 and the play will have a staged reading at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/still-by-jen-silverman-wins-yale-play-award/', 'snippet': 'Jen Silverman will receive $10,000 and the play will have a staged reading at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Still,” a play by Jen Silverman, has won the 2013 Yale Drama Series, its organizers said on Monday. The play, about three women who are each dealing with challenges of childbirth — one whose child was born dead, one who is pregnant with an unwanted child and one who is a failed midwife — was chosen by Marsha Norman, the Pulitzer Prize-winning playwright of ” ‘night, Mother,” from nearly 1,100 entries.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Still,’ by Jen Silverman, Wins Yale Play Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jen Silverman Play Wins Yale Honor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Marsha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverman, Jen (Playwright)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T13:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97bdf573-d4e9-5d1d-9c7f-14c0ba0ae10a', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97bdf573-d4e9-5d1d-9c7f-14c0ba0ae10a'}, {'abstract': 'Margaret Thatcher’s conservative prescriptions for her country’s economy have never found fertile soil on the Continent, not even amid a gloom at least as dark as that of ’70s Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/world/europe/tributes-pour-in-for-margaret-thatcher.html', 'snippet': 'Margaret Thatcher’s conservative prescriptions for her country’s economy have never found fertile soil on the Continent, not even amid a gloom at least as dark as that of ’70s Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As word of Margaret Thatcher’s death spread on Monday, it seemed fitting that Prime Minister David Cameron was engaged in what had been billed as a European tour to bring the Continent around to her conservative way of thinking, particularly about Britain’s relationship with Europe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/JP-ENGLAND/JP-ENGLAND-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/09/world/JP-ENGLAND/JP-ENGLAND-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/JP-ENGLAND/JP-ENGLAND-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/JP-ENGLAND/JP-ENGLAND-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/JP-ENGLAND/JP-ENGLAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/09/world/JP-ENGLAND/JP-ENGLAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail