agraph': '“Mommy, it’s so hard at school,” Liddy whispers, curled up beside me in her bed, in the dark. “We’re not even allowed to say the word ‘gun.’ But then they make us think about them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lockdown: Teaching Students to Hide From Guns, and Hide Their Fears', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T13:19:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen E. Dempsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Dempsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d8680e9-0f8c-52bc-aec5-f8c6f9ab4994', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d8680e9-0f8c-52bc-aec5-f8c6f9ab4994'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese officials said they had not yet found any human-to-human transmission of avian influenza, but they were tracking people who had been in contact with those who were ill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/world/asia/china-avian-flu.html', 'snippet': 'Chinese officials said they had not yet found any human-to-human transmission of avian influenza, but they were tracking people who had been in contact with those who were ill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Chinese and World Health Organization officials said Monday that they had still not yet found any human-to-human transmission of a spreading form of avian influenza, after confirming five more infections among humans over the weekend and three more on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source':