ds)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Antenna Design New York Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Outdoor Advertising', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Transit Authority', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T14:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f912946-fdf3-5bf4-99c8-404d79b2cefe', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f912946-fdf3-5bf4-99c8-404d79b2cefe'}, {'abstract': 'We chart the success of the hardest working man in show business.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/the-host-with-the-most-ryan-seacrest/', 'snippet': 'We chart the success of the hardest working man in show business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A once chubby, bespectacled kid from Atlanta who wanted to be Erik Estrada on “CHiPs,” Ryan Seacrest is now 38 and the king of all media, racing from red-carpet interviews to his traffic-cop duties on “American Idol” to producing some of television’s most cultlike reality shows. We all have Seacrest to thank for the rise of the Kardashian clan. Though he trades on celebrity excess, he has somehow remained virtually gossip-proof — save the time TMZ called him out for almost phoning in sick for “American Idol.” (He didn’t.) Ladies and gentlemen, the hardest working man in show business.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Seacrest: The Host With the Most', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Host With the Most', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'AMERICAN IDOL (TV PROGRAM)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T15:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5abae6ef-263d-5361-b8c5-cb13a434a2d7', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5abae6ef-263d-5361-b8c5-cb13a434a2d7'}, {'abstract': 'The location of the nation’s top colleges reflects the past as much as the present. As a result, many students who live far away from such colleges – especially in the Sun Belt and Mountain West – suffer.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/how-the-location-of-colleges-hurts-the-economy/', 'snippet': 'The location of the nation’s top colleges reflects the past as much as the present. As a result, many students who live far away from such colleges – especially in the Sun Belt and Mountain West – suffer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the nation’s most important companies did not exist a generation ago, and many of the most important – Amazon.com, Google, Apple, Costco, Home Depot, Microsoft, FedEx – did not exist 50 years ago. The federal government has also been transformed over the last century, with the creation of Social Security, Medicare, the Securities and Exchange Commission, the modern Federal Reserve and dozens of other agencies and programs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Location of Colleges Hurts the Economy', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e14d31d1-1b4a-50a7-a890-bf8c87b6a1ec', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e14d31d1-1b4a-50a7-a890-bf8c87b6a1ec'}, {'abstract': 'Margaret Thatcher offered inspiration to the American right and served as a role model to female leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/washington-reacts-to-thatchers-death/', 'snippet': 'Margaret Thatcher offered inspiration to the American right and served as a role model to female leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans, especially those on the right, revered Margaret Thatcher, the three-term prime minister of Britain who died Monday at age 87, as a key partner of President Ronald Reagan in the fight against communism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington Reacts to Thatcher’s Death', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank