one}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b56d1d26-46b0-5dea-b7f6-0c89695fb6d1', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b56d1d26-46b0-5dea-b7f6-0c89695fb6d1'}, {'abstract': 'A majority of older Americans use the Internet now, according to a new survey, but adoption has not been swift.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/online-habits-coming-slowly-to-older-adults/', 'snippet': 'A majority of older Americans use the Internet now, according to a new survey, but adoption has not been swift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Older adults hit a digital milestone last year: For the first time since the Pew Research Center’s Internet and American Life Project began conducting surveys, a majority (53 percent) of people over age 65 used the Internet. The proportion has since inched upward, to 54 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Habits Coming Slowly to Older Adults', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T17:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0622a7ae-2687-58eb-a514-41ff6bc3c9c9', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0622a7ae-2687-58eb-a514-41ff6bc3c9c9'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey had little to say last week about the Rutgers scandal, but on Monday he used a news conference to all but claim credit for Coach Mike Rice’s ouster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/nyregion/christie-condemns-rutgers-coach-but-stands-by-president.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey had little to say last week about the Rutgers scandal, but on Monday he used a news conference to all but claim credit for Coach Mike Rice’s ouster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It does not take much for Gov. Chris Christieof New Jersey to uncork his temper. He has called a Navy combat veteran an “idiot,” suggested reporters “take the bat” to a lawmaker in her 70s, and gone taunt-to-taunt with detractors on the boardwalk and in countless town hall meetings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/JP-CHRISTIE-01/JP-CHRISTIE-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/JP-CHRISTIE-01/JP-CHRISTIE-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/JP-CHRISTIE-01/JP-CHRISTIE-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/JP-CHRISTIE-01/JP-CHRISTIE-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/JP-CHRISTIE-01/JP-CHRISTIE-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/JP-CHRISTIE-01/JP-CHRISTIE-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/JP-CHRISTIE-01/JP-CHRISTIE-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brash Christie Plays Rutgers Circumspectly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brash Christie Plays Rutgers Circumspectly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halbfinger, David M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barchi, Robert L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Mike Jr (1969- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T17:27:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b701b8-e0ff-5a95-8714-357d3cc3a694', 'word_count': 1206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b701b8-e0ff-5a95-8714-357d3cc3a694'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists investigating Alzheimer’s found that mice lacking the protein SNX27 had the same learning and memory defects as mice with Down syndrome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/science/protein-in-alzheimers-linked-to-down-syndrome.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists investigating Alzheimer’s found that mice lacking the protein SNX27 had the same learning and memory defects as mice with Down syndrome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French geneticist Jérôme Lejeune discovered more than 50 years ago that Down syndrome is caused by the presence of an extra copy of chromosome 21. But to this day it has remained a mystery why that results in impaired physical and cognitive development. Now researchers at the Sanford-Burnham Medical Research Institute think they have found a clue.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protein Linked to Development Problems', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brain Chemistry: Protein Linked to Development Problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Down Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quenqua, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Medicine (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T17:28:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cba2caa2-7627-5799-a8c3-f6c7692dff25', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cba2caa2-7627-5799-a8c3-f6c7692dff25'}, {'abstract': 'Ten of the 32 governors who are eligible to run for re-election in 2014 have net negative approval ratings. Eight of those 10 are Republicans, including four who rode the 2010 wave to power.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/which-governors-are-most-vulnerable-in-2014/', 'snippet': 'Ten of the 32 governors who are eligible to run for re-election in 2014 have net negative approval ratings. Eight of those 10 are Republicans, including four who rode the 2010 wave to power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot can change before Election Day next year, when 36 states will vote for governor. But at this early stage — when decisions on whether to run or retire are considered and made — 10 of the 32 governors who are eligible to run for re-election have net negative approval ratings in their states.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Which Governors Are Most Vulnerable in 2014?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chafee, Lincoln', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbett, Thomas W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crist, Charlie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasich, John R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LePage, Paul R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Patrick J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Richard Dale', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 15, '