alysis of the N.C.A.A. tournament championship game between Louisville and Michigan, based on concepts of sport psychology like big-game experience, leadership behind the bench, leadership on the court, error control and consistency.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/keeping-score-which-team-has-the-stats-of-a-champion/', 'snippet': 'An analysis of the N.C.A.A. tournament championship game between Louisville and Michigan, based on concepts of sport psychology like big-game experience, leadership behind the bench, leadership on the court, error control and consistency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carlton J. Chin, a portfolio strategist and fund manager, and Jay P. Granat, psychotherapist, are authors of “Who Will Win the Big Game? A Psychological & Mathematical Method.”\xa0 They have previously written about the B.C.S.national title game, this year’s Super Bowl and last year’s N.C.A.A. tournament. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Which Team Has the Stats of a Champion?', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beilein, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burke, Trey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitino, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Louisville', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T20:05:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By CARLTON J. CHIN and JAY P. GRANAT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlton', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'CHIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'GRANAT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': N