ghts-and-scents-of-mexico-city/', 'snippet': 'The third issue of Swallow Magazine has an unusual feature: scratch-and-sniff stickers that are imbued with the aromas of the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to stand out in the crowded field of food publications. But Swallow Magazine may do just that with its latest issue,\xa0on Mexico City, which includes a scratch-and-sniff feature that also brings you the smells of the sprawling metropolis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Swallow Magazine, the Food, Sights and Scents of Mexico City', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smell (Olfaction)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casey, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Diana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolaas, Sissel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swallow Magazine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T20:13:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de8ec7d7-fe91-5a87-b669-50979c0eda97', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de8ec7d7-fe91-5a87-b669-50979c0eda97'}, {'abstract': 'THL Partners agreed on Monday to buy CompuCom Systems, a privately held information technology consultancy. The deal values CompuCom at about $1.1 billion, according to a person briefed on the matter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/08/thl-to-buy-compucom-a-technology-services-firm/', 'snippet': 'THL Partners agreed on Monday to buy CompuCom Systems, a privately held information technology consultancy. The deal values CompuCom at about $1.1 billion, according to a person briefed on the matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The private equity firm THL Partners agreed on Monday to buy CompuCom Systems, a privately held information technology services provider, from another private equity firm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'THL to Buy CompuCom, a Technology Services Firm', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CompuCom Systems Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'THL Partners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T20:13:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dc088c7-547f-50d0-860e-959a2f67c003', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dc088c7-547f-50d0-860e-959a2f67c003'}, {'abstract': 'R. Rex Parris, the mayor of Lancaster, Calif., wants the city to be the first to produce more electricity from solar energy than it consumes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/us/lancaster-calif-focuses-on-becoming-solar-capital-of-universe.html', 'snippet': 'R. Rex Parris, the mayor of Lancaster, Calif., wants the city to be the first to produce more electricity from solar energy than it consumes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LANCASTER, Calif. — There are at least two things to know about this high desert city. One, the sun just keeps on shining. Two, the city’s mayor, a class-action lawyer named R. Rex Parris, just keeps on competing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/us/SOLAR-2/SOLAR-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/09/us/SOLAR-2/SOLAR-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/us/SOLAR-2/SOLAR-2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/us/SOLAR-2/SOLAR-2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/us/SOLAR-2/SOLAR-2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/09/us/SOLAR-2/SOLAR-2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/us/SOLAR-2/SOLAR-2-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Help From Nature, a Town Aims to Be a Solar Capital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Help From Nature, a Town Aims to Be a Solar Capital', 'name'