st', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-08T21:48:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0fa5278-fcef-5196-bab6-5ffe9c73c61a', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0fa5278-fcef-5196-bab6-5ffe9c73c61a'}, {'abstract': 'Marya Wethers performed at Danspace Project in a program that also included a collaboration by Enrico D. Wey and Jon Kinzel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/arts/dance/marya-wethers-and-enrico-d-wey-and-jon-kinzel-at-danspace.html', 'snippet': 'Marya Wethers performed at Danspace Project in a program that also included a collaboration by Enrico D. Wey and Jon Kinzel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before “(w)hole, again” starts, its choreographer, Marya Wethers, lies sprawled on the floor in sweats, her face covered by a knit hat. Beside her are one sock, one boot, one boxing glove. There’s a fork but no spoon, a jar of peanut butter but no jelly. Among these halves, her body looks abandoned.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/09WETHERS/09WETHERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/09WETHERS/09WETHERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/09WET