y about Margaret Thatcher over the next few days, although probably nothing like the “Reagasm” of 2004. And there will in particular be many assertions that Thatcher turned around a moribund British economy. So, is this right?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Did Thatcher Turn Britain Around?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T00:17:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcc5c055-11f7-5ab3-81aa-a0ff1446e616', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcc5c055-11f7-5ab3-81aa-a0ff1446e616'}, {'abstract': 'The proposal comes amid sharp criticism from advocacy groups and Congress over how the military has handled a series of sexual assault cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/us/politics/pentagon-to-ask-congress-to-overhaul-court-martial-system.html', 'snippet': 'The proposal comes amid sharp criticism from advocacy groups and Congress over how the military has handled a series of sexual assault cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Pentagon announced Monday that it would ask Congress to overhaul the court-martial system used to prosecute the nearly 5,000 service members annually accused of crimes, scaling back the power of senior commanders to overturn convictions and dismiss charges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/us/HAGEL/HAGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_na