ed to use it to her advantage. For those who knew her in her prime, however, it did not do justice to her. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thatcher, Reagan and Their Special Relationship', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thatcher, Reagan and Their Special Relationship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T00:58:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wapshott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wapshott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6947bb5e-42fb-56b2-a27b-1539c0ec996c', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6947bb5e-42fb-56b2-a27b-1539c0ec996c'}, {'abstract': 'The military academies wouldn’t lower their standards to enroll top athletes. Would they?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/opinion/nocera-the-military-prep-school-scam.html', 'snippet': 'The military academies wouldn’t lower their standards to enroll top athletes. Would they?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there any institution of higher learning that isn’t gaming the system to gain athletic advantage? I’ve come to believe the answer is no.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'sub