 up politics in New York than healthy, hard-fought elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest scandals from Albany have generated a slew of proposals to clear out New York’s political swamp. After the arrests of a state senator, an assemblyman, a City Council member, a suburban mayor and two Republican Party leaders last week on various corruption charges, Gov. Andrew Cuomo said he was preparing a list of reforms and tougher penalties to repair the system and — though this will take some doing — the state’s badly tarnished reputation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Reform Will Require', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Reform Will Require', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T01:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e89b9036-a830-5fb4-b4b0-b9f3822c86c6', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e89b9036-a830-5fb4-b4b0-b9f3822c86c6'}, {'abstract': 'Robinson Cano hit two home runs against Cleveland and Manager Terry Francona, who has seen it all before in Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/sports/baseball/robinson-cano-powers-yankees-past-indians-with-two-home-runs.html', 'snippet': 'Robinson Cano hit two home runs