in': 'Desecration on Doorways in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desecration On Doorways In Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vandalism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maag, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T02:18:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz and Christopher Maag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maag', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa6917c2-a87e-5171-ae1e-9c2298983421', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa6917c2-a87e-5171-ae1e-9c2298983421'}, {'abstract': 'Serbia on Monday rejected a European Union deal on Kosovo aimed at overcoming ethnic enmities, throwing into doubt its plans to join the bloc.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/world/europe/serbia-kosovo-deal-is-rejected.html', 'snippet': 'Serbia on Monday rejected a European Union deal on Kosovo aimed at overcoming ethnic enmities, throwing into doubt its plans to join the bloc.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Serbia on Monday rejected a European Union deal on Kosovo aimed at overcoming ethnic enmities, throwing into doubt its plans to join the bloc. Serbia had until Tuesday to say whether it would accept an agreement in which Serbia would tacitly accept the authority of the government in Pristina in northern Kosovo in return for receiving a start date for negotiations to join the European Union. Kosovo declared independence from Serbia in 2008. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Serbia: Kosovo Deal Is Rejected', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Serbia: Kosovo Deal Is Rejected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T02:25:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/718e4ecb-0312-54fb-a107-5c13d9482447', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/718e4ecb-0312-54fb-a107-5c13d9482447'}, {'abstract': 'A coroner ruled Monday that the death of a Polish immigrant after he was repeatedly stunned with a police Taser in the Vancouver airport was a homicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/world/americas/canada-report-on-taser-death.html', 'snippet': 'A coroner ruled Monday that the death of a Polish immigrant after he was repeatedly stunned with a police Taser in the Vancouver airport was a homicide.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A coroner ruled Monday that the death of a Polish immigrant after he was repeatedly stunned with a police Taser in the Vancouver airport was a homicide. The fatal confrontation between members of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and Robert Dziekanski in 2007 was captured on video and led to a debate in Canada about the use of Tasers. The coroner’s report was delayed because of a special public inquiry. The new finding has no legal consequences for the police. While no criminal charges were laid against the four officers, they have been charged with perjury related to their testimony to the inquiry. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Report on Taser Death', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Report on Taser Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stun Guns', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Canadian Mounted Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dziekanski, Robert', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T02:28:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/282ea181-1a0b-563b-85fa-943ed9229c4b', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/282ea181-1a0b-563b-85fa-943ed9229c4b'}, {'abstract': 'A roadside bomb killed at least 9 civilians and wounded at least 20 people on a bus on Monday in the Sayad Abad district of Wardak Province, said Fazal Karim Muslim, the district governor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/world/asia/afghanistan-bomb-kills-9.html', 'snippet': 'A roadside bomb killed at least 9 civilians and wounded at least 20 people on a bus on Monday in the Sayad Abad district of Wardak Province, said Fazal Karim Muslim, the district governor.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A roadside bomb killed at least nine civilians on a public bus on Monday. The attack, which also wounded at least 20 people, occurred in the Sayad Abad district of Wardak Province, an area seen as a strategic staging ground for insurgent attacks on Kabul, said Fazal Karim Muslim, the district governor. Last week, 44 civilians were killed in an insurgent attack on a government compound in Farah Province. On Saturday, a suicide bomber struck a convoy of Afghan and coalition officials, killing five Americans in Zabul Province. And in Kunar Province, at least 10 children were killed Saturday in an airstrike called in by American and Afghan troops who were pursuing a Taliban commander. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: Bomb Kills 9', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: Bomb Kills 9', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T02:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_de