5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T03:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9d86fd7-5a13-5ecc-bc47-51875f21b2ee', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9d86fd7-5a13-5ecc-bc47-51875f21b2ee'}, {'abstract': 'Months after their separate kidnappings in Afghanistan, two French civilians were free of their captors on Monday, French and Afghan officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/world/asia/afghanistan-2-french-civilians-are-freed.html', 'snippet': 'Months after their separate kidnappings in Afghanistan, two French civilians were free of their captors on Monday, French and Afghan officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Months after their separate kidnappings in Afghanistan, two French civilians were free of their captors on Monday, French and Afghan officials said. One of the men, identified as a freelance photojournalist, escaped his captors in Wardak Province and was transferred to France’s embassy in Kabul, an Afghan Interior Ministry spokesman said. The man, identified as Pierre Borghi, had been taken hostage on a street in Kabul in November by four armed men, the spokesman said, according to Reuters. French officials had made no public statement regarding the capture of Mr. Borghi or the other man, whose identity was not announced but whom French news media identified as a humanitarian aid worker. French news media and the families of French captives typically publicize hostage situations; such was not the case for either of the men freed on Monday, whose cases were not included by French officials or advocacy groups in their tallies of hostages throughout the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: 2 French Civilians Are Freed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: 2 French Civilians Are Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T03:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/915a9602-0a7c-5144-a7df-6b25bba05ad2', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/915a9602-0a7c-5144-a7df-6b25bba05ad2'}, {'abstract': 'The Japanese Army set up the battery of interceptor missiles on the Defense Ministry grounds in Tokyo as the nation prepared for a possible North Korean missile test.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/world/asia/japan-arms-tokyo-against-north-korean-missiles.html', 'snippet': 'The Japanese Army set up the battery of interceptor missiles on the Defense Ministry grounds in Tokyo as the nation prepared for a possible North Korean missile test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The Japanese Army set up a battery of interceptor missiles on the grounds of the Defense Ministry in central Tokyo on Tuesday, as the nation girded itself for a possible missile test by North Korea, maybe as soon as this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wary of North Korea, Japan Puts Missile Defense in Tokyo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wary of North Korea, Japan P