 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75ff0a33-6e59-5f5e-a170-09984d16a3cf'}, {'abstract': 'J.C. Penney replaced its chief of 17 months with his predecessor. | Big investors are battling over the fate of Energy Future Holdings. | Mary Jo White is confirmed as the new leader of the S.E.C. | Margaret Thatcher, who died on Monday, had doubts about a “European superstate” that resonate today.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/j-c-penney-ousts-a-leader-ackman-championed/', 'snippet': 'J.C. Penney replaced its chief of 17 months with his predecessor. | Big investors are battling over the fate of Energy Future Holdings. | Mary Jo White is confirmed as the new leader of the S.E.C. | Margaret Thatcher, who died on Monday, had doubt...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hedge fund manager William A. Ackman had bet on Ron Johnson as the man to revive the fortunes of J.C. Penney. But on Monday the embattled retailer ousted Mr. Johnson, its chief executive of 17 months, going back to the previous C.E.O., Myron E. Ullman III.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'J.C. Penney Ousts a Leader Ackman Championed', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T11:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/059013f2-567a-503a-b0db-e5985936b515', 'word_count': 1724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/059013f2-567a-503a-b0db-e5985936b515'}, {'abstract': 'The Connecticut town may be ground zero for the 1 percent, but its schools have been witness to a low-income economic phenomenon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/magazine/who-knew-greenwich-conn-was-a-model-of-equality.html', 'snippet': 'The Connecticut town may be ground zero for the 1 percent, but its schools have been witness to a low-income economic phenomenon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manuel Bonilla looked at me, confused. I had just asked him if he worried about entering his son into the Greenwich, Conn., public-school system. Greenwich, of course, is one of the wealthiest towns in America, home to hedge-fund billionaires like Steven A. Cohen, who has a world-renowned art collection and had a private ice rink. Bonilla is a handyman whose family struggles to make the rent. Wasn’t he just a little concerned that his child would feel self-conscious?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 500}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1250, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Knew That Greenwich, Conn., Was a Model of Equality?', 'kicker': 'It’s the Economy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Other Greenwich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T11:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d7d1b2d-c6f6-58df-b667-4803d1841570', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d7d1b2d-c6f6-58df-b667-4803d1841570'}, {'abstract': 'Why all the channeling? There’s nothing wrong with comparing a young singer to an older one, a memoir writer to a famous literary character, or a yoga aficionado to Gumby. But to my ear, at least, the freshness of those recent comparisons was lost because we fell back on a faddish and annoying cliché: So-and-so is “channeling” his “inner” what’s-his-name.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/phrases-we-love-too-much-4/', 'snippet': 'Why all the channeling? There’s nothing wrong with comparing a young singer to an older one, a memoir writer to a famous literary character, or a yoga aficionado to Gumby. But to my ear, at least, the freshness of those recent comparisons was lost...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why all the channeling?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phrases We Love Too Much', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T12:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26e520ee-ac77-5894-8594-9cd5a82f6faf', 'word_count': 1444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26e520ee-ac77-5894-8594-9cd5a82f6faf'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Kantor sings the number “If I Didn’t Believe in You” from the Second Stage revival of the Jason Robert Brown musical.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/in-performance-adam-kantor-of-the-last-five-years/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Kantor sings the number “If I Didn’t Believe in You” from the Second Stage revival of the Jason Robert Brown musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason Robert Brown’s 2002 musical “The Last Five Years” is a two-character show about a couple, Jamie and Cathy, whose relationship is deteriorating. The story uses an unconventional chronology: Jamie’s arc begins when he meets Cathy and then progresses forward, while Cathy’s begins with the couple’s parting kiss and runs backward. In this number, Adam Kantor, who plays Jamie, is accompanied by Gary Sieger on guitar in an excerpt from “If I Didn’t Believe in You.” The show, directed by Mr. Brown, continues through May 12 at Second Stage Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Adam Kantor of ‘The Last Five Years’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Jason Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kantor, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T12:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e935aa5d-daf6-57b7-afd1-ba47f936e5f6', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e935aa5d-daf6-57b7-afd1-ba47f936e5f6'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/opinion-report-margaret-thatcher/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Margaret Thatcher', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T12:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/481c87dd-4bba-5a4e-9544-4163ddc973ee', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/481c87dd-4bba-5a4e-9544-4163ddc973ee'}, {'abstract': 'Israel’s finance minister embarrasses himself by revealing how little he knows about the middle class.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/not-your-average-jane-doe/', 'snippet': 'Israel’s finance minister embarrasses himself by revealing how little he knows about the middle class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEL AVIV — Her name is Riki Cohen, she is 37 and a teacher, and she lives in Hadera, a small city between Tel Aviv and Haifa. She has three children and a husband who works in the high-tech sector. Together, the Cohens earn just over $5,500 a month. They travel abroad every two years and worry about having to assist their children financially well into adulthood. Also, they are imaginary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Your Average Jane Doe', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapid, Yair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yesh Atid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T12:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6710efbd-0155-5754-a30d-54a91d9cdaec', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6710efbd-0155-5754-a30d-54a91d9cdaec'}, {'abstract': 'The Chilean-American writer on writing in exile and an upcoming libretto for an opera based on Hindu philosophical texts.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/a-conversation-with-author-ariel-dorfman/', 'snippet': 'The Chilean-American writer on writing in exile and an upcoming libretto for an opera based on Hindu philosophical texts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ariel Dorfman is a Chilean-American writer, poet, playwright and essayist. He went into political exile in 1973 when President Salvador Allende Gossens of Chile died in a military coup and his democratically elected government was overthrown. Mr. Dorfman has been a strong voice against political oppression and human rights abuses. His notable works include “Death and the Maiden,” a play that was turned into a Hollywood film in 1994 by the same name. After living in Europe for several years, he settled in the United States and has taught literature and Latin American studies at Duke University for nearly three decades. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28-Ariel-IndiaInk/28-Ariel-IndiaInk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28-Ariel-IndiaInk/28-Ariel-IndiaInk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28-Ariel-IndiaInk/28-Ariel-IndiaInk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1016, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28-Ariel-IndiaInk/28-Ariel-IndiaInk-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1740, 'width': 1753, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28-Ariel-IndiaInk/28-Ariel-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda