/', 'snippet': 'Will the president’s first budget proposal since Newtown challenge legislative riders that make it difficult to combat illegal firearms?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, President Obama will unveil his first budget proposal since the massacre in Newtown, Connecticut. One thing to look for is whether he will challenge the quiet weakening of gun enforcement embedded in the recently signed Continuing Resolution, the stopgap spending plan for the second half of this fiscal year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guns and Money', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T13:56:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c9ed59-0f40-56ff-96e0-6727c87758f7', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c9ed59-0f40-56ff-96e0-6727c87758f7'}, {'abstract': 'The inventive conductor will lead a production of “The Marriage of Figaro” in the 2013 Mostly Mozart Festival at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/ivan-fischer-returning-to-mostly-mozart-festival-with-some-new-tricks/', 'snippet': 'The inventive conductor will lead a production of “The Marriage of Figaro” in the 2013 Mostly Mozart Festival at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Along with meticulous musical preparation, the inventive conductor Ivan Fischer likes to mix up orchestra seatings and strew singers amid the instrumentalists. He polls audiences for their choice of encore. At the Mostly Mozart Festival two years ago Mr. Fischer used a chorus to create human tableau sets for a concert version of “Don Giovanni.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivan Fischer Returning to Mostly Mozart Festival With Some New Tricks', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beethoven, Ludwig van', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischer, Ivan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handel, George Frederick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Budapest Festival Orchestra', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orchestra of the Age of Enlightenment', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f02f7deb-7c41-5dc9-96bd-bbf611365191', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f02f7deb-7c41-5dc9-96bd-bbf611365191'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/what-were-reading-668/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Science Daily: Radical mutterings from the annual meeting of the American Chemical Society: a runny egg yolk may not be the most delicious egg yolk after all. — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28660b7a-83a8-5fec-bc9c-5e7ce2310058', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28660b7a-83a8-5fec-bc9c-5e7ce2310058'}, {'abstract': 'The revival of Indian mythology in contemporary fiction is yet another example of how traditional India has adapted to development, with the attendant gains and losses.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/the-return-of-the-ramayana/', 'snippet': 'The revival of Indian mythology in contemporary fiction is yet another example of how traditional India has adapted to development, with the attendant gains and losses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The news last month that Amish Tripathi was offered $1 million to write his next series of books astounded India’s English-language publishing industry. Advances of even $25,000 are rare here, and Tripathi still isn’t sure of the new work’s precise theme. That the deal was struck simply on the success of his 2010 trilogy about Shiva, the Hindu deity, is the starkest measure yet that Indian mythology has become the most marketable segment of India’s English-language book market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Return of the Ramayana', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:10:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hartosh Singh Bal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hartosh', 'middlename': 'Singh', 'lastname': 'Bal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99ef9313-82fa-51de-988b-ba4b4bfb9d62', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99ef9313-82fa-51de-988b-ba4b4bfb9d62'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry said that the administration still favored a diplomatic solution, but that additional pressure on President Bashar al-Assad was needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/world/middleeast/kerry-talks-up-palestinian-economic-development.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry said that the administration still favored a diplomatic solution, but that additional pressure on President Bashar al-Assad was needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — On the eve of a meeting with the Syrian opposition, Secretary of State John Kerry said Tuesday that the Obama administration was weighing “stepped-up” efforts to support the rebel fighters, and that such proposals had been “front and center” in administration discussions over the past week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Meeting Syrian Opposition, Kerry Says U.S. Is Considering More Support', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before Meeting Syria Opposition, Kerry Says U.S. Is Considering More Support', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:20:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon and Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89e69500-44fd-532d-8cb2-7dbcb4ceea3f', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89e69500-44fd-532d-8cb2-7dbcb4ceea3f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Phillips, associated with The Times for more than 20 years, wrote a 1965 exposé of a man in Queens with an Orthodox Jewish background who was a senior Ku Klux Klan official.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/business/media/mccandlish-phillips-times-reporter-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Phillips, associated with The Times for more than 20 years, wrote a 1965 exposé of a man in Queens with an Orthodox Jewish background who was a senior Ku Klux Klan official.', 'lead_paragraph': 'McCandlish Phillips, a former reporter for The New York Times who wrote one of the most famous articles in the newspaper’s history — exposing the Orthodox Jewish background of a senior Ku Klux Klan official — before forsaking journalism to spread the Gospel, died on Tuesday in Manhattan. He was 85.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/phillips1/phillips1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/business/phillips1/phillips1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/phillips1/phillips1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/phillips1/phillips1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1448, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/phillips1/phillips1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/business/phillips1/phillips1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/phillips1/phillips1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McCandlish Phillips, Who Exposed a Jewish Klansman, Is Dead at 85', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'McCandlish Phillips, Who Exposed A Jewish Klansman, Is Dead at 85', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'