nness World Records', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zipcar Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aeeca1b-6ccf-55d0-a5a7-70440745364e', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aeeca1b-6ccf-55d0-a5a7-70440745364e'}, {'abstract': 'Theatergoers attending the West End production of “Billy Elliott the Musical” voted at Monday’s performance to retain the song “Merry Christmas Maggie Thatcher,” whose lyrics refer to celebrating her death.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/after-an-audience-vote-billy-elliot-musical-keeps-an-anti-thatcher-song/', 'snippet': 'Theatergoers attending the West End production of “Billy Elliott the Musical” voted at Monday’s performance to retain the song “Merry Christmas Maggie Thatcher,” whose lyrics refer to celebrating her death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as much of Britain mourned the death of Margaret Thatcher on Monday, the West End production of “Billy Elliot the Musical” went ahead that evening with a song that refers to celebrating her death. The BBC reported that the musical, adapted from the Stephen Daldry movie, retained the number “Merry Christmas Maggie Thatcher” when it was performed on Monday night at the Victoria Palace theater in London, after its audience voted in favor of keeping it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After an Audience Vote, ‘Billy Elliot’ Musical Keeps an Anti-Thatcher Song', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daldry, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John, Elton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6709c540-405c-5510-8e07-ec0fe60d140e', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6709c540-405c-5510-8e07-ec0fe60d140e'}, {'abstract': 'The agency had halted food distribution after protesters, angry that a cash-assistance program was ending,  stormed its main compound last Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/world/middleeast/un-relief-agency-resumes-full-operation-in-gaza.html', 'snippet': 'The agency had halted food distribution after protesters, angry that a cash-assistance program was ending,  stormed its main compound last Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM – The United Nations Relief and Works Agency said that it was resuming full operations in Gaza on Tuesday, reversing a decision to suspend food distribution after protesters stormed its main compound on Thursday. The agency provides staples and other services in Gaza for 815,000 Palestinian refugees and their descendants, nearly half the population of the Hamas-run enclave. The protesters were angry about the cancellation of a cash-assistance program for the poor because of a budget deficit. The agency said in a statement that it was reopening its installations across Gaza based on assurances from local parties, but that it would be forced to close them again if its staff or facilities were threatened or its operations hindered by demonstrations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Relief Agency Resumes Full Operation in Gaza', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:37:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e60011f4-71c1-58d8-94b9-edeac3f2b88c', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e60011f4-71c1-58d8-94b9-edeac3f2b88c'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday in The Times, articles about a student loan rate that is set to rise (again), the return of a morning sickness drug and a surprise path to a better sex life — hip surgery.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/tuesday-reading-hip-surgery-for-a-better-sex-life/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday in The Times, articles about a student loan rate that is set to rise (again), the return of a morning sickness drug and a surprise path to a better sex life — hip surgery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Hip Surgery for a Better Sex Life', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T14:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfd58881-8dc6-5a00-a4b1-f7fb5513667d', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfd58881-8dc6-5a00-a4b1-f7fb5513667d'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/the-gun-report-april-9-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers think we don’t pay enough attention to defensive gun use. We have a couple of examples today, but there is a rarely reported dark side to relying on firearms for self-protection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: April 9, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 4