5:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/530b8df9-943a-531f-9cc1-da495a3935ee', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/530b8df9-943a-531f-9cc1-da495a3935ee'}, {'abstract': 'Center Tyson Chandler is again having discomfort in his neck, and his status for the team’s final five regular-season games is unclear.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/knicks-chandler-doubtful-for-wizards-game/', 'snippet': 'Center Tyson Chandler is again having discomfort in his neck, and his status for the team’s final five regular-season games is unclear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyson Chandler is again having discomfort in his neck and was considered doubtful for the Knicks’ game against the Washington Wizards on Tuesday night at Madison Square Garden. His status for the final five regular-season games was unclear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks’ Chandler Doubtful for Wizards Game', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandler, Tyson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T16:40:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/631dac29-4d63-5655-99fb-d20d0ad506f0', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/631dac29-4d63-5655-99fb-d20d0ad506f0'}, {'abstract': 'A loophole may make some Parent Plus education loans eligible for an income-related repayment option.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/a-student-debt-repayment-option-for-some-parents/', 'snippet': 'A loophole may make some Parent Plus education loans eligible for an income-related repayment option.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parents who take out federal Parent Plus loans to help pay for their children’s college education typically don’t qualify for some breaks available to student borrowers themselves, like repayment options that take their income into account.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Student Debt Repayment Option for Some Parents', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kantrowitz, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T16:48:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed85a5d6-8ea0-58e0-a243-9b637f6cc384', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed85a5d6-8ea0-58e0-a243-9b637f6cc384'}, {'abstract': 'James Crosby, a former chief executive of HBOS, says he will ask authorities to remove his knighthood in light of a damning report published last week that blamed him in part for the mortgage lender’s 2008 collapse.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/former-british-bank-c-e-o-to-give-up-knighthood/', 'snippet': 'James Crosby, a former chief executive of HBOS, says he will ask authorities to remove his knighthood in light of a damning report published last week that blamed him in part for the mortgage lender’s 2008 collapse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – For some British bankers, a knighthood is not for life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former British Bank Chief to Give Up Knighthood', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T16:57:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51ae21a-0812-5007-8c5a-668899f3a7a8', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51ae21a-0812-5007-8c5a-668899f3a7a8'}, {'abstract': 'Based on my experience, I suspect San Diego suffers from what Brad Feld refers to as the “patriarch problem.”', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/torn-between-two-start-up-communities/', 'snippet': 'Based on my experience, I suspect San Diego suffers from what Brad Feld refers to as the “patriarch problem.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most start-ups fail.\xa0It’s a fact.\xa0It’s also a fact that I don’t consider failure an option. I started Fashioning Change in San Diego where I went through the Founder Institute, a tech accelerator that connected me to some of the top technology minds in San Diego and around the country. I entered the program as the only social enterprise, as one of the youngest participants and as the only woman of the 23 entrepreneurs accepted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Torn Between Two Start-Up Communities', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feld, Brad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Founder Institute Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Diego (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santa Monica (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T17:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Herrera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herrera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/754e4633-764a-5d35-9b56-3d69dfab5d42', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/754e4633-764a-5d35-9b56-3d69dfab5d42'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of “Great Gatsby” editions offers an illuminating cross section of 83 years of book design.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/a-book-by-its-covers/', 'snippet': 'A collection of “Great Gatsby” editions offers an illuminating cross section of 83 years of book design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francis Coradal-Cugat’s original cover art for “The Great Gatsby,” which Baz Luhrmann brings to the big screen next month, depicts a disembodied face floating in a night sky. It is one of the lasting images in literature, but that hasn’t kept book designers from trying to outdo it. The scholar and F. Scott Fitzgerald biographer Matthew J. Bruccoli spent his adult life stockpiling those efforts \xad— pulpy paperbacks, fancy slip-covers, French-flapped foreign editions — and today his trove is not only one of the world’s most complete collections but also an illuminating cross section of 83 years of book design. Now housed at the University of South Carolina, the collection is worth several million dollars but Bruccoli, who died in 2008, claimed he was never motivated by money. “You don’t buy books as an investment,” he said. “You buy them because it gives you pleasure to read them, to touch them . . . to see them on shelves.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '138', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Book by its Covers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Book By Its Covers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruccoli, Matthew J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Great Gatsby (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T17:04:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbb450db-1e2c-560b-9f48-22ba9aa4a650', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbb450db-1e2c-560b-9f48-22ba9aa4a650'}, {'abstract': 'The former prime minister expressed exactly where working women stood in the 1980s: in tailored suits that were a carapace of protection in what was essentially a man’s world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/fashion/for-margaret-thatcher-a-wardrobe-was-armor.html', 'snippet': 'The former prime minister expressed exactly where working women stood in the 1980s: in tailored suits that were a carapace of protection in what was essentially a man’s world.', 'lead_paragraph': '“THE LIPS OF MARILYN MONROE and the eyes of Caligula” was a neat summing up of the “power woman” presented by Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/fashion/11THATCHER1/11THATCHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/fashion/11THATCHER1/11THATCHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/fashion/11THATCHER1/11THATCHER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/fashion/11THATCHER1/11THATCHER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1403, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/fashion/11THATCHER1/11THATCHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/fashion/11THATCHER1/11THATCHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/fashion/11THATCHER1/11THATCHER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Margaret Thatcher, a Wardrobe Was Armor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Margaret Thatcher, A Wardrobe as Ar