dubbed the Twin’Z, has center opening doors and is dotted, outside and in, with hundreds of LEDs. The project was the idea of Laurens van den Acker, the Renault design director.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Renault Shows Edgy Concept at Milan Furniture Fair', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Renault Shows Concept At Milan Furniture Fair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Furniture Fair', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovegrove, Ross', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michelin Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Renault SA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T18:38:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00129291-20e8-5435-b549-e6e5828f83a4', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00129291-20e8-5435-b549-e6e5828f83a4'}, {'abstract': 'Beijing has allowed remarkable transparency in the coverage of the bird flu outbreak. Living in Beijing, I have to hope the transparency is real, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/bird-flu-concerns-and-north-korean-jitters/', 'snippet': 'Beijing has allowed remarkable transparency in the coverage of the bird flu outbreak. Living in Beijing, I have to hope the transparency is real, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China has now confirmed 28 cases of infection with the bird flu virus H7N9. Eight people have died. The government has learned many lessons from the SARS outbreak in 2003 and subsequent cover-up, and so far the World Health Organization has publicly praised China’s handling of this new flu variant. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bird Flu Concerns and North Korean Jitters', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Tests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinese Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sina Weibo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yum Brands Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T18:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c97abdb-4749-501a-aea9-f445573a9d20', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c97abdb-4749-501a-aea9-f445573a9d20'}, {'abstract': 'Red wine might not occur to you with chicken, coconut milk and the spicing, but many options would not be out of line.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/a-wild-card-pairing-for-coconut-curry/', 'snippet': 'Red wine might not occur to you with chicken, coconut milk and the spicing, but many options would not be out of line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many people would simply pair beer with Melissa Clark’s rich coconut curry, a wise and sensible choice. Pilsner, Saison, Belgian white ales, India pale ales and any other tart, bracing brew would do nicely. But many wines would work surprisingly well, too. There are the versatile usuals, of course: Champagne, off-dry German rieslings, demi-sec Vouvrays, crisp sauvignon blancs. I think a good amontillado sherry would be delicious; assertive enough to cut through the richness of the coconut milk and reflect the sweet, spicy, herbal flavors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wild-Card Pairing for Coconut Curry', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T18:45:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e860d91-a0d7-5dfa-957e-7caf23a94659', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e860d91-a0d7-5dfa-957e-7caf23a94659'}, {'abstract': 'If you like the music of José Feliciano, whose acoustic guitar and soothing vocals made him a sensation, then try the singer and guitarist Ben Howard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/booming/if-you-like-jose-feliciano-try-ben-howa