'lastname': 'Gillen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/97c90236-b9dd-5319-a951-38e2187721fd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/97c90236-b9dd-5319-a951-38e2187721fd'}, {'abstract': 'On his latest album, “Wheelhouse,” the traditionalist country singer Brad Paisley touches on several social issues, among them race relations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/arts/music/brad-paisleys-wheelhouse.html', 'snippet': 'On his latest album, “Wheelhouse,” the traditionalist country singer Brad Paisley touches on several social issues, among them race relations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These are country music’s postmilitarization years. A decade ago, there were songs about strong soldiers and a just war, weeping soldiers and unimpeachable ideology — the genre latched onto the political moment and held fast like a remora. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10PAISLEY/10PAISLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10PAISLEY/10PAISLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10PAISLEY/10PAISLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10PAISLEY/10PAISLEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20