ame': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/263ae85f-c0a6-5aa1-ba21-07a86a5d036a', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/263ae85f-c0a6-5aa1-ba21-07a86a5d036a'}, {'abstract': 'Located on a hip strip of Sunset Boulevard, a barber shop embodies quiet California cool.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/vain-glorious-the-new-california-barber-shop/', 'snippet': 'Located on a hip strip of Sunset Boulevard, a barber shop embodies quiet California cool.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes, all you need is a sign. After clerking at a grocery store and touring as a musician for 11 years, Brian Girgus decided it was time for a life change and looking back, assessed what it would take: “I realized I should cut hair. I always did it anyways for girlfriends, myself or other friends.” He committed to working long nights after class and taking out a bank loan to finance barber school, until one incredible chance encounter with lady luck. “I went thrift shopping and tried on a coat,” Girgus said, “and in that coat found all of the money I needed for school, in cash.” On the first day of classes, he paid for his tuition in full.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | The New California Barber Shop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vain Glorious: The New California Barber Shop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbers and Barbering', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-09T21:56:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kati