', 'snippet': 'The City of New York and Brookfield Properties will pay more than $230,000 to settle a lawsuit asserting that books and other property were damaged or destroyed when Zuccotti Park was cleared in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As myriad court battles pitting the Occupy Wall Street movement against New York City agencies proceed, protesters claimed a victory on Tuesday, based not on how they were treated, but on how their books were mistreated. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suit Settled With Occupy Wall St. Over Seizure of Library at a Park', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suit Settled With Occupy Wall St. Over Seizure of Library at a Park', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookfield Properties Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T00:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04db4b69-a31b-576c-ad31-ff0627694997', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04db4b69-a31b-576c-ad31-ff0627694997'}, {'abstract': 'In his 17 months trying to remake the chain, Ronald B. Johnson relied on his instincts and rebuffed the doubts of others, associates say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/business/how-an-