g-simmering issue of judicial nominees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/jp-JUDGES/jp-JUDGES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/us/jp-JUDGES/jp-JUDGES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/jp-JUDGES/jp-JUDGES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/jp-JUDGES/jp-JUDGES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1251, 'width': 1708, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/jp-JUDGES/jp-JUDGES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/us/jp-JUDGES/jp-JUDGES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/us/jp-JUDGES/jp-JUDGES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Pushes His Choice for Position on Appeals Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Pushes Choice to Join Appeals Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Srinivasan, Sri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T01:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/856e9b8b-b354-586b-aabb-c785aa2f7389', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/856e9b8b-b354-586b-aabb-c785aa2f7389'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of making undercover investigation of animal abuses in factory farms a crime, we need laws that guarantee our right to know how our food is being produced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/eating-with-our-eyes-closed.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of making undercover investigation of animal abuses in factory farms a crime, we need laws that guarantee our right to know how our food is being produced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The food that comes from factory farms is ultimately consumed by the public, which gives the public an interest in knowing how that food is produced. But in most of the major agricultural states, laws have been introduced or passed that would make it illegal to gather evidence, by filming or photography, about the internal operations of factory farms where animals are being raised. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eating With Our Eyes Closed', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eating With Our Eyes Closed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruelty to Animals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T01:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcf3fb8a-de8a-58dc-abec-c0136d5fbd96', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcf3fb8a-de8a-58dc-abec-c0136d5fbd96'}, {'abstract': 'Is the rise in reported cases of A.D.H.D. in school-age children accurate, and are the potent drugs to treat it being overused?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/worry-over-attention-deficit-hyperactivity-disorder.html', 'snippet': 'Is the rise in reported cases of A.D.H.D. in school-age children accurate, and are the potent drugs to treat it being overused?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is hard not to be concerned about the large number of children who have been given a diagnosis of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, a condition that impairs the ability to focus on a task or to control impulses. A new analysis of government data found that almost one in five boys of high school age in the United States and 11 percent of school-age children over all had been reported to have the disorder at some point in their lives. The troubling question is whether they had or still have A.D.H.D. that actually needs treatment with potent drugs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Worry Over Attention Deficit Cases', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Worry Over Attention Deficit Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADDERALL (DRUG)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T01:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d08eee6d-e744-56f5-854b-559a3bead095', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d08eee6d-e744-56f5-854b-559a3bead095'}, {'abstract': 'Attempts in the House to undercut derivatives regulation would lead to future bailouts of reckless risk-taking by banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/not-enough-reform-on-derivatives.html', 'snippet': 'Attempts in the House to undercut derivatives regulation would lead to future bailouts of reckless risk-taking by banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, several bills to pre-empt the regulation of derivatives will be the focus of a hearing in the House Financial Services Committee. The bills, which have already passed the Agriculture Committee, must be stopped if the world is to be made safe from reckless risk-taking by banks. As it turns out, Representative Jeb Hensarling, Republican of Texas and the new head of the Financial Services Committee, may be the man to stop them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Enough Reform on Derivatives', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Enough Reform on Derivatives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Financial Services Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hensarling, Jeb', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T01:23:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6033d4b1-e0cb-5b1a-a331-cd42ec931ecc', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6033d4b1-e0cb-5b1a-a331-cd42ec931ecc'}, {'abstract': 'Promontory Financial is a consulting firm stocked with former government officials and paid billions by banks to help them navigate an onslaught of new regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/09/for-former-regulators-a-home-on-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'Promontory Financial is a consulting firm sto