the maps so their incumbents are protected from any serious challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/nyregion/the-qualities-of-the-squid-as-observed-in-the-capitol.html', 'snippet': 'The two main political parties have a deal that allows each side to fix the maps so their incumbents are protected from any serious challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In nature, the octopus and the squid are known for their quick-changing colors, allowing them to blend into any environment. Lacking spines, they can slip through the tiniest crevices. Yet they have tremendous strength in their tentacles, which are lined with suction-cup structures that have so much power they can burst an artery in a human, capsize boats, or stay fixed to a rock until they are good and ready to let go.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT-01/SUB-ABOUT-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT-01/SUB-ABOUT-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT-01/SUB-ABOUT-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT-01/SUB-ABOUT-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1528, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT-01/SUB-ABOUT-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT-01/SUB-ABOUT-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/SUB-ABOUT-01/SUB-ABOUT-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Qualities of the Squid, as Observed in the Capitol', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Qualities Of the Squid, As Observed In the Capitol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T01:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a987c254-3fc7-52c4-a74d-5498cc5529f9', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a987c254-3fc7-52c4-a74d-5498cc5529f9'}, {'abstract': 'The Arab Spring now seems more akin to the Thirty Years’ War than the fall of the Berlin Wall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/friedman-the-arab-quarter-century.html', 'snippet': 'The Arab Spring now seems more akin to the Thirty Years’ War than the fall of the Berlin Wall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I guess it’s official now: The term “Arab Spring” has to be retired. There is nothing springlike going on. The broader, but still vaguely hopeful, “Arab Awakening” also no longer seems valid, given all that has been awakened. And so the strategist Anthony Cordesman is probably right when he argues: It’s best we now speak of the “Arab Decade” or the “Arab Quarter Century” — a long period of intrastate and intraregional instability, in which a struggle for both the future of Islam and the future of the individual Arab nations blend together into a “clash within a civilization.” The ending: TBD.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas