'_id': 'nyt://article/3b3df595-4d27-5098-88ba-b17281be92d0', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b3df595-4d27-5098-88ba-b17281be92d0'}, {'abstract': 'The scandal over horse meat sold as beef re-emerged with a Dutch alert about 50,000 tons of meat sold in Europe and a recall of a product in Britain containing a veterinary drug.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/world/europe/traces-of-horse-drug-found-in-british-beef-product.html', 'snippet': 'The scandal over horse meat sold as beef re-emerged with a Dutch alert about 50,000 tons of meat sold in Europe and a recall of a product in Britain containing a veterinary drug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — After disappearing briefly from public view, the scandal over horse meat sold as beef re-emerged on Wednesday with an alert over 50,000 tons of meat sold across Europe and an earlier recall of a product in Britain containing a veterinary drug banned from the human food chain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Horse Meat Problems Resurface Across Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Horse Meat Problems Resurface Across Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterinary Medicine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slaughterhouses', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T08:40:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88583195-035b-5e8c-a687-46cd29e6a75e', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88583195-035b-5e8c-a687-46cd29e6a75e'}, {'abstract': 'Taking the plunge back into public life after a marital (and political) catastrophe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/magazine/anthony-weiner-and-huma-abedins-post-scandal-playbook.html', 'snippet': 'Taking the plunge back into public life after a marital (and political) catastrophe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day in early February, I met Anthony Weiner and Huma Abedin for breakfast at the Gramercy Park Hotel, one of their regular joints, just a few blocks from their apartment on Park Avenue South. The first thing Weiner said when I sat down was that their 13-month-old son, Jordan, had just moments ago taken his first step. They were both giddy, kvelling with baby-pride, especially Weiner, who, with all his free time, has become his son’s primary caretaker. This is what life is like now for the man whose name is invariably followed in print by some version of “the disgraced former congressman who sent out a lewd picture of himself via Twitter.” He seems to spend much of his time within a five-block radius of his apartment: going to the park with Jordan; picking up his wife’s dry cleaning and doing the grocery shopping; eating at his brother Jason’s two restaurants in the neighborhood. This is what happens after a scandal: Ranks are closed and the world shrinks to a tiny dot. It is a life in retreat. And for a man who was known, pre-scandal, for his overweening ambition, his constant presence on cable news, his hard-charging schedule that verged on lunacy, well, it has been quite a change.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14weiner1/14weiner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14weiner1/14weiner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14weiner1/14weiner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14weiner1/14weiner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14weiner1/14weiner1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14weiner1/14weiner1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/magazine/14weiner1/14weiner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony Weiner and Huma Abedin’s Post-Scandal Playbook', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Post-Scandal Playbook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Meter, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abedin, Huma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 