 — Medicare and Social Security — created by Democratic presidents. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/us/BUDGET1/BUDGET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/us/BUDGET1/BUDGET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/us/BUDGET1/BUDGET1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/us/BUDGET1/BUDGET1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1309, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/us/BUDGET1/BUDGET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/11/us/BUDGET1/BUDGET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/us/BUDGET1/BUDGET1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Budget Opens Rift for Democrats on Social Benefits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Budget Whittles Democratic Party Pillars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calmes, Jackie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T11:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d0a17ec-17ea-50a2-ba0d-eaa9f7534629', 'word_count': 1189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d0a17ec-17ea-50a2-ba0d-eaa9f7534629'}, {'abstract': 'Does a campaign like International Topless Jihad Day really help feminists in the Arab world?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/topless-protest-may-hurt-feminist-cause-in-the-arab-world/', 'snippet': 'Does a campaign like International Topless Jihad Day really help feminists in the Arab world?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — You may have missed it, but April 4 was International Topless Jihad Day. Announced by Femen, the radical feminist group that originated in Ukraine, it was organized in solidarity with Amina Tyler, a 19-year-old Tunisian woman who last month sparked a storm in Tunisia by posting two topless photos of herself online. In one, she faces the camera with both hands held up defiantly, her middle fingers unfurled; her torso bears an inscription cursing “your morals.” In the other photo, she wrote “my body belongs to me and is not a source of anyone’s honor.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By the Teeth of Their Skin', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Femen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T11:39:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Issandr El Amrani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Issandr', 'middlename': 'El', 'lastname': 'Amrani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0de5f997-08f6-519b-95d0-d7216a31049d', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0de5f997-08f6-519b-95d0-d7216a31049d'}, {'abstract': 'The Promontory Financial Group is facing scrutiny in Congress. | Herbalife finds itself in the middle of an insider trading scandal. | Life Technologies appears poised to be at the center of a bidding contest. | Europe’s competition commissioner sometimes communicates with companies using text messages.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/shadow-regulator-under-scrutiny/', 'snippet': 'The Promontory Financial Group is facing scrutiny in Congress. | Herbalife finds itself in the middle of an insider trading scandal. | Life Technologies appears poised to be at the center of a bidding contest. | Europe’s competition commissioner s...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary L. Schapiro, who ran the Securities and Exchange Commission until last year, is only the latest former political insider to join the Promontory Financial Group, which has such a star-studded roster of former bureaucrats that it has become known as Wall Street’s shadow regulator. With these connections, the firm “has emerged as a major power broker in Washington, helping Wall Street navigate an onslaught of new rules and regulatory scrutiny,” Ben Protess and Jessica Silver-Greenberg write in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shadow Regulator Under Scrutiny', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T11:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73d7f8f7-73dc-5e2e-b740-be0a6d6faff5', 'word_count': 2143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73d7f8f7-73dc-5e2e-b740-be0a6d6faff5'}, {'abstract': 'The service retransmits TV broadcasts without paying stations the fees that cable operators pay, so networks are determined to shut it down — even, they say, if they have to go cable-only, Brian Stelter reports in Wednesday’s New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/daily-report-aereos-inroads-bring-sharp-reaction-from-networks/', 'snippet': 'The service retransmits TV broadcasts without paying stations the fees that cable operators pay, so networks are determined to shut it down — even, they say, if they have to go cable-only, Brian Stelter reports in Wednesday’s New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Aereo is a service that scoops up the free signals of local television stations and streams them to the phones and computers of paying subscribers. Because Aereo cuts off the stations from the retransmission fees that they have grown to depend on, they are determined to shut down the service — even, the station owners say, if they have to go cable-only, Brian Stelter reports in Wednesday’s New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Aereo’s Inroads Bring Sharp Reaction From Networks', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Televisi