: 'nyt://article/7d76ee5d-5ec7-5dfe-bbbf-03de1cd76b06', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d76ee5d-5ec7-5dfe-bbbf-03de1cd76b06'}, {'abstract': 'A new ad promoting Chelsea’s new jersey for the 2013-14 season paints the players blue.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/chelsea-kind-of-blue/', 'snippet': 'A new ad promoting Chelsea’s new jersey for the 2013-14 season paints the players blue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is only April, but already Chelsea and its equipment sponsor Adidas are looking ahead to next season, when the club will begin anew its quest to win England’s Premier League … and sell thousands of new jerseys. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/sports/soccer/chelsea/chelsea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/sports/soccer/chelsea/chelsea-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/sports/soccer/chelsea/chelsea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/sports/soccer/chelsea/chelsea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chelsea: Kind of Blue', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADIDAS AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T13:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb0a3dff-a0d9-501c-a861-001db0a8b399', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb0a3dff-a0d9-501c-a861-001db0a8b399'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever the cause of issues in couples’ sex lives, the key is loving communication, says Ronald Levant, an expert on male sexuality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/booming/advice-for-couples-about-their-sex-lives-part-1.html', 'snippet': 'Whatever the cause of issues in couples’ sex lives, the key is loving communication, says Ronald Levant, an expert on male sexuality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers recently submitted questions about male sexuality to Dr. Ronald F. Levant, a professor of psychology and director of the Psychology Department Counseling Clinic at the University of Akron. Dr. Levant was president of the American Psychological Association and is an author or editor of 14 books, including “Men and Sex: New Psychological Perspectives.” Dr. Levant asked the counselors that he supervises in his clinic, all Ph.D. students in psychology who see a broad range of clients, to help him compose answers to these questions. Thanks are due to Mike Aguilar, Brittany Baker, Natalie Grandy, Craig Libman and Arielle Riutort. Because of the large number of submissions, not every question was addressed. In particular, they were not able to answer questions on medical issues, as their expertise is psychological, not medical. More answers will be posted next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advice for Couples About Their Sex Lives, Part 1', 'kicker': 'Ask an Expert', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T13:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d93507f-bc42-5291-9694-eb997b613039', 'word_count': 2171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d93507f-bc42-5291-9694-eb997b613039'}, {'abstract': 'The 2006-2010 American Community Survey reveals that more people, on average, moved to Manhattan from Los Angeles annually than, for example, from Suffolk County.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/census-takes-a-look-at-new-yorkers-migration-patterns/', 'snippet': 'The 2006-2010 American Community Survey reveals that more people, on average, moved to Manhattan from Los Angeles annually than, for example, from Suffolk County.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much for Horace Greeley. Between 2006 and 2010, more people, on average, moved to Manhattan from Los Angeles annually (3,251) than, for example, from Suffolk County (2,301). And more moved to Manhattan from Brooklyn (11,469) than from any other county in the United States or from any other country. (Europe was second.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Census Takes a Look at New Yorkers’ Migration Patterns', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T13:51:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ef3fb98-c0f7-512a-8240-b6fadc0ad29d', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ef3fb98-c0f7-512a-8240-b6fadc0ad29d'}, {'abstract': 'George Soros and Jacob Lew are among those calling for Europe’s leaders to rethink stringent financial policies that they claim are making a bad economic situation worse.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/europe-urged-to-make-a-u-turn-on-austerity/', 'snippet': 'George Soros and Jacob Lew are among those calling for Europe’s leaders to rethink stringent financial policies that they claim are making a bad economic situation worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Austerity in Europe is under fire, and not just from protesters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/LEW/LEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/business/LEW/LEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/LEW/LEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/LEW/LEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1213, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/LEW/LEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/business/LEW/LEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/business/LEW/LEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Urged to Make a U-Turn on Austerity', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lew, Jacob J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montebourg, Arnaud', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soros, George', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T13:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c64d1b7e-7ebe-535c-b297-43fb8fc8c54e', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c64d1b7e-7ebe-535c-b297-43fb8fc8c54e'}, {'abstract': 'The iPad becomes a child’s easel, thanks to ArtSee Studio from WowWee, designed to offer protection against drops and reduce the chance a preschooler might end up in your email.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/the-ipad-as-childs-easel/', 'snippet': 'The iPad becomes a child’s easel, thanks to ArtSee Studio from WowWee, designed to offer protection against drops and reduce the chance a preschooler might end up in your email.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IPad cases for children abound these days, but if your intention is to create a child’s easel, ArtSee Studio from WowWee ($40) is the best bet. Designed to offer both protection against drops and reduce the chance a preschooler might end up in your email, the plastic case includes a home button lock, a rubber-tipped stylus and five stamps of the variety you might find at the post office. Instead of ink, each stamp has a unique dot pattern that triggers an artistic effect when placed against the iPad’s screen. Want to add a swimming dolphin? Use the sticker stamp. Want to make your dolphin move? Use the Arrow stamp, and trace a course. After you snap your iPad into the holder and download the free app, called ArtSee Studio, your child is free to sketch. One weak point — our testers found it hard to “undo” a sticker once it has been placed. But they were impressed by the powerful drawing options, which include such wonders as a rainbow crayon. Saving projects is automatic, and there is a set of games like connect the dots and concentration.  The case fits all generations of iPads.Download the app here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The iPad as Child’s Easel', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T14:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e837bb84-6e05-57c5-864f-4ac381636ca3', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e837bb84-6e05-57c5-864f-4ac381636ca3'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/what-were-reading-669/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times: The fight to save a family-owned oyster bed in Northern California has thrown together some very strange bedfellows, including Alice Waters and Republicans trying to promote the Keystone XL pipeline and 