KPMG and the Pain That Comes of Breached Trust', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herbalife Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KPMG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skechers USA Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T14:54:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07bf6804-d52b-5969-b15c-22b7a4447598', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07bf6804-d52b-5969-b15c-22b7a4447598'}, {'abstract': 'A Swiss school’s design students offer bright ideas and innovation to luxury companies.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/applied-arts/', 'snippet': 'A Swiss school’s design students offer bright ideas and innovation to luxury companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last several years, the coolest design schools were those, like Design Academy Eindhoven in the Netherlands, that turned out the most conceptual work, much of it laced with social commentary. But now the school whose name seems to be everywhere is the ÉCAL/University of Art and Design Lausanne. Like many of its peers, the 192-year-old Swiss institution offers an undergraduate degree in industrial design. But unlike many schools, it also has something called the Master of Advanced Studies in Design for Luxury and Craftsmanship, which was founded five years ago and has made a name for itself through its collaborations — with luxury goods companies like Baccarat, Christofle, Bernardaud and Audemars Piguet — that bring new ideas to old-line manufacturers.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Applied Arts', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Applied Arts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Furniture Fair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T15:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bb11b94-61a0-5903-85bd-a332e06da05f', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bb11b94-61a0-5903-85bd-a332e06da05f'}, {'abstract': 'Google Maps has added information on public transportation in several cities.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/subway-on-way-maps-tell-you/', 'snippet': 'Google Maps has added information on public transportation in several cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google Maps has added information on public transportation in several cities. The service now provides up-to-date departure times for seven New York City (above) subway lines and for buses and trams in the greater Salt Lake City area, and service alerts for Washington’s Metrorail subway. Updates are available in many other major cities, including London, Madrid and San Diego.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subway on Way? Maps Tell You', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Online: Subway on Way? Maps Tell You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T15:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9baa9c1f-a57f-5c13-9a62-cc656f037598', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9baa9c1f-a57f-5c13-9a62-cc656f037598'}, {'abstract': 'Terms of the settlement agreement were not disclosed.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/taymor-producers-reach-settlement-in-spider-man-legal-battle/', 'snippet': 'Terms of the settlement agreement were not disclosed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After more than a year of brinkmanship at the negotiating table the producers of the musical “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” and their former director, Julie Taymor, announced on Wednesday that they had settled their acrimonious legal battle over profits, copyright claims and artistic credit for the $75 million show, the most expensive in Broadway history.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10artsbeat-spider/10artsbeat-spider-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10artsbeat-spider/10artsbeat-spider-articleLarge.jpg',