ard, while disagreements between adults are kept in the background.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/what-makes-a-successful-stepfather/', 'snippet': 'In forming new family relationships, children need to feel that their frustrations are heard, while disagreements between adults are kept in the background.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How mothers and their new partners feel about becoming a stepfamily is one thing, and how the children involved feel is quite another. In 2009, more than 7 percent of children lived with at least one stepparent, yet much of the research and writing on the topic centers on how the adults navigate their new family dynamic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Makes a Successful Stepfather?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T16:53:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc35a143-c3ab-5fa4-9ffc-f745cb7e470a', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc35a143-c3ab-5fa4-9ffc-f745cb7e470a'}, {'abstract': 'Times reporters analyze how the White House’s budget request would affect federal agencies and programs.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/latest-updates-on-obamas-budget-proposal/', 'snippet': 'Times reporters analyze how the White House’s budget request would affect federal agencies and programs.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:10 p.m. | Updated  A condensed version of this post is available here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights From Obama’s Budget Proposal', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T16:54:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a263c60-0a47-5595-8481-0b308d1445af', 'word_count': 2873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a263c60-0a47-5595-8481-0b308d1445af'}, {'abstract': 'The British shoe brand introduces a new line of sneaker-inspired footwear for the spring season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/high-low-dr-martens-sneakers/', 'snippet': 'The British shoe brand introduces a new line of sneaker-inspired footwear for the spring season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Injecting a tinge of athletic spirit to its archive of iconic punk-cult classics, the British shoe brand Dr. Martens introduces a new line of sneaker-inspired footwear for the spring season. The Farrell style, the standout in the new collection, combines the classic Dr. Martens air-cushioned wedge sole with a sleek smooth leather upper available in three colors (black, navy and cherry). Resembling many of the chunky-soled shoes that have treaded the runway in recent collections of Raf Simons, Acne and Marni, the Dr. Martens Farrell is a fresh alternative that can be worn with as much regularity as a favorite sneaker. And for under $100, it’s difficult not to want all three.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High Low | Dr. Martens Sneakers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'High Low: Dr.