ur “every man for himself” family policies are never going to change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you send your children to public school, are they still your children? If you trust that should they fall off their bike while riding along on the sidewalk in front of the neighbor’s house, he might run out with a Band-Aid, is that the end of the nuclear family? Does taking support for those children, in the form of the Children’s Health Insurance Program, Head Start or the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, mean you have you ceded your place as mother or father to the collective?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Melissa Harris-Perry’s ‘Uncontroversial Comment’ About Children', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris-Perry, Melissa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T19:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f58830f8-c7c5-511a-8dd6-1da5f0987346', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f58830f8-c7c5-511a-8dd6-1da5f0987346'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent review of A. B. Yehoshua’s novel “The Retrospective.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/books/review/roman-charity.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to a recent review of A. B. Yehoshua’s n