b9a-5bc1-9da1-c397f800a9de'}, {'abstract': 'The annual pension payment for James Crosby, the former chief executive of the failed British bank HBOS, will still be more than 400,000 pounds, 23 times more than the 17,700 pound average income of retired households in Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/bankings-crocodile-tears/', 'snippet': 'The annual pension payment for James Crosby, the former chief executive of the failed British bank HBOS, will still be more than 400,000 pounds, 23 times more than the 17,700 pound average income of retired households in Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story is told of a young heir whose family fell on times hard times and he could no longer afford to keep his polo ponies. He still had a big house and enough trust fund income to make a paid career optional, but it was hard to look his polo-playing friends in the face. The shame was almost unbearable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banking’s Crocodile Tears', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HBOS PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T19:17:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Hadas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hadas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b51de029-c671-56fd-ba48-635a03401925', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b51de029-c671-56fd-ba48-635a03401925'}, {'abstract': 'The new bill would require all banks to have capital equal to 10 percent of their assets. Unsurprisingly, the financial industry doesn’t like it.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/the-answer-to-too-big-to-fail/', 'snippet': 'The new bill would require all banks to have capital equal to 10 percent of their assets. Unsurprisingly, the financial industry doesn’t like it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senators Sherrod Brown, D-Ohio, and David Vitter, R-Louisiana, have a new bill that would make banks keep much higher levels of capital. Not surprisingly, representatives for the financial industry are already claiming that such a requirement would ruin the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Answer to Too Big to Fail?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Sherrod', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vitter, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T19:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d936bd8-56ce-59fe-b11e-ba2a55599c23', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d936bd8-56ce-59fe-b11e-ba2a55599c23'}, {'abstract': 'The amount of language children hear in their first three years plays an important role in their future learning: the more talk from parents, the better.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/the-power-of-talking-to-your-baby/', 'snippet': 'The amount of language children hear in their first three years plays an important role in their future learning: the more talk from parents, the better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time a poor child is 1 year old, she has most likely already fallen behind middle-class children in her ability to talk, understand and learn. The gap between poor children and wealthier ones widens each year, and by high school it has become a chasm. American attempts to close this gap in schools have largely failed, and a consensus is starting to build that these attempts must start long before school — before preschool, perhaps even before birth.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Power of Talking to Your Baby', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Power of Talking to Baby', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T19:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b141503-39ce-51a9-85a5-a09099089039', 'word_count': 1810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b141503-39ce-51a9-85a5-a09099089039'}, {'abstract': 'Related Companies and Oxford Property Group announced that they had completed the financing for a 47-story office tower and signed up three tenants for the building: Coach, L’Oreal USA and SAP.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/three-major-tenants-sign-leases-for-first-tower-at-hudson-yards/', 'snippet': 'Related Companies and Oxford Property Group announced that they had completed the financing for a 47-story office tower and signed up three tenants for the building: Coach, L’Oreal USA and SAP.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when developers and city officials thought that the city’s financial institutions would lead the development of the rail yards on the Far West Side of Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/10-YARDS/10-YARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/10-YARDS/10-YARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/10-YARDS/10-YARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/10-YARDS/10-YARDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/10-YARDS/10-YARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/nyregion/10-YARDS/10-YARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/n