'snippet': 'Debating the national pastime’s current state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That’s the bold claim advanced last week by Michael Brendan Dougherty, who just took a step away from political writing to found a baseball newsletter (news-email?) called “The Slurve”, and who gives a great interview\xa0about the decision here. His case that baseball is peaking acknowledges the sport’s various difficulties (the Hall of Fame’s steroid problems, the pace of games, the Florida Marlins), but then follows with this:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Baseball Golden Age?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yankee Stadium (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T19:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a7a3641-b97e-59d3-8a5e-b4f558ba949d', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a7a3641-b97e-59d3-8a5e-b4f558ba949d'}, {'abstract': 'The document, which is in Arabic, cites specific cases of civilian disappearances, torture and death at the hands of Egypt’s military.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/leaked-documents-accuse-egyptian-army-of-civilian-deaths-in-2011-unrest/', 'snippet': 'The document, which is in Arabic, cites specific cases of civilian disappearances, torture and death at the hands of Egypt’s military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A leaked report published on Wednesday by The Guardian implicates Egypt’s armed forces of participating in the disappearance, torture and killing of civilians across the country during the 2011 Egyptian revolution, an uprising in which the military initially professed neutrality before President Hosni Mubarak was removed from power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaked Report to Egypt’s President Implicates Army in Torture and Killing of Civilians', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T19:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/063bf8e3-1ace-5777-b246-e55ae9941b0e', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/063bf8e3-1ace-5777-b246-e55ae9941b0e'}, {'abstract': 'A study of ninth graders found that each additional hour of sleep was linked to a reduction in body mass index.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/less-sleep-more-weight/', 'snippet': 'A study of ninth graders found that each additional hour of sleep was linked to a reduction in body mass index.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study suggests that adolescent obesity could be decreased if teenagers got more sleep, and the heaviest would benefit most.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/health/well_childhood/well_childhood-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sleep Less, Weigh More', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childhood: Less Sleep, More Weight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T19:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71d84aa1-8310-525f-96b6-3af3e9dcb279', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71d84aa1-8310-525f-96b6-3af3e9dcb279'}, {'abstract': 'The department said on Tuesday that their visit was licensed as an educational exchange.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/beyonc-and-jay-zs-cuba-trip-was-approved-treasury-dept-says/', 'snippet': 'The department said on Tuesday that their visit was licensed as an educational exchange.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As it turns out, Beyoncé and Jay-Z were never in much danger of serving the 10-year jail sentence, or paying the $250,000 fine, that their visit to Cuba last week supposedly might have cost them. Treasury Department regulations prohibit Americans from traveling to Cuba “unless authorized by a general or specific license,” and several Florida lawmakers have raised strong objections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10artsbeat-jayz/10artsbeat-jayz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10artsbeat-jayz/10artsbeat-jayz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 822}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10artsbeat-jayz/10artsbeat-jayz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 748, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/arts/10artsbeat-jayz/10artsbeat-jayz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1496, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima