n of Goldman Sachs, is keeping both of those roles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Reaches Deal to Let C.E.O. Be Chairman', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blankfein, Lloyd C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CtW Investment Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T21:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/191bf5b5-e7aa-5708-afa5-e070c9f1215b', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/191bf5b5-e7aa-5708-afa5-e070c9f1215b'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Thile, the mandolinist, and Brad Mehldau, the jazz pianist, joined forces at the Bowery Ballroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/arts/music/chris-thile-and-brad-mehldau-at-bowery-ballroom.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Thile, the mandolinist, and Brad Mehldau, the jazz pianist, joined forces at the Bowery Ballroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Thile and Brad Mehldau come from different worlds but the same species, and whatever feels unlikely about their pairing is eclipsed by what feels perfectly natural. Mr. Thile, the mandolinist and singer with Punch Brothers, is a progressive-bluegrass pacesetter; Mr. Mehldau is the most influential jazz pianist of the last 20 years. Both are team players who can still give the impression of aesthetic self-containment. Both love Bach and the Beatles, and both have developed fan bases bigger and broader (and younger) than their genre silos can accommodate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/THILE/THILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/THILE/THILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/THILE/THILE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/THILE/THILE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/THILE/THILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/THILE/THILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/THILE/THILE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bluegrass and Jazz, Meeting in More Than the Middle', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bluegrass and Jazz, Meeting in More Than the Middle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 