l': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/arts/television/the-moment-a-reality-show-with-kurt-warner-on-usa.html', 'snippet': 'The former N.F.L. quarterback Kurt Warner hosts a reality show in which aspirants get some lightning training and a make-or-break tryout for their dream jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Moment,” a new reality series on USA in which people are given the chance to try out for the dream job they thought had passed them by, wants us to root for the weekly hopeful, of course. But here’s the thing: Success for those people would mean that the Western educational and economic systems are giant houses of cards and that everything we have come to believe about how the socio-economic structure ought to work is a lie.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the American Dream a Two-Week Endeavor', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making the American Dream a Two-Week Endeavor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warner, Kurt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T21:18:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4538277-49c2-5518-9ff9-56e59c803aad', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4538277-49c2-5518-9ff9-56e59c803aad'}, {'abstract': 'The brother-in-law of an adviser to President Hamid Karzai was killed in a raid by Afghan commandos and American advisers, adding to growing tensions in the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/world/asia/death-of-man-with-ties-to-karzai-adds-to-tensions-with-military.html', 'snippet': 'The brother-in-law of an adviser to President Hamid Karzai was killed in a raid by Afghan commandos and American advisers, adding to growing tensions in the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A special operations raid meant to disrupt a Taliban arms operation in southern Afghanistan ended in the death of a man with family ties to the Afghan president’s inner circle, leading to tensions between regional officials and the military, officials say.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man With Ties to Karzai Dies in a Military Raid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man With Ties to Karzai Dies in a Military Raid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Special Operations Command', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shah, Taimoor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Janan, Khiraullah', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Janan, Hajji', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T21:22:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed and Taimoor Shah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Taimoor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b91fb24c-1b7f-5568-92ad-47107ba4eeda', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b91fb24c-1b7f-5568-92ad-47107ba4eeda'}, {'abstract': 'Yes came to the Beacon Theater for a show comprising three of its most durable albums: all from the 1970s, each played from start to finish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/arts/music/yes-at-the-beacon-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Yes came to the Beacon Theater for a show comprising three of its most durable albums: all from the 1970s, each played from start to finish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite one of music’s most positive names the veteran quintet Yes has seen more than its share of turbulence and rivalries over a life span that has now reached its 45th year. A hard-touring institution, the current Yes came to the Beacon Theater on Tuesday night for a show comprising three of its most durable albums: all from the 1970s, each played from start to finish. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11YES/11YES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11YES/11YES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 597}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11YES/11YES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1019, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11YES/11YES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1