alks I heard at HTML5 Dev Conf, as well as some from talks I missed but heard good things about.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:18 p.m. | Updated  A few of the videos are now available.Last week, I attended the HTML5 Dev Conf in San Francisco. Overall the event was quite illuminating; I got a strong sense of where the web development community sees itself, and where it would like to go. This week’s links are to slides of talks I heard, as well as some I couldn’t attend but heard good things about. This is by no means an exhaustive list. (A few of the videos are now available; look for more on the HTML5 Dev Conf video page.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Links: HTML5 Dev Conf Edition', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-10T21:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andre Behrens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andre', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Behrens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/725d65e2-eae5-5a75-addf-57a71d097207', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725d65e2-eae5-5a75-addf-57a71d097207'}, {'abstract': 'Manet comes to life in a film about an exhibition at the Royal Academy; it will be shown on Thursday in theaters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/movies/manet-portraying-life-documentary-on-royal-academy-show.html', 'snippet': 'Manet comes to life in a film about an exhibition at the Royal Academy; it will be shown on Thursday in theaters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cultural events are reaching ever-wider audiences through various conduits these days, including HD simulcasts and screenings of operas and plays in movie theaters. Last year an art exhibition received this treatment for the first time. The result was “Leonardo Live,” an HD film tour of the acclaimed (and thronged) exhibition “Leonardo da Vinci: Painter in the Court of Milan,” a blockbuster at the National Gallery in London. It was directed by the documentary maker Phil Grabsky.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11MANET/11MANET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11MANET/11MANET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11MANET/11MANET-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 807, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11MANET/11MANET-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 807, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11MANET/11MANET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11MANET/11MANET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/arts/11MANET/11MANET-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Went to a Movie and an Art Exhibition Broke Out', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Went to a Movie and an Art Exhibition Broke Out',