ires better treatment and suicide prevention for inmates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are about 33,000 mentally ill prisoners in state prisons in California, close to 30 percent of the prison population. The number of suicides in state prisons has soared in recent years, to about 24 suicides per 100,000 inmates a year, a rate about 48 percent higher than the national average.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mental Illness in California Prisons', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mental Illness in California Prisons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karlton, Lawrence K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T01:09:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/16ee3bcb-b6c0-53fa-a8d8-e5a3118c261b', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16ee3bcb-b6c0-53fa-a8d8-e5a3118c261b'}, {'abstract': 'The problem of qualified low-income students who rarely end up at elite colleges is easy to fix and can be done at very low cost, a compelling study shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/opinion/from-poverty-to-a-top-tier-college.html', 'snippet': 'The problem of qualified low-income students who rarely end up at elite colleges is easy to fix and can be done at very low cost, a compelling study shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because educational opportunity has much to do with upward mobility, it is distressing that low-income students who qualify for top-tier colleges rarely end up there. Flummoxed by the admissions process and scared off by what they think will be unmanageable costs, many of these students settle for lesser colleges with lower graduation rates, less financial aid (which means more debt) and less marketable degrees. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Poverty to a Top-Tier College', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Poverty to a Top-Tier College', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Equal Educational Opportunities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T01:09:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dae3d47e-7aa1-5169-9c2e-7353ba8d852b', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dae3d47e-7aa1-5169-9c2e-7353ba8d852b'}, {'abstract': 'The plan for 2014 includes a troubling cut to Social Security and other better ideas that put Republicans on the spot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/opinion/president-obamas-budget.html', 'snippet': 'The plan for 2014 includes a troubling cut to Social Security and other better ideas that put Republicans on the spot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama knew full well that many Democrats and liberals would be sharply critical of his decision to propose reducing the Social Security cost-of-living adjustment, one of the centerpieces of his 2014 budget, which was released on Wednesday. In fact, he was counting on it. He wanted to show that he was willing to antagonize his supporters to get a budget compromise, putting Republicans on the spot to do the same.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The President’s Budget', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The President’s Budget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T01:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0b3fca3-3814-5725-9ae3-f1a6b2085477', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0b3fca3-3814-5725-9ae3-f1a6b2085477'}, {'abstract': 'Before a rally in Washington, Erika Andiola, a 25-year-old activist, spoke about what the movement means to her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/opinion/questions-for-a-young-immigration-rights-activist.html', 'snippet': 'Before a rally in Washington, Erika Andiola, a 25-year-old activist, spoke about what the movement means to her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The video for “"El Hielo,” or “The Ice,” by the Los Angeles-based band La Santa Cecilia, was shot with a cast of undocumented immigrants, some of them leaders in the immigrant-rights movement. One is Erika Andiola, 25, of Mesa, Ariz., a 2009 graduate of Arizona State University and one of the founders of DRM Action Coalition, a group pushing for the Dream Act, a bill to grant legal status to unauthorized immigrants who were brought to the United States as children, as she was. Ms. Andiola made national headlines in January when her mother and brother were detained by Immigration and Customs Enforcement and then released after a fierce outcry by immigrant groups. Ms. Andiola, like thousands of others, has had her deportation temporarily stayed under President Obama’s “deferred action” program. She now works as an aide to Representative Kyrsten Sinema, a Democrat of Arizona. In Washington on Wednesday, before the rally for immigrant citizenship on the law of the Capitol, Ms. Andiola spoke with The Times. The interview has been edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/opinion/editorial-qanda/editorial-qanda-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/opinion/editorial-qanda/editorial-qanda-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/opinion/editorial-qanda/editorial-qanda-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/opinion/editorial-qanda/editorial-qanda-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/opinion/editorial-qanda/editorial-qanda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/opinion/editorial-qanda/editorial-qanda-thumbSta