ing and the offer of a gift made by a late relative:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpts From the Taxi Compliments File', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taxi and Limousine Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T01:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f096fc16-39e2-5e13-9f77-4d2634aed4f0', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f096fc16-39e2-5e13-9f77-4d2634aed4f0'}, {'abstract': 'Even in ancient Sparta, apparently, people had to be advised to resist the urge to speak ill of the dead.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/taboo-on-speaking-ill-of-the-dead-widely-ignored-online-after-thatchers-death/', 'snippet': 'Even in ancient Sparta, apparently, people had to be advised to resist the urge to speak ill of the dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in ancient Sparta, apparently, people had to be advised to resist the urge to speak ill of the dead. According to Diogenes Laertius, among the precepts held dear by Chilon of Sparta was that “of the dead, nothing but good” should be spoken.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/world/europe/10lede_derry/10lede_derry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 518, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '