'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T02:49:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24ede285-7854-5a74-a942-783386f8606f', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24ede285-7854-5a74-a942-783386f8606f'}, {'abstract': 'President Abdu Rabbu Mansour Hadi announced a purge of Yemen’s military leadership on Wednesday that, if carried out, could sideline relatives of his predecessor, Ali Abdullah Saleh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/world/africa/yemen-president-set-to-purge-military-leadership.html', 'snippet': 'President Abdu Rabbu Mansour Hadi announced a purge of Yemen’s military leadership on Wednesday that, if carried out, could sideline relatives of his predecessor, Ali Abdullah Saleh.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Abdu Rabbu Mansour Hadi announced a purge of Yemen’s military leadership on Wednesday that could sideline relatives of his autocratic predecessor, Ali Abdullah Saleh, who agreed to step down in November 2011 but whose continued influence has troubled Yemen’s brittle transition. Mr. Hadi restructured the military in December, but the moves announced Wednesday were more far-reaching, removing Mr. Saleh’s son and two nephews from powerful security posts as well as from the country. Officials said that Mr. Saleh’s son, who was the head of the Republican Guard, had been appointed ambassador to the United Arab Emirates, and that the nephews had been made military attaches in Ethiopia and Germany. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen: President Set to Purge Military Leadership', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yemen: President Set to Purge Military Leadership', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadi, Abdu Rabbu Mansour', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T02:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd2b4a14-e4a1-5976-8278-e3c04b549211', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd2b4a14-e4a1-5976-8278-e3c04b549211'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s 2014 budget includes $1.4 trillion in spending cuts and tax hikes over 10 years compared with current policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/04/10/us/politics/obamas-mix-of-taxes-and-spending.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s 2014 budget includes $1.4 trillion in spending cuts and tax hikes over 10 years compared with current policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president’s 2014 budget includes $1.4 trillion in spending cuts and tax hikes over 10 years compared with current policies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Mix of Taxes and Spending', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T02:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5a6865ec-fdfe-5d3c-8ec8-82b9fcfb4095', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5a6865ec-fdfe-5d3c-8ec8-82b9fcfb4095'}, {'abstract': 'Qatar announced Wednesday that it would buy billions of dollars of Egyptian government bonds, giving critical support to President Mohamed Morsi to mend the  ailing economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/world/middleeast/egypt-qatar-offers-support-with-bond-purchase.html', 'snippet': 'Qatar announced Wednesday that it would buy billions of dollars of Egyptian government bonds, giving critical support to President Mohamed Morsi to mend the  ailing economy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Qatar’s government announced Wednesday that it would buy billions of dollars of Egyptian government bonds, giving critical support to President Mohamed Morsi as his government struggles to mend the country’s ailing economy. Sheik Hamad bin Jassem al-Thani, Qatar’s foreign minister, said his government would buy Egyptian bonds worth $3 billion and was exploring the possibility of supplying Egypt’s natural gas exports, to ease domestic shortages. Egypt relies heavily on natural gas to produce most of its electricity and neighborhoods in Cairo are suffering from occasional blackouts.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Qatar Offers Support With Bond Purchase', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Qatar Offers Support With Bond Purchase', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name