the first black woman to be a top prosecutor in Texas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eleven days after the Kaufman County district attorney and his wife were found shot to death at their home, Gov. Rick Perry named the prosecutor’s replacement on Wednesday, a local judge who has become the first black woman to be a top prosecutor in Texas. The new district attorney, Erleigh Norville Wiley, was appointed for a term to expire at the next general election, in November 2014. Ms. Wiley had been the judge of the county’s Court at Law since 2003, and had served 14 years in the Dallas County district attorney’s office. She will lead Kaufman County prosecutors at a time of widespread fear and anxiety after the killing of an assistant district attorney, Mark E. Hasse, on Jan. 31 and the deaths of the district attorney, Mike McLelland, and his wife, Cynthia, last month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Judge to Replace Slain Prosecutor', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Judge To Replace Slain Prosecutor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, District Attorneys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLelland, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLelland, Cynthia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kaufman County (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiley, Erleigh Norville', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T04:22:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/62cb4bf3-1678-58e5-abf1-49a2978742a1', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62cb4bf3-1678-58e5-abf1-49a2978742a1'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:30 P.M. (13) LA CLEMENZA DI TITO Elina Garanca performs the trouser role of Sesto, the devoted lover of the vengeful princess Vitellia (Barbara Frittoli), whom she persuades to assassinate the Roman emperor Tito (Giuseppe Filianoti) in this Metropolitan Opera performance of Mozart’s opera featuring Jean-Pierre Ponnelle’s 1984 staging. Kate Lindsey and Lucy Crowe (from right above) round out the cast as the young lovers Annio and Servilia. “In an alert, engaged performance with a well-balanced ensemble, what’s best in ‘Clemenza’ cuts to the quick with the elegance and efficacy found in all of Mozart’s finest works,” Steve Smith wrote in The New York Times when the production was revived in November. “Happily, it was just that kind of account that Harry Bicket, an English conductor closely associated with early-music groups and period-instrument players, elicited from the Met cast, chorus and orchestra.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T05:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'orga