ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6f8e64e-f7a9-5cae-aff6-37f09a0da196', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6f8e64e-f7a9-5cae-aff6-37f09a0da196'}, {'abstract': 'A woman’s diary, and a hard-hitting magazine story, cast a spotlight on the conditions at re-education-through-labor camps in China, which government officials have said they will reform.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/story-of-womens-labor-camp-abuse-unnerves-even-china/', 'snippet': 'A woman’s diary, and a hard-hitting magazine story, cast a spotlight on the conditions at re-education-through-labor camps in China, which government officials have said they will reform.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:50 a.m. | Updated BEIJING — In September 2011, 62-year-old Wang Guilan walked out of the Masanjia re-education through labor camp in China’s northeastern Liaoning province with a rolled-up diary, written on waterproof material, hidden in her vagina. Guards had searched her before she left but had missed the document, by a fellow inmate called Liu Hua, recounting the torture taking place in the camp on a daily basis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/world/americas/11MasanjiaRDV/11MasanjiaRDV-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/world/americas/11MasanjiaRDV/11MasanjiaRDV-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 613}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/world/americas/11MasanjiaRDV/11MasanjiaRDV-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/wo