2a-4ae86bc2546c', 'word_count': 992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba423f03-734b-5bd7-9b2a-4ae86bc2546c'}, {'abstract': 'The orchestra said on Thursday it would tour the country from May 29 to June 10 and offer master classes, coaching sessions and workshops.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/philadelphia-orchestra-to-tour-china/', 'snippet': 'The orchestra said on Thursday it would tour the country from May 29 to June 10 and offer master classes, coaching sessions and workshops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Philadelphia Orchestra is holding firm to plans for regular, lengthy visits to China. The orchestra said on Thursday it would tour the country from May 29 to June 10 and offer master classes, coaching sessions and workshops with young music students and local professional orchestra musicians. The orchestra made a similar visit last May, saying it would become a regular affair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philadelphia Orchestra to Tour China', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Orchestra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T07:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f31226b5-07d0-5e85-9f3a-dd167b9d91fc', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f31226b5-07d0-5e85-9f3a-dd167b9d91fc'}, {'abstract': 'Deforestation, increased flooding and climate change make the soil sandier, but some crops thrive.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/in-assam-searching-for-new-crops-and-farming-methods-for-depleted-soil/', 'snippet': 'Deforestation, increased flooding and climate change make the soil sandier, but some crops thrive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boralapar, ASSAM — For generations, the annual monsoon cycle blessed the upper Assam village of Boralapar with ideal conditions for paddy farming. Moderate annual flooding of the Dorpang River, a small tributary of the Brahmaputra River, enhanced the rich, loamy soil with a yearly booster dose of river-borne nutrients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/world/asia/11-farmer-IndiaInk/11-farmer-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/world/asia/11-farmer-IndiaInk/11-farmer-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/world/asia/11-farmer-IndiaInk/11-farmer-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/world/asia/11-farmer-IndiaInk/11-farmer-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/world/asia/11-farmer-IndiaInk/11-farmer-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/11/world/asia/11-farmer-IndiaInk/11-farmer-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'