such an important gift for the Metropolitan Museum of Art?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “A Billion-Dollar Gift Gives the Met a New Perspective (Cubist),” Carol Vogel writes about one of the most significant gifts in the history of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/met-cap1/met-cap1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/met-cap1/met-cap1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 910}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/met-cap1/met-cap1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/met-cap1/met-cap1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1318, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/met-cap1/met-cap1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/met-cap1/met-cap1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/arts/met-cap1/met-cap1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trove of Cubist Art Will Go to the Met', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T08:42:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fcd783a-0422-57bb-87d2-9d6ee3b3f079', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fcd783a-0422-57bb-87d2-9d6ee3b3f079'}, {'abstract': 'In his budget, President Obama should have made a stronger case for what he would like to accomplish, then found the means to pay for it, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/the-flaw-in-obamas-budget-approach/', 'snippet': 'In his budget, President Obama should have made a stronger case for what he would like to accomplish, then found the means to pay for it, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, former chief economist of the International Monetary Fund, is the Ronald A. Kurtz Professor of Entrepreneurship at the M.I.T. Sloan School of Management and co-author of “White House Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Flaw in Obama’s Budget Approach', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0265bc61-f83d-5a49-ae11-f2101cfa8338', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0265bc61-f83d-5a49-ae11-f2101cfa8338'}, {'abstract': 'A new documentary by Sebastian Junger explores the life and work of his friend and colleague Tim Hetherington.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/tim-hetherington-in-film-and-indelible/', 'snippet': 'A new documentary by Sebastian Junger explores the life and work of his friend and colleague Tim Hetherington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sebastian Junger and Tim Hetherington basked in the celebratory spotlight the night of the 2011 Academy Awards, where their groundbreaking film “Restrepo” was in the running for Best Documentary. While “Restrepo” did not take top honors, it made a powerful mark as one of the few films to delve deeply into the lives of men at war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Hetherington, Indelible on Film', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hetherington, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Junger, Sebastian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T09:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kamber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kamber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1af582fe-ba02-5f3b-9033-d670899712cf', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1af582fe-ba02-5f3b-9033-d670899712cf'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian rebels can’t agree on how to govern, and so Aleppo has two rival legal systems, each controlling its own terrain and backed by different militias.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/a-tale-of-two-courts/', 'snippet': 'Syrian rebels can’t agree on how to govern, and so Aleppo has two rival legal systems, each controlling its own terrain and backed by different militias.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALEPPO, Syria — “In this court, we just fight Bashar al-Assad,” said Marwan Qaid, the gray-haired, clean-shaven chief justice of the Mohokum al Qada al Motahed, or Integrated Judicial Council. He drew on a cigarette and smiled behind a desk piled high with legal papers. “But in the Shariah Authority, they also fight the infidels. And in their eyes, we are infidels.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tale of Two Courts', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shariah (Islamic Law)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T09:02:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthieu Aikins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthieu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aikins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7866b191-e60c-5fb6-81e5-490f4df3c197', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7866b191-e60c-5fb6-81e5-490f4df3c197'}, {'abstract': 'Have you ever been to summer camp? What was your experie