ters on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/vonn-makes-her-masters-debut/', 'snippet': 'Lindsey Vonn, who has been dating Tiger Woods, was at the Masters on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUGUSTA, Ga. – The Olympic ski racing champion Lindsey Vonn waited at a table on the Augusta National Golf Club veranda next to the putting practice green Thursday morning as Tiger Woods completed his final warm-up swings before his 10:45 a.m. tee time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/sports/golf/12vonn/12vonn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/sports/golf/12vonn/12vonn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/sports/golf/12vonn/12vonn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/sports/golf/12vonn/12vonn-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/sports/golf/12vonn/12vonn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/12/sports/golf/12vonn/12vonn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/sports/golf/12vonn/12vonn-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vonn Makes Her Masters Debut', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vonn, Lindsey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Augusta National Golf Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T14:59:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ebf5cf0-7239-576a-b9af-5c6ced5f1c51', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ebf5cf0-7239-576a-b9af-5c6ced5f1c51'}, {'abstract': 'The success of Germany’s top players and clubs in the Champions League may soon highlight the lack of it for Germany’s national team coach, Joachim Löw.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/why-bayern-and-dortmund-success-might-be-bad-for-joachim-low/', 'snippet': 'The success of Germany’s top players and clubs in the Champions League may soon highlight the lack of it for Germany’s national team coach, Joachim Löw.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last weekend Bayern Munich won the Bundesliga title. That in itself wasn’t particularly surprising: the newly crowned Deutscher Meisters have claimed the so-called salad dish trophy 22 times, pushing their collection of national championships to a dominating 23.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Bayern and Dortmund Success Might Be Bad for Joachim Löw', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayern Munich (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Borussia Dortmund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Bienkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bienkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c05adad6-3305-5180-afd3-6d1067b21e50', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c05adad6-3305-5180-afd3-6d1067b21e50'}, {'abstract': 'Designer Sam Baron reinterprets traditional European design with a French sense of humor.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/a-fine-feather/', 'snippet': 'Designer Sam Baron reinterprets traditional European design with a French sense of humor.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In “From Europe With Love ,” opening May 2 at the Cristina Grajales gallery in SoHo, the Paris-based designer Sam Baron reinterprets traditional European design with what he calls “a kind of French sense of humor.” He applies a champagne-colored lacquer to Louis XVI-style cabinets, and deconstructs the traditional process of painting these bisque porcelain birds made by the venerable Portuguese house Vista Alegre.Through July 12; 10 Greene Street. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fine Feather', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baron, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T15:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd5e0a28-36ac-5cae-b95c-4ceb46dd3cc2', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd5e0a28-36ac-5cae-b95c-4ceb46dd3cc2'}, {'abstract': 'Tell us where you find peace and tranquillity in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/where-do-you-find-quiet-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Tell us where you find peace and tranquillity in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where do you go to find peace in this boisterous city? With eight million New Yorkers and 50 million tourists a year all packed into 301 square miles, is there a special park bench, riverside fishing spot or underused historic site where you go to cherish the sound of silence?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/quiet-cityroom/quiet-cityroom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/quiet-cityroom/quiet-cityroom-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/quiet-cityroom/quiet-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/quiet-cityroom/quiet-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/quiet-cityroom/quiet-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/quiet-cityroom/quiet-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/nyregion/quiet-cityroom/quiet-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Do You Find Quiet in New York?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T15:11:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d0ea915-b32c-5800-8bc6-7bbdb85702cf', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d0ea915-b32c-5800-8bc6-7bbdb85702cf'}, {'abstract': 'An Anolis tigrinus moved across a tree branch in Venezuela.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/100000002166473/the-tiger-anole.html', 'snippet': 'An Anolis tigrinus moved across a tree branch in Venezuela.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Anolis tigrinus moved across a tree branch in Venezuela.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/science/video-saw-lizard-clip/video-saw-lizard-clip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/science/video-saw-lizard-clip/video-saw-lizard-clip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/science/video-saw-lizard-clip/video-saw-lizard-clip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/11/science/video-saw-lizard-clip/video-saw-lizard-clip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/science/video-saw-lizard-clip/video-saw-lizard-clip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tiger Anole', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T15:13:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'Jonathan Losos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Losos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/74413151-9f68-5ab8-b5b5-f3f8301477db', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/74413151-9f68-5ab8-b5b5-f3f8301477db'}, {'abstract': 'Just because he’s taking some shots from the left doesn’t mean Obama has sold out.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/obamas-progressive-budget/', 'snippet': 'Just because he’s taking some shots from the left doesn’t mean Obama has sold out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing to be said about the budget President Obama delivered this week is that, at last, he has one. Until now his answer to the brutal specifics of the Republicans’ law-of-the-jungle budget has been a slogan – “a balanced approach.” Now he has provided (mostly) hard, credible numbers to show what he means by that slogan. I wish he’d produced such a document a year ago and campaigned on it, which would strengthen his claim to a popular mandate. But give the guy credit. It was time to put up or shut up, and he put up. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Progressive Budget', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T15:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbf064ce-5311-563d-ba12-1d485aec692d', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbf064ce-5311-563d-ba12-1d485aec692d'}, {'abstract': 'Going into the field and finding a blur of activity: lizards eating, scratching, pooping, posturing, courting and almost constantly on the move.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/an-embarrassment-of-anoles/', 'snippet': 'Going into the field and finding a blur of activity: lizards eating, scratching, pooping, posturing, courting and almost constantly on the move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Losos, professor and curator of herpetology at Harvard’s Museum of Comparative Zoology, writes from Colombia, where he is studying the biodiversity of anole lizards, an evolutionarily successful group that has produced 400 species throughout Central and South America and the Caribbean islands. For m