er': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfbd789c-2155-5745-8fca-4e33be901730', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfbd789c-2155-5745-8fca-4e33be901730'}, {'abstract': 'People expressing their opinion on the Internet are not exactly in short supply. But there is an increasing sense that the time is ripe to develop and implement technology that allows for commenting across sites. Maybe it will make us better people. Or drive us crazy.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/speak-up-the-internet-cant-hear-you/', 'snippet': 'People expressing their opinion on the Internet are not exactly in short supply. But there is an increasing sense that the time is ripe to develop and implement technology that allows for commenting across sites. Maybe it will make us better peopl...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Internet might have looked very different than it does today. When Marc Andreessen and Eric Bina were building Mosaic, the browser that practically created the Web in 1993, they included the ability to annotate any page. Discussions immediately sprang up. But they quickly realized that the server to host the annotations would have had to scale to enormous size, which was not practical. So they took the feature out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/technology/11bits-iannotate/11bits-iannotate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 285, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/technology/11bits-iannotate/11bits-iannotate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 285}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/technology/11bits-iannotate/11bits-iannotate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 1024, '