8b0c735-8174-5e21-8d2f-4c15b6dd4c4b', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b0c735-8174-5e21-8d2f-4c15b6dd4c4b'}, {'abstract': 'The resurrected Dance Theater of Harlem returned to the stage with a bold choice, Balanchine’s “Agon,” and three other works in a mixed program at Jazz at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/arts/dance/dance-theater-of-harlem-at-the-rose-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The resurrected Dance Theater of Harlem returned to the stage with a bold choice, Balanchine’s “Agon,” and three other works in a mixed program at Jazz at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Founded in 1969 to dispel the myth that blacks couldn’t dance classical ballet, Dance Theater of Harlem toured internationally for decades as a shining symbol that they could. For decades there were also administrative and financial troubles, and in 2004, mounting debts forced the troupe to go on hiatus. Now it has returned, and on Wednesday at the Rose Theater at Jazz at Lincoln Center the nervousness was palpable. Everyone wants this company to succeed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DTH/12DTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 303, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DTH/12DTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 303}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DTH/12DTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 518, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DTH/12DTH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1036, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp