ern, who purchased two for herself, despite concerns that our outfielders “will blend in with the grass.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/magazine/11-softball-tshirt/11-softball-tshirt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/11/magazine/11-softball-tshirt/11-softball-tshirt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/magazine/11-softball-tshirt/11-softball-tshirt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/magazine/11-softball-tshirt/11-softball-tshirt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/magazine/11-softball-tshirt/11-softball-tshirt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/11/magazine/11-softball-tshirt/11-softball-tshirt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/11/magazine/11-softball-tshirt/11-softball-tshirt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now That’s What We Call a Softball Jersey', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T21:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4135735f-d718-5622-8961-3162cc16a3b3', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4135735f-d718-5622-8961-3162cc16a3b3'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s Nathaniel Popper discusses Bitcoin, the online currency that has attracted a number of investors, including Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/timescast-bitcoin-has-real-world-investors/', 'snippet': 'The Times’s Nathaniel Popper discusses Bitcoin, the online currency that has attracted a number of investors, including Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times’s Nathaniel Popper discusses Bitcoin, the online currency that has attracted a number of investors, including Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast: Bitcoin Has Real-World Investors', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T21:20:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36f2b256-dfda-5359-a835-83ddce90e6a5', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36f2b256-dfda-5359-a835-83ddce90e6a5'}, {'abstract': '“Disconnect,” with Jason Bateman and Hope Davis, offers a montage of overlapping stories about thievery, humiliation and exposed secrets on the Internet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/movies/disconnect-directed-by-henry-alex-rubin.html', 'snippet': '“Disconnect,” with Jason Bateman and Hope Davis, offers a montage of overlapping stories about thievery, humiliation and exposed secrets on the Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jittery characters who scuttle through the three stories that make up “Disconnect” are struggling to make their way through today’s treacherous cyberwilderness. Some are predators, others prey. Naïve travelers who venture into territory taken over by upstart tribes of technological outlaws risk being ambushed, fleeced and humiliated. Law enforcement is often helpless to catch up with tricksters adept at staying ahead of the game. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN/DISCONNECT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN/DISCONNECT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN/DISCONNECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN/DISCONNECT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DISCONNECT1_SPAN/DISCONNECT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Horror at Every Turn of a Dark Cyberjungle', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Horror at Every Turn Of a Dark Cyberjungle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bateman, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'DisConnect (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Marc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Henry-Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T21:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7463db2a-3c73-5716-8e86-92d8bf2489af', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7463db2a-3c73-5716-8e86-92d8bf2489af'}, {'abstract': 'Giosetta Fioroni’s solo show of films and silvery works at the Drawing Center is a reminder of how little Americans know of Pop Art in Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/arts/design/giosetta-fioroni-largento-at-the-drawing-center.html', 'snippet': 'Giosetta Fioroni’s solo show of films and silvery works at the Drawing Center is a reminder of how little Americans know of Pop Art in Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Giosetta Fioroni: L’Argento” proves that the field of postwar Italian art, though crowded at the moment, is far from exhausted. This show at the Drawing Center complements recent gallery exhibitions of Lucio Fontana, Piero Manzoni, Giorgio Griffa, Gianni Colombo and Luigi Ghirri, not to mention museum surveys of Michelangelo Pistoletto and Alighiero Boetti, introducing us to the only female member of the School of the Piazza del Popolo (named for a popular Roman artists’ hangout).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DRAWING/DRAWING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 873, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DRAWING/DRAWING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 873}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DRAWING/DRAWING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DRAWING/DRAWING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DRAWING/DRAWING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DRAWING/DRAWING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DRAWING/DRAWING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Detached Look at Pop Art From Post-Fascist Italy', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Detached Look at Pop Art From Post-Fascist Italy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drawing Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drawing Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T21:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5045dd2a-79e6-58e8-9f1b-480ba7e2faeb', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5045dd2a-79e6-58e8-9f1b-480ba7e2faeb'}, {'abstract': 'In Ken Loach’s “Angels’ Share,” a hot-headed hooligan from Glasgow’s underclass turns out to have an extraordinary talent for identifying different varieties of whisky.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/movies/the-angels-share-a-comedy-by-ken-loach.html', 'snippet': 'In Ken Loach’s “Angels’ Share,” a hot-headed hooligan from Glasgow’s underclass turns out to have an extraordinary talent for identifying different varieties of whisky.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Angels’ Share,” the twinkly title of Ken Loach’s new comedy, is slang for the roughly 2 percent of malt whisky that evaporates while it ages in a cask. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ANGELS_SPAN/ANGELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ANGELS_SPAN/ANGELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': 