': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc54b5e-8f45-542f-849b-44658ea431bb'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s three great halls, at Grand Central Terminal, the American Museum of Natural History and the Metropolitan Museum of Art, each have an artistic side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/realestate/when-murals-were-in-flower.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s three great halls, at Grand Central Terminal, the American Museum of Natural History and the Metropolitan Museum of Art, each have an artistic side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great halls of Grand Central, the American Museum of Natural History and the Metropolitan Museum of Art each present different painted faces: Grand Central has a swath of the heavens at nighttime, redone 15 years ago; the natural history museum has murals of the life of Theodore Roosevelt, restored last fall; and the Metropolitan Museum, well ... where are the murals, anyway?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/10/realestate/10FYI2/streets-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/06/10/realestate/10FYI2/streets-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/10/realestate/10FYI2/streets-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/10/realestate/10FYI2/streets-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1281, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/06/10/realestate/10FYI2/14STREETS