er, Howard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gioni, Massimiliano', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edmondson, William', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Traylor, Bill', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonovitz, Jill', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonovitz, Sheldon', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:09:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/54a02f35-adb7-55be-8d9c-b0e9d48c3689', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54a02f35-adb7-55be-8d9c-b0e9d48c3689'}, {'abstract': 'A selected, critical guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/arts/design/museum-and-gallery-listings-for-april-12-18.html', 'snippet': 'A selected, critical guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum and Gallery Listings for April 12-18', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:10:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f7cfdf7-3c33-5104-b721-3ee4f0648919', 'word_count': 5029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f7cfdf7-3c33-5104-b721-3ee4f0648919'}, {'abstract': '“Da Vinci’s Demons,” a new series on Starz, casts Leonardo as an action hero and sleuth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/arts/television/da-vincis-demons-on-starz.html', 'snippet': '“Da Vinci’s Demons,” a new series on Starz, casts Leonardo as an action hero and sleuth.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Da Vinci’s Demons” proposes a new definition of Renaissance man. Painting, drawing and inventing are no longer sufficient. To be the hero of a 21st-century pay-cable historical drama, Leonardo must also fight like a mixed-martial-arts star, bed the boss’s mistress (the boss being Lorenzo de’ Medici) and solve crimes like a combination of Sherlock Holmes and Gil Grissom from “CSI.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DEMONS/12DEMONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DEMONS/12DEMONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DEMONS/12DEMONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DEMONS/12DEMONS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DEMONS/12DEMONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DEMONS/12DEMONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12DEMONS/12DEMONS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The He-Man Who Gave Mona Lisa That Smile', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The He-Man Who Gave Mona Lisa That Smile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goyer, David S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7af9ca-dfe4-5030-ae13-8fb12213ad9f', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7af9ca-dfe4-5030-ae13-8fb12213ad9f'}, {'abstract': 'Suggestions on how to deal with a promotion denied, a dishonest roommate, unwanted nicknames and a hastily discarded job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/fashion/take-the-long-view.html', 'snippet': 'Suggestions on how to deal with a promotion denied, a dishonest roommate, unwanted nicknames and a hastily discarded job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During a job review, my boss told me I was in line for promotion when my supervisor moved up. Well, my supervisor left. But the boss promoted a woman who joined the company after me rather than giving me the job as promised. He said this woman will make a better manager than I would. (I’m a man.) I think this is reverse-sexism, but I’m not sure what to do about it. Talk to human resources, my boss’s boss or just eat it? J. D.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Take the Long View', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Take the Long View', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:13:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/d357279a-cecf-53d3-a245-a27f063edffb', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d357279a-cecf-53d3-a245-a27f063edffb'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural events in New York for children, teenagers and families.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/arts/spare-times-for-children-for-april-12-18.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural events in New York for children, teenagers and families.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘BEAUTY AND THE BEAST’', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Children for April 12-18', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times For Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:16:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurel Graeber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graeber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/43581146-b474-5215-b535-62c26481371e', 'word_count': 4340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43581146-b474-5215-b535-62c26481371e'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s new budget, while admirable in many respects, comes up short in one big way.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/11/deficit-reduction-minus-the-reduction/', 'snippet': 'The president’s new budget, while admirable in many respects, comes up short in one big way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s new budget, released on Wednesday, is stuffed with constructive ideas. It bravely outlines concrete steps to begin fixing Social Security. It flouts today’s all-deficit-cutting, all-the-time mentality with important proposals for fresh spending on infrastructure and universal prekindergarten education. It includes detailed plans to close tax loopholes and raise needed revenues from the wealthy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deficit Reduction, Minus the Reduction', 'kicker': 'Steven Rattner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:16:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Rattner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rattner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f30beef9-c5c7-5619-a9f4-275a62f4b875', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f30beef9-c5c7-5619-a9f4-275a62f4b875'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Novak, a writer for “The Office” and one of the show’s stars, is expected to publish the first book next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/business/media/bj-novak-actor-and-writer-signs-two-book-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Novak, a writer for “The Office” and one of the show’s stars, is expected to publish the first book next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The comedian, actor and writer B.J. Novak has sold two books to Knopf in a seven-figure deal. The first book, a work of fiction, is expected to be published in 2014, Nicholas Latimer, a spokesman for Knopf, said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'B.J. Novak, Actor and Writer, Signs Two-Book Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Actor and Writer\r\nSigns Two-Book Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knopf, Alfred A, Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Novak, B J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Office (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:18:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d76f0413-a430-5a03-aa15-48497f6b8438', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d76f0413-a430-5a03-aa15-48497f6b8438'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of walking tours, cultural events and more in the New York area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/arts/spare-times-for-april-12-18.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of walking tours, cultural events and more in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘Passages Through the Fire: Jews and the Civil War’ (through Aug. 11) It was not uncommon during the Civil War for family members to take opposing sides. Of the five sons of Abraham Jonas, who served as postmaster general of Quincy, Ill., and his wife, Louisa, four sided with the Confederacy — though one brother later became a Union soldier. The only one supporting the Union from the start was the youngest, Edward Jonas, above right, in an undated image.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for April 12-18', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/baeefe82-585c-56fc-9d93-6e04e122d0e7', 'word_count': 3266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baeefe82-585c-56fc-9d93-6e04e122d0e7'}, {'abstract': 'Our relationship was not an obvious one, but neither of us liked the obvious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/fashion/health-scare-turns-out-to-be-a-blessing.html', 'snippet': 'Our relationship was not an obvious one, but neither of us liked the obvious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dude was a doctor who wanted to leave medicine. We met almost 20 years ago, when he applied to a writing fellowship program at the movie studio where I was an executive. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14SUBMODERNLOVE_SPAN/0414-SUBMODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14SUBMODERNLOVE_SPAN/0414-SUBMODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 331}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14SUBMODERNLOVE_SPAN/0414-SUBMODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14SUBMODERNLOVE_SPAN/0414-SUBMODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1130, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14SUBMODERNLOVE_SPAN/0414-SUBMODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14SUBMODERNLOVE_SPAN/0414-SUBMODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14SUBMODERNLOVE_SPAN/0414-SUBMODERNLOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite the Losses, So Much Gained', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite the Losses, So Much Gained', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Keith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a38fe3fa-6e99-53bd-96d0-84c74b659d63', 'word_count': 1518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a38fe3fa-6e99-53bd-96d0-84c74b659d63'}, {'abstract': '“Antiviral” is the first feature film directed by Brandon Cronenberg, the son of David Cronenberg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/movies/antiviral-directed-by-brandon-cronenberg.html', 'snippet': '“Antiviral” is the first feature film directed by Brandon Cronenberg, the son of David Cronenberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wormy apple doesn’t fall far from the rotting tree. In saying that, I don’t mean to cast aspersions on the Cronenberg family bloodline but only to point out that in his first feature, “Antiviral,” the 33-year-old Brandon Cronenberg exhibits the same obsession with mutilation and infection as his father, David, did in movies like “Crash” and “The Fly.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Autographs Are Far Less of a Mess', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Autographs Are Far Less Of a Mess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cronenberg, Brandon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a23d636-6e10-5dc6-942a-e0f9639a0017', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a23d636-6e10-5dc6-942a-e0f9639a0017'}, {'abstract': 'In “Arcadia,” a film directed by Olivia Silver that opens on Friday in Brooklyn, three children grow ever more suspicious about their father’s intentions during a family road trip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/movies/arcadia-directed-by-olivia-silver.html', 'snippet': 'In “Arcadia,” a film directed by Olivia Silver that opens on Friday in Brooklyn, three children grow ever more suspicious about their father’s intentions during a family road trip.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Arcadia” opens at dusk with four people slipping out of a house like thieves. As soon as they climb into the car it becomes evident that the man and the three children with him are related. Yet when one of the kids, 12-year-old Greta (Ryan Simpkins), pauses to look at some family photographs, the air stirs. Something has happened here, but it takes time — along with many miles, a few fights, some misunderstandings and a young awakening — to know what. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ARCADIA_SPAN/12ARCADIA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ARCADIA_SPAN/12ARCADIA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 312}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ARCADIA_SPAN/12ARCADIA_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ARCADIA_SPAN/12ARCADIA_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 929, 'width': 1787, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ARCADIA_SPAN/12ARCADIA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ARCADIA_SPAN/12ARCADIA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12ARCADIA_SPAN/12ARCADIA_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eyeing That Empty Seat', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eyeing That Empty Seat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Arcadia (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Olivia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-11T22:42:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/16885672-020a-5436-87ab-faf14defcb9f', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16885672-020a-5436-87ab-faf14defcb9f'}, {'abstract': 'In its 12th season the Tribeca Film Festival, which begins Wednesday and includes the premieres of 53 features, has woven itself into the fabric of the New York cultural schedule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/movies/tribeca-film-festival.html', 'snippet': 'In its 12th season the Tribeca Film Festival, which begins Wednesday and includes the premieres of 53 features, has woven itself into the fabric of the New York cultural schedule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In any life there are moments of acute awareness when you suddenly realize the degree to which you’ve grown up. The Tribeca Film Festival, which begins its 12th season on Wednesday, is experiencing such a flash.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12TRIBECA_SPAN/12TRIBECA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12TRIBECA_SPAN/12TRIBECA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12TRIBECA_SPAN/12TRIBECA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12TRIBECA_SPAN/12TRIBECA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1081, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12TRIBECA_SPAN/12TRIBECA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12TRIBECA_SPAN/12TRIBECA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12TRIBECA_SPAN/12TRIBECA_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Festival Now Comfortable in Its Skin', 'kicker': 'C