ournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Augusta National Golf Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leishman, Marc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Sergio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T01:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/198a52e0-5688-5f98-b724-0591efde3b15', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/198a52e0-5688-5f98-b724-0591efde3b15'}, {'abstract': 'In a pilot program, the Police Department has distributed some smartphones to its officers, allowing them to look up suspects’ criminal histories and verify their identification.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/nyregion/new-tool-for-police-officers-quick-access-to-information.html', 'snippet': 'In a pilot program, the Police Department has distributed some smartphones to its officers, allowing them to look up suspects’ criminal histories and verify their identification.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the officers walked up to the entrance of a Harlem housing project, a loose knot of people out front scattered into the damp, dark night and a few lingerers cast cold stares at the officers. One of the officers reached into his pocket and pulled out the newest tool in the Police Department’s crime-fighting arsenal: a smartphone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/nyregion/NYPD-1/NYPD-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLa