Ed', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/896d29e0-d765-508a-b760-0dd0912d806b', 'word_count': 11, 'uri': 'nyt://article/896d29e0-d765-508a-b760-0dd0912d806b'}, {'abstract': 'This isn’t hard, folks.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/simple-natural-goodness/', 'snippet': 'This isn’t hard, folks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the baffling aspects of economic debate during this Lesser Depression, or so it seems to me, is the apparent urge of many economists to shy away from straightforward conclusions, the urge to make the simple complicated and the clear blurry. That’s certainly what seems to be happening in this round-robin from me, to Cowen/Andolfatto, to Brad DeLong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Simple Natural Goodness', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T11:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2386e6e-1576-508f-9d94-19dc2969da79', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2386e6e-1576-508f-9d94-19dc2969da79'}, {'abstract': 'Driving in a private vehicle through the streets of Delhi, in broad daylight, is no guarantee that a woman will escape harassment.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/women-drivers-in-delhi-face-frequent-sexual-harassment/', 'snippet': 'Driving in a private vehicle through the streets of Delhi, in broad daylight, is no guarantee that a woman will escape harassment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — In February, I was driving my car through a busy street in Connaught Place when a taxi driver began honking his horn at me. It was around noon, and honking is hardly unusual for chaotic Delhi traffic, but the driver kept angrily pounding on his horn. The noise ended only after the taxi had pulled beside me at a red light. Then the driver angled his car to block mine. I was stunned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/asia/09-female-driver-IndiaInk/09-female-driver-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/09/world/asia/09-female-driver-IndiaInk/09-female-driver-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/asia/09-female-driver-IndiaInk/09-female-driver-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 572, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/asia/09-female-driver-IndiaInk/09-female-driver-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/09/world/asia/09-female-driver-IndiaInk/09-female-driver-IndiaInk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/09/world/asia/09-female-driver-IndiaInk/09-female-driver-IndiaInk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag