a 22 percent increase in first-quarter profit on Friday as the bank, which is the nation’s largest home lender, continued to notch record gains even while its mortgage machine slowed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wells Fargo Profit Rises 22%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stumpf, John G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T12:33:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b44d60ac-1fba-5e5b-8ca1-ff83b1aec042', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b44d60ac-1fba-5e5b-8ca1-ff83b1aec042'}, {'abstract': 'Street traffic is exploding in Cambodia. And no one can keep up.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/development-and-its-discontent/', 'snippet': 'Street traffic is exploding in Cambodia. And no one can keep up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHNOM PENH — In 2010, the Cambodian government unveiled with great fanfare the country’s first traffic overpass. The $6 million project — lit with a futuristic blue neon swoosh — was intended to ease congestion where a major boulevard that runs north-south through Phnom Penh intersects with twin bridges that cross the Bassac River, just to the east. Prime Minister Hun Sen called the Sky Bridge Project a “great achievement” and proclaimed that it would end traffic problems in the area.It wasn’t long before commuters discovered a catch: By making it easier for motorists traveling north-south to keep going straight, the new overpass made it impossible for them to turn left onto the intersecting east-west road. The result is a mess. Now, drivers heading south who want to cross the river must first take a right and drive away for several hundred meters and then make a U-turn and head back. And motorists heading north are forced to turn right, which necessarily takes them onto the bridges — meaning that they are forced to cross the river, turn around and cross the river again. Congestion in the area is worse than ever, and the traffic more dangerous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Development and Its Discontent', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T12:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Wallace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2affd493-02d9-5f61-820e-8bd51aebe9a4', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2affd493-02d9-5f61-820e-8bd51aebe9a4'}, {'abstract': 'Huong Hoang, who uses the name Junie Hoang in her film work, said she had been exposed to possible age discrimination.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/actress-loses-suit-over-sites-posting-of-her-age/', 'snippet': 'Huong Hoang, who uses the name Junie Hoang in her film work, said she had been exposed to possible age discrimination.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A jury in Seattle has found against Huong Hoang, the actress who sued the Internet Movie Database and its parent company, Amazon, for posting her age without her permission. The verdict, reached in Federal Court on Thursday, rejected a breach of contract claim against IMDB by Ms. Hoang, who uses the name Junie Hoang in her screen work. Marsha J. Pechman, a judge in the United States District Court for the Western District of Washington, had already dropped Amazon from the case, and dismissed other claims. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Actress Loses Suit Over Site’s Posting of Her Age', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoang, Junie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pechman, Marsha J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internet Movie Database', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T12:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de87df14-38fd-5a19-9e0d-c9b53b326380', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de87df14-38fd-5a19-9e0d-c9b53b326380'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/opinion-repo