-9433-a46c7e5760ba'}, {'abstract': 'Many parents prefer to “redshirt” a young child by holding her out of kindergarten for an extra year. This reader has the opposite problem — her just-shy-of-the-cut-off child is ready to go.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/ready-for-kindergarten-and-missing-the-cutoff/', 'snippet': 'Many parents prefer to “redshirt” a young child by holding her out of kindergarten for an extra year. This reader has the opposite problem — her just-shy-of-the-cut-off child is ready to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After reading “Kindergarten ‘Redshirting’ Gets Tougher in N.Y.C., With Repercussions,” a reader wrote to say she had the “opposite problem.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ready for Kindergarten, and Missing the Cutoff', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T13:35:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb084a7-1099-5d82-9134-98a852e43fa1', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb084a7-1099-5d82-9134-98a852e43fa1'}, {'abstract': 'The old stuff doesn’t work anymore. And that’s why I want to hire people who are trying to create new things.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/debating-the-merits-of-hiring-great-recession-graduates/', 'snippet': 'The old stuff doesn’t work anymore. And that’s why I want to hire people who are trying to create new things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intrigued. Inspired. Insulted. I summoned all three feelings as I glanced through the responses to my last post, “Why I Like to Hire Great Recession Graduates.” In the post, I talked about how many recent graduates — tempered by the tough economy they have experienced — are making excellent employees in fast-growth companies where a hunger to work and a will to win override the need for entitlements, praise and corner offices. In fact, I suggested, these recent graduates have adjusted to the new reality much better than some of their parents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debating the Merits of Hiring Great Recession Graduates', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T13:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cliff Oxford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cliff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oxford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e820a3aa-6b04-5187-999a-6fbc4fe9be76', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e820a3aa-6b04-5187-999a-6fbc4fe9be76'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers have been working across party lines on legislation advocates say could help keep killers like the gunman in Newtown, Conn., from slipping through the cracks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/us/politics/senators-make-bipartisan-push-for-mental-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers have been working across party lines on legislation advocates say could help keep killers like the gunman in Newtown, Conn., from slipping through the cracks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — While the Senate has been consumed with a divisive debate over expanded background checks for gun buyers, lawmakers have been quietly working across party lines on legislation that advocates say could help prevent killers like Adam Lanza, the gunman in the Newtown, Conn., massacre, from slipping through the cracks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Gun Debate, No Rift on Better Care for Mentally Ill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Gun Debate, Accord Emerges On Mental Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Alliance on Mental Illness', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lanza, Adam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stabenow, Debbie', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T14:13:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be3a7df5-bfea-5e82-85cd-88c46b9cadf7', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be3a7df5-bfea-5e82-85cd-88c46b9cadf7'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve has been effective in holding inflation to a target. But it is not clear whether fighting inflation and fostering job creation can be effectively pursued in tandem.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/the-impact-if-any-of-the-feds-dual-mandate/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve has been effective in holding inflation to a target. But it is not clear whether fighting inflation and fostering job creation can be effectively pursued in tandem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Rosengren, the president of the Federal Reserve Bank of Boston, made a compelling case on Friday morning that the Fed’s dual mandate doesn’t really matter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Impact (if Any) of the Fed’s Dual Mandate', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosengren, Eric S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T14:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f3be688-4845-51f9-a39