'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pocono Raceway', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T16:29:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d687d744-6c75-50c1-a0eb-7ae471899b00', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d687d744-6c75-50c1-a0eb-7ae471899b00'}, {'abstract': 'Hayley Williams of the group Paramore says her influences include Debbie Harry of Blondie and Elvis Presley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/arts/music/hayley-williams-of-paramore-on-her-new-album.html', 'snippet': 'Hayley Williams of the group Paramore says her influences include Debbie Harry of Blondie and Elvis Presley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tennessee pop-punk band Paramore, fronted by Hayley Williams, is attempting a reintroduction. It has to. Its self-titled fourth album, just released on Fueled by Ramen, follows two years of turmoil in which the brothers Josh and Zac Farro, the nine-year-old band’s founding guitarist and drummer, quit. On his blog Josh Farro called Paramore “a manufactured product of a major label” and accused Ms. Williams of hogging the spotlight. She stood up for her band and its authenticity on MTV. (Zac Farro later said his brother had regrets about the post.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN/14PLAYLIST1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Growing Up on a Musical Diet of Presley and Blondie', 'kicker': 'Guest Playlist | Hayley Williams', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growing Up on a Musical Diet of Presley and Blondie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramore (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Hayley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T16:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdc40439-3824-58d4-a066-aa29712389c6', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdc40439-3824-58d4-a066-aa29712389c6'}, {'abstract': 'How Montgomery C. Meigs won the Civil War, one load of supplies at a time.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/americas-quartermaster/', 'snippet': 'How Montgomery C. Meigs won the Civil War, one load of supplies at a time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In July 1862, George B. McClellan’s Peninsula Campaign ended and Union forces slowly began their trek back from Virginia’s backwaters, stunned by their losses. But if it was a failure on the battlefield, as a logistical operation, it was a stunning success, one of the great organizational feats of human history, all thanks to one man: Quartermaster General Montgomery C. Meigs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s Quartermaster', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T16:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35ef3074-b6fe-5acc-b65a-ede911f2862b', 'word_count': 1698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35ef3074-b6fe-5acc-b65a-ede911f2862b'}, {'abstract': 'Starting with “Jerry Springer: The Opera,” Nicholas Hytner has repositioned the three-stage complex as arguably the defining theatrical address in the English-speaking world. And he still has two years to go.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/in-the-hytner-era-the-national-theater-hit-its-mark/', 'snippet': 'Starting with “Jerry Springer: The Opera,” Nicholas Hytner has repositioned the three-stage complex as arguably the defining theatrical address in the English-speaking world. And he still has two years to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON—At last, a date has been named. I’m referring not to the next general election but to a handover to come that may loom larger in the minds of culturally minded Britons. Nicholas Hytner has announced that he will step down at the end of March 2015 as artistic director of the National Theater, a position he has filled with considerable glory since 2003, over time repositioning the primacy of the three-auditorium complex as arguably the defining theatrical address in the English-speaking world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12rdv-hytner/12rdv-hytner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/12/arts/12rdv-hytner/12rdv-hytner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '