 and not even 10 professors. I found Mr. Abouabdalla at Caffe Strada. He had arranged his books on the table as if to answer my question.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/nyregion/beliefs/beliefs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/13/nyregion/beliefs/beliefs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/nyregion/beliefs/beliefs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/nyregion/beliefs/beliefs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/nyregion/beliefs/beliefs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/13/nyregion/beliefs/beliefs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/nyregion/beliefs/beliefs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Muslim College Mixes Subjects to Achieve an American Feel', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Muslim College Mixes Subjects To Achieve an American Feel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zaytuna College', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T17:18:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8fd3886-ce38-5961-8f9d-4826d68dccb1', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8fd3886-ce38-5961-8f9d-4826d68dccb1'}, {'abstract': 'Dark rum, ripe banana, butterscotch and a touch of sea salt. Go forth and bake these chocolate banana blondie bars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/dining/blondies-have-more-fun-without-fudge.html', 'snippet': 'Dark rum, ripe banana, butterscotch and a touch of sea salt. Go forth and bake these chocolate banana blondie bars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I imagined a pan full of chocolate banana blondie bars, I could see exactly what I wanted. A bittersweet bottom crowned with a brown-butter, rum-scented, banana-imbued butterscotch blondie. Two distinct layers and a complex set of flavors harmonizing in every gooey bite. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Without the Fudge, Blondies Have More Fun', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Without the Fudge, Blondies Have More Fun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bananas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N