 group with ties to old-fashioned means of music discovery, releases a limited-edition 10-inch vinyl.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/now-listening-ra-ra-riot-all-i-fear/', 'snippet': 'An indie rock group with ties to old-fashioned means of music discovery, releases a limited-edition 10-inch vinyl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The indie rock outfit Ra Ra Riot is no stranger to old-fashioned means of music discovery. After all, the group, which first cut its chops playing house parties at Syracuse University, gained notoriety only after putting in stints at CMJ and South by Southwest and garnering positive reviews for its tireless live shows. It’s fitting, then, that the band — made up of Wes Miles on vocals, Rebecca Zeller on violin, Mathieu Santos on bass and Milo Bonacci on guitar — should be fans of Record Store Day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Listening | Ra Ra Riot, ‘All I Fear’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ra Ra Riot', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T18:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e477b30-6a44-5e55-b50d-9240273fd601', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e477b30-6a44-5e55-b50d-9240273fd601'}, {'abstract': 'Everything at Miss Terroir bore a hand-made pride of place, distinct in flavor and redolent of origins. It was as far from clichéd brunch fare as I could imagine.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/in-france-where-brunch-is-au-courant/', 'snippet': 'Everything at Miss Terroir bore a hand-made pride of place, distinct in flavor and redolent of origins. It was as far from clichéd brunch fare as I could imagine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My wife and I darted over to Paris for a long weekend to visit our 21-year-old son, Peter, who is spending the semester studying abroad and absorbing the numerous cultural pleasures that Europe has to offer. Unexpectedly among those pleasures, he said, Parisians are currently obsessed with brunch, a bane of the New York food-obsessed, who writhe in agony over the popular banality of bad eggs Benedict and dreadful Bloody Marys. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In France, Where Brunch Is Au Courant', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T18:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c10443-d92f-50ae-9071-d81bc06f8142', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c10443-d92f-50ae-9071-d81bc06f8142'}, {'abstract': 'Images of Maria Tallchief, one of the most brilliant American ballerinas of the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/04/12/arts/dance/20130412TALLCHIEF.html', 'snippet': 'Images of Maria Tallchief, one of the most brilliant American ballerinas of the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Images of Maria Tallchief, one of the most brilliant American ballerinas of the 20th century.', 'source': 'The New York 