ing or medical license or having your driver’s license suspended.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/what-happens-if-you-dont-pay-your-taxes/', 'snippet': 'There are lots of nonmonetary penalties, like being denied a hunting or medical license or having your driver’s license suspended.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who commit tax fraud can face big fines and even imprisonment. Just ask the recently released Wesley Snipes, who had served most of a three-year sentence for not filing his taxes. The timing of his release, just ahead of the tax filing deadline, may not have been an accident; the Internal Revenue Service appears to ramp up publicity of its tax fraud cases right before April 15, a 2010 study found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens if You Don’t Pay Your Taxes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snipes, Wesley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T18:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31bf9a0b-7ae3-5bec-be2d-46dd8ecadd01', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31bf9a0b-7ae3-5bec-be2d-46dd8ecadd01'}, {'abstract': 'A reconfigured 42nd-floor apartment comes with impressive views of Central Park, the Hudson River and the cityscape.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/big-ticket-a-reconfigured-aerie-sold-for-16-25-million/', 'snippet': 'A reconfigured 42nd-floor apartment comes with impressive views of Central Park, the Hudson River and the cityscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An indulgent and elegant apartment on the 42nd floor of the Trump International Hotel and Tower, which was reconfigured to a two-bedroom, two-and-a-half-bath aerie from the original four bedrooms and six baths by the designer Jeffrey Bilhuber, sold for $16.25 million and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/realestate/14TICKET/14TICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/realestate/14TICKET/14TICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/realestate/14TICKET/14TICKET-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/realestate/14TICKET/14TICKET-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 1332, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/realestate/14TICKET/14TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/realestate