, 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joseph and Jill Biden’s 2012 Tax Returns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Jill Tracy Jacobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T19:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f5f92953-a9ba-5954-bf0d-d887600acce6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f5f92953-a9ba-5954-bf0d-d887600acce6'}, {'abstract': 'Nick Pologeorgis is expanding his line of accessories, adding jackets and vests in mink, nutria, Mongolian and other furs.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/a-fur-man-known-to-insiders-adds-some-fun/', 'snippet': 'Nick Pologeorgis is expanding his line of accessories, adding jackets and vests in mink, nutria, Mongolian and other furs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FEW TIMES A YEAR, Nick Pologeorgis leaves his family’s business on West 29th Street to attend the fur auctions in Toronto, Seattle and St. Petersburg, the home of the Russian sable market. His father, Stanley, started Pologeorgis Furs in 1960; after Nick graduated from Boston University in 1984 with a degree in finance, he joined the firm. His sister, Joan, works on the production side. Lately, if there’s one thing Mr. Pologeorgis has noticed at the auctions, aside from rising prices (they have doubled in the last three years), it’s the number of Chinese bidders. No doubt the two are connected.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fur Man, Known to Insiders, Adds Some Fun', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fur Man, Known to Insiders, Adds Some Fun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fur', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kors, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rucci, Ralph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T19:03:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e7c4c45-27b0-51bc-9e5d-8e701b288776', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e7c4c45-27b0-51bc-9e5d-8e701b288776'}, {'abstract': 'In the city that inspired some of Christopher Isherwood’s notable fiction, searching for traces of the writer’s life there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/travel/looking-for-christopher-isherwoods-berlin.html', 'snippet': 'In the city that inspired some of Christopher Isherwood’s notable fiction, searching for traces of the writer’s life there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Christopher Isherwood moved to Berlin in 1929, the 25-year-old British novelist could not quite bring himself to settle down in one place.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/travel/14FOOTSTEPS1/14FOOTSTEPS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/travel/14FOOTSTEPS1/14F