of the United States’ counterterrorism efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a letter sent to President Obama this week, the nation’s leading human rights organizations questioned the legal basis for targeted killing and called for an end to the secrecy surrounding the use of drones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/world/13Drones/13Drones-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/13/world/13Drones/13Drones-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/world/13Drones/13Drones-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/world/13Drones/13Drones-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/world/13Drones/13Drones-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/13/world/13Drones/13Drones-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/world/13Drones/13Drones-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rights Groups, in Letter to Obama, Question Legality and Secrecy of Drone Killings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rights Groups, in Letter to Obama, Question Legality and Secrecy of Drone Killings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Open Society Foundations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights First', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Constitutional Rights', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T19:14:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5964c2a4-87f1-5c38-ba7a-38535db39a96', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5964c2a4-87f1-5c38-ba7a-38535db39a96'}, {'abstract': 'The service’s music feature is still hidden from the public, but it appears to be a way to learn what music is becoming popular.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/business/media/clues-emerge-about-twitters-music-feature.html', 'snippet': 'The service’s music feature is still hidden from the public, but it appears to be a way to learn what music is becoming popular.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twitter is an online service where millions of people go to chat. Now the company behind it is hoping that it will also be where they go to find new music.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter Will Introduce a Music Application', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twitter Will Introduce A Music Application', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T19:26:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73038866-542e-5254-8245-3522156c8e69', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73038866-542e-5254-8245-3522156c8e69'}, {'abstract': 'Guan was assessed a one-stroke penalty after the 17th hole of his second round for slow play, carding a three-over 75 for a 36-hole total of four-over 148, near the projected cut.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/near-cutline-guan-is-penalized-for-slow-play/', 'snippet': 'Guan was assessed a one-stroke penalty after the 17th hole of his second round for slow play, carding a three-over 75 for a 36-hole total of four-over 148, near the projected cut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUGUSTA, Ga. — The talk during the first day of the Masters was how the Chinese teenager Guan Tianlang seemed so far ahead of his time. At 14, he was playing with the game and the poise of a player twice his age. But on Friday, Guan was punished for dawdling, with a one-stroke penalty for slow play after the 17th hole of his second round at Augusta National Golf Club.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/sports/golf/13Guan/13Guan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 921, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/13/sports/golf/13Guan/13Guan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 921}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/sports/golf/13Guan/13Guan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/sports/golf/13Guan/13Guan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1335, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/sports/golf/13Guan/13Guan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/13/sports/golf/13Guan/13Guan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/sports/golf/13Guan/13Guan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Near Cut Line, Guan Is Penalized for Slow Play', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Clock, a Clank and a New Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masters Golf Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crenshaw, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guan Tianlang', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manassero, Matteo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Augusta National Golf Club', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T19:28:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d75688d1-81be-53c3-bf66-ffc816c523fe', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d75688d1-81be-53c3-bf66-ffc816c523fe'}, {'abstract': 'In Louis C. K.’s latest stand-up special for HBO, the comic pulls and pushes his audience with a more assured tone than he shows in his sitcom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/arts/television/louis-ck-oh-my-god-a-stand-up-special-on-hbo.html', 'snippet': 'In Louis C. K.’s latest stand-up special for HBO, the comic pulls and pushes his audience with a more assured tone than he shows in his sitcom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Louis C. K. walks onto a stage in Phoenix at the beginning of “Louis C. K.: Oh My God,” his new HBO stand-up special, and responds to the crowd’s applause with what feels like a practiced bit of false modesty — “I don’t necessarily agree with you but I appreciate it very much” — it’s the only moment that feels inauthentic in the hourlong show. If he didn’t agree with the audience, would he have been doing this for more than a quarter-century?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', '