securities filing.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/goldman-directors-get-a-pay-raise/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs directors, who were already among the best-compensated corporate directors in the country, will receive an additional 500 shares a year, according to a securities filing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs directors are getting a pay raise.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Raises Directors’ Pay by 500 Shares', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Goldman Raises Directors’ Pay by 500 Shares', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blankfein, Lloyd C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohn, Gary D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiro, James J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T19:57:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa048803-8ee4-5403-8f42-8ed1fdee424b', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa048803-8ee4-5403-8f42-8ed1fdee424b'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the work of a 33-year-old Harvard professor, a specialist in public economics, who won a prestigious award for achievement in the field by those under 40.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/raj-chetty-wins-the-john-bates-clark-medal/', 'snippet': 'A look at the work of a 33-year-old Harvard professor, a specialist in public economics, who won a prestigious award for achievement in the field by those under 40.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raj Chetty, an economist at Harvard University, has won the 2013 John Bates Clark Medal, a laurel considered by many economists to be second only to the Nobel Prize. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raj Chetty Wins the John Bates Clark Medal', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chetty, Raj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ECONOMIC ASSN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T19:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e523b17-df59-5804-8524-2512ae026c06', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e523b17-df59-5804-8524-2512ae026c06'}, {'abstract': 'What hair shade will Betty sport? What will Don do after he takes a drink? Make your predictions as part of our “Mad Men” quiz.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/mad-men-predictions-what-do-you-think-will-happen-sunday/', 'snippet': 'What hair shade will Betty sport? What will Don do after he takes a drink? Make your predictions as part of our “Mad Men” quiz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the season premiere of “Mad Men,” Don Draper showed up drunk at a funeral and his ex-wife, Betty, showed up brunet after a foray to the East Village. Though it’s a sure bet Don will be drinking again on Sunday’s episode (when does he not?), any guesses on what else will happen? In a new feature, here’s your chance to make your predictions. Check back next week to see how you did.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mad Men’ Predictions: What Do You Think Will Happen Sunday?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T20:03:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4447a892-68fc-55d1-a947-2abe77ce8001', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4447a892-68fc-55d1-a947-2abe77ce8001'}, {'abstract': 'Stratus Consulting said it was misled by a lawyer for Ecuadorean villagers who have been battling Chevron for decades over environmental damage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/business/research-recanted-in-oil-pollution-case-in-ecuador.html', 'snippet': 'Stratus Consulting said it was misled by a lawyer for Ecuadorean villagers who have been battling Chevron for decades over environmental damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — An environmental case that has pitted Chevron against Ecuadorean Amazon villagers for two decades has taken another bizarre twist, with an American consulting firm now recanting research favorable to the villagers’ claims of pollution in remote tracts of jungle. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/business/Chevron/Chevron-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/13/business/Chevron/Chevron-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/business/Chevron/Chevron-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/business/Chevron/Chevron-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/business/Chevron/Chevron-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/13/business/Chevron/Chevron-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/business/Chevron/Chevron-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Consultant Recants in Chevron Pollution Case in Ecuador', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Consultant Recants in Chevron Pollution Case in Ecuador', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krauss, Clifford', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donziger, Steven R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stratus Consulting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T20:13:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bcec3ca-d694-5a11-bf60-072a4b64f448', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bcec3ca-d694-5a11-bf60-072a4b64f448'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Volume 5 of “American Vampire,” about a new breed of bloodsucker, enters the list at No. 2.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/graphic-books-best-sellers-scott-snyders-american-vampire/', 'snippet': 'This week, Volume 5 of “American Vampire,” about a new breed of bloodsucker, enters the list at No. 2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writer Scott Snyder seems to be making a home out of our hardcover list. This week, Volume 5 of “American Vampire,” about a new breed of bloodsucker, enters the list at No. 2. (He is also the writer behind the Batman stories at No. 1 and No. 8.) In this latest installment of “American Vampire,” Mr. Snyder has been blessed with two gifted collaborators: Rafael Albuquerque, the original series artist, and Dustin Nguyen, who illustrates a spin-off story included in this collection. Though vampires have seemingly given up their number one status in pop culture to zombies, Mr. Snyder proves there are still plenty of tales to tell about these creatures of the night. Mr. Nguyen lends his wonderfully expressive and moody art to an adventure involving the hunt for the granddaddy of all vampires, Dracula, while Mr. Albuquerque illustrates the exploration of all things related to Skinner Sweet, the first American vampire, who is more vicious and less bothered by sunlight. The only drawback to reading this book in collected form is that the reader does not get to long savor the cliffhangers with which Mr. Snyder ends most issues. (Click here for a profile on Mr. Snyder from Sept. 2011.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers:  Scott Snyder’s  ‘American Vampire’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T20:16:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c55b1f73-462e-545d-b9ca-d94cd58555b2', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c55b1f73-462e-545d-b9ca-d94cd58555b2'}, {'abstract': 'From fine jewelry to home goods to tropical properties, T breaks down the world of the designer India Hicks.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/the-business-of-being-india-hicks/', 'snippet': 'From fine jewelry to home goods to tropical properties, T breaks down the world of the designer India Hicks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India Hicks adds another facet to her ever-growing brand with the debut of her home line for HSN this week. The author, model, designer, hotelier and mother has curated a brand that encompasses both her English upbringing and current Island lifestyle. The daughter of David Nightingale Hicks, the famed interior designer, and Lady Pamela Mountbatten, India has been surrounded by style from an early age. From fine jewelry to home goods to tropical properties, T Magazine breaks down the world of India Hicks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Business of Being | India Hicks', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hicks, India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T20:17:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b336c4d7-b4fb-5d48-9ffa-d6f18f8497e2', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b336c4d7-b4fb-5d48-9ffa-d6f18f8497e2'}, {'abstract': 'Conjuring the flavors of the bygone, fancy Italian spot with a chicken breast version of saltimbocca.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/dining/a-nod-to-old-elegance-with-saltimbocca-chicken.html', 'snippet': 'Conjuring the flavors of the bygone, fancy Italian spot with a chicken breast version of saltimbocca.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few of the old-school Italian restaurants remain in San Francisco’s North Beach neighborhood — the kind of places where the waiters wear red jackets, the wine list is bound in leather and the menu’s size makes it hard to see one’s tablemates. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17KITCH5_SPAN/17KITCH5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17KITCH5_SPAN/17KITCH5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17KITCH5_SPAN/17KITCH5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None,