: 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Serbia and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T20:26:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e60b8cd-6060-521f-9fcd-08eacda08239', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e60b8cd-6060-521f-9fcd-08eacda08239'}, {'abstract': 'Blazing a high-tech path to the 17th century.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/adam-smith-hates-bitcoin/', 'snippet': 'Blazing a high-tech path to the 17th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There have been many good pieces written on the dubious economics of Bitcoin; I especially liked this one by Neil Irwin. One thing I haven’t seen emphasized, however, is the extent to which the whole concept of having to “mine” Bitcoins by expending real resources amounts to a drastic retrogression — a retrogression that Adam Smith would have scorned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adam Smith Hates Bitcoin', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T20:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f1bf443-a57a-5135-ab43-8a3d9bdf33f7', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f1bf443-a57a-5135-ab43-8a3d9bdf33f7'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Milka Djordjevich is performing her solo “Kinetic Makeover” at the Chocolate Factory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/arts/dance/milka-djordjevichs-kinetic-makeover-at-chocolate-factory.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Milka Djordjevich is performing her solo “Kinetic Makeover” at the Chocolate Factory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the start of “Kinetic Makeover,” the choreographer Milka Djordjevich stands with her back to the audience. She stands there a long time, in silence, dressed in a pink and blue top and tight sherbet-orange pants (designed by Reid Bartelme). Almost imperceptibly, she begins to sway side to side. Gradually, the swaying swells, her knees bending, her torso pitching, until she has rocked herself onto the floor in a seated position and turned her face front. . Her eyes continue to ticktock, left, right, left. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/arts/13MILKA/13MILKA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/13/arts/13MILKA/13MILKA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 702}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/arts/13MILKA/13MILKA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/arts/13MILKA/13MILKA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1751, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/arts/13MILKA/13MILKA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/13/arts/13MILKA/13MILKA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/13/arts/13MILKA/13MILKA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Someone’s Ruffled Her Feathers, and She’s in Perpetual Motion', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Someone’s Ruffled Her Feathers, And She’s in Perpetual Motion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chocolate Factory, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djordjevich, Milka', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T20:31:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8e57866-d5a3-52f6-8484-093fd2911d7b', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8e57866-d5a3-52f6-8484-093fd2911d7b'}, {'abstract': 'Experts offer strategies for controlling and managing conflict, which can make families happier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/fashion/negotiating-peace-at-home.html', 'snippet': 'Experts offer strategies for controlling and managing conflict, which can make families happier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I CALLED IT THE 7:42 P.M. FIGHT. It happened every night when my wife and I gathered to discuss the detritus of our lives. Who’s waking up early with the kids? Who’s going to take Grandma to the eye doctor? What do you mean you forgot to pick up the milk?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14THISLIFE_SPAN/14THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 181, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14THISLIFE_SPAN/14THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 181}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14THISLIFE_SPAN/14THISLIFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14THISLIFE_SPAN/14THISLIFE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14THISLIFE_SPAN/14THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14THISLIFE_SPAN/14THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/fashion/14THISLIFE_SPAN/14THISLIFE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons in Domestic Diplomacy', 'kicker': 'This Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons in Domestic Diplomacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiler, Bruce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's