t weekend, April 20–21, The New York Times will host an Editors’ Lab event. Organized by the Global Editors Network (GEN), the Editors’ Lab will bring together teams from top media companies for two days of working sessions and talks. Each team will consist of a journalist, a designer and a developer. The hack event at the Times building will be the fifth in a tournament series that began in Buenos Aires and culminates at the GEN News Summit in Paris in June. We’ll post details next week; meanwhile, you can learn more at the GEN site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Lab at the NYT', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-12T21:46:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marci Windsheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marci', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Windsheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2012efd7-1bb4-52d0-9e62-04b1f09f97ff', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2012efd7-1bb4-52d0-9e62-04b1f09f97ff'}, {'abstract': 'Criterion is releasing a Blu-ray of Alex Cox’s Reagan-era comedy “Repo Man”; Grapevine Video issues a complete version of Allan Dwan’s “Getting Mary Married” (1919).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/movies/homevideo/coming-dvds-repo-man-getting-mary-married.html', 'snippet': 'Criterion is releasing a Blu-ray of Alex Cox’s Reagan-era comedy “Repo Man”; Grapevine Video issues a complete version of Allan Dwan’s “Getting Mary Married” (1919).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Repo Man', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/arts/14KEHR_SPAN/