graph': 'The Aug. 22, 2005, obituary for Edna Potvin in The Glens Falls Post-Star included a note about her car: “Mrs. Potvin was well known in the Glens Falls area for the immaculate turquoise and black 1962 Oldsmobile Starfire, which she drove until the age of 90.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Other Car Is… a 1962 Oldsmobile Starfire', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T00:54:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Koscs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koscs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a67f0bdc-22d5-5721-8d5b-9cb844b7d162', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a67f0bdc-22d5-5721-8d5b-9cb844b7d162'}, {'abstract': 'A sudden round of finger-pointing in the American intelligence community this week also highlighted the sensitivity surrounding nuclear threats in the wake of failures in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/world/asia/contrasting-views-on-north-korea-underscore-sensitivities-and-lack-of-evidence.html', 'snippet': 'A sudden round of finger-pointing in the American intelligence community this week also highlighted the sensitivity surrounding nuclear threats in the wake of failures in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On the hawkish end is the Pentagon’s intelligence arm, the Defense Intelligence Agency, which fears that North Korea could threaten American troops with a nuclear weapon on a crude missile. On the skeptical end is the State Department, which has more doubts about Pyongyang’s capabilities. And somewhere in the middle is the Central Intelligence Agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contrasting Views on North Korea Underscore Sensitivities and Lack of Evidence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contrasting Views on North Korea Underscore Sensitivities and Lack of Evidence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapper, James R Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T00:58:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/129dd483-bc1f-548e-ab2f-027809be798b', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/129dd483-bc1f-548e-ab2f-027809be798b'}, {'abstract': 'Under new security measures at the Kentucky Derby, horses will be under 24-hour surveillance and those with access to the horses must log in and log out. Expanded drug testing also will be in place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/sports/greater-doping-scrutiny-planned-for-kentucky-derby.html', 'snippet': 'Under new security measures at the Kentucky Derby, horses will be under 24-hour surveillance and those with access to the horses must log in and log out. Expanded drug testing also will be in place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 72 hours before the Kentucky Derby traditionally have been filled with steam, as it is known in racetrack parlance — rumors about which horse is due for a big race and which veterinarians are working overtime to get their horses to the gate. But for the first time in the 139 years of the race, the authorities this year will know precisely who is going into which barn in the hours leading up to the race and for what reason.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mindful of Drugs, Race Officials Will Keep Closer Eye on Kentucky Derby', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mindful of Drugs, Race Officials Will Keep Closer Eye on Kentucky Derby', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kentucky Horse Racing Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T00:58:59+0000', 'do