ensure that inmates are given the services they need to have a chance at crime-free lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With corrections costs exceeding $50 billion a year, federal and state officials are understandably eager to make sure that the hundreds of thousands of people released annually from prison get the drug treatment, job placement and support services they need to have a chance at crime-free lives. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Building Better Halfway Houses', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building Better Halfway Houses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T01:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d07ef1f-4e31-5d0e-9071-4a75d1ed37b7', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d07ef1f-4e31-5d0e-9071-4a75d1ed37b7'}, {'abstract': 'City leaders should promptly disavow negative ads before the attacks spiral out of control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/opinion/a-phantom-ad-joins-new-yorks-mayoral-race.html', 'snippet': 'City leaders should promptly disavow negative ads before the attacks spiral out of control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City voters have enjoyed the best and fairest campaign finance system in the country for almost 25 years. Now, a shadowy group organized as New York City Is Not for Sale is attempting to influence this year’s mayoral race with a secretive, independent committee much like those that have so tainted federal elections in recent years. This is the last thing the city needs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Phantom Ad Comes to New York', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Phantom Ad Comes to New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NYC Is Not for Sale', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T01:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a018b4f1-7c65-5c67-8567-863495639c60', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a018b4f1-7c65-5c67-8567-863495639c60'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry travels through Asia with no sign that he has found a real solution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/opinion/the-north-korea-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry travels through Asia with no sign that he has found a real solution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Secretary of State John Kerry sent several important messages to North Korea after talks on Friday in Seoul with South Korean leaders. Speaking at a news conference, he said that the United States would defend its South Korean and Japanese allies if there was conflict, that the international community would never accept the North as a nuclear weapons state, and that Washington was willing to resume long-stalled negotiations but only if the North Koreans agreed to move seriously on denuclearization.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The North Korea Problem', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The North Korea Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T01:48:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a8b5ed6-d97d-5cfb-bd9b-348fe6a542e0', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a8b5ed6-d97d-5cfb-bd9b-348fe6a542e0'}, {'abstract': 'With the purchase of the fleece, an old prejudice ebbs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/opinion/a-box-of-sheep.html', 'snippet': 'With the purchase of the fleece, an old prejudice ebbs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, a sheep arrived in a box. Not the whole sheep, which is still, I hope, grazing happily in a pasture somewhere in northeast Washington State. Only its fleece. I’ve raised many animals but never sheep. My dad, who raised them as a farm boy, left me with a vicious prejudice against them, and the only sheep I saw as a boy did nothing to counter it. They stood — a dim, ghostly flock — in a grove they had denuded entirely of grass and undergrowth. It occurs to me now that this was the fault of the farmer, not of the sheep, who have no more interest in eating bare dirt than I do.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Box of Sheep', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Box of Sheep', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sheep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinkenborg, Verlyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wool and Woolen Goods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T01:48:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/44c2b5c8-85ee-5eba-ab40-2f0636a57719', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44c2b5c8-85ee-5eba-ab40-2f0636a57719'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/nyregion/events-in-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in Connecticut. Items for the calendar should be sent at least three weeks in advance to ctcal@nytimes.com.', 