 Joe Kennedy’s ill-judged, career-killing statement in 1940 that “democracy is finished in England” to the 1963 assassination of his son John in Dallas. But wise theatergoers will pay no attention at all to these hard facts. They will instead just follow along with the fancies of the playwright, William Mastrosimone, as he constructs a clever, vastly entertaining counter-history of Camelot.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14ARTSCT1/14ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 926, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14ARTSCT1/14ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 926}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14ARTSCT1/14ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14ARTSCT1/14ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1192, 'width': 772, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14ARTSCT1/14ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14ARTSCT1/14ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14ARTSCT1/14ARTSCT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main