terview-with-the-chief-of-enrollment-in-the-new-york-city-education-department.html', 'snippet': 'Questions for Robert Sanft, the chief executive of the Office of Student Enrollment in New York City’s Education Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As chief executive of the Office of Student Enrollment in New York City’s Education Department, Robert Sanft, 41, places tens of thousands of students each year in public schools. He and his team of nearly 200 handle prekindergarten admissions, gifted and talented slots and the high school matching process. A graduate of New York public schools, Mr. Sanft lives in Windsor Terrace, Brooklyn, with his wife, his son, a fourth grader, and his daughter, who is in prekindergarten. They attend public school.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14QA/14QA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 1711, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14QA/14QA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1711}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14QA/14QA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 360, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14QA/14QA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14QA/14QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/14QA/14QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailw