 'Quotation of the day for Saturday, Apr. 13, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '"I wish they would have made an example of somebody else other than a 14-year-old kid, you know?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, Apr. 13, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T03:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/f370251c-22a3-5170-ab30-9bc27f0e5ad5', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f370251c-22a3-5170-ab30-9bc27f0e5ad5'}, {'abstract': 'German prosecutors charged former President Christian Wulff with corruption on Friday, more than a year after he quit amid accusations that he had accepted favors from business executives before becoming president.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/world/europe/germany-former-president-wulff-charged.html', 'snippet': 'German prosecutors charged former President Christian Wulff with corruption on Friday, more than a year after he quit amid accusations that he had accepted favors from business executives before becoming president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'German prosecutors charged former President Christian Wulff with corruption on Friday, more than a year after he quit amid accusations that he had accepted favors from business executives before becoming president. Mr. Wulff, 53, was picked by Chancellor Angela Merkel in 2010 for the largely ceremonial post. He quit 20 months later after the revelations about vacations with rich friends and favors and gifts that he had accepted earlier in his political career. On Friday, prosecutors in Hanover accused Mr. Wulff of allowing a movie producer to pay for a family vacation in 2008, while Mr. Wulff was governor of Lower Saxony. In exchange, prosecutors said, Mr. Wulff lobbied the engineering giant Siemens to help promote one of the producer’s films. Mr. Wulff, who denies the allegations, rejected an offer to settle the case by paying a fine.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Former President Wulff Charged', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Former President Charged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wulff, Christian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T03:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ed722e0-d8fd-5ad5-9082-bb2b58c39d33', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ed722e0-d8fd-5ad5-9082-bb2b58c39d33'}, {'abstract': 'The National Rifle Association’s sponsorship of a Sprint Cup event was negotiated by the race’s host, Texas Motor Speedway, but the decision has put Nascar in the center of the gun control debate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/sports/autoracing/race-sponsorship-by-nra-puts-nascar-in-hot-seat.html', 'snippet': 'The National Rifle Association’s sponsorship of a Sprint Cup event was negotiated by the race’s host, Texas Motor Speedway, but the de