e festival is leaning heavily on Brits, the sorts of acts loved by people who think adventure has been disproportionately distributed across the pond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coachella has become one of the primary American summer music institutions, not from a loyalty to domestic acts, but because it is warm to an idea that arose around the indie-mainstream collapse of the 1990s: subcultures can be mainstreamed too. The festival, one of the primary American summer music institutions with its 90,000 or so attendees this weekend and next, relies on that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coachella: A Heavy Lean Toward the British', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bugg, Jake', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marr, Johnny', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T04:44:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fa55672-28e6-5048-a83c-fc8d15720061', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fa55672-28e6-5048-a83c-fc8d15720061'}, {'abstract': 'The snow and 34-degree weather did not slow down the Mets, who scored five runs in each of the first two innings and rolled over the Twins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/sports/baseball/mets-pound-ball-against-twins-to-stay-warm.html', 'snippet': 'The snow and 34-degree weather did not slow down the Mets, who scored five runs in each of the 