n talking about DNWR in the US context, but it’s a much bigger issue in Europe, where the whole adjustment strategy relies on “internal devaluation”: countries that experienced large capital inflows during the period 2000-2007 are supposed to regain competitiveness by cutting costs, and that’s really hard if nominal wages have to come down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DNWR in the EA', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T21:50:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b086a2e6-39c3-58e1-b4fd-f6d7646f423e', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b086a2e6-39c3-58e1-b4fd-f6d7646f423e'}, {'abstract': 'Best. Puzzle. Ever. By Elizabeth C. Gorski, of course.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/my-treat/', 'snippet': 'Best. Puzzle. Ever. By Elizabeth C. Gorski, of course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — Oh my, I loved this puzzle. Your mileage may vary. But as far as I’m concerned, the only thing that would have made this puzzle better is if we had some sort of technology here at The New York Times that would make the puzzle lickable. Maybe scratch ‘n’ sniff, as a second choice. But definitely lickable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘My Treat’', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T22:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aaf7231-ee9e-5c41-8432-f5c689b2bbcf', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aaf7231-ee9e-5c41-8432-f5c689b2bbcf'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Byrne analyzed top-flight matches and wrote a chess column for The New York Times from 1972 to 2006.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/crosswords/chess/robert-byrne-chess-grandmaster-dies-at-84.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Byrne analyzed top-flight matches and wrote a chess column for The New York Times from 1972 to 2006.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Byrne, an international grandmaster and United States chess champion who, as the chess columnist for The New York Times, analyzed top-flight matches from 1972 through 2006, the eras of Bobby Fischer and Garry Kasparov, died on Friday at his home in Ossining, N.Y. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/12-byrne-obit-1/12-byrne-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/12-byrne-obit-1/12-byrne-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/12-byrne-obit-1/12-byrne-obit-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/12-byrne-obit-1/12-byrne-obit-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1489, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/12-byrne-obit-1/12-byrne-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/12-byrne-obit-1/12-byrne-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/nyregion/12-byrne-obit-1/12-byrne-obit-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Byrne, Chess Grandmaster, Dies at 84', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robert Byrne, a Chess Grandmaster, Dies at 84', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Bruce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrne, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischer, Bobby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T22:05:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6ba57ac-2e66-5f57-986e-cde52dfb4e76', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ba57ac-2e66-5f57-986e-cde52dfb4e76'}, {'abstract': 'A suite of young American bands tried to find a path out of the current American rock scene.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/13/coachella-trash-talk-and-mona-are-sparks-of-creative-rock/', 'snippet': 'A suite of young American bands tried to find a path out of the current American rock scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIO, Calif. — American rock music might get a bad rap, but its cancer begins from within. Major labels have all but tabled creative ambition, meaning that even bona fide indie stars may have to content themselves with being miniscene champions for life. Early on Saturday at Coachella, there was a suite of young American bands trying to find a path out of the darkness. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coachella: A Few Sparks of Creative Rock', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gaslight Anthem', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mona (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shovels & Rope (Music Group)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trash Talk (Music Group)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-13T22:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e558e77b-06f6-57ef-9032-51be4c28b438', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e558e77b-06f6-57ef-9032-51be4c28b438'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s proposal to trim future Medicare and Social Security benefits as part of a deficit compromise could force Democrats to take an uncomfortable stand on a measure that is unpopular with their base.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/us/politics/president-obamas-budget-revives-benefits-as-divisive-issue.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s proposal to trim future Medicare and Social Security benefits as part of a deficit compromise could force Democrats to take an uncomfortable stand on a measure that is unpopular with their base.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Whether or not Republicans ever agree to a budget deal with President Obama, one thing seems certain: now that he has officially put Social Security and Medicare benefits on the negotiating table, opponents on his party’s left will make that an issue for Democrats in the midterm elections next year — and perhaps in the 2016 presidential contest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Budget Revives Benefits as Divisive Issue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama’s Budget Revives Benefits as Divisive Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calmes, Jackie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_dat