'Cabrera, Angel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-14T01:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08df823a-f109-5e10-a831-8094c332afdf', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08df823a-f109-5e10-a831-8094c332afdf'}, {'abstract': 'The fans booed, early and often, as Yankees pitcher Phil Hughes struggled against the Orioles, who pummeled Hughes for nine hits, including three home runs, and five runs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/sports/baseball/hughes-booed-in-yankees-loss-to-orioles.html', 'snippet': 'The fans booed, early and often, as Yankees pitcher Phil Hughes struggled against the Orioles, who pummeled Hughes for nine hits, including three home runs, and five runs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The grumbling began with a lone fan who had given up on Phil Hughes in the third inning. “Take him out! Take him ouuuuuut!” He was louder with each hard hit. Soon, a few others started to boo. By the fourth, as Hughes walked off the mound with his head bowed after being removed from the game, the crowd was more decided.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/sports/baseball/14yankees1-img/14yankees1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/sports/baseball/14yankees1-img/14yankees1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp