com/2013/04/15/world/asia/jakarta-gives-ultimatum-to-aceh-on-rebel-banner.html', 'snippet': 'The strife-torn Aceh Province passed a bylaw last month that declared the banner of a former armed separatist movement to be the province’s official flag and seal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — The Indonesian government has given the leaders of strife-torn Aceh Province until Tuesday to annul a bylaw passed last month that declares the banner of a former armed separatist movement to be the province’s official flag and seal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rebel Flag Flies Over a Province, and Indonesia Wants It Torn Down', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rebel Flag Flies Over a Province, and Indonesia Wants It Torn Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ACEH PROVINCE (INDONESIA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cochrane, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yudhoyono, Susilo Bambang', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Aceh Movement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-14T12:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Cochrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59d444b4-73af-593a-9549-397e7b932ebb', 'word_count': 1027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59d444b4-73af-593a-9549-397e7b932ebb'}, {'abstract': 'If you pay a nanny or baby sitter more than $1,800 a year, you are required to be paying employment taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/should-you-be-paying-taxes-on-your-baby-sitter/', 'snippet': 'If you pay a nanny or baby sitter more than $1,800 a year, you are required to be paying employment taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to hear a pin drop, ask a room of parents whether they report employment taxes for their baby sitter or nanny. My (admittedly unscientific) conclusion, drawn from four years of Manhattan motherhood, is that many families do not. In a 2011 discussion of nanny compensation on Park Slope Parents, most families reported paying their caregivers completely off the books, while very few said they paid the tax. Susan Fox, founder of Park Slope Parents, suspects the off-the-books number among her readers is well over half. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should You Be Paying Taxes on Your Baby Sitter?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-14T12:49:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacoba Urist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacoba', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Urist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ad6129b-3556-56b8-9f68-34b849e5286a', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ad6129b-3556-56b8-9f68-34b849e5286a'}, {'abstract': 'Just another printing press fanatic.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/14/milton-friedman-currency-debaser/', 'snippet': 'Just another printing press fanatic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong links to a Forbes piece by Tim Lee from last year that I missed, which in turn quotes Milton Friedman on the macroeconomic views that prevailed in the early 1930s:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milton Friedman, Currency Debaser', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-14T13:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0023b62f-ff9b-5bb1-825f-11bf4a8c128c', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0023b62f-ff9b-5bb1-825f-11bf4a8c128c'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s William Neuman reports from Caracas, Venezuela, on the morning of an election for the successor to Hugo Chávez, who died in March.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/americas/100000002171096/venezuela-goes-to-the-polls.html', 'snippet': 'The Times’s William Neuman reports from Caracas, Venezuela, on the morning of an election for the successor to Hugo Chávez, who died in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times’s William Neuman reports from Caracas, Venezuela, on the morning of an election for the successor to Hugo Chávez, who died in March.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/14/world/video-venezuela-election-am/video-venezuela-election-am-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/14/world/video-v