zing their peppy song in the lullaby that Andrea Zalkin sang to the tiny, fragile baby clutched to her chest in the neonatal unit. But there was something unintentionally poignant in the title she chose for her son: “Eight Days a Week” is more time than can fit on the calendar. Ms. Zalkin’s baby, Hudson, born 13 weeks early, has had too little time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Music’s Charms, Soothing Premature Hearts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Live Music’s Charms, Soothing Premature Hearts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belluck, Pam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Premature Babies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pediatrics (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T04:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e06a2a98-6774-55df-bfc8-b60010323910', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e06a2a98-6774-55df-bfc8-b60010323910'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (13) WONDER WOMEN! THE UNTOLD STORY OF AMERICAN SUPERHEROINES In this “Independent Lens” presentation, the director Kristy Guevara-Flanagan and the producer Kelcey Edwards chronicle the evolution of Wonder Woman, from her genesis in 1941 as a DC Comics character — the creation of William Moulton Marston, a Harvard-trained pop psychologist — to present-day incarnations and what she says about society’s feelings toward powerful women. Among those interviewed are the ’70s television stars Lynda Carter (the “New Original Wonder Woman” TV film and the series “The New Adventures of Wonder Woman”), above, and Lindsay Wagner (“The Bionic Woman”) and the feminist writer and activist Gloria Steinem.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T04:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/eadaac1d-e117-5389-b554-7a0098c4dc4c', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eadaac1d-e117-5389-b554-7a0098c4dc4c'}, {'abstract': 'A number of the hedge fund leaders who had giant paydays last year earned their riches the old-fashioned way: by posting big returns on their investments.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/pay-stretching-to-10-figures/', 'snippet': 'A number of the hedge fund leaders who had giant paydays last year earned their riches the old-fashioned way: by posting big returns on their investments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, the criticism about giant Wall Street hedge funds — those that command billions of investor dollars from pension funds, endowments and the wealthy — is that they’re simply too big to beat the market.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Fund Titans’ Pay Stretching to 10 Figures', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pay Stretching to 10 Figures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T04:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Creswell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Creswell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfb15825-0679-5503-915b-bfd9616a2731', 'word_count': 1439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfb15825-0679-5503-915b-bfd9616a2731'}, {'abstract': 'Ford and General Motors will jointly develop a new generation of 9- and 10-speed automatic transmissions.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/rivals-in-the-showroom-ford-and-g-m-will-make-transmissions-jointly/', 'snippet': 'Ford and General Motors will jointly develop a new generation of 9- and 10-speed automatic transmissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ford Motor and General Motors announced on Monday that they would jointly develop new transmissions with 9 speeds for front-wheel-drive vehicles and 10 speeds for rear-drive cars and trucks. The new transmissions, with more forward gear ratios than either company now offers, are expected to reach the market beginning in 2016. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rivals in the Showroom, Ford and G.M. Will Develop Transmissions Jointly', 'kicker': 'Whee