s celebrities, to lead an ad campaign promoting Israeli technology and innovation abroad. She agreed, free of charge. Apparently it was a success: “My Instagram feed has more readers than Israel’s most popular newspaper,” Refaeli bragged in a tweet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supermodel and Draft-Dodger', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T13:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8f3d1eb-fca5-501d-86da-925380b3b95d', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8f3d1eb-fca5-501d-86da-925380b3b95d'}, {'abstract': 'A former partner at McKinsey who releases her third album Monday on switching gears from corporate America to classical music.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/a-conversation-with-singer-chandrika-krishnamurthy-tandon/', 'snippet': 'A former partner at McKinsey who releases her third album Monday on switching gears from corporate America to classical music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK CITY — On her newest album, the singer Chandrika Krishnamurthy Tandon has reimagined “Raghupati Raghav Raja Ram,” a devotional bhajan, or hymn, in different musical traditions including Brazilian bossa nova and Chinese rhythms. Some of the tunes are fast-paced, others more meditative, but the lead voice is always unmistakably Ms. Tandon’s.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Singer Chandrika Krishnamurthy Tandon', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nooyi, Indra K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McKinsey & Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T13:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8b7a8b1-d808-50ff-b477-6c96848c271c', 'word_count': 1243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8b7a8b1-d808-50ff-b477-6c96848c271c'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court turned down a case concerning a New York State law that requires people seeking permits to carry guns in public to demonstrate that they have a special need for self-protection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/us/politics/supreme-court-declines-gun-law-case.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court turned down a case concerning a New York State law that requires people seeking permits to carry guns in public to demonstrate that they have a special need for self-protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court said Monday that it would not weigh in on a major Second Amendment question that has divided the lower courts: May states bar or strictly limit the carrying of guns in public for self-defense?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justices Refuse Case on Gun Law in New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justices Refuse Case On Gun Law In New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posner, Richard A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T13:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9de41fa0-44a5-5799-9933-8e2cbc953aed', 'word_count': 683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9de41fa0-44a5-5799-9933-8e2cbc953aed'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/what-were-reading-monday-draft/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Smithsonian: Don’t fret the invasion of the cicadas. Fry them up! Here are some tips for how to collect and prepare them for eating. Our favorite is No. 2: gather twice as many as you and your family think you can eat. — Maria Newman', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T14:10:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ac6119a-ebb5-5f3e-95aa-b297de2cc6ca', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ac6119a-ebb5-5f3e-95aa-b297de2cc6ca'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Scott rewrote his own history at the Masters and became a champion everyone could love.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/sports/swoon-over-the-masters.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Scott rewrote his own history at the Masters and became a champion everyone could love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Adam Scott dropped to his knees after his putt plunked into the cup on the second playoff hole at the Masters Sunday evening, golf has been in full swoon. The golfing gods couldn’t have come up with a champion they’d love more if had they drawn him up in an animation studio. He is young and fun and personable and as the young female portion of his fan base would say, adorbs! Australians, of course, are over the moon. They can now forget that whole Greg Norman thing ever happened. And the stuffy old men in the green eyeshades who run golf? They’d be forming a conga line if they did that sort of thing. Scott gives their moldering sport a shot of curb appeal lacking since the legend of Tiger Woods lost a battle with a fire hydrant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/golf/16leadingpic/16leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 850, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/golf/16leadingpic/16leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 850}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/golf/16leadingpic/16leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's