N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T14:12:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98c360ea-08a4-5ac8-bd75-77794a0e5f2b', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98c360ea-08a4-5ac8-bd75-77794a0e5f2b'}, {'abstract': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/triple-play-baseball-quiz-week-2-results/', 'snippet': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The perhaps overachieving Mets have a better record than their crosstown rivals, but they are the correct answer to Question No. 1 thanks to the hot start by the Atlanta Braves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Triple Play: Week 2 Results', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T14:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53d2c789-c94f-5d95-965a-7e0f5fadf75f', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53d2c789-c94f-5d95-965a-7e0f5fadf75f'}, {'abstract': 'There are some delicious ways to enjoy the benefits of brown rice with less concern about arsenic contamination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/health/beet-green-rice-and-ricotta-blinis.html', 'snippet': 'There are some delicious ways to enjoy the benefits of brown rice with less concern about arsenic contamination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve always been a big promoter of brown rice, and I was happily testing recipes last week for short-, medium- and long-grain varieties when I remembered that there had been reports in the past year about dangerous arsenic levels in rice, particularly in brown rice. I thought about shelving the recipe tests and choosing another subject for this week’s Recipes for Health, but then I decided to take a closer look at the reports to see if there was a way to make rice viable for health-conscious rice lovers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'