, 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Barker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f72aa36c-0d3f-5f95-ad0b-22f4f0facaab', 'word_count': 1375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f72aa36c-0d3f-5f95-ad0b-22f4f0facaab'}, {'abstract': 'Past winners of the award, which comes with a $30,000 prize, have gone on to be major opera stars.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/isabel-leonard-wins-richard-tucker-award/', 'snippet': 'Past winners of the award, which comes with a $30,000 prize, have gone on to be major opera stars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Richard Tucker Foundation said on Monday that the mezzo-soprano Isabel Leonard had won its award named after the American tenor. The award, which comes with a $30,000 prize, is conferred on singers who the foundation deems are about to plunge into major international careers, and it often makes good calls. Past winners include Angela Meade, Joyce DiDonato, John Relyea, Matthew Polenzani, Deborah Voigt and Renée Fleming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Isabel Leonard Wins Richard Tucker Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiDonato, Joyce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleming, Renee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonard, Isabel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meade, Angela', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polenza