reakfast-at-tiffanys-will-close-on-sunday/', 'snippet': 'Richard Greenberg’s adaptation of the Truman Capote novella will finish at a financial loss after 17 previews and 38 regular performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Broadway play “Breakfast at Tiffany’s” will close on Sunday after 17 preview performances and 38 regular performances, the producers said on Monday. The play, adapted by the Tony Award winner Richard Greenberg (“Take Me Out”) from the Truman Capote novella, opened on March 20 to largely negative reviews.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/15/arts/15artsbeat-tiffanys/15artsbeat-tiffanys-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/15/arts/15artsbeat-tiffanys/15artsbeat-tiffanys-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 478}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/15/arts/15artsbeat-tiffanys/15artsbeat-tiffanys-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/15/arts/15artsbeat-tiffanys/15artsbeat-tiffanys-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1510, 'width': 1894, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/15/arts/15artsbeat-tiffanys/15artsbeat-tiffanys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/15/arts/15artsbeat-tiffanys/15artsbeat-tiffanys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag