ier Manzano, a freelance photographer working with Agence France-Presse, has won the Pulitzer in feature photography for his picture of two Syrian rebel fighters taking aim through a pockmarked wall in Aleppo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographs of Syria Sweep Pulitzer Prizes', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pulitzer Prizes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abd, Rodrigo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brabo, Manu', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contreras, Narciso', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamra, Khalil', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manzano, Javier', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muheisen, Muhammed', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T22:42:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Newman and James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5613c78e-4781-54b7-8165-38708ac868b8', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5613c78e-4781-54b7-8165-38708ac868b8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Davis, the longest-serving principal conductor of the London Symphony Orchestra, brought enthusiasm and authority to his music-making.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/arts/music/colin-davis-exuberant-british-conductor-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Davis, the longest-serving principal conductor of the London Symphony Orchestra, brought enthusiasm and authority to his music-making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Colin Davis, one of the most acclaimed British conductors of the 20th century, who brought immense authority and an almost palpable zest to his music-making on both sides of the Atlantic, died on Sunday. He was 85. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/DAVIS1-obit/DAVIS1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/DAVIS1-obit/DAVIS1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/DAVIS1-obit/DAVIS1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/DAVIS1-obit/DAVIS1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/DAVIS1-obit/DAVIS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/DAVIS1-obit/DAVIS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/DAVIS1-obit/DAVIS1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cr