e days of deliberations, jurors in the murder trial of a schizophrenic man accused of killing a psychologist in her Upper East Side office in 2008 sent a note to the judge insisting that they were deadlocked. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Again, Tarloff Jury Reports Deadlock', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Again, Tarloff Jury Reports Deadlock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tarloff, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLaughlin, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Faughey, Kathryn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T23:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b88bfed-3858-5771-b949-a0cf86bb94ad', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b88bfed-3858-5771-b949-a0cf86bb94ad'}, {'abstract': 'Europe is divided over the road to recovery: is strict belt-tightening or an easing of monetary policy and some stimulus best? The tension in that question will be on full display in Washington this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/business/global/europe-split-over-austerity-as-a-path-to-growth.html', 'snippet': 'Europe is divided over the road to recovery: is strict belt-tightening or an easing of monetary policy and some stimulus best? The tension in that question will be on full display in Washington this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In the last year, the International Monetary Fund has performed a major reassessment of how it thinks austerity harms a weak, financially troubled economy. But while warning of the perils of slow growth, it still often insists on austerity for just such economies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-jp-FUND/16-jp-FUND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-jp-FUND/16-jp-FUND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-jp-FUND/16-jp-FUND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-jp-FUND/16-jp-FUND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-jp-FUND/16-jp-FUND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-jp-FUND/16-jp-FUND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-jp-FUND/16-jp-FUND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Split Over Austerity as a Path to Growth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Path to Growth Splits Europe, With Austerity A Central Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowrey, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchard, Olivier J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagarde, Christine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-15T23:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6815fa8-9867-5345-9be8-5d32de4244ea', 'word_count': 1073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6815fa8-9867-5345-9be8-5d32de4244ea'}, {'abstract': 'How my obsession with author interviews resulted in new writing habits, as well as a lot of wasted time.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/stupid-writer-tricks/', 'snippet': 'How my obsession with author interviews resulted in new writing habits, as well as a lot of wasted time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day a couple of years ago, when I found my desk drawer so full of microphone headsets that it would no longer close, I realized it was time for an intervention. I could no longer deny it: I needed to stop reading interviews with authors. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stupid Writer Tricks', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T00:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2ca52c9-47cb-55fc-8af7-c0b9cd071472', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2ca52c9-47cb-55fc-8af7-c0b9cd071472'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Azrin, an author of “The Token Economy,” a foundational text, helped alter the way psychologists approached behavior-modifying techniques.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/health/nathan-azrin-behavioral-psychologist-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Azrin, an author of “The Token Economy,” a foundational text, helped alter the way psychologists approached behavior-modifying techniques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Nathan Azrin was appointed director of treatment development at Anna State Hospital in Illinois in 1958, a majority of the patients he was expected to treat were schizophrenic, emotionally withdrawn and in many cases mute after years in institutions. Few bothered getting dressed; most spent their days in hospital gowns.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/us/AZARIN-obit/AZARIN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'x