icle/f0b10999-c8d4-5090-b29f-c28a8569a046'}, {'abstract': 'In campaign offices around the city, aides are awaiting polls that could offer a more precise gauge of Mr. Weiner’s political appeal, should he declare his candidacy for mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/nyregion/strategists-assess-what-a-weiner-candidacy-would-do-to-the-mayoral-race.html', 'snippet': 'In campaign offices around the city, aides are awaiting polls that could offer a more precise gauge of Mr. Weiner’s political appeal, should he declare his candidacy for mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony D. Weiner has not declared his candidacy, hired a staff or even held a news conference. But already, New York City’s mayoral contenders are strategizing about what they have to do to prevent the former Queens congressman from making it to City Hall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strategists Assess How a Weiner Candidacy Would Shake Up the Race for Mayor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strategists Assess How a Weiner Candidacy Would Shake Up the Race for Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T01:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aee8349f-fd2f-579d-95b2-a382aa8fc829', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aee8349f-fd2f-579d-95b2-a382aa8fc829'}, {'abstract': 'The urinary incontinence brand is ditching absorbency descriptions in favor of what it calls lifestyle terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/business/media/tena-tries-fresh-terms-for-a-delicate-topic.html', 'snippet': 'The urinary incontinence brand is ditching absorbency descriptions in favor of what it calls lifestyle terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BECAUSE it’s not the cheeriest of topics, advertising for products that treat women’s urinary incontinence tends to steer clear of medical terminology. Poise, a Kimberly-Clark brand, uses the term “light bladder leakage,” while Tena, an SCA Personal Care brand, uses one that could just as easily describe the kitchen sink, “unexpected leaks.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-ADCO/16-ADCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-ADCO/16-ADCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-ADCO/16-ADCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/business/16-ADCO/16-ADCO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1075, 'width': 1915, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': N