': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb83e0ad-c1b4-5b68-a7d0-d9ad5a2ecae0', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb83e0ad-c1b4-5b68-a7d0-d9ad5a2ecae0'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should reverse the rulings that gave a member of the Cherokee Nation the right to revoke an adoption of his biological child.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/opinion/a-wrenching-adoption-under-the-indian-child-welfare-act.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should reverse the rulings that gave a member of the Cherokee Nation the right to revoke an adoption of his biological child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian Child Welfare Act was passed in 1978 to prevent state and local welfare offices from separating Indian children from their parents, many without good reason, and placing them in non-Indian homes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wrenching Adoption Case', 'kicker': 'Edtorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wrenching Adoption Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T01:16:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/018f40c6-91e7-5ce8-beb0-cbdca6528c2e', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/018f40c6-91e7-5ce8-beb0-cbdca6528c2e'}, {'abstract': 'Westchester County has failed to abide by a court order issued more than three years ago to build hundreds of affordable units.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/opinion/westchester-loses-again-on-fair-housing.html', 'snippet': 'Westchester County has failed to abide by a court order issued more than three years ago to build hundreds of affordable units.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than three years have passed since Westchester County signed a landmark consent decree to settle a fair-housing lawsuit — years the county and County Executive Rob Astorino have spent shirking their obligations, challenging the deal in court, and losing. It lost again on April 5, when the United States Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit upheld a district judge’s ruling that the county was in violation of terms of the court order. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Westchester Loses Again on Fair Housing', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Westchester Loses Again on Fair Housing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astorino, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T01:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d785e150-c656-5767-96db-a11ac3962dec', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d785e150-c656-5767-96db-a11ac3962dec'}, {'abstract': 'Leading academic institutions failed to inform parents of premature babies of the real risks involved in a medical study. How could this happen?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/opinion/an-ethical-breakdown-in-medical-research.html', 'snippet': 'Leading academic institutions failed to inform parents of premature babies of the real risks involved in a medical study. How could this happen?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite reforms to protect patients from being harmed by medical research in recent decades, 23 academic institutions authorized a research project that failed to meet the most basic standard: providing an informed consent document to parents that accurately described the risks and benefits of the research to be conducted on extremely premature babies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ethical Breakdown', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Ethical Breakdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Premature Babies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama at Birmingham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office for Human Research Protections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T01:19:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cd8d45a-e839-585c-a056-965c34991218', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cd8d45a-e839-585c-a056-965c34991218'}, {'abstract': 'Following accusations that the case was being ignored by the national news media, reporters descended Mon