 marathon is the most unifying of sporting events. The city that shows up to cheer on thousands of runners doesn’t really know or care much about who wins; there are no sides to root for or against. Those who stand on the sidelines — as they have done in Boston since 1897 — come to celebrate runners from around the world. The country or neighborhood of origin of the competitors matters far less than their stamina.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bombs at the Marathon', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bombs at the Marathon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T01:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbcf2e14-ca28-53d1-a16e-35ded77f2816', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbcf2e14-ca28-53d1-a16e-35ded77f2816'}, {'abstract': 'The proposal to restructure debt is the opening move in what many say could be a long and contentious battle between the company and its largest creditors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/15/energy-future-holdings-offers-bankruptcy-plan/', 'snippet': 'The proposal to restructure debt is the opening move in what many say could be a long and contentious battle between the company and its largest creditors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Energy Future Holdings, the Texas energy giant that was taken private in 2007 in a record-breaking $45 billion buyout, disclosed a potential bankruptcy plan to its creditors on Monday.', 'print_section'