 anniversary of his death was significant.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/cautious-call-for-political-reform-in-china/', 'snippet': 'The death in April 1989 of a reform-minded leader, Hu Yaobang, led to huge democracy demonstrations that ended on June 4, 1989, with an army assault in Beijing. So praise for Mr. Hu in Communist Party media on the 24th anniversary of his death was...', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — This week marks the beginning of a sensitive political memory in China – the anniversary of the start of the 50-day-long democracy protests, nearly a quarter of a century ago, that ran until June 4, 1989, when ordinary people seized on the sudden death of a former leader seen as a political liberal to call for change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/asia/16HuRDV2/16HuRDV2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/world/asia/16HuRDV2/16HuRDV2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/asia/16HuRDV2/16HuRDV2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/asia/16HuRDV2/16HuRDV2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/asia/16HuRDV2/16HuRDV2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/world/asia/16HuRDV2/16HuR