sible for the torture of detainees after the Sept. 11, 2001, terrorist attacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Constitution Project’s Report on Detainee Treatment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T13:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/fc4e3096-275c-5edf-93ba-60850a60b866', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/fc4e3096-275c-5edf-93ba-60850a60b866'}, {'abstract': 'The fund projects worldwide growth of about 3.3 percent this year and 4 percent in 2014; that is a reduction of 0.2 percentage points since January for this year’s figures, and is unchanged for 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/business/economy/imf-lowers-estimates-for-global-growth-for-2013.html', 'snippet': 'The fund projects worldwide growth of about 3.3 percent this year and 4 percent in 2014; that is a reduction of 0.2 percentage points since January for this year’s figures, and is unchanged for 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With economic leaders gathering in Washington for the World Bank and International Monetary Fund spring meetings this week, the I.M.F. has nudged down its estimates for world growth in 2013. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/business/17-FUND/17-FUND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/17/business/17-FUND/17-FUND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/business/17-FUND/17-FUND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/business/17-FUND/17-FUND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I.M.F. Lowers Estimates for Global Economic Growth for 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.M.F. Lowers Estimates for Global Economic Growth for 2013', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowrey, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T13:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f742df8-b25b-5fd0-a8db-62276c153dd9', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f742df8-b25b-5fd0-a8db-62276c153dd9'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, Microsoft will begin offering a new, more basic cloud computing service that competes directly with Amazon’s similar services. And to make sure it’s taken seriously, Microsoft said it will match Amazon’s prices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/microsoft-crashing-amazons-cloud-party/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, Microsoft will begin offering a new, more basic cloud computing service that competes directly with Amazon’s similar services. And to make sure it’s taken seriously, Microsoft said it will match Amazon’s prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As president of Microsoft’s server and tools division, a $19 billion-a-year business devoted to databases, servers and other software products, Satya Nadella has a predictable cast of competitors to worry about. There is Oracle, VMware, SAP and a bunch of other makers of highly technical products that make everyday services like banking and airline reservations work, even if the software running them is invisible to most consumers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/technology/16bits-microsoft/16bits-microsoft-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/technology/16bits-microsoft/16bits-microsoft-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/technology/16bits-microsoft/16bits-microsoft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/technology/16bits-microsoft/16bits-microsoft-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/technology/16bits-microsoft/16bits-microsoft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/technology/16bits-microsoft/16bits-microsoft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/technology/16bits-microsoft/16bits-microsoft-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft Takes Aim at Amazon With a New Cloud Service', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Microsoft’s Shot\r\nAt the Cloud', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T13:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1870120b-5440-5979-a585-d624507a4ae2', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1870120b-5440-5979-a585-d624507a4ae2'}, {'abstract': 'Both working parents are equally in need of child care. So why do I suddenly think of my salary as paying that bill?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/why-do-i-think-my-salary-pays-for-child-care/', 'snippet': 'Both working parents are equally in need of child care. So why do I suddenly think of my salary as paying that bill?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, I wrote an eBook about how couples manage their money. As part of my research, I read “The Creation of Domestic Currencies” by the Princeton professor Viviana Zelizer, who studies the way economics and emotion intertwine. Dr. Zelizer writes about how in the 1920s and ’30s, when wives earned money — no matter how much money it was or how important it was to the family’s bottom line — it was treated as “pin money” and was earmarked for the more frivolous expenses. Maybe it would be used to buy a special dress for the baby. It probably would not be used to buy a house.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Do I Think My Salary Pays for Child Care?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T13:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Grose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e28e353-aff3-5b93-9b71-697b869f15b8', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e28e353-aff3-5b93-9b71-697b869f15b8'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs reports first-quarter profit of $2.2 billion. | SoftBank strikes back after Dish Network made a rival bid for Sprint Nextel. | Energy Future Holdings has a plan to resolve its troubles, but creditors appear less than enthusiastic. | Gold prices fell 9 percent on Monday, the steepest drop in 30 years.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/goldmans-earnings-show-strength/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs reports first-quarter profit of $2.2 billion. | SoftBank strikes back after Dish Network made a rival bid for Sprint Nextel. | Energy Future Holdings has a plan to resolve its troubles, but creditors appear less than enthusiastic. | ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs on Tuesday reported profit of $2.2 billion in the first quarter, driven by strength in investment banking and lending. The earnings of $4.29 a share represented a 9 percent increase from the quarter a year earlier. The results beat analysts’ expectations of $3.89 a share, according to Thomson Reuters. “Our strong client franchise across our businesses drove generally solid results. Still, the potential for macroeconomic instability was felt in the quarter and constrained overall corporate and investor activity,” Lloyd C. Blankfein, Goldman’s chairman and chief executive, said in a statement. Goldman’s stock rose slightly in premarket trading on Tuesday. A conference call to discuss the results is being held at 9:30 a.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman’s Earnings Show Strength', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T13:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/391a9d7d-aa8d-5da0-bb25-0969f8363734', 'word_count': 1502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/391a9d7d-aa8d-5da0-bb25-0969f8363734'}, {'abstract': 'Just as the fight for civil rights defined an era for America, the fight for girls’ education is an urgent moment for Asia and the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/opinion/global/fighting-for-girls-education.html', 'snippet': 'Just as the fight for civil rights defined an era for America, the fight for girls’ education is an urgent moment for Asia and the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regarding “Girls Who Risk Their Lives for Education” by Gordon Brown (Views, April 9): Just as the fight for civil rights defined an era for America, the current fight for girls’ rights to education comes at a ripe and urgent moment for Asia and the Middle East. At a time when revolutions rock false republics and new powers struggle to balance political rights with economic prosperity, women and girls are demanding a guarantee of an equal stake in the futures of their respective countries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting for Girls’ Education', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T13:02:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c65e7bd4-2f96-5d4f-b38f-87c56d140603', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c65e7bd4-2f96-5d4f-b38f-87c56d140603'}, {'abstract': 'A special committee of Dell’s board has reached an agreement with Carl C. Icahn that limits his ownership stake in the company while allowing him to contact other shareholders about a possible bid for the computer maker.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/dell-strikes-deal-with-icahn/', 'snippet': 'A special committee of Dell’s board has reached an agreement with Carl C. Icahn that limits his ownership stake in the company while allowing him to contact other shareholders about a possible bid for the computer maker.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:11 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dell Reaches a Deal With Icahn', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dell, Michael S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Blackstone Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T13:10:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/197e7e2a-5ca1-50b0-b4a1-e169a8b02d5d', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/197e7e2a-5ca1-50b0-b4a1-e169a8b02d5d'}, {'abstract': 'A close result for Hugo Chávez’s chosen sucessor, Nicolás Maduro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/opinion/global/patrick-chappatte-cartoon-venezuelas-election.html', 'snippet': 'A close result for Hugo Chávez’s chosen sucessor, Nicolás Maduro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A close result for Hugo Chávez’s chosen sucessor, Nicolás Maduro.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/opinion/glob