 the region’s largest institutions can receive in bonuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS – European lawmakers voted on Tuesday to cap banker bonuses at the region’s largest institutions, as part of a major set of reforms designed to curb the financial industry’s risky behavior.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Votes to Curb Banker Bonuses', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barroso, Jose Manuel Durao', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T14:43:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott and James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea3833aa-db18-5f04-a21e-c6c0fd453bac', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea3833aa-db18-5f04-a21e-c6c0fd453bac'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/the-gun-report-april-16-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes a shooting can last 14 years. That’s how long it took Jerry Jackson to die after being shot and paralyzed in Kansas City, Mo. Sometimes the aftermath lasts 36 years, as it did for Walter Johnson; 20 years, as it did for Keith Cunningham;\xa023 years, as it did for David A. Thornsley; and sometimes\xa0two and a half, as was the case for Willie Thomas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: April 16, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dayton (Ohio)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Richmond (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trenton (NJ)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Palm Beach (Fla)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T14:52:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdd9fd15-468f-55c1-983c-484f46627167', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdd9fd15-468f-55c1-983c-484f46627167'}, {'abstract': 'Barbra Streisand, recipient of the Film Society’s annual Chaplin Award, is answering select reader questions.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/barbra-streisand-is-taking-your-questions/', 'snippet': 'Barbra Streisand, recipient of the Film Society’s annual Chaplin Award, is answering select reader questions.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:08 p.m. | Updated: Comments are now closed. Responses are published.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/barbra/barbra-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/barbra/barbra-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 846}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/barbra/barbra-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/barbra/barbra-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1328, 'width': 942, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/barbra/barbra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/barbra/barbra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/barbra/barbra-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Barbra Streisand Is Taking Your Questions', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streisand, Barbra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T15:01:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54a9c26a-07dd-5745-b29e-ecf4f7a2f053', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54a9c26a-07dd-5745-b29e-ecf4f7a2f053'}, {'abstract': 'T has an envelope-style clutch with a natural edge.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/catch-of-the-day/', 'snippet': 'T has an envelope-style clutch with a natural edge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to believe that these soft, buttery clutches were once swimming in Lake Victoria and are now eliciting oohs and aahs on a breakfast table at Balthazar in New York. Passers-by stop to ask how to snare one of them. Nile perch leather clutches in natural beige and smoky blue gray are exquisite and surprisingly sturdy. Susan Easton, a former graphic designer who traverses the globe seeking such treasures, found the leather in Kisumu, Kenya, where she met the wives of fishmongers who skin and prepare the fish for sale. Each piece, hand-sewn by an artisan born to a family of tailors, is made from a single fish hide and is sewn along the bottom of the envelope-style clutch, which leaves a flap with an interesting, natural edge. The metal clasp is made of reclaimed brass, hammered and shaped like a fish scale. Get hooked.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catch of the Day', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T15:02:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d6c39d-41e5-51b7-9c87-5b6cbebd84a2', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d6c39d-41e5-51b7-9c87-5b6cbebd84a2'}, {'abstract': 'Tara Siegel Bernard of the Your Money team wants to come to your home and help you sort out your financial life. If you think you have a compelling case, nominate yourself in the comments section.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/need-a-financial-tuneup-nominate-yourself-here/', 'snippet': 'Tara Siegel Bernard of the Your Money team wants to come to your home and help you sort out your financial life. If you think you have a compelling case, nominate yourself in the comments section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is your financial life in disarray or in need of fine-tuning? Do you have a long list of money-related tasks that you can’t seem to get done?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Need a Financial Tuneup? Nominate Yourself Here', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T15:14:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Sieg