ike libations (Parkside Fizz, Paris 75) and nibbled a selection of local cheeses and passed hors d’oeuvres before dinner. During cocktails, Diana Taylor and Elizabeth Leeds were resplendent in coordinating green dresses from Oscar de la Renta and Rag & Bone, respectively.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Schoolyard NYC Spring Benefit', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomfield, April', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gyllenhaal, Jake', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyons, Jenna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Rooster (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotted Pig (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b12f4b0-74c1-5d2c-9d19-72186aea5183', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b12f4b0-74c1-5d2c-9d19-72186aea5183'}, {'abstract': 'If you like the  iconic Judy Collins, then you will enjoy the music and songwriting of Amy Speace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/booming/if-you-like-judy-collins-try-amy-speace.html', 'snippet': 'If you like the  iconic Judy Collins, then you will enjoy the music and songwriting of Amy Speace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, Val Haller, a music-obsessed baby boomer and the founder of the Web site Valslist.com, matches tracks from h