ss Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82f0c209-c851-5d31-8079-d2cff174d4c8', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82f0c209-c851-5d31-8079-d2cff174d4c8'}, {'abstract': 'Supporters of abortion rights called the law, banning most abortions at the 12th week of pregnancy, a “violation of over 40 years of settled United States Supreme Court precedent.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/us/suit-seeks-to-block-arkansas-abortion-law.html', 'snippet': 'Supporters of abortion rights called the law, banning most abortions at the 12th week of pregnancy, a “violation of over 40 years of settled United States Supreme Court precedent.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Supporters of abortion rights on Tuesday filed a challenge to the new Arkansas law banning most abortions at the 12th week of pregnancy, calling it a “violation of over 40 years of settled United States Supreme Court precedent” and a threat to “the rights, liberty and well-being of Arkansas women and their families.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suit Seeks to Block Arkansas Abortion Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arkansas: Challenge to New Law Curbing Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:23:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3f0c3d5-293f-57d4-af07-2820e827d382', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3f0c3d5-293f-57d4-af07-2820e827d382'}, {'abstract': 'How much damage from a calculation mistake?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/holy-coding-error-batman/', 'snippet': 'How much damage from a calculation mistake?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The intellectual edifice of austerity economics rests largely on two academic papers that were seized on by policy makers, without ever having been properly vetted, because they said what the Very Serious People wanted to hear. One was Alesina/Ardagna on the macroeconomic effects of austerity, which immediately became exhibit A for those who wanted to believe in expansionary austerity. Unfortunately, even aside from the paper’s failure to distinguish between episodes in which monetary policy was available and those in which it wasn’t, it turned out that their approach to measuring austerity was all wrong; when the IMF used a measure that tracked actual policy, it turned out that contractionary policy was contractionary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holy Coding Error, Batman', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/658e2611-803f-5623-99ec-4779c8fc5501', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/658e2611-803f-5623-99ec-4779c8fc5501'}, {'abstract': 'Nostalgia for old-fashioned restaurants does not extend to the wine.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/chianti-and-more-for-traditional-italian-dishes/', 'snippet': 'Nostalgia for old-fashioned restaurants does not extend to the wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Tanis shares his recipe for saltimbocca chicken in his column, City Kitchen. Here are some thoughts on what to drink with that dish; share your suggestions in the comments section below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chianti and More for Traditional Italian Dishes', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:48:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b3429f3-a084-583c-8259-9edd93055a77', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b3429f3-a084-583c-8259-9edd93055a77'}, {'abstract': 'Inside the chef Dani García’s first restaurant outside Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/04/17/dining/20130417-REST.html', 'snippet': 'Inside the chef Dani García’s first restaurant outside Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inside the chef Dani García’s first restaurant outside Spain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/20130417-REST-slide-AUL2/20130417-REST-slide-AUL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType':