multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8e0e362c-1951-5876-9cca-c0b93852065e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8e0e362c-1951-5876-9cca-c0b93852065e'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights include premieres by Peter Martins, Justin Peck, Angelin Preljocaj and Liam Scarlett.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/new-york-city-ballet-announces-2013-14-season/', 'snippet': 'Highlights include premieres by Peter Martins, Justin Peck, Angelin Preljocaj and Liam Scarlett.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2013-14 season of New York City Ballet will include the world premieres of ballets by Peter Martins, Justin Peck, Angelin Preljocaj and Liam Scarlett, as well as original scores by Marc-André Dalbavie (Mr. Martins) and Sufjan Stevens (Mr. Peck), the company announced on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Ballet Announces 2013-14 Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:50:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/761e1808-ddf1-52e1-9337-062a2f8e1974', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/761e1808-ddf1-52e1-9337-062a2f8e1974'}, {'abstract': 'A provision in President Obama’s budget would prevent the taxation of student debt forgiven under income-related payment plans.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/budget-would-eliminate-taxes-on-forgiven-student-debt/', 'snippet': 'A provision in President Obama’s budget would prevent the taxation of student debt forgiven under income-related payment plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s proposed budget for the 2014 fiscal year would prevent the taxation of student debt that is forgiven under federal income-based repayment plans, according to the Institute for College Access and Success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Budget Would Eliminate Taxes on Forgiven Student Debt', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Project on Student Debt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:52:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1028009a-8ccc-5631-82dd-a435299a44c4', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1028009a-8ccc-5631-82dd-a435299a44c4'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said he did not believe that North Korea had the ability to miniaturize a nuclear weapon, and he added he would not “reward” the North for provocative acts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/us/politics/obama-voices-doubts-on-north-korean-nuclear-warhead.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama said he did not believe that North Korea had the ability to miniaturize a nuclear weapon, and he added he would not “reward” the North for provocative acts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama said in an interview broadcast Tuesday that he did not believe that North Korea yet had the ability to miniaturize a nuclear weapon to fit atop a missile, and he said nothing would shake him from a strategy of refusing to “reward” the kind of provocative behavior exhibited by Kim Jong-un, the North’s leader.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Doubts That North Korea Can Make a Nuclear Warhead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Doubts That North Korea Can Make a Nuclear Warhead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:52:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger and Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f2d17a5-c72f-5bfa-a0c3-973f6546d1aa', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f2d17a5-c72f-5bfa-a0c3-973f6546d1aa'}, {'abstract': 'At Manzanilla, which is at its best about half the time, Dani García offers exceptional additions to the growing catalog of great Spanish tastes in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/dining/reviews/restaurant-review-manzanilla-in-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'At Manzanilla, which is at its best about half the time, Dani García offers exceptional additions to the growing catalog of great Spanish tastes in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wylie Dufresne was sitting at the end of the bar. In about three weeks he would open another restaurant of his own, but he had given himself a night off to check out somebody else’s, Manzanilla. Its chef and owner is Dani García, a big deal in Andalusia and, as the first guy to bring liquid nitrogen into the kitchen, a member in good standing of the modernist sorcerers’ club. At his flagship restaurant, Calima in Marbella, Mr. García makes trompe l’oeil tomatoes and fashions chocolate butterflies with mango wings. Simply by opening Manzanilla, his first restaurant outside Spain, on East 26th Street, he has drastically increased the number of chefs in town with whom Mr. Dufresne might conceivably swap recipes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17REST1_SPAN/17REST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17REST1_SPAN/17REST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17REST1_SPAN/17REST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17REST1_SPAN/17REST1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17REST1_SPAN/17REST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17REST1_SPAN/17REST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/dining/17REST1_SPAN/17REST1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Import With a Foot in Spain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Import With a Foot in Spain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manzanilla (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Dani', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c32b34e1-8a12-5803-a1cd-9d9b585110e9', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c32b34e1-8a12-5803-a1cd-9d9b585110e9'}, {'abstract': '“Torture” and “terror” are not neutral nouns; in the context of our post-9/11 politics, they are verdicts, and sometimes badges of political allegiance.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/the-t-words/', 'snippet': '“Torture” and “terror” are not neutral nouns; in the context of our post-9/11 politics, they are verdicts, and sometimes badges of political allegiance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Terror. Torture. Name it and claim it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The T Words', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T17:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42fa866-26d1-5960-a075-800997c31cee', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42fa866-26d1-5960-a075-800997c31cee'}, {'abstract': 'The season will also include new work from Suzan-Lori Parks, Mike Daisey and Elevator Repair Service.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/public-theater-season-to-include-fun-home-and-new-play-in-apple-family-series/', 'snippet': 'The season will also include new work from Suzan-Lori Parks, Mike Daisey and Elevator Repair Service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Public Theater’s 2013-14 season, announced on Tuesday, will include the new musical “Fun Home,” based on the graphic novel by Alison Bechdel, and the new play “Regular Singing,” the fourth and final part of the critically acclaimed Apple family series by Richard Nelson. In addition, all four plays in the Apple series – which are each set on important days or anniversaries in American civic life – will be performed at the Public in repertory, with “Regular Singing” opening on Nov. 22 – the 50th anniversary of the Kennedy assassination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main'