act-chapin-sisters/', 'snippet': 'On their new album, the Chapin Sisters channel the Everly Brothers to sublime effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abigail and Lily Chapin have been singing together their entire lives, and performing as a band, the Chapin Sisters, for almost a decade. For their latest project, the pair decided to compose an album entirely of Everly Brothers songs — not so much as a tribute but, according to Abigail, 33, as “a master class.” Because the folk-pop duo began their career as a trio — their half-sister, Jessica Craven, left the group to start a family in 2009 — they’d been studying the Everlys for clues as to how to move from what Abigail describes as “an almost doo-wop style, in which one of us is singing and the other two were kind of backing her up,” to a sound that features the kind of two-part harmonies that the Brothers are famous for, in which both singers deliver almost every line “as a single storyteller.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sister Act | Chapin Sisters', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chapin Sisters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Everly Brothers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T21:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Waterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0aaa86e-96f4-5129-a9e4-30f9d993be12', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0aaa86e-96f4-5129-a9e4-30f9d993be12'}, {'abstract': 'Want to know about the benefits of juice cleanses? Can fresh juices make you look Gwyneth Paltrow-radiant?', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/dr-leo-galland-is-answering-your-fresh-juice-questions/', 'snippet': 'Want to know about the benefits of juice cleanses? Can fresh juices make you look Gwyneth Paltrow-radiant?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can 16 ounces of vegetable juice really help “cleanse” your body of toxins? And which toxins are we talking about? What are “live enzymes,” anyway, and should you be ingesting more of them? If you’ve got gobs of fruit (and the sugar that comes from it) squeezed into your cold-pressed juice, is that ultimately a good thing or a bad thing? What’s up with wheatgrass and liquid chlorophyll? Should fresh juice be pasteurized? Can a juice cleanse really make your skin as glowingly radiant as Gwyneth Paltrow’s? ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/dining/dj-drgalland/dj-drgalland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/dining/dj-drgalland/dj-drgalland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 701}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/dining/dj-drgalland/dj-drgalland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 877, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/dining/dj-drgalland/dj-drgalland-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 1092, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/dining/dj-drgalland/dj-drgalland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c