://slideshow/68bdc461-24a8-5e38-b53d-78f7ddaac62f'}, {'abstract': 'An NBC special report drew the most viewers, but all cable news channels reported a spike in audiences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/business/media/viewers-flock-to-tv-news-after-boston-blasts.html', 'snippet': 'An NBC special report drew the most viewers, but all cable news channels reported a spike in audiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of viewers turned to cable news starting Monday afternoon as word spread of the bomb attacks at the Boston Marathon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TV Viewers Flock to News Programs After Boston Blasts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T22:18:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1728340-4d17-5381-b89a-d168065c821b', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1728340-4d17-5381-b89a-d168065c821b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Summerall was a place-kicker who later went on to a career in broadcasting, forming a famous team with John Madden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/sports/football/pat-summerall-star-with-nfl-giants-and-on-tv-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Summerall was a place-kicker who later went on to a career in broadcasting, forming a famous team with John Madden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pat Summerall, the Giants’ outstanding place-kicker who went on to team with John Madden for 21 seasons in network television’s most prominent N.F.L. broadcast twosome, died on Tuesday in Dallas. He was 82.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/summerall-2/summerall-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/summerall-2/summerall-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/summerall-2/summerall-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/summerall-2/summerall-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1337, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/summerall-2/summerall-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/summerall-2/summerall-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/sports/summerall-2/summerall-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pat Summerall, Star Kicker With Giants and a Calm Voice on TV, Dies at 82', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pat Summerall, Star Kicker With Giants and a Calm Voice on TV, Dies at 82', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summerall, Pat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldstein, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madden, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T22:18:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/87a767fd-ee41-5990-b2dd-8442118e4573', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87a767fd-ee41-5990-b2dd-8442118e4573'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Deceptive Practice: The Mysteries and Mentors of Ricky Jay” invites viewers to join one of Mr. Jay’s magical mystery tours. But don’t expect him to reveal where that coin went.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/movies/deceptive-practice-the-mysteries-and-mentors-of-ricky-jay.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Deceptive Practice: The Mysteries and Mentors of Ricky Jay” invites viewers to join one of Mr. Jay’s magical mystery tours. But don’t expect him to reveal where that coin went.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Deceptive Practice: The Mysteries and Mentors of Ricky Jay” is a mouthful of a title, if not nearly as charmingly loquacious as those for some of Mr. Jay’s books, including “Learned Pigs & Fireproof Women: Unique, Eccentric and Amazing Entertainers: Stone Eaters, Mind Readers, Poison Resisters, Daredevils, Singing Mice, etc., etc., etc., etc.” Those four punctuating “etc.’s” — what more could there be? — are an especially nice touch because they suggest that Mr. Jay has so much up his pushed-up sleeves that he couldn’t possibly squeeze everything into a single title.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/jpdeceptive/jpdeceptive-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/jpdeceptive/jpdeceptive-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 679}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/jpdeceptive/jpdeceptive-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 905, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/jpdeceptive/jpdeceptive-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1810, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/jpdeceptive/jpdeceptive-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/jpdeceptive/jpdeceptive-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/arts/jpdeceptive/jpdeceptive-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping His Secrets Well Up His Sleeve', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping His Secrets Well Up His Sleeve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay, Ricky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edelstein, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Molly', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T22:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/273a702a-6b6d-5449-95aa-57c2693d9e9d', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/273a702a-6b6d-5449-95aa-57c2693d9e9d'}, {'abstract': 'A re-cap of The Times Magazine’s softball game last night against New York magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/how-we-got-more-than-even-with-new-york-magazine/', 'snippet': 'A re-cap of The Times Magazine’s softball game last night against New York magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Duke and Carolina never play each other until the final month of the college basketball season. And the Army-Navy game traditionally is the last contest of the college football regular season. So, yes, it seemed a wee unnatural that The New York Times Magazine and New York magazine would meet in the season opener of their media softball league on Monday night. It was pegged as our big rivalry game of the year for reasons I’m not entirely clear about. I guess some of our people used to work there and vice versa. (Oh, and they also beat us last year.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/magazine/16-softball/16-softball-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/magazine/16-softball/16-softball-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/magazine/16-softball/16-softball-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/magazine/16-softball/16-softball-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/magazine/16-softball/16-softball-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/magazine/16-softball/16-softball-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/magazine/16-softball/16-softball-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How We Got More Than Even With New York Magazine', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T22:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce561be9-f38c-5a45-88c1-84933d060225', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce561be9-f38c-5a45-88c1-84933d060225'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of restaurants that offer the experience of eating animal heads.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/16/where-to-find-fish-rabbit-and-duck-heads-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'A listing of restaurants that offer the experience of eating animal heads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to a renewed appreciation of China’s rustic culinary roots, eating animal heads has become fashionable in Beijing, as Craig Smith writes in this week’s Dining section. There are restaurants solely devoted to the preparation of fish, rabbit and duck heads. In New York you may search long and hard without finding such a restaurant. Look carefully, though — not only in the warrens of a mall in Flushing, Queens, but also on Restaurant Row in Manhattan — and you may be surprised to see what’s looking back. Though the cooking process may render an entire head a nearly uniform brown, there’s no mistaking a rabbit’s incisors or a duck’s bill.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/dining/dj-head/dj-head-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/dining/dj-head/dj-head-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 