elope addressed to Senator Roger Wicker of Mississippi showed positive results for the toxin in tests at a mail facility in Washington. It was sent to the F.B.I. for more analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/us/politics/toxic-ricin-detected-on-mail-sent-to-senator.html', 'snippet': 'An envelope addressed to Senator Roger Wicker of Mississippi showed positive results for the toxin in tests at a mail facility in Washington. It was sent to the F.B.I. for more analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A letter sent to a Mississippi senator tested positive for the poison ricin, federal authorities revealed Tuesday, adding to security concerns in the Capitol after the Boston Marathon bombing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter Mailed to Senator Tests Positive for Ricin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Toxic Ricin Is Detected in Letter Mailed to Senator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wicker, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ricin (Poison)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-16T23:35:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf343438-e829-58de-960d-34b6f1e91350', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf343438-e829-58de-960d-34b6f1e91350'}, {'abstract': 'With polar ice melting each year, the governments of five countries wi