e_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e871a022-2cb7-5e37-9c10-71f7b0e18c7b', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e871a022-2cb7-5e37-9c10-71f7b0e18c7b'}, {'abstract': 'Prof. Ronald F. Levant answers readers’ questions  about re-entering the dating world, impotence and other male sexuality problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/booming/advice-from-expert-on-male-sexuality-part-2.html', 'snippet': 'Prof. Ronald F. Levant answers readers’ questions  about re-entering the dating world, impotence and other male sexuality problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers recently submitted questions about male sexuality to Dr. Ronald F. Levant, a professor of psychology and director of the Psychology Department Counseling Clinic at the University of Akron. Part 1 of his answers can be found here. Dr. Levant was president of the American Psychological Association and is an author or editor of 14 books, including “Men and Sex: New Psychological Perspectives.” Dr. Levant asked the counselors whom he supervises in his clinic, all Ph.D. students in psychology who see a broad range of clients, to help him compose answers to these questions. Thanks are given to Mike Aguilar, Brittany Baker, Natalie Grandy, Craig Libman and Arielle Riutort. Because of the large number of submissions, not every question was addressed. In particular, we were not able to answer questions on medical issues, as our expertise is psychological, not medical. This feature is closed to further questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/03/booming/03expert-booming-malesex/03expert-booming-malesex-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advice From Expert on Male Sexuality, Part 2', 'kicker': 'Ask an Expert', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impotence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a284511-a918-5355-b754-79116c288b8d', 'word_count': 2996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a284511-a918-5355-b754-79116c288b8d'}, {'abstract': 'No matter how you finance your business, it makes sense to think about how you are going to get out before you decide to get in.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/the-tax-implications-of-starting-a-business-with-retirement-money/', 'snippet': 'No matter how you finance your business, it makes sense to think about how you are going to get out before you decide to get in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I wrote about the risks of using retirement money to finance your business. I spent some time looking at a strategy called ROBS — rollover as business start-up — and came to the conclusion that although it is being done by thousands of businesses, it has yet to receive the full blessing of either the Internal Revenue Service or the Department of Labor. As a result, I would advise my clients to stay away from the strategy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tax Implications of Starting a Business With Retirement Money', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Gains Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T11:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Patrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e7636e8-de9c-52a1-a927-a1ffc914180a', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e7636e8-de9c-52a1-a927-a1ffc914180a'}, {'abstract': 'Picture walking in the dark in a Vietnamese forest where you can see only the tiny area right in front of your feet, illuminated by a flashlight or a headlamp. Now imagine trying to do your work in this dark world.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/waiting-for-the-dark/', 'snippet': 'Picture walking in the dark in a Vietnamese forest where you can see only the tiny area right in front of your feet, illuminated by a flashlight or a headlamp. Now imagine trying to do your work in this dark world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary E. Blair is a postdoctoral researcher in the American Museum of Natural History’s Center for Biodiversity and Conservation, where she coordinates the Enhancing Diversity in Conservation Science Initiative.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/saw-blair-2-4/saw-blair-2-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/science/saw-blair-2-4/saw-blair-2-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/saw-blair-2-4/saw-blair-2-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/saw-blair-2-4/saw-blair-2-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/saw-blair-2-4/saw-blair-2-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/science/saw-blair-2-4/saw-blair-2-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/science/saw-blair-2-4/saw-blair-2-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting for the Dark', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T11:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary E. Blair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Blair', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adb1430f-41e6-559d-84f9-43883a9a2883', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adb1430f-41e6-559d-84f9-43883a9a2883'}, {'abstract': 'The founder of microfinance discusses his fight to protect the Grameen Bank and the future of social business.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/beyond-profit-a-talk-with-muhammad-yunus/', 'snippet': 'The founder of microfinance discusses his fight to protect the Grameen Bank and the future of social business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, in a ceremony at the United States Capitol, Congressional leaders will present the founder of the Grameen Bank, Muhammad Yunus, with the Congressional Gold Medal in recognition of his “efforts to combat global poverty.”\xa0 The award places Yunus in the company of a small group of people – including Norman Borlaug, Martin Luther King, Jr., Nelson Mandela, Elie Wiesel, Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, and Mother Teresa — who have received this award, as well as the Presidential Medal of Freedom and the Nobel Peace Prize.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Profit: A Talk With Muhammad Yunus', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microfinance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yunus, Muhammad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grameen Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T11:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a4f6388-24c0-5f13-b425-5b5916fdd545', 'word_count': 2390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a4f6388-24c0-5f13-b425-5b5916fdd545'}, {'abstract': 'Still Reinhartrogoffing.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/further-further-thoughts-on-death-by-excel/', 'snippet': 'Still Reinhartrogoffing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few somewhat unrelated notes on the Reinhart-Rogoff fiasco:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Further Further Thoughts On Death By Excel', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T11:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1669eaa-1dca-5308-9c48-e8451b5a64c0', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1669eaa-1dca-5308-9c48-e8451b5a64c0'}, {'abstract': 'The music teacher who hated horses, and won the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/horse-soldiers-blogging/', 'snippet': 'The music teacher who hated horses, and won the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was little I loved, just loved the John Ford movie The Horse Soldiers, a dramatization of Grierson’s Raid; I think I made my father take me four times. As an adult, unfortunately, I found it more or less unwatchable — the prettification of war just won’t wash for me now. (The famous scene with the military school students never happened during that raid; something like it did happen during Sherman’s sweep through the Carolinas, but it was a slaughter).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Horse Soldiers Blogging', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T11:12:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b68fbae6-30ea-5fc8-9562-54cc73780385', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b68fbae6-30ea-5fc8-9562-54cc73780385'}, {'abstract': 'Apple’s iTunes program includes a setting that lets you take holiday music, podcasts and other types of audio out of the mix when 