it had fired the two rockets in support of Palestinian prisoners held in Israeli jails.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Two rockets fired from the Egyptian Sinai Peninsula struck the southern Israeli resort of Eilat on Wednesday, causing no damage or injuries, according to the Israeli military. The first such attack on that city in a year, it underscored the continuing threat from militants operating across the desert border.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Militants in Egyptian Sinai Fire Rockets Into Israel but Do No Damage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militants in Egyptian Sinai Fire Rockets Into Israel but Do No Damage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eilat (Israel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T15:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d198267-6f1d-5265-bb38-a88ae349cb42', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d198267-6f1d-5265-bb38-a88ae349cb42'}, {'abstract': 'Casey Garret Johnson, who served as a political analyst in Afghanistan from 2008 to 2012, discusses the function of an Islamic court system.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/afghan-islamic-courts-a-pre-taliban-system-with-post-2014-potential/', 'snippet': 'Casey Garret Johnson, who served as a political analyst in Afghanistan from 2008 to 2012, discusses the function of an Islamic court system.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The American military has built much of its transition strategy in Afghanistan around establishing local police forces to help keep the peace. In recent months, much has been made about the rise of indigenous anti-insurgent forces, separate from the American-sponsored local police, in the historical Taliban strongholds of Ghazni and Kandahar Provinces. Implicit in the praise for these forces is that indigenous militias of this type represent a vital local vision for the future and a sustainable means of keeping the Taliban at bay after 2014.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Islamic Courts: A Pre-Taliban System With Post-2014 Potential?', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kandahar (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panjwai (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T15:40:45+0000', 