_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/us/politics/officials-intercept-suspicious-letter-sent-to-obama.html', 'snippet': 'Federal agents arrested a man suspected of sending letters feared to have been tainted with the poison ricin to President Obama and a Mississippi senator, according to two officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Federal agents arrested a man on Monday suspected of sending letters feared contaminated by the poison ricin to President Obama and a Mississippi senator, according to two officials with knowledge of the case. The suspect was identified as Paul Kevin Curtis of Tupelo, Miss.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mississippi Man Is Arrested in Sending of Suspicious Letters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officials Intercept Suspicious Letter Sent to Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T15:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42658f8-248f-57d4-8729-f0e42018f1db', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42658f8-248f-57d4-8729-f0e42018f1db'}, {'abstract': 'Bennie M. Ginyard, of South Ozon