ndra-bernhard-looks-back-on-the-king-of-comedy/', 'snippet': 'Sandra Bernhard, the actress and comedian, recalls her audition process and working with Jerry Lewis on Martin Scorsese’s dark satire about a dangerously frustrated standup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been 30 years since Rupert Pupkin made his notorious debut on “The Jerry Langford Show,” a moment that exists only within the reality of “The King of Comedy,” Martin Scorsese’s dark satire about a struggling standup (played by Robert De Niro) who kidnaps his favorite talk-show host (Jerry Lewis). But it’s also a more tangible milestone for the film’s co-star Sandra Bernhard, who played Masha, an equally unhinged fan who helps Pupkin carry out his twisted show-biz schemes: for Ms. Bernhard, “The King of Comedy” was a breakthrough (for which she was cast from the comedy-club scene in Los Angeles) that garnered critical praise and led her to a wider stage and screen career.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/kingofcomedy/kingofcomedy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/kingofcomedy/kingofcomedy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/kingofcomedy/kingofcomedy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/kingofcomedy/kingofcomedy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/arts/kingofcomedy/kingofcomedy-t