ion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fc6f822-9471-5d74-92ed-e506b303d9e0', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fc6f822-9471-5d74-92ed-e506b303d9e0'}, {'abstract': 'Sebastian Junger’s documentary about the war photojournalist Tim Hetherington, who was killed in 2011 in Libya, will be on HBO on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/arts/television/jungers-film-which-way-is-the-front-line-from-here-on-hbo.html', 'snippet': 'Sebastian Junger’s documentary about the war photojournalist Tim Hetherington, who was killed in 2011 in Libya, will be on HBO on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British-born photojournalist Tim Hetherington starts and stops, groans and grimaces, as he tries to explain why he’s made a career of taking his cameras as close as possible to the places where men are killing each other. He manages to get out, “The important thing for me is to make work that is connected to people,” before shaking his head in disgust: “Blah blah blah blah blah.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/arts/18WHICHWAY/18WHICHWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/arts/18WHICHWAY/18WHICHWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/arts/18WHICHWAY/18WHICHWAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/arts/18WHICHWAY/18WHICHWAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy':