lly jar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Deborah Ehrlich, a glass designer in Accord, N.Y., needed a new porch light almost four years ago, she designed one. “The idea was a jelly jar,” she said. But it is a refined version, made by artisans in Sweden with whom Ms. Ehrlich has worked for 13 years. The material is Swedish crystal. “You can blow it very thin, and it doesn’t break,” Ms. Ehrlich said. The light, which has a white glazed porcelain base and a rubbed brass shade holder, is now in production. Fully assembled, it measures 4 inches wide and 8 inches high, and sells for $225 at Artware Editions, 270 Bowery, second floor (Houston Street), (212) 463-7490; artwareeditions.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18LIGHTING_SPAN/18LIGHTING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18LIGHTING_SPAN/18LIGHTING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18LIGHTING_SPAN/18LIGHTING_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18LIGHTING_SPAN/18LIGHTING_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18LIGHTING_SPAN/18LIGHTING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18LIGHTING_SPAN/18LIGHTING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18LIGHTING_SPAN/18LIGHTING_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inspiration From a PB&J', 'kicker': 'Currents | Lighting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inspiration From a PB&J', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Artware Editions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T22:06:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0486525-77af-50d3-a5ab-ab1f61ebc263', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0486525-77af-50d3-a5ab-ab1f61ebc263'}, {'abstract': 'Christie’s is holding an auction of villa furnishings chosen by Michael S. Smith, the Obamas’ White House decorator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/garden/christies-auction-of-villa-furnishings-chosen-by-michael-s-smith.html', 'snippet': 'Christie’s is holding an auction of villa furnishings chosen by Michael S. Smith, the Obamas’ White House decorator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On April 23 and 24, Christie’s will stage an auction of the contents of a Palladian-style villa in Malibu, Calif., that was designed by Michael S. Smith, the Obamas’ White House decorator. The auction includes many museum-quality pieces, including a Sean Scully painting and a Persian rug that once belonged to the Agnelli family of Italy. A Chinese brown lacquer altar table, shown, has an estimated sale price of $4,000 to $6,000. There’s also a trove of Asian art and antiques, Old Master paintings and historic European furniture (more than 450 lots) with an estimated sale value of $3.5 million to $5 million. It took Mr. Smith five years to accumulate all the treasures, and he may bid at the auction himself. “I’m not done with anything,” he said. “I’d buy it all again.” So attached is he to the project that he wrote a book about it, “Building Beauty: The Alchemy of Design” (Rizzoli, $55). Information: (212) 636-2000 or Christies.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18EVENTS/18CURR6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18EVENTS/18CURR6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 933}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18EVENTS/18CURR6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18EVENTS/18CURR6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1317, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18EVENTS/18CURR6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18EVENTS/18CURR6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18EVENTS/18CURR6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He Wouldn’t Change a Thing', 'kicker': 'Currents | Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Wouldn’t Change Anything', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Michael S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Arlene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T22:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bd0d892-6d00-50f6-832b-2919d645acb0', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bd0d892-6d00-50f6-832b-2919d645acb0'}, {'abstract': 'Limited-edition furnishings made from recycled materials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/garden/designs-that-help-redefine-craft.html', 'snippet': 'Limited-edition furnishings made from recycled materials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By weekday, John Liston is a glass artisan working for other artists and architects in Oakland, Calif. But the rest of the time, he experiments with his own furniture and lighting in a cooperative studio in San Francisco. Out of these efforts have come burnt-recycled-wood cabinets ($11,000), lights with industrial-glass orbs perched on scrap-metal tripods ($25,000) and other mixed-media pieces, which he displays at craft shows. One of his cheeriest works is his bright orange Ribbon chair, shown, made of crisscrossed steel slats ($6,000).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18FURNITURE/18CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18FURNITURE/18CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 625}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18FURNITURE/18CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 984, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18FURNITURE/18CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1968, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18FURNITURE/18CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18FURNITURE/18CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18FURNITURE/18CURR5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Designs That Help Redefine ‘Craft’', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Designs That Help Redefine ‘Craft’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keenan, Sandy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T22:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandy Keenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3c99262-fe7c-5767-84ee-0bb6caa92af5', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3c99262-fe7c-5767-84ee-0bb6caa92af5'}, {'abstract': '“The Flower Recipe Book” is a practical guide to flower arranging by Alethea Harampolis and Jill Rizzo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/garden/the-flower-recipe-book-by-alethea-harampolis-and-jill-rizzo.html', 'snippet': '“The Flower Recipe Book” is a practical guide to flower arranging by Alethea Harampolis and Jill Rizzo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t be misled by the title: “The Flower Recipe Book,” by Alethea Harampolis and Jill Rizzo (Artisan, $24.95), is not a guide for making hibiscus enchiladas or scented-geranium sorbet. Rather, it’s a beautifully illustrated and practical guide to the ephemeral art of fresh-flower arranging.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18BOOKS_SPAN/18BOOKS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/garden/18BOOKS_SPAN/18BOOKS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'