akers kill crucial gun control legislation a mere 18 weeks after the massacre in Newtown, Conn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/opinion/the-senate-fails-americans-on-gun-bills.html', 'snippet': 'Bowing to the gun lobby rather than the public, lawmakers kill crucial gun control legislation a mere 18 weeks after the massacre in Newtown, Conn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 45 senators, the carnage at Sandy Hook Elementary School is a forgotten tragedy. The toll of 270 Americans who are shot every day is not a problem requiring action. The easy access to guns on the Internet, and the inevitability of the next massacre, is not worth preventing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Senate Fails Americans', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Senate Fails Americans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T23:16:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcf75a87-0e69-5522-9d0d-89e87c8eb9c4', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcf75a87-0e69-5522-9d0d-89e87c8eb9c4'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Prunier, originally recruited by the Army as a translator, was part of a clandestine mission to teach 200 Viet Minh guerrillas how to use American weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/world/asia/henry-a-prunier-army-operative-who-helped-trained-vietnamese-troops-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Prunier, originally recruited by the Army as a translator, was part of a clandestine mission to teach 200 Viet Minh guerrillas how to use American weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henry A. Prunier taught Vo Nguyen Giap, the Vietnamese general who withstood the armies of France and the United States, how to throw a grenade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/world/PRUNIER2-obit/PRUNIER2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/world/PRUNIER2-obit/PRUNIER2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 867}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/world/PRUNIER2-obit/PRUNIER2-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/world/PRUNIER2-obit/PRUNIER2-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1920, 'width': 1329, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/world/PRUNIER2-obit/PRUNIER2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/18/world/PRUNIER2-obit/PRUNIER2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/world/PRUNIER2-obit/PRUNIER2-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Henry A. Prunier, 91, U.S. Soldier Who Trained Vietnamese Troops, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Henry Prunier, 91, Dies; \r\nWas Part of U.S. Mission\r\nTo Train the Viet Minh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prunier, Henry A (1921-2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T23:32:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d201f416-1f02-590e-afaa-a108dc5b907b', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d201f416-1f02-590e-afaa-a108dc5b907b'}, {'abstract': 'Stemming from a Virgil Exner-designed, Ghia-built Chrysler concept, the Dual-Ghia convertible was a favorite among late-1950s Hollywood stars.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/italian-coachwork-in-american-proportions-the-dual-ghia-convertible/', 'snippet': 'Stemming from a Virgil Exner-designed, Ghia-built Chrysler concept, the Dual-Ghia convertible was a favorite among late-1950s Hollywood stars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After seeing what sorts of concept-car tricks automakers were up to at the last few auto shows, it’s fun to dust off the pages of history and examine the concepts that designers dreamed up in the 1950s. Today, form usually follows function\xa0— with the possible exception of the huge, masculine grilles currently in vogue\xa0— but during the early years of the jet age, the Big Three fielded many flamboyant, sleek concepts with lines that brought to mind images of rockets blasting off into outer space.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Coachwork in American Proportions: the Dual-Ghia Convertible', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Convertibles (Autos)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carmichael, Hoagy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Exner, Virgil M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sinatra, Frank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-17T23:38:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37893689-3062-5682-91eb-449792d8e105', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37893689-3062-5682-91eb-449792d8e105'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry suggested a recount in the presidential vote and said he had yet to evaluate whether Washington would recognize Nicolás Maduro’s victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/world/americas/kerry-encourages-recount-in-venezuela.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry suggested a recount in the presidential vote and said he had yet to evaluate whether Washington would recognize Nicolás Maduro’s victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — Secretary of State John Kerry said Wednesday that Venezuela should hold a recount of votes cast in its presidential election, which the country’s electoral authorities say was narrowly won by a protégé of former President Hugo Chávez. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/americas/a1-2-sub-venezuela/a1-2-sub-venezuela-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/16/world/americas/a1-2-sub-venezuela/a1-2-sub-venezuela-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/americas/a1-2-sub-venezuela/a1-2-sub-venezuela-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/americas/a1-2-sub-venezuela/a1-2-sub-venezuela-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1416, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/16/world/americas/a1-2-sub-venezuela/a1-2-sub-venezuela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/16/world/americas/a1-2-sub-venezuela/a1-2-sub-venezuela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'captio