ion': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Isles’ Road to Playoffs Is Barnstorming Tour', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Isles’ Road to Playoffs Is Barnstorming Tour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kreda, Allan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streit, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nabokov, Evgeni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:03:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kreda', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kreda', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2152e903-5462-5e86-bf8f-1255e2e3cdff', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2152e903-5462-5e86-bf8f-1255e2e3cdff'}, {'abstract': 'Before Knicks fans get too excited about Carmelo Anthony’s first scoring title, note that the N.B.A.’s leading scorer has rarely played for the league champion.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/only-one-title-matters-and-its-not-scoring/', 'snippet': 'Before Knicks fans get too excited about Carmelo Anthony’s first scoring title, note that the N.B.A.’s leading scorer has rarely played for the league champion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Knicks fans get too excited about Carmelo Anthony’s first scoring title, note that the N.B.A.’s leading scorer has rarely played for the league champion. That feat has been accomplished 11 times by five players, and six of those times were by one player: Michael Jordan. No one has done it since Shaquille O’Neal led the Lakers to a title in 1999-2000.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Only One Title Matters (and It’s Not Scoring)', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Only One Title Matters (and It’s Not Scoring)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd2c92d1-ed88-58bc-8fc4-54487579dbc0', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd2c92d1-ed88-58bc-8fc4-54487579dbc0'}, {'abstract': 'In a Unicef report, the United States once again ranked among the worst wealthy countries for children’s well-being.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/opinion/blow-the-kids-are-not-all-right.html', 'snippet': 'In a Unicef report, the United States once again ranked among the worst wealthy countries for children’s well-being.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States has done it again — and not in a good way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kids Are (Not) All Right', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Kids Are (Not) All Right', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United Nations Children's Fund", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:03:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles M. Blow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb91439-c6b6-57bc-a0ad-948d72cad8a5', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb91439-c6b6-57bc-a0ad-948d72cad8a5'}, {'abstract': 'Cooking is not only a democratic pleasure, it is also daily creativity, it’s economic, it’s healthy, and it’s a link to the natural world.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/pollan-cooks/', 'snippet': 'Cooking is not only a democratic pleasure, it is also daily creativity, it’s economic, it’s healthy, and it’s a link to the natural world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The seven most famous words in the movement for good food are: “Eat food. Not too much. Mostly plants.” They were written, of course, by Michael Pollan, in “In Defense of Food: An Eater’s Manifesto,” the follow-up to “The Omnivore’s Dilemma.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pollan Cooks!', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pollan Cooks!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollan, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77528dc2-17dd-5d0a-9dd8-55c74e47a97c', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77528dc2-17dd-5d0a-9dd8-55c74e47a97c'}, {'abstract': 'The breach caused by Hurricane Sandy allows the ocean to pour into the bay, flushing it with badly needed clean and oxygen-rich water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/opinion/fire-islands-lucky-break.html', 'snippet': 'The breach caused by Hurricane Sandy allows the ocean to pour into the bay, flushing it with badly needed clean and oxygen-rich water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fire Island, the long ribbon of sand, grass and dwarf-pine forest that lies off the South Shore of Long Island, has two main jobs. One is to be a lovely setting for vacation cottages and deer. The other is to be the barrier that encloses the placid Great South Bay and protects large swaths of the suburban mainland from the open Atlantic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire Island’s Lucky Break', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Suburban Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fire Island’s Lucky Break', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downes, Lawrence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fire Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great South Bay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d5c189a-6ade-537a-9d0e-0bb32c2736bb', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d5c189a-6ade-537a-9d0e-0bb32c2736bb'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court’s five conservatives have gutted a generation of careful, court-made law used to address abuses abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/opinion/the-supreme-courts-setback-for-human-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court’s five conservatives have gutted a generation of careful, court-made law used to address abuses abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court’s conservatives dealt a major blow Wednesday to the ability of American federal courts to hold violators of international human rights accountable. The court declared that a 1789 law called the Alien Tort Statute does not allow foreigners to sue in American courts to seek redress “for violations of the law of nations occurring outside the United States.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Giant Setback for Human Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Giant Setback for Human Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alien Tort Statute (1789)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:06:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7be56e9c-cd88-5061-bdfd-011a1ae07df6', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7be56e9c-cd88-5061-bdfd-011a1ae07df6'}, {'abstract': 'The Costa Rican federation has wants to play its World Cup qualifier against the United States at Estadio Saprissa in September.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/17/surprise-ticos-want-to-play-u-s-at-saprissa/', 'snippet': 'The Costa Rican federation has wants to play its World Cup qualifier against the United States at Estadio Saprissa in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It never snows in Costa Rica, but other unmentionable items have been know to rain down on opposing players at Estadio Ricardo Saprissa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/sports/soccer/usloggo/usloggo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/sports/soccer/usloggo/usloggo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/sports/soccer/usloggo/usloggo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/21/sports/soccer/usloggo/usloggo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surprise! Ticos Want to Play U.S. at Saprissa', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Costa Rica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d15b3772-588e-52d3-8516-44eb93484557', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d15b3772-588e-52d3-8516-44eb93484557'}, {'abstract': 'Everyone invokes Simón Bolívar, even if they embody what he hated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/opinion/arana-latin-americas-go-to-hero.html', 'snippet': 'Everyone invokes Simón Bolívar, even if they embody what he hated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can you name an American founder whose name is shouted in the streets, whose legacy inspires fanatical worship, whose image is used to bolster ideals not his own, whose mantle is claimed by both left and right? There is no Washington party, no Jeffersonian republic. No one runs for president in Madison’s name. But in Latin America, as the Venezuelan election on Sunday reminded us, the question is easy, and the answer is Simón Bolívar. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/opinion/marie-arana/marie-arana-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/opinion/marie-arana/marie-arana-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/opinion/marie-arana/marie-arana-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/opinion/marie-arana/marie-arana-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/opinion/marie-arana/marie-arana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/20/opinion/marie-arana/marie-arana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/opinion/marie-arana/marie-arana-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latin America’s Go-To Hero', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Guest Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latin America’s Go-To Hero', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arana, Marie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolivar, Simon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Arana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/be5b0a01-1c46-50fb-b14a-0b94a4c838bb', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be5b0a01-1c46-50fb-b14a-0b94a4c838bb'}, {'abstract': 'Saying it was frustrated with some of the worst criminal violence in the world, the Honduran congress suspended the attorney general and his assistant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/world/americas/honduras-attorney-general-is-suspended.html', 'snippet': 'Saying it was frustrated with some of the worst criminal violence in the world, the Honduran congress suspended the attorney general and his assistant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saying it was frustrated with some of the worst criminal violence in the world, the Honduran congress suspended the attorney general and his assistant and replaced them with a temporary oversight committee. The three-person commission will have 60 days to analyze why the prosecutor’s office has been unable to solve so many criminal cases, and will generate a plan to improve the trustworthiness of the institution. Honduras, which has become a major drug route to the United States, has one of the highest homicide rates in the world. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honduras: Attorney General Is Suspended', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honduras: Attorney General Suspended', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1e2079-044f-5ede-8f96-de4b47492156', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1e2079-044f-5ede-8f96-de4b47492156'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt’s chief prosecutor on Wednesday ordered the transfer of former President Hosni Mubarak from a Cairo military hospital back to prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/world/middleeast/egypt-mubarak-to-be-moved-to-prison.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s chief prosecutor on Wednesday ordered the transfer of former President Hosni Mubarak from a Cairo military hospital back to prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Egypt’s chief prosecutor on Wednesday ordered the transfer of former President Hosni Mubarak from a Cairo military hospital back to prison. Mr. Mubarak is expected to be held there pending a retrial on charges including complicity in the killing of protesters during the 2011 revolt that toppled him. He had been in the hospital since December after injuring himself during a fall in the prison shower, his lawyers said. The prosecutor ordered the transfer after Mr. Mubarak appeared Saturday in a Cairo courtroom, where, despite being on a gurney, the former president appeared in good health and high spirits, waving to supporters. A medical board subsequently ruled that Mr. Mubarak was well enough to be sent back to prison. A judge scheduled May 11 as the date for the new trial. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Mubarak to Be Moved to Prison', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Mubarak to Be Moved to Prison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'El Sheikh, Mayy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T01:12:29+0000', 'doc