le/e278169f-ae51-59d8-9551-77cfb51fd205', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e278169f-ae51-59d8-9551-77cfb51fd205'}, {'abstract': 'Ernie Paniccioli cuts an impressive figure, both for his activism and for his documenting of hip-hop’s biggest names going back to when they were teenagers looking to change the world.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/public-enemys-private-photographer/', 'snippet': 'Ernie Paniccioli cuts an impressive figure, both for his activism and for his documenting of hip-hop’s biggest names going back to when they were teenagers looking to change the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ernie Paniccioli leaned in close. “Yo, take a minute,” he insisted. “You’ve got to listen to this from Public Enemy!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Enemy’s Private Photographer', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chuck D (1960- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Enemy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T09:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/840b58fc-c103-507e-9aad-3e1a4b7f2a77', 'word_count': 1047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/840b58fc-c103-507e-9aad-3e1a4b7f2a77'}, {'abstract': 'How a toxic clash of personalities cost NBC’s “Today” its No. 1 ranking. Matt Lauer may yet lead the show back to the top spot, but the morning is tougher now than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/magazine/who-can-save-the-today-show.html', 'snippet': 'How a toxic clash of personalities cost NBC’s “Today” its No. 1 ranking. Matt Lauer may yet lead the show back to the top spot, but the morning is tougher now than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One Wednesday last month, Ann Curry, camouflaged in a hat and trench coat, trudged into the art-deco lobby of 30 Rockefeller Plaza. It had been nine months since she was pushed out as co-host of the “Today” show. Curry was now NBC’s “national and international correspondent” and the anchor at large for “Today,” but these titles seemed honorary. Curry had appeared on “Today” only a handful of times since her ouster. She had no role in NBC’s coverage of election night or Inauguration Day. She taped a few stories for “Rock Center,” the prime-time newsmagazine show, but as she explained on Twitter, her bosses kept rescheduling them. Curry had moved to an office on the 27th floor of 30 Rock, far from her NBC News bosses on the third floor. On this morning, she was at work on a short “NBC Nightly News” segment about the anniversary of Martin Luther King Jr.’s death. It would be only her sixth appearance on the network all year.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21morning1/21morning1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21morning1/21morning1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21morning1/21morning1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21morning1/21morning1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21morning1/21morning1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21morning1/21morning1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21morning1/21morning1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waking Up on the Wrong Side of a Ratings War', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waking Up On The Wrong Side Of A Rating War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Ann', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Today (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauer, Matt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capus, Steve', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burke, Steve', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fili-Krushel, Patricia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, James F', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T09:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6301a40-43e4-5fdb-8eb1-e6c4615ab3c0', 'word_count': 6024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6301a40-43e4-5fdb-8eb1-e6c4615ab3c0'}, {'abstract': 'The 81-year-old spy writer is in the midst of a hardy late-career bloom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/magazine/john-le-carre-has-not-mellowed-with-age.html', 'snippet': 'The 81-year-old spy writer is in the midst of a hardy late-career bloom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Saturday morning in February, two dozen or so scent hounds streamed through the streets of St. Buryan, a small village in Cornwall, England. Behind them drifted a loose formation of men and women perched atop well-groomed horses and wearing boots, breeches and hunting coats. As the fox hunt clopped through town, John le Carré, the pre-eminent spy writer of the 20th century, sipped from a paper cup of warm whiskey punch, doled out by a local pub to riders and spectators.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21lecarre1/mag-21lecarre-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21lecarre1/mag-21lecarre-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 781}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21lecarre1/mag-21lecarre-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 787, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21lecarre1/mag-21lecarre-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 1051, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21lecarre1/mag-21lecarre-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21lecarre1/mag-21lecarre-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/magazine/21lecarre1/mag-21lecarre-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John le Carré Has Not Mellowed With Age', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘I have Pretended To Be A Gentleman For So Long’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Carre, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Delicate Truth (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T09:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6098dba-a543-585f-a28a-08f37f00844a', 'word_count': 4016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6098dba-a543-585f-a28a-08f37f00844a'}, {'a