 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca0db9b9-60e2-5dac-a76f-b520f27cff4a', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca0db9b9-60e2-5dac-a76f-b520f27cff4a'}, {'abstract': 'Security analysts in South Korea and the United States expressed cautious optimism that after weeks of threats, both sides might be ready to calm tensions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/world/asia/north-korea-tension.html', 'snippet': 'Security analysts in South Korea and the United States expressed cautious optimism that after weeks of threats, both sides might be ready to calm tensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — By North Korean standards, the invective issued over the past week has bordered on civil. Instead of near daily threats of nuclear annihilation for the “nest of evil” in the United States and promises to “press the button,” the North in recent days has grumbled over a “crafty ploy” and “cunning trick” by America and its allies to strip the North of its nuclear arsenal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/world/0419KOREA/0419KOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/world/0419KOREA/0419KOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/world/0419KOREA/0419KOREA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/world/0419KOREA/0419KOREA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType'