cle/afea1286-a80a-508b-8a8f-3e9a3d95eeca'}, {'abstract': 'The new Mexican government’s best strategy for dealing with drug crimes is to stop talking about them.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/the-mexican-government-wants-to-curb-crime-but-without-talking-about-it/', 'snippet': 'The new Mexican government’s best strategy for dealing with drug crimes is to stop talking about them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — There will be no more drug executions in Mexico, no more levantones (kidnappings with intent to murder) or encajuelados (dead bodies in car trunks, or cajuelas). There will be no more mob bosses, no more mob soldiers, no more hit men.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Talk the Talk', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T10:56:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlos Puig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Puig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85deb973-c1fb-5534-a8ca-d599ad74ca40', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85deb973-c1fb-5534-a8ca-d599ad74ca40'}, {'abstract': 'To encourage banks to lend, the agency is cutting fees and streamlining programs. But will it be enough?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/the-s-b-a-wants-to-encourage-more-small-loans/', 'snippet': 'To encourage banks to lend, the agency is cutting fees and streamlining programs. But will it be enough?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last several years, the Small Business Administration has attempted to expand its loan-guarantee programs by making them available to bigger businesses. But with the 2014 budget that the White House sent to Congress last week, the Obama administration is trying to solve a problem at the other end of the spectrum: how to induce banks to make smaller loans, to smaller businesses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The S.B.A. Wants to Encourage More Small Loans', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T11:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5734c0c-8c00-5795-b6a9-33d1db2497e5', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5734c0c-8c00-5795-b6a9-33d1db2497e5'}, {'abstract': 'Two top lieutenants to the bank’s former chief executive, Robert E. Diamond Jr.,are stepping down. And in an effort to bolster its American operations, Barclays named Skip McGee, a former Lehman Brothers banker, chief executive of Barclays Americas.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/barclays-investment-chief-rich-ricci-to-step-down/', 'snippet':