64b1e296', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67cde446-fbcd-5bc2-9ba9-919f64b1e296'}, {'abstract': 'Welcome springtime with these Great Gatsby pieces, an ode to Art Deco and flappers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/market-sweep-deco-darling/', 'snippet': 'Welcome springtime with these Great Gatsby pieces, an ode to Art Deco and flappers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Sweep | Deco Darling', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Market Sweep: Deco Darling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T15:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1496e76c-f963-58e9-933a-3c2b3257a70b', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1496e76c-f963-58e9-933a-3c2b3257a70b'}, {'abstract': 'Abijah GIlbert and the bloody, intimate guerrilla fighting in Civil War Kentucky.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/neighbor-vs-neighbor/', 'snippet': 'Abijah GIlbert and the bloody, intimate guerrilla fighting in Civil War Kentucky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Confederate rout at Perryville in October 1862 squelched the South’s large-scale ambitions for the Bluegrass State. Afterward, Kentucky had its own internal proxy civil war, and its citizens had more to fear from one another than from some “foreign” invader. As the Southern war effort started to show early signs of futility in 1863, an untold number of Kentucky Confederates returned home, just as the Federal Army’s recruitment of former slaves disillusioned conservative Unionists. Together, they took out their frustrations on their Loyalist neighbors, some of whom gamely returned fire. In no other state, save perhaps Missouri, did this sort of “intimate” fighting determine the course of the war more than in Kentucky. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neighbor vs. Neighbor', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T15:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By T.R.C. Hutton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'T.', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'C', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4922e9a-43de-5ccb-bb58-0daffc05272b', 'word_count': 1436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4922e9a-43de-5ccb-bb58-0daffc05272b'}, {'abstract': 'A protest in Ahmedabad against a power tariff hike by the Gujarat government.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/image-of-the-day-april-18-2/', 'snippet': 'A protest in Ahmedabad against a power tariff hike by the Gujarat government.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/world/asia/18-POD-IndiaInk/18-POD-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/world/asia/18-POD-IndiaInk/18-