cates’ passion is steeped in irony.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/all-worked-up-about-guns/', 'snippet': 'The NRA’s dismissal of gun control advocates’ passion is steeped in irony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a guy who works with words for a living, I marvel at the gun lobby’s gift for turning logic inside out. The bumper-sticker classic: “Guns don’t kill people, people kill people.” The post-Newtown twist: “The only thing that stops a bad guy with a gun is a good guy with a gun.” And this week we have the latest cynical talking point: Let’s not legislate with our emotions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Worked Up About Guns', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T15:37:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bad36583-3ebe-5e5e-98bb-f6e820892826', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bad36583-3ebe-5e5e-98bb-f6e820892826'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Drummond, a protégé of Harry Partch’s, shared Mr. Partch’s affinity for microtonality and creating outlandish instruments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/arts/music/dean-drummond-composer-and-musician-dies-at-64.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Drummond, a protégé of Harry Partch’s, shared Mr. Partch’s affinity for microtonality and creating outlandish instruments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dean Drummond, an imaginative composer and musician whose ensemble, Newband, performed on a combination of standard and newly invented instruments, died on April 13 at a hospital in Princeton, N.J. He was 64 and lived in Montclair, N.J., where he was the director of the Harry Partch Institute at Montclair State University.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/DRUMMOND-obit/DRUMMOND-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/DRUMMOND-obit/DRUMMOND-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/DRUMMOND-obit/DRUMMOND-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/DRUMMOND-obit/DRUMMOND-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1275, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/DRUMMOND-obit/DRUMMOND-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/DRUMMOND-obit/DRUMMOND-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/DRUMMOND-obit/DRUMMOND-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dean Drummond, Musician and Instrument Maker, Dies at 64', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dean Drummond, 64, Musician and Instrument Maker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drummond, Dean', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kozinn, Allan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montclair (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montclair State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T15:50:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/74699eb1-a9fe-5e5f-bbdc-3d3642088895', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74699eb1-a9fe-5e5f-bbdc-3d3642088895'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art is presenting “Velázquez’s Portrait of Duke Francesco I d’Este” to aid the Modena region in its recovery from last year’s earthquakes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/arts/design/velazquezs-portrait-of-duke-francesco-i-deste-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art is presenting “Velázquez’s Portrait of Duke Francesco I d’Este” to aid the Modena region in its recovery from last year’s earthquakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In delicate diplomatic moments, art is sometimes called on to serve as ambassador. At just such a point in the Thirty Years’ War, the Spanish king, Philip IV, dispatched his court artist — Velázquez — to paint an Italian dignitary.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19VELAZQUEZ/19VELAZQUEZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'a