count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55b57c1c-7ffc-51ad-94b0-e64e485c2d18'}, {'abstract': 'John Derian’s latest collaboration with the French ceramic tableware company Astier de Villatte is user-friendly.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/john-derian-for-astier-de-villatte/', 'snippet': 'John Derian’s latest collaboration with the French ceramic tableware company Astier de Villatte is user-friendly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early next month, the latest products of John Derian’s ongoing collaboration with the French ceramic tableware company Astier de Villatte will be available in the United States. They include a mug and teapot with an image of an eye that was taken from a 19th-century medical book, as well as a plate called Starfish at Night and a serving bowl covered with a coral-like pattern in blue. Unlike the designer’s famous decoupage plates, these pieces are dishwasher-safe (on the gentle setting). “I love the fact that they’re user-friendly,” Derian says.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Derian for Astier de Villatte', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sips of Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Derian, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Astier de Villatte', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T16:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0b84487-58aa-5eb4-9abd-57e7e5e39b82', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b84487-58aa-5