s are collaborating on a new show that will feature jazz interpretations of Mr. Sondheim’s love songs.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/sondheim-and-marsalis-to-collaborate-on-show-for-city-center/', 'snippet': 'Stephen Sondheim and Wynton Marsalis are collaborating on a new show that will feature jazz interpretations of Mr. Sondheim’s love songs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Sondheim and Wynton Marsalis are collaborating on a new show to be staged at the New York City Center next November that will feature jazz interpretations of Mr. Sondheim’s love songs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sondheim and Marsalis to Collaborate on Show for City Center', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sondheim and Marsalis To Collaborate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marsalis, Wynton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sondheim, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Center Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0b00de6-6bd5-5f3c-9c11-619f06f3dc1e', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0b00de6-6bd5-5f3c-9c11-619f06f3dc1e'}, {'abstract': 'A fractured bone in his foot has muddied the immediate future of Mets prospect Travis d’Arnaud', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/injury-sidetracks-mets-darnaud/', 'snippet': 'A fractured bone in his foot has muddied the immediate future of Mets prospect Travis d’Arnaud', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — Minor league catcher Travis d’Arnaud, the Mets’ top position player prospect, will fly to New York on Friday to see team doctors after fracturing a bone in his foot, General Manager Sandy Alderson said Thursday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Injury Sidetracks Mets’ D’Arnaud', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "d'Arnaud, Travis", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ade7d77-8285-59c9-8702-45aa170f6545', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ade7d77-8285-59c9-8702-45aa170f6545'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to a combination of Web-mail and cloud-storage services, sending large files as attachments is easier these days.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/tip-of-the-week-sending-huge-e-mail-attachments/', 'snippet': 'Thanks to a combination of Web-mail and cloud-storage services, sending large files as attachments is easier these days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, high-definition video recordings and high-resolution photographs are easier to make with smartphones and other affordable gear. While great for personal creativity, some people may be seeing more of that old “This file exceeds the attachment limit” message from their e-mail providers when they try to share the files privately with friends. To help users send files larger than the usual 10- to 25-megabyte limit, Google, Yahoo and Microsoft have all melded their Web-based mail with online storage services.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Sending Huge E-Mail Attachments', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dropbox Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:22:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b591f183-8acc-502e-a2a2-139cede3e27d', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b591f183-8acc-502e-a2a2-139cede3e27d'}, {'abstract': 'A conceal-carry amendment received more votes, than the background check expansion. Both measures attracted a simple majority, but failed to reach the 60-vote threshold.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/the-other-gun-vote/', 'snippet': 'A conceal-carry amendment received more votes, than the background check expansion. Both measures attracted a simple majority, but failed to reach the 60-vote threshold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Manchin-Toomey amendment to expand background checks could have passed: It received 54 ayes, and would have received 55 if Senate Majority Leader Harry Reid hadn’t voted no for procedural reasons. But the so-called “world’s greatest deliberative body” agreed to a 60-vote threshold for the gun-safety bill. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Other Gun Vote', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornyn, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:25:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcf0ea21-4748-5d3e-be55-020474e611e8', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcf0ea21-4748-5d3e-be55-020474e611e8'}, {'abstract': 'The following is a transcript of President Obama’s remarks at an interfaith memorial service for the victims of the Boston Marathon bombing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/us/obamas-remarks-at-boston-service.html', 'snippet': 'The following is a transcript of President Obama’s remarks at an interfaith memorial service for the victims of the Boston Marathon bombing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following is a transcript of President Obama’s remarks at an interfaith memorial service for the victims of the Boston Marathon bombing at the Cathedral of the Holy Cross in Boston on Thursday, as provided by the White House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Remarks at Boston Service', 'kicker': 'Text', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/04c9f684-7255-5b73-bf31-7af2188eec32', 'word_count': 1824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04c9f684-7255-5b73-bf31-7af2188eec32'}, {'abstract': 'A majority of Americans believe that high-income people do not pay enough in taxes, but that majority has been shrinking over the last couple of decades, according to new data from Gallup.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/on-whether-the-rich-pay-too-little-in-taxes/', 'snippet': 'A majority of Americans believe that high-income people do not pay enough in taxes, but that majority has been shrinking over the last couple of decades, according to new data from Gallup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday Bruce Bartlett mentioned that a majority of Americans believe that high-income people do not pay enough in taxes. That majority, though, has been shrinking over the last couple of decades, according to new data from Gallup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Whether the Rich Pay Too Little in Taxes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/747a5f25-1fcc-5fd2-9bbc-546b2404179b', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/747a5f25-1fcc-5fd2-9bbc-546b2404179b'}, {'abstract': 'Mourning the victims of the marathon bombings, President Obama spoke at a church service in Boston. He also praised the spirit of the city.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/video-obama-praises-bostons-spirit/', 'snippet': 'Mourning the victims of the marathon bombings, President Obama spoke at a church service in Boston. He also praised the spirit of the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mourning the victims of the marathon bombings, President Obama spoke at a church service titled “Healing Our City” at the Cathedral of the Holy Cross in Boston. He also praised the spirit of the city. Transcript »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Obama Praises Boston’s Spirit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:35:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3c15565-8a02-57b7-b664-d791467eb70b', 'word_count': 37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3c15565-8a02-57b7-b664-d791467eb70b'}, {'abstract': 'The problem is not Maryland corporate law, but that CommonWealth has a bylaw provision that requires that all shareholder disputes be arbitrated.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/whats-at-stake-in-the-fight-over-commonwealth-reit/', 'snippet': 'The problem is not Maryland corporate law, but that CommonWealth has a bylaw provision that requires that all shareholder disputes be arbitrated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to see one possible dystopian future for takeovers, you should take a gander at what is going on in the takeover bid for CommonWealth REIT, a real estate investment trust that owns more than 500 office buildings. It’s not pretty, and it’s all a result of \xa0CommonWealth’s claim that all its disputes with shareholders must be arbitrated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s at Stake in the Fight Over a REIT', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f817a6f3-bfee-5a97-ada4-841438ab5fe4', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f817a6f3-bfee-5a97-ada4-841438ab5fe4'}, {'abstract': 'In a study involving about 10,000 people, the new test detected 92 percent of the cancers picked up by colonoscopy, according to the company that makes the test.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/business/new-test-detects-most-colorectal-cancers-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'In a study involving about 10,000 people, the new test detected 92 percent of the cancers picked up by colonoscopy, according to the company that makes the test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new noninvasive screening test can detect most cases of colorectal cancer and also many precancerous polyps, potentially helping to sharply reduce the death toll from the disease, according to results of a study released on Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-CANCER/19-jp-CANCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-CANCER/19-jp-CANCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-CANCER/19-jp-CANCER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-CANCER/19-jp-CANCER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 1378, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-CANCER/19-jp-CANCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-CANCER/19-jp-CANCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-CANCER/19-jp-CANCER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Noninvasive Cancer Test Is Effective, Study Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Noninvasive Cancer Test Is Effective, Study Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colon and Colorectal Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colonoscopy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EXACT Sciences Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T17:48:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c01471ac-43dc-5551-a5da-d8d16f5812ca', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c01471ac-43dc-5551-a5da-d8d16f5812ca'}, {'abstract': 'Good Samaritans can be virtual, too. After the Boston Marathon attack, Tim Jones, an explosives expert and chief of a social media management company, began tracking Web chatter on explosives, offering the data to the Boston police, whom he has been working with since 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/buzzient-boston-marathon-investigation/', 'snippet': 'Good Samaritans can be virtual, too. After the Boston Marathon attack, Tim Jones, an explosives expert and chief of a social media management company, began tracking Web chatter on explosives, offering the data to the Boston police, whom he has be...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When two bombs exploded at Monday’s Boston Marathon, good Samaritans of all sorts rushed in, from off-duty medical personnel to residents who opened their homes to evacuees. Tim Jones, the chief executive of Buzzient, a Boston-area social media management start-up, felt a similar urge to help, using his company’s ability to search Web history on forums, comments and social media, to focus on specific topics — \xa0like explosives.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia