 no longer together, one of whom used to be a man.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/fashion/21MODERNLOVE/21MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/fashion/21MODERNLOVE/21MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/fashion/21MODERNLOVE/21MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/fashion/21MODERNLOVE/21MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1604, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/fashion/21MODERNLOVE/21MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/21/fashion/21MODERNLOVE/21MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/fashion/21MODERNLOVE/21MODERNLOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Humiliation to Appreciation', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Humiliation to Appreciation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:07:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Chagnot', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chagnot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b4b77f7-6f93-5fe4-a8de-6ba6abf6ac97', 'word_count': 1513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b4b77f7-6f93-5fe4-a8de-6ba6abf6ac97'}, {'abstract': 'A writer reflects on what it’s like not to agree with popular opinion, prompted by his lukewarm response to the much-celebrated “Matilda.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/theater-talkback-in-the-minority/', 'snippet': 'A writer reflects on what it’s like not to agree with popular opinion, prompted by his lukewarm response to the much-celebrated “Matilda.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ll admit, I don’t have it as bad as poor little Matilda. For her assorted deviances from the norm, she is called stupid at home and routinely humiliated at school. I, on the other hand, am merely made to feel uncomfortable, alienated, and perhaps a shade indignant on account of my most recent heresy: I didn’t much like “Matilda the Musical.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: In the Minority', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Weinert-Kendt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinert-Kendt', 'qualifier': None, 'title':