eaks from writing and her new rescue dog, Oscar.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/life-interrupted-a-chat-with-suleika/', 'snippet': 'Suleika Jaouad, “Life, Interrupted” columnist, answers questions about her treatment, why she sometimes takes breaks from writing and her new rescue dog, Oscar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was just about a year ago when Well readers first met Suleika Jaouad, who at 22 was facing a cancer diagnosis and a potentially lifesaving bone marrow transplant. Her first column “Life, Interrupted: Facing Cancer in Your 20s,” captivated readers and transformed Ms. Jaouad from an unknown writer to a national advocate for young people with cancer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/health/19Well_suleika/19Well_suleika-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/health/19Well_suleika/19Well_suleika-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/health/19Well_suleika/19Well_suleika-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 531, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/health/19Well_suleika/19Well_suleika-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 531, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/health/19Well_suleika/19Well_suleika-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/health/19Well_suleika/19Well_suleika-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/health/19Well_suleika/19Well_suleika-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life, Interrupted: A Chat With Suleika', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leukemia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae5a62db-f362-52d9-87b6-a4d90750e81a', 'word_count': 1636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae5a62db-f362-52d9-87b6-a4d90750e81a'}, {'abstract': 'In this age of stage-managed interviews, there are still some celebrity profiles out there worth reading.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/the-long-celebrity-profile-endangered-yes-but-not-yet-dead/', 'snippet': 'In this age of stage-managed interviews, there are still some celebrity profiles out there worth reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently on the Arts Beat blog, Dwight Garner recommended three collections of classic celebrity profiles —\xa0all of which, he notes, were “written before the celebrity-industrial complex was fully formed, when a journalist could still push past an artist’s P.R. phalanx and come back with a story that possessed real feeling and offbeat detail.” (The books in question are Rex Reed’s “People Are Crazy Here,” published 1974; Kenneth Tynan’s “The Sound of Two Hands Clapping,” published 1975; and Michael Lydon’s “Rock Folk: Portraits from the Rock ‘n’ Roll Pantheon,” published 1971.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long Celebrity Profile: Endangered, Yes, but Not Yet Dead', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45703f09-b5f7-541c-a36a-2d5d8d8bd1a3', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45703f09-b5f7-541c-a36a-2d5d8d8bd1a3'}, {'abstract': 'The aid organizations said the new permit requirements were an effort by the Hamas-led government to collect information that is none of its business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/world/middleeast/foreign-agencies-in-gaza-protest-new-exit-permit-rules.html', 'snippet': 'The aid organizations said the new permit requirements were an effort by the Hamas-led government to collect information that is none of its business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA CITY — About two dozen international aid agencies that operate in Gaza have suspended travel by their local employees to Israel and the West Bank to protest new exit permit requirements imposed by the Hamas-led government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aid Agencies in Gaza Protest New Exit Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aid Agencies In Gaza Protest New Exit Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:22:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a56dfc80-2a5a-5c96-9c5c-540e252a133a', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a56dfc80-2a5a-5c96-9c5c-540e252a133a'}, {'abstract': 'Golden State’s Stephen Curry set the N.B.A. record for 3-pointers, a shot that has risen in prominence over the past 10 seasons.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/stephen-curry-and-the-rise-of-the-3-pointer/', 'snippet': 'Golden State’s Stephen Curry set the N.B.A. record for 3-pointers, a shot that has risen in prominence over the past 10 seasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the final game of the Golden State Warriors’ regular season, Stephen Curry broke the N.B.A. single-season mark for 3-pointers. His record-setting 270th came with 6:49 left in the second quarter, surpassing Ray Allen’s total from the 2005-6 season, but doing so with 61 fewer attempts.(Curry added two more 3’s later.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephen Curry and the Rise of the 3-Pointer', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden State Warriors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:39:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve McPherson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McPherson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c87aa5c-8d0c-59a4-af9c-131337e07ada', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c87aa5c-8d0c-59a4-af9c-131337e07ada'}, {'abstract': 'Every Firehouse Subs restaurant features a custom, hand-painted mural that pays tribute to local firefighters.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/the-small-picture-a-sense-of-community/', 'snippet': 'Every Firehouse Subs restaurant features a custom, hand-painted mural that pays tribute to local firefighters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We recently asked small-business owners to send us photographs that capture the soul of their businesses in a single shot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Small Picture: A Sense of Community', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jacksonville (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49e50bd3-3d23-5785-ab74-9e3912481a33', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49e50bd3-3d23-5785-ab74-9e3912481a33'}, {'abstract': 'To the faithful, gold is different from any other commodity. But its precipitous rise since the financial crisis, and its recent sharp fall, sure make it look like one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/business/gold-currency-to-some-is-acting-like-a-speculative-commodity.html', 'snippet': 'To the faithful, gold is different from any other commodity. But its precipitous rise since the financial crisis, and its recent sharp fall, sure make it look like one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do you get when you combine evangelical fervor with leverage and rising speculation?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Man’s Currency Is Another Man’s Bet', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Man’s Currency Is Another Man’s Bet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Standard (Monetary)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e381ef3f-8e0d-536b-bc94-e78a10eeb738', 'word_count': 1313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e381ef3f-8e0d-536b-bc94-e78a10eeb738'}, {'abstract': 'Saying hi to ‘friends’; being grilled by the in-laws about money; the etiquette behind watching a wedding online; and what to do with all of those framed photos from relatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/fashion/hello-dear-friend.html', 'snippet': 'Saying hi to ‘friends’; being grilled by the in-laws about money; the etiquette behind watching a wedding online; and what to do with all of those framed photos from relatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While walking through my neighborhood, I frequently pass familiar faces from high school and college. Often, these old friends have become more distant Facebook friends. Am I obliged to say hello to these people, whose honeymoons and pets are well known to me, even if we haven’t communicated face to face in years? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hello, Dear ‘Friend’?', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hello, Dear ‘Friend’?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T18:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/693bbe77-0887-5e78-92c8-874819cf3a5a', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/693bbe77-0887-5e78-92c8-874819cf3a5a'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Spade debuts a new line of sleepwear, Sleepy Jones, inspired by creative types and meant to be worn whether you’re in the bedroom or not.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/sleepy-jones-ready-for-copy/', 'snippet': 'Andy Spade debuts a new line of sleepwear, Sleepy Jones, inspired by creative types and meant to be worn whether you’re in the bedroom or not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A nod to the creative types of yore who weren’t afraid to pair intimate apparel with formal dress — the David Hockneys and Pablo Picassos of the world — the new “not-quite-ready-to-wear” label Sleepy Jones launches this week. Designed by Andy Spade, the fashion-world veteran who helped start Kate Spade (his wife’s namesake line) before opening the New York storefront and branding agency Partners & Spade, the colorful collection of men’s and women’s crisp pajama separates and jaunty underwear is meant to encourage luxuriating in the kinds of things that comfortable nightclothes inspire one to do. “Essentially, we’re designing an everyday uniform for reading, writing, painting, pondering and playing — whether you’re in the bedroom or not,” Spade says. With practical and stylish boxers features like a coin pocket for the men and Liberty of London fabric for the women, you may soon find yourself answering the door in your underwear.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sleepy Jones', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Job? What Job?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pajamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spade, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spade, Kate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T19:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e049047-b8ff-50a7-8f46-88646cd16cdb', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e049047-b8ff-50a7-8f46-88646cd16cdb'}, {'abstract': 'Pep Carrió’s new book, “Days,” documents four years of his daily visual meditations.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/seizing-the-day/', 'snippet': 'Pep Carrió’s new book, “Days,” documents four years of his daily visual meditations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seizing the Day', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T19:14:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azadeh Ensha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azadeh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ensha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/725d307a-aaa9-5f37-bada-b2e346ea19a5', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725d307a-aaa9-5f37-bada-b2e346ea19a5'}, {'abstract': 'In “Waiting to Be Heard,” Amanda Knox acknowledges her own mistakes and says she was the victim of mistreatment by Italian authorities while imprisoned over the murder of her roommate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/books/in-memoir-amanda-knox-testifies-in-public-court-of-approval.html', 'snippet': 'In “Waiting to Be Heard,” Amanda Knox acknowledges her own mistakes and says she was the victim of mistreatment by Italian authorities while imprisoned over the murder of her roommate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While imprisoned in Italy for four years over the murder of her roommate, Amanda Knox fended off sexual harassment from guards and an overture from a cellmate. On the night of the killing, she was smoking marijuana and watching a movie with her Italian boyfriend. And those infamous cartwheels that Ms. Knox reportedly performed in the police station never happened.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/world/0419KNOX/0419KNOX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legac