blican office holders played a central role in the thirty-year process that forced the country to finally focus on repairing its generally mediocre public school system.\xa0Education minded governors like Lamar Alexander of Tennessee were early to the cause. And as President, George W. Bush pushed through the No Child Left Behind Act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Versus the Business Community', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No Child Left Behind Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T19:25:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a826806d-3048-5c70-977d-2a80db90d834', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a826806d-3048-5c70-977d-2a80db90d834'}, {'abstract': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau has recommended ways to sort out the various credentials used by financial advisers who claim to have expertise in helping older people.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/telling-the-difference-among-50-senior-financial-credentials/', 'snippet': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau has recommended ways to sort out the various credentials used by financial advisers who claim to have expertise in helping older people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say you’re a 70-year-old retiree, and you’d like some help managing your finances. Should you hire an adviser who is an A.R.A., an A.R.P.C., a C.S.A. or a C.R.F.A.?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telling the Difference Among 50 ‘Senior’ Financial Credentials', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alphabet Soup Of Advisers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T19:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d6a3498-b297-558e-a64d-05a03ee0d0d7', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d6a3498-b297-558e-a64d-05a03ee0d0d7'}, {'abstract': '“The Dispensable Nation,” by Vali Nasr, a former senior adviser to Richard C. Holbrooke, asserts that the foreign policy pursued under President Obama has diminished America’s leadership role in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/books/the-dispensable-nation-by-vali-nasr.html', 'snippet': '“The Dispensable Nation,” by Vali Nasr, a former senior adviser to Richard C. Holbrooke, asserts that the foreign policy pursued under President Obama has diminished America’s leadership role in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of Vali Nasr’s provocative and uneven new book, “The Dispensable Nation: American Foreign Policy in Retreat,” plays on President Bill Clinton’s description of the United States as the world’s one “indispensable nation.” Mr. Nasr — who was a senior adviser to Richard C. Holbrooke, the Obama administration’s special representative for Afghanistan and Pakistan (AfPak) — suggests in this sharply critical volume that the foreign policy pursued under Mr. Obama has diminished America’s leadership role in the world. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19JPBOOKNASR/JPBOOKNASR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19JPBOOKNASR/JPBOOKNASR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 908}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19JPBOOKNASR/JPBOOKNASR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19JPBOOKNASR/JPBOOKNASR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1647, 'width': 1088, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19JPBOOKNASR/19JPBOOKNASR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19JPBOOKNASR/19JPBOOKNASR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19JPBOOKNASR/19JPBOOKNASR-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Superpower, Leading From Behind', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Superpower, Leading From Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nasr, Vali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T19:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fccbff57-6b04-5894-b806-4ea9b1782d5c', 'word_count': 1380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fccbff57-6b04-5894-b806-4ea9b1782d5c'}, {'abstract': 'Malai Marke could be just another restaurant on Curry Row in the East Village. Until the food arrives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/dining/reviews/hungry-city-malai-marke-in-the-east-village.html', 'snippet': 'Malai Marke could be just another restaurant on Curry Row in the East Village. Until the food arrives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first dish to be depleted at my table was always the okra. Each time, the crenelated pods arrived still firm and green after a flare in the pan with a few workhorses from the Indian larder (garlic, ginger, onions, coriander), the flavor not disguised by spices but amplified, crisp and grassy, without a suspicion of stickiness. I could not stop ordering it.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24HUNGRY_SPAN/24HUNGRY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articl