merica since the Newtown shooting, even though legislation died in the Senate this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000002179733/guns-did-newtown-change-anything.html', 'snippet': 'The Times’s Michael Luo discusses whether attitudes toward guns have changed in America since the Newtown shooting, even though legislation died in the Senate this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times’s Michael Luo discusses whether attitudes toward guns have changed in America since the Newtown shooting, even though legislation died in the Senate this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/us/video-gun-culture-post-newtown/video-gun-culture-post-newtown-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/18/us/video-gun-culture-post-newtown/video-gun-culture-post-newtown-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/us/video-gun-culture-post-newtown/video-gun-culture-post-newtown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/18/us/video-gun-culture-post-newtown/video-gun-culture-post-newtown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/18/us/video-gun-culture-post-newtown/video-gun-culture-post-newtown-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guns: Did Newtown Change Anything?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T21:14:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul, Pedro Rafael Rosado, Erica Berenstein and Alyssa Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': 'Rafael', 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Alyssa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/139494de-7a04-5cde-9385-c1e7ba69efe9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/139494de-7a04-5cde-9385-c1e7ba69efe9'}, {'abstract': 'Robin Roberts, whose return to “Good Morning America” after a rare blood disorder and bone marrow transplant has been widely covered this year, had something of a setback this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/arts/television/robin-roberts-update.html', 'snippet': 'Robin Roberts, whose return to “Good Morning America” after a rare blood disorder and bone marrow transplant has been widely covered this year, had something of a setback this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robin Roberts, right, whose return to “Good Morning America” after a rare blood disorder and bone marrow transplant has been widely covered this year, had something of a setback this month, she said on Thursday in a Facebook post to her fans. “Last week, in the middle of my Key West vacation, I began not to feel well,” she wrote. “Nothing serious, just under the weather.” Her trip was cut short and her doctors admitted her to a hospital in New York for several days to fight off an infection. She emphasized on Facebook that “it’s extremely common, post bone marrow transplant, to have complications,” and said hers had not been severe. Nevertheless the news was worrisome to some viewers. Since returning to the show in February after a five-month medical leave, Ms. Roberts has been a host on the show for three days most weeks. But she hasn’t been on since April 5, owing to her vacation and then her hospitalization. When she is resting, two others at ABC News, Amy Robach and Elizabeth Vargas, take turns filling in for her. In her Facebook post Ms. Roberts said she was “feeling much better” and would be back on the show next week.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robin Roberts Update', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robin Roberts Update', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Robin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bone Marrow', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Good Morning America (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T21:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/22d58173-8f26-5c5e-9e9e-9e46050d52b1', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22d58173-8f26-5c5e-9e9e-9e46050d52b1'}, {'abstract': 'The center-left’s official candidate, Franco Marini, a former union leader and president of the Senate, was unable to get the two-thirds majority required.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/world/europe/italian-lawmakers-fail-to-elect-a-president.html', 'snippet': 'The center-left’s official candidate, Franco Marini, a former union leader and president of the Senate, was unable to get the two-thirds majority required.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Italian lawmakers failed to elect a new president in the first two rounds of voting on Thursday. The center-left’s official candidate, Franco Marini, a former union leader and president of the Senate, was unable to get the two-thirds majority required, even with the votes of the center-right, which supported the choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Lawmakers Fail to Elect a President', 'kicker': 'World Briefing ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napolitano, Giorgio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-18T21:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/feb828b2-2124-5840-84ab-13c71e9a7007', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feb828b2-2124-5840-84ab-13c71e9a7007'}, {'abstract': '“Onement VI,” a 1953 painting by Barnett Newman, is expected to sell for $30 million to $40 million at Sotheby’s next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/arts/design/barnett-newmans-onement-vi-at-sothebys.html', 'snippet': '“Onement VI,” a 1953 painting by Barnett Newman, is expected to sell for $30 million to $40 million at Sotheby’s next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barnett Newman had very specific opinions about how viewers should look at his abstract paintings. For a show in 1951 at the Betty Parsons Gallery in New York, he tacked a notice to the wall that read: “There is a tendency to look at large pictures from a distance. The large pictures in this exhibition are intended to be seen from a short distance.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19VOGEL/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19VOGEL/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 568}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19VOGEL/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 970, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19VOGEL/VOGEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1940, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':