': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e8d8704-2b69-5813-add1-91257c09c727', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e8d8704-2b69-5813-add1-91257c09c727'}, {'abstract': '“Herman’s House” chronicles the friendship of Jackie Sumell, a New York artist, and Herman Wallace, a convicted murderer who has spent most of the last four decades in solitary confinement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/movies/hermans-house-directed-by-angad-bhalla.html', 'snippet': '“Herman’s House” chronicles the friendship of Jackie Sumell, a New York artist, and Herman Wallace, a convicted murderer who has spent most of the last four decades in solitary confinement.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Herman’s House” chronicles the unlikely friendship of Jackie Sumell, a high-strung, politically engaged New York artist, and Herman Wallace, a convicted murderer in his early 70s who has spent most of the last four decades in solitary confinement at the Louisiana State Penitentiary, known as Angola. Although this documentary has a powerful political subtext, it is best described as a conceptual art piece about confinement, attached to a dual biography of the artist and the prisoner. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19HERMAN1_SPAN/SUBHERMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19HERMAN1_SPAN/SUBHERMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/arts/19HERMAN1_SPAN/SUBHERMAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima