ntonio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T00:25:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/566970c4-b5a0-5579-96bb-2ebc0d467e1f', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/566970c4-b5a0-5579-96bb-2ebc0d467e1f'}, {'abstract': 'In critical remarks, a spokesman for the Afghan president said that an airstrike in which 12 children were killed was part of a C.I.A.-run operation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/world/asia/after-airstrike-afghan-points-to-cia-and-secret-militias.html', 'snippet': 'In critical remarks, a spokesman for the Afghan president said that an airstrike in which 12 children were killed was part of a C.I.A.-run operation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The spokesman for President Hamid Karzai said Thursday that the C.I.A. was responsible for calling in an airstrike on April 7 that left 17 Afghan civilians dead, 12 of them children, and that the secret Afghan militias that the agency controls behaved as if they were “responsible to no one.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/world/0419AFGHANISTAN01/0419AFGHANISTAN01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {