s_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0b21f49-beae-5f06-839d-dabfa84dc989', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0b21f49-beae-5f06-839d-dabfa84dc989'}, {'abstract': 'The forthcoming execution of Robert Pruett, convicted in the 1999 killing of a corrections officer, has put focus back on the pay and staffing issues that unions say undermine guards’ safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/us/execution-revives-debate-over-texas-prison-staffing.html', 'snippet': 'The forthcoming execution of Robert Pruett, convicted in the 1999 killing of a corrections officer, has put focus back on the pay and staffing issues that unions say undermine guards’ safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In December 1999, Daniel Nagle, a corrections officer, stood on the Texas Capitol steps, leading a rally to ask lawmakers for a pay raise for his fellow prison employees. His union had been at odds with the prison administration for months over whether a staffing shortage was compromising safety. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/us/19ttPrison/19ttPrison-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/us/19ttPrison/19ttPrison-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/us/19ttPrison/19ttPrison-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty