al surge, but you cannot make muscles do what you want them to do in a bonk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finish Line', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T00:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f4d2894-41c5-53c1-aa76-75522180ff16', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f4d2894-41c5-53c1-aa76-75522180ff16'}, {'abstract': 'Christine C. Quinn, the Council speaker and a Democratic candidate for mayor, has firm control of a staff of 16, many of them her supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/nyregion/city-outreach-unit-run-by-quinn-also-helps-her-with-publicity.html', 'snippet': 'Christine C. Quinn, the Council speaker and a Democratic candidate for mayor, has firm control of a staff of 16, many of them her supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Its friendly name and sizable budget suggest an altruistic resource for all five boroughs: the Community Outreach Unit of the New York City Council, a taxpayer-financed office that has organized rallies to protect student subway discounts and sponsored adult education fairs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/quinn/quinn-articleLa