s.com/2013/04/19/world/europe/russia-dagestan-will-let-putin-choose-its-next-governor.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers in Russia’s Dagestan region voted Thursday to cancel popular elections for governor and allow President Vladimir V. Putin to choose its next leader.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Lawmakers in Russia’s Dagestan region voted Thursday to cancel popular elections for governor and allow President Vladimir V. Putin to choose its next leader. A new law signed by Mr. Putin this month allows Russian republics to scrap the elections, which were restored last year under Mr. Putin’s predecessor, Dmitri A. Medvedev. Dagestan is the first Russian republic to opt out of the elections. Mr. Putin has said the law was needed to protect the rights of minorities in regions like the volatile North Caucasus republics where elections could provoke ethnic strife. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Dagestan Will Let Putin Choose Its Next Governor', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Dagestan Will Let Putin Choose Its Next Governor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dagestan (Russia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T01:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2fe186f-c34f-58ef-a818-d1c6d3a80e6b', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2fe186f-c34f-58ef-a818-d1c6d3a80e6b'}, {'abstract': 'Shares of Apple were trading for more than $700 last year, but they have tumbled back and analysts are trying to understand why.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/technology/after-apples-rise-a-bruising-fall.html', 'snippet': 'Shares of Apple were trading for more than $700 last year, but they have tumbled back and analysts are trying to understand why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where’s the old love, Apple? ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-APPLE/19-jp-APPLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-APPLE/19-jp-APPLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-APPLE/19-jp-APPLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-APPLE/19-jp-APPLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-APPLE/19-jp-APPLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-APPLE/19-jp-APPLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/business/19-jp-APPLE/19-jp-APPLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge'