major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tribeca Film Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Shola', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T01:39:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e91e4aaf-be28-5159-baf3-ac896f113ff5', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e91e4aaf-be28-5159-baf3-ac896f113ff5'}, {'abstract': 'Russian authorities on Thursday accused the political opposition leader Aleksei A. Navalny and his brother, Oleg, of defrauding business associates of at least $125,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/world/europe/russia-opposition-activist-faces-more-legal-trouble.html', 'snippet': 'Russian authorities on Thursday accused the political opposition leader Aleksei A. Navalny and his brother, Oleg, of defrauding business associates of at least $125,000.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Russian authorities on Thursday announced yet another criminal case against the political opposition leader Aleksei A. Navalny, accusing him and his brother, Oleg, of defrauding business associates of at least $125,000 in a complex scheme. Mr. Navalny, a fierce critic of President Vladimir V. Putin who rose to prominence as an anticorruption blogger, is already facing four other criminal cases. One case, involving an embezzlement charge, began in Kirov, northeast of Moscow, on Wednesday. The judge in that case granted a one-week postponement to give Mr. Navalny’s lawyers more time to prepare. Mr. Navalny learned of the new charges as he arrived back in Moscow on an overnight train from Kirov. In response, he mocked investigators. “I woke up on the train and learned they filed another criminal case,” he wrote on Twitter. “This means we had a successful trip. Good morning.” Moments later, he added, “The Navalny Brothers are becoming a lasting phrase, like Mario Brothers.” Mr. Navalny has called the charges in all the cases politically motivated. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Opposition Activist Faces More Legal Trouble', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Opposition Activist Faces More Legal Trouble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T01:40:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ade9a16-46fa-5f00-bfed-661caedc7eee', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ade9a16-46fa-5f00-bfed-661caedc7eee'}, {'abstract': 'A Guatemalan judge ruled Thursday that all the testimony in the genocide trial of the former dictator Efraín Ríos Montt, 86, was invalid and would have to be repeated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/world/americas/guatemala-judge-says-testimony-in-genocide-trial-must-be-repeated.html', 'snippet': 'A Guatemalan judge ruled Thursday that all the testimony in the genocide trial of the former dictator Efraín Ríos Montt, 86, was invalid and would have to be repeated.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Guatemalan judge ruled Thursday that all the testimony in the genocide trial of the former dictator Efraín Ríos Montt, 86, was invalid and would have to be repeated. The decision, based on a technicality, was a victory for Mr. Ríos Montt’s lawyers, who had filed a barrage of injunctions seeking to stop or postpone the trial. Over the past month, the court has heard testimony from dozens of people who survived army-led rampages through villages in the Mayan highlands three decades ago during the country’s long civil war. Mr. Ríos Montt’s lawyers argue that their client did not know about the atrocities being committed by his troops. Prosecution witnesses this week described a rigid military chain of command leading directly to Mr. Ríos Montt. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guatemala: Judge Says Testimony in Genocide Trial Must Be Repeated', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guatemala: Judge Says Testimony in Genocide Trial Must Be Repeated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rios Montt, Efrain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T01:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/880e478e-3f9b-5b8a-8058-0bffb6850b44', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/880e478e-3f9b-5b8a-8058-0bffb6850b44'}, {'abstract': 'TGIF, with Ned White.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/18/givernys-most-famous-resident/', 'snippet': 'TGIF, with Ned White.', 'lead_paragraph': '“And, has thou slain the Jabberwock? Come to my arms, my beamish boy!O frabjous day! Callooh! Callay!’ He chortled in his joy.” — Lewis Carroll’s “Jabberwocky”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giverny’s Most Famous Resident', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T02:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/412a31c3-ea23-5499-b93e-5fb1e1fe99e7', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/412a31c3-ea23-5499-b93e-5fb1e1fe99e7'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on April 19, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/pageoneplus/corrections-april-19-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on April 19, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: