'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/68c29a7f-8d2d-5801-9925-d851b6507973', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/68c29a7f-8d2d-5801-9925-d851b6507973'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13) CELEBRATION: STEPHANIE BLYTHE MEETS KATE SMITH Ms. Blythe, above, the mezzo-soprano heard at the Metropolitan Opera this season in Verdi’s “Ballo in Maschera” and Wagner’s “Ring” cycle, pays tribute to the singer Kate Smith, who helped galvanize the nation during World War II, in this “Live From Lincoln Center” presentation. The concert, taped in February at the Allen Room as part of the American Songbook series, features “When the Moon Comes Over the Mountain,” “We’ll Meet Again,” “God Bless America” and “Look for the Silver Lining.” In “BAM150,” at 10, Michael Sladek chronicles the history of the Brooklyn Academy of Music, founded in 1861, with performance footage of Robert Wilson’s production of “The Threepenny Opera,” Les Arts Florissants’ “Atys” and William Forsythe’s “I Don’t Believe in Outer Space,” and interviews with the actors Alan Rickman and Maggie Gyllenhaal, the performance artist Laurie Anderson, the choreographer Mark Morris and the director Peter Brook.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8deac298-ce77-5dc5-bd3c-9e571da5f92d', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8deac298-ce77-5dc5-bd3c-9e571da5f92d'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/news-quiz-april-19-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | April 19, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T05:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2a95719-e8c7-53ab-9351-32d41309f50d', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2a95719-e8c7-53ab-9351-32d41309f50d'}, {'abstract': 'The teenage suspect in the Boston Marathon bombings, Dzhokhar A. Tsarnaev, was taken into custody in Watertown, Mass., after a search that left his brother dead and the Boston area virtually shut down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/us/boston-marathon-bombings.html', 'snippet': 'The teenage suspect in the Boston Marathon bombings, Dzhokhar A. Tsarnaev, was taken into custody in Watertown, Mass., after a search that left his brother dead and the Boston area virtually shut down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The teenage suspect in the Boston Marathon bombings, whose flight from the police after a furious gunfight overnight prompted an intense manhunt that virtually shut down the Boston area all day, was taken into custody Friday night after the police found him in nearby Watertown, Mass., officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2nd Bombing Suspect Caught After Frenzied Hunt Paralyzes Boston', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2nd Bombing Suspect Is Captured, Wounded, After A Frenzied Manhunt Paralyzes Boston', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Tamerlan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Watertown (Mass)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T05:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye, William K. Rashbaum and Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32e89baa-b617-53e3-a9b0-dd86ee110f68', 'word_count': 2065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32e89baa-b617-53e3-a9b0-dd86ee110f68'}, {'abstract': 'The F.B.I. releases pictures of two suspects in the Boston bombings; a new Jewish museum in Warsaw; Germany approves the Cyprus bailout; Anna Netrebko in “Eugene Onegin” ; and the impact of hits in rugby.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/iht-quick-read-april-19/', 'snippet': 'The F.B.I. releases pictures of two suspects in the Boston bombings; a new Jewish museum in Warsaw; Germany approves the Cyprus bailout; Anna Netrebko in “Eugene Onegin” ; and the impact of hits in rugby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS In a direct appeal for help from the public, the F.B.I. on Thursday released pictures and video of two young men who officials believe may be responsible for the explosions that killed three people and wounded more than 170 during the Boston Marathon. Katharine Q. Seelye reports from Boston, Michael S. Schmidt from Washington, and Michael Cooper from New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/sports/rugby/19iht-rugbby19-span/19iht-rugbby19-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/sports/rugby/19iht-rugbby19-span/19iht-rugbby19-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/sports/rugby/19iht-rugbby19-span/19iht-rugbby19-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/sports/rugby/19iht-rugbby19-span/19iht-rugbby19-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image