 have proven themselves to be formidable competitors on the international stage.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/evolucin-changes-in-latin-american-photojournalism/', 'snippet': 'During the recent awards season, Latin American photographers have proven themselves to be formidable competitors on the international stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the photographers Pablo Corral Vega and Loup Langton held the first Pictures of the Year Latin America contest in 2011, they had no idea how many submissions they would receive. About 17,000 images arrived, shot by 600 photographers from Mexico to Argentina, and they declared it a success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Challenging an Old Narrative in Latin American Photojournalism', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T09:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbe233ea-032f-502a-9429-75b69c661bd9', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbe233ea-032f-502a-9429-75b69c661bd9'}, {'abstract': 'The recent Sotheby’s auction of Amrita Jhaveri’s art collection signals resurgence of the Indian art market, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/sothebys-auction-boosts-indian-art-sales/', 'snippet': 'The recent Sotheby’s auction of Amrita Jhaveri’s art collection signals resurgence of the Indian art market, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI —The Indian art market appears to be on the rebound after Sotheby’s first international evening sale of Indian art in New York last month fetched nearly $7 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/world/asia/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/17/world/asia/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/world/asia/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/world/asia/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 945, 'width': 1395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/world/asia/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/world/asia/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/world/asia/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk/17-indian-painting-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge',