xpression you hear tossed around a lot. It tells me quickly that the people using it are not really all that innovative and in most cases do not know what it takes to build a fast-growth company. When the fast growth starts to fade, as it always does, the problem is rarely innovation. More often, it’s an inability to do the things that have to follow innovation. It’s really about getting stuff done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why ‘Innovate or Die’ Is a Lie', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sky Zone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T11:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cliff Oxford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cliff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oxford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72e0910b-93a9-5068-8371-e518f9a06362', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72e0910b-93a9-5068-8371-e518f9a06362'}, {'abstract': 'When Microsoft retires technical support for Windows XP next year, the system will no longer get security patches and other updates.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/qa-extending-and-ending-support-for-windows-xp/', 'snippet': 'When Microsoft retires technical support for Windows XP next year, the system will no longer get security patches and other updates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Extending (And Ending) Support for Windows XP', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'su