ne-in-boston-region.html', 'snippet': 'The hub of the universe, as Boston’s popular nickname would have it, was on lockdown from first light until near dark on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The scene was extraordinary. The hub of the universe, as Boston’s popular nickname would have it, was on lockdown from first light until near dark on Friday. A vast dragnet for one man had brought a major American city to a standstill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eerie Stillness at the Center of a Frenzied Crime Scene', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shops Locked, Streets Barren, City Falls Into Eerie Stillness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/264ac727-ae85-58cb-8460-c3526b8d9658', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/264ac727-ae85-58cb-8460-c3526b8d9658'}, {'abstract': 'General Electric delivered a solid gain in first-quarter earnings despite lower demand for industrial equipment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/business/ge-posts-16-rise-in-quarterly-profit.html', 'snippet': 'General Electric delivered a solid gain in first-quarter earnings despite lower demand for industrial equipment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Electric delivered a solid gain in first-quarter earnings on Friday despite economic weakness, especially in Europe, which is holding back demand for industrial equipment.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.E. Reports a 16% Rise in Quarterly Profit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.E. Reports a 16% Rise in Quarterly Profit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohr, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53ccc3e7-79ea-5d25-af64-71adf163dbe8', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53ccc3e7-79ea-5d25-af64-71adf163dbe8'}, {'abstract': 'Mohamed Morsi is burying a report by the very fact-finding committee he created to investigate abuses against protesters during Egypt’s revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/morsi-had-vowed-to-fight-impunity-in-egypt-but-is-now-perpetuating-it/', 'snippet': 'Mohamed Morsi is burying a report by the very fact-finding committee he created to investigate abuses against protesters during Egypt’s revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — For over two years we have been living surrounded by the faces of the shuhada, or martyrs: the many hundreds of protesters and bystanders who disappeared or died in the 2011 revolution and other violent clashes that followed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State of Denial', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missing Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ursula Lindsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ursula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df94d1de-e9c3-5b26-881d-dc2d75b57873', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df94d1de-e9c3-5b26-881d-dc2d75b57873'}, {'abstract': 'MTV renews its weekly late-night show ‘Nikki and Sara Live,” and the stars are told during a taping of Katie Couric’s show.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/comics-get-a-second-mtv-season-and-they-hear-the-news-from-katie-couric/', 'snippet': 'MTV renews its weekly late-night show ‘Nikki and Sara Live,” and the stars are told during a taping of Katie Couric’s show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Changes in network late-night talk shows may be drawing the big headlines, but much activity in that field has been taking place on cable. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comics Get a Second MTV Season, and They Hear the News From Katie Couric', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glaser, Nikki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schaefer, Sara', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:18:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb9c6af0-ef05-5f8f-b863-b36eaa8b6009', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb9c6af0-ef05-5f8f-b863-b36eaa8b6009'}, {'abstract': 'I thought it would be great if my children enjoyed watching the films I liked. I was right, until I pushed my luck.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/yippee-ki-yay-movie-night/', 'snippet': 'I thought it would be great if my children enjoyed watching the films I liked. I was right, until I pushed my luck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It started late last summer. It was 8 o’clock at night and we — my husband; 8-year-old son, Zane; 4-year-old son, Otto; and I — were sacked out on the couch, a thick blanket of potato-chip shards covering our lazy mass. It was time to put the kids to bed, and I could see that my husband was dreading the thought, the forever-grueling affair of reading and reading and reading some more, then, when he’s on the verge of sleep himself, having to answer questions like, “Daddy, why do we have skin?” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yippee-Ki-Yay, Movie Night', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hope Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/580734bd-9d28-5199-85d9-f6e979d12651', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/580734bd-9d28-5199-85d9-f6e979d12651'}, {'abstract': 'The Gregory Brothers’ latest musical mash-up features Gov. Chris Christie, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, former Congressman Ron Paul and special guests who argue for the reform of U.S. drug laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000002180127/the-war-on-drugs-is-a-failure.html', 'snippet': 'The Gregory Brothers’ latest musical mash-up features Gov. Chris Christie, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, former Congressman Ron Paul and special guests who argue for the reform of U.S. drug laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Gregory Brothers’ latest musical mash-up features Gov. Chris Christie, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, former Congressman Ron Paul and special guests who argue for the reform of U.S. drug laws.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/opinion/drugwar-opdoc-image/drugwar-opdoc-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/opinion/drugwar-opdoc-image/drugwar-opdoc-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/opinion/drugwar-opdoc-image/drugwar-opdoc-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/opinion/drugwar-opdoc-image/drugwar-opdoc-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 1436, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/opinion/drugwar-opdoc-image/drugwar-opdoc-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/opinion/drugwar-opdoc-image/drugwar-opdoc-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/opinion/drugwar-opdoc-image/drugwar-opdoc-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The War on Drugs Is a Failure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:32:31+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'The Gregory Brothers', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Gregory Brothers'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/08ad411c-6aed-5c24-aedf-a72cd75b580d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/08ad411c-6aed-5c24-aedf-a72cd75b580d'}, {'abstract': 'The Gregory Brothers’ musical mash-up features Gov. Chris Christie, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and former Congressman Ron Paul, who argue for the reform of United States drug laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/opinion/gregory-brothers-the-war-on-drugs-is-a-failure.html', 'snippet': 'The Gregory Brothers’ musical mash-up features Gov. Chris Christie, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and former Congressman Ron Paul, who argue for the reform of United States drug laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could it truly be a coincidence that April 20 lands only five short days after Tax Day? Surely the Internal Revenue Service orchestrated this calendar synchronicity, understanding that after another harrowing round of W-2s, 1099s and 1040s, many Americans relish the hard-earned opportunity to illegally relax, while conveniently relieving their glaucoma in the process. \xa0Legally, in some states. \xa0If they have glaucoma. \xa0Or a doctor who will say they have glaucoma. Or backaches sometimes. (For the uninitiated, “420” is a code for pot smoking and April 20 a sort of countercultural holiday.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/multimedia/video-opdoc-drugwar/video-opdoc-drugwar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/multimedia/video-opdoc-drugwar/video-opdoc-drugwar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/multimedia/video-opdoc-drugwar/video-opdoc-drugwar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/multimedia/video-opdoc-drugwar/video-opdoc-drugwar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/multimedia/video-opdoc-drugwar/video-opdoc-drugwar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The War on Drugs Is a Failure’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '&#8216;The War on Drugs Is a Failure&#8217;', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:34:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Gregory Brothers', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Gregory Brothers'}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a36079f3-b0ba-55ae-8789-f9fa991354ac', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a36079f3-b0ba-55ae-8789-f9fa991354ac'}, {'abstract': 'Two days after the explosion at a fertilizer plant in this town sliced by a busy railroad and highway in Central Texas, the death toll rose to 14 but only a few people were still presumed missing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/us/texas-explosion.html', 'snippet': 'Two days after the explosion at a fertilizer plant in this town sliced by a busy railroad and highway in Central Texas, the death toll rose to 14 but only a few people were still presumed missing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST, Tex. — Two days after the explosion at a fertilizer plant in this town sliced by a busy railroad and highway in Central Texas, the death toll rose to 14, but with the search of damaged structures nearly finished by Friday afternoon, only a few people were still presumed missing, local and county officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/us/20texas1/20texas1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/20/us/20texas1/20texas1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, '