sk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos and Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66ec9e79-a21c-5630-b158-6b2a0551ca9d', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66ec9e79-a21c-5630-b158-6b2a0551ca9d'}, {'abstract': 'The hacking of major banks and technology giants garner headlines, but it’s the tech-driven start-ups and growth companies that can stand to lose their entire business if they are victims of cyberattacks, the authors write.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/cyberattacks-a-huge-threat-to-start-ups-and-their-investors/', 'snippet': 'The hacking of major banks and technology giants garner headlines, but it’s the tech-driven start-ups and growth companies that can stand to lose their entire business if they are victims of cyberattacks, the authors write.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Craig A. Newman and Daniel L. Stein are litigation partners with Richards Kibbe & Orbe, the New York-based law firm. Mr. Newman also serves as chief executive of the Freedom2Connect Foundation, a nonprofit group focused on promoting Internet freedom through the use of technology. Mr. Stein is a former federal prosecutor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyberattacks a Huge Threat to Start-Ups, and Their Investors', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T13:49:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig A. Newman and Daniel L. Stein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Stein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/596e8d05-b40a-5917-8dd6-e3059b76cc7c', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/596e8d05-b40a-5917-8dd6-e3059b76cc7c'}, {'abstract': 'People who have not completed high school are most likely to start their own businesses, according to a new report.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/americas-biggest-entrepreneurs-high-school-dropouts/', 'snippet': 'People who have not completed high school are most likely to start their own businesses, according to a new report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among America’s most celebrated entrepreneurs are college dropouts like Mark Zuckerberg, Bill Gates, Steve Jobs and Michael Dell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s Biggest Entrepreneurs: High School Dropouts', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dropouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T14:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': '