he essential facts of life.” For two years, two months and two days, he walked, observed, listened, wrote and read. The result was “Walden,” the book that made him one of the most beloved American writers, regarded by many as the country’s first environmentalist.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/books/review/0421-bks-Wulf/0421-bks-Wulf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 112, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/10/books/review/0421-bks-Wulf/0421-bks-Wulf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 112}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/books/review/0421-bks-Wulf/0421-bks-Wulf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 191, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/books/review/0421-bks-Wulf/0421-bks-Wulf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/books/review/0421-bks-Wulf/0421-bks-Wulf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/10/books/review/0421-bks-Wulf/0421-bks-Wulf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/10/books/review/0421-bks-Wulf/0421-bks-Wulf-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Man for All Seasons', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Man for All Seasons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thoreau, Henry David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T14:17:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrea Wulf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wulf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3996a929-2ce7-5068-ac60-69fd974b9d62', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3996a929-2ce7-5068-ac60-69fd974b9d62'}, {'abstract': 'Should novelists try harder to confront long-term environmental crises?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/books/review/writing-the-end.html', 'snippet': 'Should novelists try harder to confront long-term environmental crises?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 30 last year, after staying up late to edit the final proofs of my novel, I woke to discover it had already been adapted for television — by CNN, MSNBC, Fox News and every other channel that had interrupted its programming to show images of a flooded New York City. Nature had taken a few liberties with the adaptation. In my novel, New York is hit by Tammy, a Category 3 hurricane; Hurricane Sandy was a Category 1. But the aftermath was largely the same: massive destruction, displacement and despair, modern catastrophe’s dismal triad.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/books/review/0421-bks-Rich/0421-bks-Rich-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 112, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/books/review/0421-bks-Rich/0421-bks-Rich-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 112}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/books/review/0421-bks-Rich/0421-bks-Rich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 192, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/books/review/0421-bks-Rich/0421-bks-Rich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/books/review/0421-bks-Rich/0421-bks-Rich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/21/books/review/0421-bks-Rich/0421-bks-Rich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/books/review/0421-bks-Rich/0421-bks-Rich-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Writing the End', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Writing the End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Nathaniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T14:18:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', '