Red Door, has suffered structural woes, but that has not dimmed his vision nor his energy for music, musicians and art.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/his-studio-is-in-disrepair-but-his-passion-for-music-is-intact/', 'snippet': 'Side Street: Giorgio Gomelsky’s storied studio, known as the Red Door, has suffered structural woes, but that has not dimmed his vision nor his energy for music, musicians and art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time Raul Gonzalez and his bandmates in Barra Libre sat down to discuss recording with Giorgio Gomelsky, they spent hours talking – about everything but music. He told them – as he has everyone from the Rolling Stones to Jeff Buckley – that they had to be sure they were doing it for the music, not the money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/19sidestreet-cityroom/19sidestreet-cityroom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/19sidestreet-cityroom/19sidestreet-cityroom-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/19sidestreet-cityroom/19sidestreet-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/19sidestreet-cityroom/19sidestreet-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/19sidestreet-cityroom/19sidestreet-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/19sidestreet-cityroom/19sidestreet-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/19sidestreet-cityroom/19sidestreet-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Studio Is in Disrepair, but His Passion for Music Is Intact', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T14:24:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43b627cb-042f-5b45-b6e6-ade0ba1e50ba', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43b627cb-042f-5b45-b6e6-ade0ba1e50ba'}, {'abstract': 'What do you want to hear when you’re drinking at a bar late at night, before the bartender kicks you out?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/playlist-songs-to-close-down-a-bar-to/', 'snippet': 'What do you want to hear when you’re drinking at a bar late at night, before the bartender kicks you out?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Drink column, I write about the darkness, weirdness and sometime greatness of late-late-night drinking. My complete suggested playlist appears in the magazine, but here are seven selections to get you started—or, I suppose, to get things ended. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Playlist: Songs to Close Down a Bar To', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T14:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da9690c5-7925-5bd7-b5ee-7836ee02405b', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da9690c5-7925-5bd7-b5ee-7836ee02405b'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re going to be a late-late-night drinker, you need good company and the right beverage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/magazine/the-proper-way-to-close-a-bar.html', 'snippet': 'If you’re going to be a late-late-night drinker, you need good company and the right beverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a few minutes, it felt as if we really might go through with it. This must’ve been 1996. It was past closing time at the Liquor Store (a much-missed TriBeCa corner bar). An indulgent bartender dimmed the lights and locked the door and let a few regulars stay. After many hours of drinking and talking, crazy notions take hold, and two painters and I got it in our heads that we should catch a cab as soon as the sun rose, go straight to J.F.K. and get on whatever flight would take us the farthest, cheapest. But in that bright light of day, we realized that, for us, cheapest couldn’t possibly be cheap enough. With one credit card and about $30 in cash among us, our dream was quickly dashed. But it was a good dream while it lasted.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':