': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeb01b97-097b-5bf0-92b7-be24e10ddc2d', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeb01b97-097b-5bf0-92b7-be24e10ddc2d'}, {'abstract': 'A fight stick accessory for the new fighting game “Injustice: Gods Among Us” is designed to mimic arcade-style game play.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/for-a-battle-between-superman-and-batman-you-need-a-big-weapon/', 'snippet': 'A fight stick accessory for the new fighting game “Injustice: Gods Among Us” is designed to mimic arcade-style game play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Accompanying the release on Tuesday of “Injustice: Gods Among Us,” the new fighting game from Warner Bros. Interactive Entertainment, was a range of supporting products, including comic books, action figures, an album and a mobile app. One of the largest accessories is a fight stick that is included with the Battle Edition of the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Superman and Batman Battle, You Need a Big Weapon', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superman (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T16:43:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10d2a71e-4e1a-57c0-87b5-679ab3d3bf02', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10d2a71e-4e1a-57c0-87b5-679ab3d3bf02'}, {'abstract': 'The N.B.A. playoffs will begin this weekend, with four games on Saturday, including the Celtics at New York and the Bulls at Brooklyn, and four more on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/sports/basketball/in-the-2013-nba-playoffs-it-is-lebron-james-vs-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'The N.B.A. playoffs will begin this weekend, with four games on Saturday, including the Celtics at New York and the Bulls at Brooklyn, and four more on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the beginning of the season the N.B.A. appeared to have two superpowers: the defending champion Miami Heat and the superstar-packed Los Angeles Lakers. While the Lakers proved unworthy of the attention, the Heat casually went about a season in which they put together the second longest winning streak in league history and made the rest of the teams appear to be playing for second place.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/nbapreview/nbapreview-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/nbapreview/nbapreview-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/nbapreview/nbapreview-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/nbapreview/nbapreview-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/nbapreview/nbapreview-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/nbapreview/nbapreview-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/nbapreview/nbapreview-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'LeBron James vs. the World', 'kicker': '2013 N.B.A. Playoffs Preview', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LeBron James vs. the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T16:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b940aa-816a-5027-9134-a5f9e284aae7', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b940aa-816a-5027-9134-a5f9e284aae7'}, {'abstract': 'Why should any new rules favor money market funds that invest in government debt over those buying corporate debt?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/no-need-for-2-tracks-in-money-market-overhaul/', 'snippet': 'Why should any new rules favor money market funds that invest in government debt over those buying corporate debt?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two-tier money market fund reform is as clear as mud. The Securities and Exchange Commission is trying again to regulate these mutual funds, which compete with bank deposit accounts. But the rules could favor funds that invest in government debt over those buying corporate debt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Need for 2 Tracks in Money Market Overhaul', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Market Accounts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackRock Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T16:50:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Agnes T. Crane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb1b4301-a7df-5785-9570-f7a82d42b7d1', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb1b4301-a7df-5785-9570-f7a82d42b7d1'}, {'abstract': 'But the organization plans to continue excluding gay adults.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/boy-scouts-may-lift-ban-on-gay-youths/', 'snippet': 'But the organization plans to continue excluding gay adults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Associated Press is reporting that the Boy Scouts of America will lift its ban on openly gay youth members, but continue excluding gay adult leaders, pending approval from the national board. If the board votes to accept the resolution at its annual meeting next month, “no youth may be denied membership in the Boy Scouts of America on the basis of sexual orientation or preference alone.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boy Scouts May Lift Ban on Gay Youths', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T16:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4daab0ea-8264-561f-a3c9-8c1682c33a3f', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4daab0ea-8264-561f-a3c9-8c1682c33a3f'}, {'abstract': 'The immigration legislation in the Senate recognizes that trying to make the Mexican border impermeable to illegal entry is unrealistic. But opponents may yet challenge that premise.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/the-challenge-of-securing-the-border/', 'snippet': 'The immigration legislation in the Senate recognizes that trying to make the Mexican border impermeable to illegal entry is unrealistic. But opponents may yet challenge that premise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two decades ago, the border with Mexico was not as big a priority as it is today. The Border Patrol‘s entire budget was only $362.6 million in 1993 — some $584 million in today’s money. It had 4,028 agents. Unsurprisingly, perhaps, border patrolling wasn’t amazingly effective.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Challenge of Securing the Border', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Border Patrol (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T17:02:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eduardo Porter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eduardo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Porter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b82c0c9-81c9-5599-9533-41ed7410b127', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b82c0c9-81c9-5599-9533-41ed7410b127'}, {'abstract': 'Often, not responding to an e-mail or telephone call might say “no” unintentionally, though sometimes that is exactly what we meant to say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/your-money/the-anxiety-of-the-unanswered-e-mail.html', 'snippet': 'Often, not responding to an e-mail or telephone call might say “no” unintentionally, though sometimes that is exactly what we meant to say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OVER the last few weeks, I’ve repeatedly run up against one of the classic frustrations of modern life — sending out e-mails and hearing nothing back.', 'print_section': 'B', 'p