-to-your-ears.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to a number of audio tours you can carry in your pocket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re the sort of traveler who avoids group walking tours because they’re not to your liking or not in your budget, it doesn’t mean you have to wander the ruins of Pompeii without hearing how the city perished, or visit London Bridge without being told of its roots in Roman times. You don’t need a group tour; you just need a smartphone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Their Mouth to Your Ears', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Their Mouth to Your Ears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Walking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T17:42:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55434ed1-773e-5bd3-b44f-8cac52b6721e', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55434ed1-773e-5bd3-b44f-8cac52b6721e'}, {'abstract': 'The Bronx High School of Science spent more than a dozen years and $1 million on a Holocaust museum and studies center. “Great scientists have to be ethical people,” said the school’s principal.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/in-the-basement-of-a-school-known-for-science-a-holocaust-museum/', 'snippet': 'The Bronx High School of Science spent more than a dozen years and $1 million on a Holocaust museum and studies center. “Great scientists have to be ethical people,” said the school’s principal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bronx High School of Science has produced more scientific leaders than many countries, including eight Nobel Prize winners in physics and chemistry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Basement of a School Known for Science, a Holocaust Museum', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx High School of Science', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T17:46:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6652eb22-5366-5d85-83a9-66df8e5bec27', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6652eb22-5366-5d85-83a9-66df8e5bec27'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Brecht was suspended, the university said on Friday, as it investigates accusations of verbal abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/sports/rutgers-suspends-lacrosse-coach-amid-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'Brian Brecht was suspended, the university said on Friday, as it investigates accusations of verbal abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rutgers said Friday that it had suspended the head coach of its men’s lacrosse team and was investigating accusations of verbal abuse, the latest developments in the athletics controversy that has gripped the univer