ents; and, of course, “Game of Thrones,” with its boiled-wool cloaks and armored corsets, have inspired a flurry of fashion stories and runway interpretations. “Da Vinci’s Demons” is but the latest costume extravaganza poised to charm the fashion set.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Historical Dramas Play Out in Fashion, Too', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Historical Dramas Play Out in Fashion, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Eighties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T18:41:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth LaFerla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LaFerla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d14b307-3ca8-5b94-8672-8f1522a305f9', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d14b307-3ca8-5b94-8672-8f1522a305f9'}, {'abstract': '“All New X-Men” is No. 3 on this week’s hardcover list.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/graphic-books-best-sellers-x-men-travel-back-in-time/', 'snippet': '“All New X-Men” is No. 3 on this week’s hardcover list.', 'lead_paragraph': '“All New X-Men,” written by Brian Michael Bendis and illustrated by Stuart Immonen, enters the graphic books hardcover best-seller list this week at No. 3. Mr. Bendis is no stranger to team books. Since 2004, he has also been the guiding hand of the Avengers, and has pushed that team of heroes, which includes Captain America, Iron Man and Thor, to new heights of popularity. In fact, the Avengers started to outshine the X-Men, who had previously been Marvel’s top franchise. “All New X-Men,” which collects the first five issues of the new series, is wonderfully entertaining. Time-travel stories are old hat, but Mr. Bendis manages to squeeze some delight out of this one. The original X-Men have traveled from the past to the present and are alarmed by what they see: one of them has betrayed their founder, Charles Xavier; one of them has evolved beyond recognition; another of them is dead. Though it may cause problems with the space-time continuum, the younger team opts to stay in the present, hoping to right some wrongs. I, for one, am eager to see what happens next.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/books/20graphicbooks/20graphicbooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 398, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/books/20graphicbooks/20graphicbooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 398, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/books/20graphicbooks/20graphicbooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/20/books/20graphicbooks/20graphicbooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: X-Men Travel Back in Time', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': 