a-51c6-9431-6f7c5d518b04'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y.C. Nature: The bloodroot, with its icy white flowers and sap of a striking color, may last just a day or two at most.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/gory-name-icy-bloom/', 'snippet': 'N.Y.C. Nature: The bloodroot, with its icy white flowers and sap of a striking color, may last just a day or two at most.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in an environment as man-made as New York City’s, nature stubbornly persists — in park woodlands, empty lots, and between the cracks of the sidewalk. In an occasional series, Dave Taft, a senior-level park ranger in New York City with the National Park Service, will be offering close-in portraits of the city’s plants and animals.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21NATURE2/21NATURE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21NATURE2/21NATURE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 671}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21NATURE2/21NATURE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 916, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21NATURE2/21NATURE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1831, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21NATURE2/21NATURE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21NATURE2/21NATU