pector was accused of randomly pepper-spraying Occupy Wall Street protesters, and another was accused of punching a man.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/no-charges-for-police-commanders-over-actions-during-protests/', 'snippet': 'One deputy inspector was accused of randomly pepper-spraying Occupy Wall Street protesters, and another was accused of punching a man.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the Occupy Wall Street protests and their aftermath, they were the online-video symbols for those who said the New York Police Department was using excessive force:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/20bologna-cityroom/20bologna-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/20bologna-cityroom/20bologna-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/20bologna-cityroom/20bologna-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/20bologna-cityroom/20bologna-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/20bologna-cityroom/20bologna-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 0, 'width': 0, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Charges for Police Commanders Over Actions During Protests', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Charges for Police Inspectors Over Occupy Protests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bologna, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T23:44:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b01a773-4b25-5d62-ad9a-c6c522b8b043', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b01a773-4b25-5d62-ad9a-c6c522b8b043'}, {'abstract': 'A Canadian woman charged with plotting to smuggle Saadi el-Qaddafi, a son of the former Libyan dictator, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, into Mexico was released from prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/world/americas/canadian-accused-in-plot-to-help-qaddafis-son-is-released.html', 'snippet': 'A Canadian woman charged with plotting to smuggle Saadi el-Qaddafi, a son of the former Libyan dictator, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, into Mexico was released from prison.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Canadian woman charged with plotting to smuggle Saadi el-Qaddafi, a son of the former Libyan dictator, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, into Mexico was released from a Mexican prison on Friday. The case of the woman, Cynthia Vanier, is linked to actions of senior executives of SNC-Lavalin, an international engineering company based in Montreal that had enjoyed a close relationship with the Qaddafi family. Ms. Vanier, who had traveled to Libya for the company, said she was in Mexico to promote a water project. Her release after 18 months of detention followed an appeal to Mexico’s Supreme Court challenging the terms of her arrest. SNC-Lavalin remains the subject of police investigations in Canada and Switzerland, and two of its former executives have been charged with fraud, conspiracy and forgery in Montreal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Canadian Accused in Plot to Help Qaddafi’s Son Is Released', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Canadian Accused in Plot To Help Qaddafi’s Son Is Released', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Saadi el-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vanier, Cynthia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-19T23:52:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/79d784c0-1784-59c2-8c5d-10a14f3fef95', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79d784c0-1784-59c2-8c5d-10a14f3fef95'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/nyregion/events-in-westchester.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreati