 'nyt://article/5e7ded81-4144-5e24-ba86-7b73230efc5f'}, {'abstract': 'Mark S. Hoebee directs the Paper Mill Playhouse’s production of “Thoroughly Modern Millie,” a play based on a 1967 film written by Richard Morris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/nyregion/a-review-of-thoroughly-modern-millie-in-millburn.html', 'snippet': 'Mark S. Hoebee directs the Paper Mill Playhouse’s production of “Thoroughly Modern Millie,” a play based on a 1967 film written by Richard Morris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening scene looks like a New Yorker cover, one of those great Art Deco drawings that make you want to slurp up the city like ice cream or sip it languidly like a bathtub-gin martini with olives. Impressionistic shapes in pale, pale colors pretend to be the Manhattan skyline. Singers and dancers in neutral 1920s dresses, cloches and men’s wear are uniform enough to be figures on a travel poster, bouncy enough to be naughty.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ARTSNJ_SPAN/21subARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ARTSNJ_SPAN/21subARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ARTSNJ_SPAN/21subARTSNJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ARTSNJ_SPAN/21subARTSNJ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1130, 'width': 1930, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':