ne, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/jp-braves/jp-braves-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/jp-braves/jp-braves-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/jp-braves/jp-braves-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/jp-braves/jp-braves-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1501, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/jp-braves/jp-braves-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/jp-braves/jp-braves-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/jp-braves/jp-braves-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Janitor to Rookie, Hitting Fourth for Braves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Janitor to Rookie, Hitting Fourth for Braves ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Braves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCann, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gattis, Evan (1986- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Fredi (1964- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman, Freddie (1989- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T00:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69858dc6-1af0-5fe6-8a02-51b190d4790e', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69858dc6-1af0-5fe6-8a02-51b190d4790e'}, {'abstract': 'From Debussy on, non-musical systems have influenced composers. Here’s how Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi’s concept of flow shaped my work for strings.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/19/the-music-of-flow/', 'snippet': 'From Debussy on, non-musical systems have influenced composers. Here’s how Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi’s concept of flow shaped my work for strings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a composer who studied music and mathematics, I have always found numbers, structure, and science accessible touch-points. But something more interesting evolved over the past several years as I returned to the Hungarian psychologist Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi’s work on “flow.” Coined in 1969, he defined flow as “the state in which people are so involved in an activity that nothing else seems to matter.” No surprise then that some of his first participants were composers: this is a constant aspiration. Composers have a reputation for working methods that include long sessions alone in their workplace with intense focus on their work, occasionally — indeed, arguably ideally — eventually losing a sense of time. I was attracted to this idea and felt a kinship, less to my working method but more in the way I thought and organized my music. But how was I to use “flow” in any musically meaningful way?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Music of ‘Flow’', 'kicker': 'The Score', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cage, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Debussy, Claude', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xenakis, Iannis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T01:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Carrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d91a2c3-196e-5cd6-8bd7-f8f0263f395c', 'word_count': 1433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d91a2c3-196e-5cd6-8bd7-f8f0263f395c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Neuharth’s business model, characterized by stripped-down costs and generous margins, reshaped the industry, tilting the balance between profits and public service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/business/media/al-neuharth-executive-who-built-gannett-and-usa-today-is-dead-at-89.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Neuharth’s business model, characterized by stripped-down costs and generous margins, reshaped the industry, tilting the balance between profits and public service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Neuharth, the brash and blustery media mogul who built the Gannett Company into a communications Leviathan and created USA Today, for years America’s best-selling newspaper, died on Friday at his home in Cocoa Beach, 