an avant-garde playwright and director, said he finds weekends depressing, and is really energized only by doing his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The avant-garde playwright and director Richard Foreman, who is 75, founded the Ontological-Hysteric Theater in 1968, and for years the theater performed his playful, disorienting and theory-infused works at St. Mark’s Church in the Bowery. He also makes film and video, and released the movie “Once Every Day” in February. Mr. Foreman, who was awarded a MacArthur Fellowship in 1995, lives in SoHo with his wife, Kate Manheim, 68, an actress and artist. When he is not in rehearsals for his new play, “Old-Fashioned Prostitutes (A True Romance),” opening at the Public Theater on April 30, he spends his Sundays at home, reading, watching television and ruminating on France and SoHo as they used to be.  ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE4/21ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE4/21ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE4/21ROUTINE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE4/21ROUTINE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE4/21ROUTINE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7