juggernaut — but it helps that they are playing bad teams.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/rangers/rangers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/rangers/rangers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 319}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/rangers/rangers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/rangers/rangers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1088, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/rangers/rangers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/rangers/rangers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/20/sports/rangers/rangers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers’ Recipe: Good Bounces, Bad Opponents, Ugly Goals', 'kicker': 'Rangers 8, Sabres 4', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rangers’ Recipe: Good Bounces, Bad Opponents, Ugly Goals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buffalo Sabres', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Brad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T03:44:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30fa9e85-601d-5e30-879a-a5bab1bced85', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30fa9e85-601d-5e30-879a-a5bab1bced85'}, {'abstract': 'Power producers would have to curb the tainted water they discharge into waterways under a proposal issued by the Environmental Protection Agency on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/us/epa-issues-plan-on-tainted-water-from-power-plants.html', 'snippet': 'Power producers would have to curb the tainted water they discharge into waterways under a proposal issued by the Environmental Protection Agency on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Power producers would have to curb the tainted water they discharge into waterways under a proposal issued by the Environmental Protection Agency on Friday, the latest in a series of rules focused on utilities that burn coal. The agency proposed four options for regulating the waste from power plants, which are the top source of pollutants in streams, rivers and other waters. The final rules would have the most impact on coal-fired plants, which are the primary source of the pollutants, and would be phased in beginning in 2017. The Sierra Club, which sued the agency to issue the rules, said the announcement was an important step. “When finalized in their strongest form, the Environmental Protection Agency’s common-sense and affordable standards will save lives, prevent children from getting sick, and ensure our water is safe to drink and our fish safe to eat,” said Michael Brune, the group’s executive director. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Issues Plan on Tainted Water From Power Plants', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.P.A. Issues Plan On Tainted Water From Power Plants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sierra Club', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T03:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9afa3607-58e8-5aa4-89d6-00d0619bfaad', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9afa3607-58e8-5aa4-89d6-00d0619bfaad'}, {'abstract': 'The N.B.A.’s board of governors will not vote on the sale of the Sacramento Kings until the week after next at the earliest, Commissioner David Stern said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/sports/basketball/nba-still-weighing-sale-of-kings.html', 'snippet': 'The N.B.A.’s board of governors will not vote on the sale of the Sacramento Kings until the week after next at the earliest, Commissioner David Stern said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.B.A.’s board of governors will not vote on the sale of the Sacramento Kings until the week after next at the earliest, Commissioner David Stern said. The finance and relocation committees are still gathering information about the competing bids to buy the club, and they will probably recommend a winning bid to the board of governors toward the end of next week. The board of governors then must take seven business days to consider the recommendation. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Still Weighing Sale of Kings', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Still Weighing Sale of Kings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sacramento Kings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, David Joel (1942- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T04:10:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c7a1f2-2fa1-571d-89ef-15b920f4fefd', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55c7a1f2-2fa1-571d-89ef-15b920f4fefd'}, {'abstract': 'New York Road Runners has increased security at its four-mile race this weekend in Central Park in response to the bomb attacks at the Boston Marathon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/sports/increased-security-for-central-park-race.html', 'snippet': 'New York Road Runners has increased security at its four-mile race this weekend in Central Park in response to the bomb attacks at the Boston Marathon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Road Runners has increased security at its four-mile race this weekend in Central Park in response to the bomb attacks at the Boston Marathon. In an e-mail message to club members, Road Runners told entrants in the City Parks Foundation Run to arrive early on Sunday and expect to go through a security screening. Runners were asked to avoid taking bags to the race. Those who do will have the contents transferred into clear bags. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Increased Security for Central Park Race', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Running', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Increased Security for Central Park Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T04:18:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/74369611-56be-5dfc-84b7-1a1c11947ab6', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74369611-56be-5dfc-84b7-1a1c11947ab6'}, {'abstract': 'The earthquake struck the western region of Sichuan Province, where a previous quake killed 70,000 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/world/asia/china-earthquake.html', 'snippet': 'The earthquake struck the western region of Sichuan Province, where a previous quake killed 70,000 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YUXI, China — Many residents of this tiny village in the mountainous region of southwest China spent Saturday night in tents and makeshift shelters, too scared to sleep in their flimsy homes after an earthquake killed 188 people early that morning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surviving China’s Latest Earthquake, but Afraid to Go Home ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surviving China’s Latest Earthquake, but Afraid to Go Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlez, Jane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T04:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1974306c-2ec2-51da-ac96-efacceb1f711', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1974306c-2ec2-51da-ac96-efacceb1f711'}, {'abstract': 'Now that the Barclays Center is midway through its maiden season of organizing fights, Brooklyn gyms are again alive with the sounds of thumping gloves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/04/21/nyregion/boxing-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Now that the Barclays Center is midway through its maiden season of organizing fights, Brooklyn gyms are again alive with the sounds of thumping gloves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the Barclays Center is midway through its maiden season of organizing fights, Brooklyn gyms are again alive with the sounds of thumping gloves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Borough Laces Up Its Gloves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays Center (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Gleason's Gym", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starrett City Boxing Club', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T04:34:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/31e1310f-e4b8-588b-a041-865bfe6b55c7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/31e1310f-e4b8-588b-a041-865bfe6b55c7'}, {'abstract': 'With the Barclays Center midway through its first season of organizing boxing matches, local gyms in the borough are again alive with hometown fighters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/nyregion/fans-hope-barclays-center-will-revive-brooklyn-boxing.html', 'snippet': 'With the Barclays Center midway through its first season of organizing boxing matches, local gyms in the borough are again alive with hometown fighters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks before fight night, the Brooklyn boxer Danny Jacobs was in headgear and a padded pelvic girdle, taking rounds in an underground sparring ring at the Starrett City Boxing Club. The club, in the basement of a high-rise building near Jamaica Bay, was in the old-school mold: duct-taped heavy bags and pitted concrete floors — the sort of place where only a fighter in training would have spent such a beckoningly sunny April day.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_