': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T10:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a4dc473-f326-5e2a-865f-37c16b7df556', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a4dc473-f326-5e2a-865f-37c16b7df556'}, {'abstract': 'Gee, why didn’t our economic fantasies work?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/the-non-secret-of-our-non-success/', 'snippet': 'Gee, why didn’t our economic fantasies work?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Giles of the FT reports that central bankers are worried that they are “flying blind”; he quotes Lorenzo Bibi-Smaghi, formerly of the ECB governing board, saying “We don’t fully understand what is happening in advanced economies.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Non-Secret of Our Non-Success', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T11:04:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4530ac9e-e10a-5a48-b653-512d41ff05f9', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4530ac9e-e10a-5a48-b653-512d41ff05f9'}, {'abstract': 'Trivial breaks through where years of analysis didn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/the-good-glitch/', 'snippet': 'Trivial breaks through where years of analysis didn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been cynical about the likelihood that the Reinhart-Rogoff fiasco would lead to any real change in policy, and I still have doubts. But reflecting on the debate so far, I’m wondering a bit if I have been too cynical — or at any rate, cynical in the wrong way. For my vague, unquantifiable sense is that the debacle is changing the conversation quite a lot, even among the guys in suits. And it was the coding error that did it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Good Glitch', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T11:16:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f5f0e3-0b19-5939-aca9-767004c8ffc1', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f5f0e3-0b19-5939-aca9-767004c8ffc1'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following the aftermath of Monday’s deadly explosions at the Boston Marathon, which killed three and injured more than 170.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/updates-on-aftermath-of-boston-marathon-explosions-3/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following the aftermath of Monday’s deadly explosions at the Boston Marathon, which killed three and injured more than 170.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:27 P.M. | Men Held Saturday ‘Unrelated’ to Marathon, F.B.I. Says', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/19/nyregion/dzhokhar-yearbook-lede/dzhokhar-yearbook-lede-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 579, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i