o Paid With Their Lives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Texas Town Mourns the First Responders Who Paid With Their Lives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West (Tex)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'West Chemical and Fertilizer Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fertilizer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T16:46:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad350c5e-c597-5148-9470-193f95cad208', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad350c5e-c597-5148-9470-193f95cad208'}, {'abstract': 'Take away the dorm rooms, the classroom banter, the brown-nosing, the keg parties and the tuition, and is it still college?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/opinion/sunday/grading-the-mooc-university.html', 'snippet': 'Take away the dorm rooms, the classroom banter, the brown-nosing, the keg parties and the tuition, and is it still college?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I LEARNED many fascinating things while taking a series of free online college courses over the last few months. In my history class, I learned there was a Japanese political plot to assassinate Charlie Chaplin in 1932. In my genetics class, I learned that the ability to wiggle our ears is a holdover from animal ancestors who could shift the direction of their hearing organs.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/sunday-review/21MOOC/21MOOC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/sunday-review/21MOOC/21MOOC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/sunday-review/21MOOC/21MOOC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/sunday-review/21MOOC/21MOOC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/sunday-review/21MOOC/21MOOC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/21/sunday-review/21MOOC/21MOOC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/sunday-review/21MOOC/21MOOC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Cheers for Web U!', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Cheers for Web U!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 