'main': 'The Man Who Saved CUNY', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man Who Saved CUNY', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Randolph, Eleanor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City University of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldstein, Matthew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T17:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7364e4c7-3093-5065-822e-6558607f94c9', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7364e4c7-3093-5065-822e-6558607f94c9'}, {'abstract': 'Want a safer country and stronger rule of law? Pass comprehensive immigration reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/opinion/sunday/immigration-and-fear.html', 'snippet': 'Want a safer country and stronger rule of law? Pass comprehensive immigration reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much of the country was still waking up to the mayhem and confusion outside Boston on Friday morning when Senator Charles Grassley decided to link the hunt for terrorist bombers to immigration reform.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigration and Fear', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Immigration and Fear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grassley, Charles E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T17:09:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/045bc2f5-5d53-5a22-a4e8-15a83c77e106', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/045bc2f5-5d53-5a22-a4e8-15a83c77e106'}, {'abstract': 'On a trip through Asia, the outlines of John Kerry’s style of diplomacy emerged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/opinion/sunday/a-new-flexible-kerry.html', 'snippet': 'On a trip through Asia, the outlines of John Kerry’s style of diplomacy emerged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Kerry made his first trip to Asia as secretary of state this month amid rising tensions with North Korea and returned home on Monday with things a bit quieter, although with North Korea nobody really knows what’s next. Bouncing from Seoul to Beijing to Tokyo, the new secretary showed a commendable impulse for common-sense diplomacy, including engagement with adversaries like the North. The policy questions are: Will a White House with a proclivity for adversarial responses support his diplomatic approach? And how well will it play not only in the Oval Office but with troublesome states like North Korea?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/2