fficiating (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Workman, Haywoode', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T17:50:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hillel Kuttler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hillel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuttler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4a9eddc-d323-5790-85f1-9b84086c7526', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4a9eddc-d323-5790-85f1-9b84086c7526'}, {'abstract': 'For the Nets’ first-round playoff series against the Chicago Bulls, the arena will grow even darker, with the team distributing black T-shirts to fans in hopes of creating a “blackout” in the crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/20/nets-ploy-intimidate-with-shirts/', 'snippet': 'For the Nets’ first-round playoff series against the Chicago Bulls, the arena will grow even darker, with the team distributing black T-shirts to fans in hopes of creating a “blackout” in the crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barclays Center has a somewhat forbidding atmosphere for visiting teams. The music pumped through the arena’s loudspeakers, hand-selected by the mix-tape artist J. Period, has an aggressive attitude. The black-clad Brooklynettes dance team has a decidedly adult attitude. And the Nets, in black home uniforms that are in stark contrast with typical N.B.A. fashion, certainly look tough, even if their game is based on offensive execution more than any sort of intimidation.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets’ Ploy: Intimidate With Shirts', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nets’ Ploy: Intimidate With Shirts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'T-Shirts (Apparel)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-20T18:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/501e623b-51ce-5454-85d9-2696ca197928', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/501e623b-51ce-5454-85d9-2696ca197928'}, {'abstract': 'The author fell in love with the team, and the player Wendell Ladner in particular, when they were in the old A.B.A. The pain that would bring was not confined to basketball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/21/sports/basketball/one-fans-rocky-relationship-with-the-nets.html', 'snippet': 'The author fell in love with the team, and the player Wendell Ladner in particular, when they were in the old A.B.A. The pain that would bring was not confined to basketball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question inevitably comes twice a year: once in November, when the N.B.A. season usually starts, and again in the spring, when the playoffs near.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/21/sports/dog-chang1/dog-chang1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/21/sports/dog-chang