d” the young title hero eventually learns the meaning of fear. It seems believable that he manages to emerge confidently from his encounter with the cartoonish dragon of Robert Lepage’s staging, which returned to the Metropolitan Opera on Saturday afternoon with Jay Hunter Morris in the role. That he succumbs to fear in the final scene, however, seemed less credible.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/SIEGFRIED/SIEGFRIED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/SIEGFRIED/SIEGFRIED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 830}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/SIEGFRIED/SIEGFRIED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 740, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/SIEGFRIED/SIEGFRIED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/SIEGFRIED/SIEGFRIED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/SIEGFRIED/SIEGFRIED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/SIEGFRIED/SIEGFRIED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Way to Slay Wagner’s Dragon', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Way to Slay Wagner’s Dragon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lepage, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Jay Hunter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T20:36:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0998d0b-a192-5b03-b1b3-cdc1fdff70ca', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0998d0b-a192-5b03-b1b3-cdc1fdff70ca'}, {'abstract': 'Jasmin Vardimon Company of London made a rare American appearance, at Montclair State University in New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/arts/dance/jasmin-vardimon-company-dances-at-montclair-state.html', 'snippet': 'Jasmin Vardimon Company of London made a rare American appearance, at Montclair State University in New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTCLAIR, N.J. — The choreographer Jasmin Vardimon, born in Israel, formed her company in 1997 in London, where she has found much popular success and a post as associate artist at Sadler’s Wells. Except for once, in Texas, though, her troupe had not appeared in the United States until a run last week in the Peak Performances series at Montclair State University here. First impression: Ms. Vardimon is familiar with the work of Pina Bausch.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank