rd Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d6746e5-d7cd-547a-b5b3-35e722ff379d', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d6746e5-d7cd-547a-b5b3-35e722ff379d'}, {'abstract': 'Laura Butler Rivera stars in “so go the ghosts of méxico, part one,” a Matthew Paul Olmos play inspired by a female sheriff of a town dominated by drug cartels in Mexico.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/theater/reviews/matthew-paul-olmoss-so-go-the-ghosts-of-mexico-part-one.html', 'snippet': 'Laura Butler Rivera stars in “so go the ghosts of méxico, part one,” a Matthew Paul Olmos play inspired by a female sheriff of a town dominated by drug cartels in Mexico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010 a 20-year-old criminology student with a new baby volunteered for a job no one else would take: chief of police in the tiny Mexican border town of Práxedis Gilberto Guerrero, a place overrun by rival drug gangs. (To give you a sense of either the courageousness or foolhardiness of her decision: her predecessor had been tortured and beheaded.) The international news media quickly anointed this remarkable young mother, Marisol Valles García, as “the bravest woman in Mexico.” She proceeded by publicly withdrawing from the drug war, which she said she would leave to the feds; hiring more female officers, who didn’t carry guns; and focusing her police force’s efforts on community building and teaching family values, which she hoped would keep the gangs at bay.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/sogo/sogo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/sogo/sogo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/sogo/sogo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/sogo/sogo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/sogo/sogo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/sogo/sogo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/arts/sogo/sogo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Facing a War Zone Rife With Cartels and Zombies', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing a War Zone Rife With Cartels and Zombies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valles Garcia, Marisol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La MaMa ETC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olmos, Matthew Paul', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Laura Butler', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Meiyin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/406ca9d2-fb43-5443-ae66-0e15999b438f', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/406ca9d2-fb43-5443-ae66-0e15999b438f'}, {'abstract': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/business/treasury-auctions-set-for-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:03:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/211899da-1cd8-5b6e-9c74-d7c5009d3ebb', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/211899da-1cd8-5b6e-9c74-d7c5009d3ebb'}, {'abstract': 'The Fox musical “Glee,” which defied the ratings odds when it had its debut in 2009, will remain on the network through 2015 in a deal announced on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/arts/television/fox-renews-glee-for-2-more-seasons.html', 'snippet': 'The Fox musical “Glee,” which defied the ratings odds when it had its debut in 2009, will remain on the network through 2015 in a deal announced on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Fox musical “Glee,” which defied the ratings odds when it had its debut in 2009, will remain on the network through 2015 in a deal announced on Friday. The network ordered two more seasons of the series, giving the co-creator Ryan Murphy and the other producers an unusual opportunity to plan story lines for the characters well into the future. The current season of “Glee,” its fourth, attracts about 8.7 million viewers a week and routinely ranks among TV’s top 10 shows for 18- to 34-year-olds. In a statement Mr. Murphy thanked Fox and the studio that produces the series, 20th Century Fox Television, for their support. The fourth season has toggled between the high school glee club in Ohio and the graduates who are at a performing arts college in New York. Mr. Murphy has hinted in interviews that he wants the fifth season to focus on just one of the locations, but he has not said which one.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox Renews ‘Glee’ for 2 More Seasons', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fox Renews ‘Glee’ For 2 More Seasons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Glee (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:08:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cbd2345-8ba0-5406-8b78-cee92ec11dbf', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cbd2345-8ba0-5406-8b78-cee92ec11dbf'}, {'abstract': 'Mohamed Ibrahim Rageh had fled Mogadishu, the Somali capital, in 2009 after a spate of killings, but returned to continue his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/world/africa/reporter-for-government-radio-is-killed-in-somalia.html', 'snippet': 'Mohamed Ibrahim Rageh had fled Mogadishu, the Somali capital, in 2009 after a spate of killings, but returned to continue his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia — A Somali journalist was shot to death on Sunday outside his home in Mogadishu by unknown gunmen, becoming the fourth journalist killed in his country this year, officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reporter for Government Radio Is Killed in Somalia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mogadishu (Somalia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio Mogadishu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Somali National Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rageh, Mohamed Ibrahim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d661f439-1734-595b-bf42-e7849252d791', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d661f439-1734-595b-bf42-e7849252d791'}, {'abstract': 'The blues musician B. B. King and the rock group Los Lobos will be the headliners at the third annual Lowdown Hudson Blues Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/arts/music/free-downtown-blues.html', 'snippet': 'The blues musician B. B. King and the rock group Los Lobos will be the headliners at the third annual Lowdown Hudson Blues Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The blues musician B. B. King and the rock group Los Lobos will be the headliners at the third annual Lowdown Hudson Blues Festival, which will be held on July 10 and 11 in a plaza outside the World Financial Center in Lower Manhattan. Other acts include the rock trio Los Lonely Boys, Alejandro Escovedo and the rhythm-and-blues group the James Hunter Six. The concerts, presented by Brookfield Office Properties, are free to the public.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Downtown Blues', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free Downtown Blues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, B B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Lobos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cd99271-df1d-5471-afc8-789a795a7f63', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cd99271-df1d-5471-afc8-789a795a7f63'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Merz founded a wildlife reserve in Kenya that has helped the black rhinoceros come back from the brink of extinction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/world/africa/anna-merz-protector-of-black-rhinos-dies-at-81.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Merz founded a wildlife reserve in Kenya that has helped the black rhinoceros come back from the brink of extinction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anna Merz, who went to Kenya seeking a serene retirement but became so appalled by the slaughter of black rhinoceroses that she helped start a reserve to protect them, becoming a global leader in the fight against their extinction, died on April 4 in Melkrivier, South Africa. She was 81.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/world/ALT-MERZ-obit/ALT-MERZ-obit-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/22/world/ALT-MERZ-obit/ALT-MERZ-obit-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/world/ALT-MERZ-obit/ALT-MERZ-obit-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/world/ALT-MERZ-obit/ALT-MERZ-obit-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 1467, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 's