res polluters to acquire credits to offset their emissions. A glut of credits, combined with lower demand because of the weak economy, has driven down the price to close to zero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/04/21/business/0421-carbon.html', 'snippet': 'The European Union’s Emissions Trading System was intended to reduce carbon dioxide emissions by setting a market price on them. The system, set up in three phases, requires polluters to acquire credits to offset their emissions. A glut of credits...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Union’s Emissions Trading System was intended to reduce carbon dioxide emissions by setting a market price on them. The system, set up in three phases, requires polluters to acquire credits to offset their emissions. A glut of credits, combined with lower demand because of the weak economy, has driven down the price to close to zero.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Falling Price of Carbon Credits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:33:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/85f6af05-13a1-5338-a865-d079bfec912e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/85f6af05-13a1-5338-a865-d079bfec912e'}, {'abstract': 'Several senators want the ability to question the suspect at length without any lawyer, intensifying a recurring debate over how to handle terrorism cases arising inside the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/us/gop-lawmakers-push-to-hold-boston-suspect-as-enemy-combatant.html', 'snippet': 'Several senators want the ability to question the suspect at length without any lawyer, intensifying a recurring debate over how to handle terrorism cases arising inside the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Some Republican lawmakers want President Obama to declare the surviving Boston bombing suspect an enemy combatant in order to question him without a lawyer and other protections of the criminal justice system, intensifying a recurring debate over how to handle terrorism cases arising inside the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Lawmakers Push to Have Boston Suspect Questioned as Enemy Combatant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Lawmakers Push to Have Boston Suspect Questioned as Enemy Combatant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-21T22:33:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8353fb21-5cd0-5d0b-8f8d-c564bd3a64b4', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8353fb21-5cd0-5d0b-8f8d-c564bd3a64b4'}, {'abstract': 'Some drivers have expressed doubts about the viability of using the vehicles, arguing that any charging break would undercut earnings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/nyregion/electric-taxi-experiment-to-begin-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Some drivers have expressed doubts about the viability of using the vehicles, arguing that any charging break would undercut earnings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The taxis are not entirely yellow. Their drivers are allowed to refuse certain fares. Even the smell is different, with no oil-rich odor greeting riders at the door.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/taxi/taxi-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/taxi/taxi-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/taxi/taxi-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/taxi/taxi-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1077, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/taxi/taxi-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/taxi/taxi-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/taxi/taxi-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Electric-Taxi Experiment Asks if City’s Cabbies Can Spare the Time to Plug In', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Electric-Taxi Experiment Ask