in-manhattan-get-heavy-security.html', 'snippet': 'Bomb-sniffing dogs, a counterterrorism vehicle and radiation sweeps were among the measures at races in Central Park and the West Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A swarm of police officers was deployed. Radiation sweeps were conducted. Trash cans and parked cars were unceremoniously removed. There were bomb-sniffing dogs, capable of picking up the scent of chemical vapors drifting in the wind.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/nyc-security/nyc-security-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/nyc-security/nyc-security-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/nyc-security/nyc-security-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/nyc-security/nyc-security-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/nyc-security/nyc-security-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/nyc-security/nyc-security-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/nyregion/nyc-security/nyc-security-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Sunday Running Events in Manhattan Are Minor, but Security Isn’t', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Sunday Running Events in Manhattan Are Minor, but Security Isn’t', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruderman, Wendy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T01:22:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Ruderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2bddb9b-7400-5637-87eb-063d606f96f6', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2bddb9b-7400-5637-87eb-063d606f96f6'}, {'abstract': 'Tamerlan Tsarnaev, one of the suspects in the Boston bombings, found comfort in Dagestan, a region in the North Caucasus that is the center of violent Islamic insurgency in Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/world/europe/pilgrim-in-violent-land-suspect-found-comfort-in-dagestan.html', 'snippet': 'Tamerlan Tsarnaev, one of the suspects in the Boston bombings, found comfort in Dagestan, a region in the North Caucasus that is the center of violent Islamic insurgency in Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAKHACHKALA, Russia — Tamerlan Tsarnaev had already found religion by the time he landed in Dagestan, a combustible region in the North Caucasus that has become the epicenter of a violent Islamic insurgency in Russia and a hub of jihadist recruitment. What he seemed to be yearning for was a home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Search for Home Led Suspect to Land Marred by Strife', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pilgrim in a Violent Land: ‘Listen to the Call to Prayer’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Tamerlan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dagestan (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T01:28:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn and Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39d0bdc9-f266-5a37-99e6-d4c7f87c7d01', 'word_count': 1313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39d0bdc9-f266-5a37-99e6-d4c7f87c7d01'}, {'abstract': 'At its most fundamental level, the problem with the so-called East Midtown planning study is that it’s not a plan. The best path toward ensuring the future of the area may well be that of preservation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/opinion/a-smart-way-to-revive-east-midtown.html', 'snippet': 'At its most fundamental level, the problem with the so-called East Midtown planning study is that it’s not a plan. The best path toward ensuring the future of the area may well be that of preservation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE are told that New York needs to be lofted back into global competitiveness. That the city isn’t modern enough. Take the area around Grand Central Terminal. With 80 percent of the building stock in the neighborhood now over 50 years old, we hear, our city is falling behind, and current zoning restrictions inhibit redevelopment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Modern City in East Midtown?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Modern City in East Midtown?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Planning Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T01:28:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert A. M. Stern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Stern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e01d159-b11e-5e4f-9737-23b6d40e2201', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e01d159-b11e-5e4f-9737-23b6d40e2201'}, {'abstract': 'At least in part, the bombers’ intent was to disrupt exactly what events like the Boston Marathon celebrate: the American given, as