ts/', 'snippet': 'The courts in Russia are virtually the only point of contact between an individual or organization and the state. If only they were fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW: When I look at the editorial calendar for this week, or any other week, most of what I see are court hearings. The courts in Russia have replaced politics: They are virtually the only point of contact between an individual or organization and the state. While the state rules by decree and always in its own favor, at least in court the individual can make an argument or attempt an objection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Through the Motions', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T12:31:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3aeb598-33c4-5399-898a-e2704881adfc', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3aeb598-33c4-5399-898a-e2704881adfc'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan’s caretaker government declined on Monday to bring treason charges against Pervez Musharraf, a former military leader, saying it was beyond its mandate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/20