b': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T15:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01757fe8-373e-5c83-9a06-ee9fc59fcf9d', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01757fe8-373e-5c83-9a06-ee9fc59fcf9d'}, {'abstract': 'A cautiously worded study has found an association between the use of both S.S.R.I.’s and tricyclic antidepressants during pregnancy and an increased risk of autism spectrum disorders.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/study-links-autism-with-antidepressant-use-during-pregnancy/', 'snippet': 'A cautiously worded study has found an association between the use of both S.S.R.I.’s and tricyclic antidepressants during pregnancy and an increased risk of autism spectrum disorders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A cautiously worded study based on data collected in Sweden has found that “in utero exposure to both selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (S.S.R.I.’s) and nonselective monoamine reuptake inhibitors (tricyclic antidepressants) was associated with an increased risk of autism spectrum disorders, particularly without intellectual disability.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Links Autism With Antidepressant Use During Pregnancy', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T15:57:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a674a891-1875-5ab6-b7b3-d5492d9292e1', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a674a891-1875-5ab6-b7b3-d5492d9292e1'}, {'abstract': 'As owners, we often try throwing as much as we can against the wall to see what sticks. This is unlikely to work when it comes to search for capital.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/what-business-owners-get-wrong-when-looking-for-capital/', 'snippet': 'As owners, we often try throwing as much as we can against the wall to see what sticks. This is unlikely to work when it comes to search for capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The life of a small-business owner or entrepreneur can be chaotic. We live from priority to priority, crisis to crisis. There are only 24 hours in a day and only so many hours to sleep. Believe it or not, I still haven’t changed the phone system in our office that I posted about months ago. I have given up on it for now, moved on to higher priorities. As owners, we concentrate on pleasing our customers and whatever urgent issues arise during the day, and we let other issues — even important ones, sometimes — take a back seat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Business Owners Get Wrong When Looking for Capital', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T15:58:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6989fed1-9e95-5ac8-ad77-35adaec4402e', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6989fed1-9e95-5ac8-ad77-35adaec4402e'}, {'abstract': 'Take a trip to Evenland and ponder prime patterns in a world without odd numbers.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/evenland/', 'snippet': 'Take a trip to Evenland and ponder prime patterns in a world without odd numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is your kid entranced by math but discouraged by math contests? If so, take heart — here’s Dr. Cathy O’Neil, who received a Ph.D. in mathematics from Harvard and subsequently taught math at Barnard College.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/crosswords/JRMF-Stanford-2012/JRMF-Stanford-2012-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/crosswords/JRMF-Stanford-2012/JRMF-Stanford-2012-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/crosswords/JRMF-Stanford-2012/JRMF-Stanford-2012-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/06/crosswords/JRMF-Stanford-2012/JRMF-Stanford-2012-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/06/crosswords/JRMF-Stanford-2012/JRMF-Stanford-2012-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Primes in Evenland Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba98b376-914a-5826-8cd4-5c96510a42f8', 'word_count': 2393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba98b376-914a-5826-8cd4-5c96510a42f8'}, {'abstract': 'Premiere of new video by Superhumanoids.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/video-premiere-superhumanoids-so-strange/', 'snippet': 'Premiere of new video by Superhumanoids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those searching for early “song of the summer” candidates need look no further than “So Strange,” the new single from Superhumanoids’ forthcoming debut, “Exhibitionists” (out on June 11 from Innovative Leisure). Products of the Silver Lake scene in Los Angeles that gave rise to the likes of Silversun Pickups and the band’s current tour-mates Local Natives, the dream pop trio of Cameron Parkins, Sarah Chernoff and Max St. John wrote the song nearly two years ago in the early stages of creating their record. “It wasn’t something that was necessarily intentional,” Parkins says, “but it was the beginning of summer for us in Los Angeles, and we really wanted to capture the excitement that people have around that time.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Premiere | Superhumanoids, ‘So Strange’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T16:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19a8d0b9-262c-5c74-9ff5-f4bdccf0a33c', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19a8d0b9-262c-5c74-9ff5-f4bdccf0a33c'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Cunningham’s On the Street this week features a forceful trend in men’s wear, a 21st-century take on the Gatsby style.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/video-on-the-street-east-of-west-egg/', 'snippet': 'Bill Cunningham’s On the Street this week features a forceful trend in men’s wear, a 21st-century take on the Gatsby style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even F. Scott Fitzgerald could not have imagined the extravagance of Tiffany & Company’s Blue Book Ball Thursday night to introduce its collection of jewelry inspired by the jazz age and the new movie version of “The Great Gatsby.” Tiffany built a blue box over the skating rink at Rockefeller Center, with suspended aerialists and the Tiffany Diamond Dancers. The buffets were almost unimaginable. And, a rarity at New York high-profile events, most of the women wore their own dresses and jewels. Many guests were Asian, some in native dress. Tiffany’s focus on the era coincides with a forceful trend in men’s wear, a 21st-century take on the Gatsby style, bottom row, seen on men passing the store’s facade, marked with “fountains” of tape. On April 17, the store held a reception, bottom left and right, for the new designs, and young people dressed in the spirit. Not to be missed are the windows, each one a glittering gem, by Christopher Young. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: On the Street, East of West Egg', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Twenties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockefeller Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Great Gatsby (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T16:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c3243a-d695-5c6c-bdaa-e4eade5cd108', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c3243a-d695-5c6c-bdaa-e4eade5cd108'}, {'abstract': 'After 26 years, Pam and James Hayes-Bohanan say their marital success may be because of a couples workshop or just picking the right person.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/booming/from-early-lean-years-a-strong-marriage-bond.html', 'snippet': 'After 26 years, Pam and James Hayes-Bohanan say their marital success may be because of a couples workshop or just picking the right person.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Booming’s “Making It Last” column profiles baby boomer couples who have been together 25 years or more. Send us your story and photos through our submission form.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/booming/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/22/booming/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/booming/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 707, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/booming/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/booming/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/22/booming/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/22/booming/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1/22last-booming-hayes-bohanan1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Through Early Lean Years, a Stronger Bond', 'kicker': 'Making It Last', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'majo