ional Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T16:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/163c7eb1-b467-564b-96f3-a18fe9847e3b', 'word_count': 1374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/163c7eb1-b467-564b-96f3-a18fe9847e3b'}, {'abstract': 'The acquisition of Power-One could prove to be a smart one, the author contends. For one, ABB should also be able to reap cost savings and extra sales, by plugging Power-One into its global network.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/abbs-moment-in-the-sun/', 'snippet': 'The acquisition of Power-One could prove to be a smart one, the author contends. For one, ABB should also be able to reap cost savings and extra sales, by plugging Power-One into its global network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABB’s contrarian push into solar energy looks smart. The Swiss group is buying Nasdaq-listed Power-One for $1 billion in cash – a fully priced deal, given the solar industry’s current financial misery. But ABB insists Power-One occupies a sweet spot. That sounds plausible, and long term, the deal should add up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABB’s Moment in the Sun', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABB LTD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Power-One Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T17:01:23+0000', 'document_type': '