ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yuca (Vegetable)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pediatrics (Journal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T20:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3cd40ff-53f8-5fdd-9502-08ca8ec3541a', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3cd40ff-53f8-5fdd-9502-08ca8ec3541a'}, {'abstract': 'Salman Rushdie explains his approach to turning his novel into a screenplay.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/rushdie-on-the-midnights-children-script-if-i-want-to-hack-stuff-out-ill-hack-stuff-out/', 'snippet': 'Salman Rushdie explains his approach to turning his novel into a screenplay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Salman Rushdie’s sprawling novel “Midnight’s Children,” published in 1981, tells the story of Saleem Sinai, a boy born at the stroke of midnight on Aug. 15, 1947, the very moment when India gained independence from British rule. The book’s many characters, elements of magical realism (Saleem can telepathically communicate with other children born at the same time), and vast spatial and temporal canvas have made it notoriously difficult to film. The BBC had planned an adaptation in the 1990s, and before that producers involved with Richard Attenborough’s Academy Award-winning biopic “Gandhi” had approached Mr. Rushdie about a possible movie version. The movie will finally make it to the screen on Friday, written by none other than Mr. Rushdie. During a recent interview, he talked about the experience of turning his own novel into a screenplay. Here are edited excerpts from the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/arts/salmanrushdie/salmanrushdie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/23/arts/salmanrushdie/salmanrushdie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/arts/salmanrushdie/salmanrushdie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/arts/salmanrushdie/salmanrushdie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1333, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/arts/salmanrushdie/salmanrushdie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/23/arts/salmanrushdie/salmanrushdie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/arts/salmanrushdie/salmanrushdie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rushdie on the ‘Midnight’s Children’ Script: ‘If I Want to Hack Stuff Out, I’ll Hack Stuff Out’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-22T20:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ceb59e76-89b2-5e71-9368-67d1e7b7aa76', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ceb59e76-89b2-5e71-9368-67d1e7b7aa76'}, {'abstract': 'The Royal Canadian Mounted Police said they arrested two foreign nationals on Monday, but offered few details of a plot they linked to “Al Qaeda elements” in Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/world/americas/2-arrested-in-plot-to-attack-passenger-train-canada-says.html', 'snippet': 'The Royal Canadian Mounted Police said they arrested two foreign nationals on Monday, but offered few details of a plot they linked to “Al Qaeda elements” in Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — The Royal Canadian Mounted Police on Monday announced the arrest of two men who are accused of planning to derail a passenger train in an Al Qaeda-linked plot.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Are Accused in Canada of Plotting Train Derailment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Accused In Canada Of Plotting Derailment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocation