cedures to safeguard taxpayers when making emergency loans “as soon as is practicable.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/fed-still-owes-congress-a-blueprint-on-emergency-lending-to-banks/', 'snippet': 'Dodd-Frank, passed in 2010, required the Fed to develop policies and procedures to safeguard taxpayers when making emergency loans “as soon as is practicable.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Federal Reserve lent more than $1 trillion to big banks during the 2008 financial crisis, Congress required the central bank to devise specific ways of protecting taxpayers when doling out emergency loans to financial institutions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed Still Owes Congress a Blueprint on Its Emergency Lending', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fed Still Owes Congress a Blueprint on Its Emergency Lending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T00:45:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b438f49d-a188-57d3-8031-ec58ac97e7c8', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b438f49d-a188-57d3-8031-ec58ac97e7c8'}, {'abstract': 'Mary Jo White, the new chairwoman of the agency, is putting together her team, including one of her longtime lieutenants.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/s-e-c-picks-ceresney-and-canellos-for-enforcement/', 'snippet': 'Mary Jo White, the new chairwoman of the agency, is putting together her team, including one of her longtime lieutenants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission ushered in a new era of leadership on Monday, appointing a former federal prosecutor turned defense lawyer to help run the unit that polices the front lines of financial fraud.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Co-Directors for S.E.C. Signal Shift', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Co-Directors For S.E.C. Signal Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Canellos, George S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ceresney, Andrew J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Mary Jo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T00:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/001974e5-75d8-55a3-a667-102620c3f36c', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/001974e5-75d8-55a3-a667-102620c3f36c'}, {'abstract': 'Are victims of industrial explosions different from victims of terrorism?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/opinion/industrial-accidents-and-acts-of-terrorism.html', 'snippet': 'Are victims of industrial explosions different from victims of terrorism?', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST after lunch break one infernal Houston afternoon in 1995, I slammed the door of the company truck, cranked the engine, and punched the gas so hard that the truck fishtailed onto Jensen Drive. Beside me sat my co-worker Charlie. In his lap, he clenched a blood-drenched wad of paper towels over what had been, minutes before, his left thumb. The severed thumb, packed hurriedly on ice in a cup, rode in the center console.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Only an Accident', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Only an Accident', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West (Tex)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'West Chemical and Fertilizer Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T00:56:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Machart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Machart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8e43008-a24a-57da-bb93-9cc5fd683bfc', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8e43008-a24a-57da-bb93-9cc5fd683bfc'}, {'abstract': 'The state flower’s brief blooming period is also trespassing season, as crowds tramp through privately owned farms and ranches for the perfect photo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/us/bluebonnet-season-in-texas-brings-out-the-crowds.html', 'snippet': 'The state flower’s brief blooming period is also trespassing season, as crowds tramp through privately owned farms and ranches for the perfect photo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHAPPELL HILL, Tex. — It is bluebonnet season in Texas, when hayfields and grazing pastures are transformed into seas of indigo bloom. And while Vermonters take pride in their fall foliage and Washingtonians love their cherry blossoms, Texans can be near fanatical about bluebonnets, sometimes ignoring property laws and personal safety to wade into their fragrant midst.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23BLUEBONNET/23BLUEBONNET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23BLUEBONNET/23BLUEBONNET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23BLUEBONNET/23BLUEBONNET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23BLUEBONNET/23BLUEBONNET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 965, 'width': 1944, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23BLUEBONNET/23BLUEBONNET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 