ools?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Discipline (Students)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T01:08:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/12694180-4aca-5d35-9ba2-2285d3344570', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12694180-4aca-5d35-9ba2-2285d3344570'}, {'abstract': 'There is no good reason to deny Marilyn Tavenner a unanimous endorsement to be administrator of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/opinion/a-confirmation-of-marilyn-tavenner-is-overdue.html', 'snippet': 'There is no good reason to deny Marilyn Tavenner a unanimous endorsement to be administrator of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate Finance Committee is scheduled to hold a long-overdue vote on Tuesday on President Obama’s nominee to lead the embattled agency responsible for overseeing Medicare, Medicaid and the implementation of health care reforms. The committee ought to set aside its deep partisan divisions and unanimously endorse Marilyn Tavenner to be the administrator of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services. The full Senate should then confirm her.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Confirmation Too Long Delayed', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Confirmation Too Long Delayed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavenner, Marilyn B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Finance', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T01:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2c53e30-1f3b-5316-84d1-df5ca08f8707', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2c53e30-1f3b-5316-84d1-df5ca08f8707'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Kraft is chief executive of Kraftbox Entertainment in Hollywood and the former president of Fox Music. He is not the owner of the New England Patriots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/business/flying-when-your-name-is-prominent-but-you-are-not.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Kraft is chief executive of Kraftbox Entertainment in Hollywood and the former president of Fox Music. He is not the owner of the New England Patriots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’VE been flying most of my career. As a musician in the early days, I was flying all the time between New York and Los Angeles, and then I started working with Jim Henson and I was adding London into the mix. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'i