ulie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf68887e-6076-5770-8059-235f6bf6efdf', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf68887e-6076-5770-8059-235f6bf6efdf'}, {'abstract': 'The cautious response from President Obama is still the right approach to a confused war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/opinion/more-help-for-syrian-rebels.html', 'snippet': 'The cautious response from President Obama is still the right approach to a confused war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was more horror in Syria over the weekend, where scores of bodies, most of them civilians, were discovered in a Damascus suburb. The victims are believed to have died in a weeklong offensive by forces loyal to President Bashar al-Assad, who seems to have no misgivings whatever about a slaughter, including the use of airstrikes and missiles, that has claimed more than 70,000 lives so far during two-and-a-half years of war. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Help for Syrian Rebels', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Help for Syrian Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T01:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'n