rimination.html', 'snippet': 'Employers have created a disadvantaged class by making hiring decisions based on credit reports. New York City can fix that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People fall behind on their bills for many reasons — a recession that costs them jobs, a divorce, an illness. Now comes a further obstacle to getting their lives in order: employers who screen job applicants based on credit histories. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit History Discrimination', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Credit History Discrimination', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T01:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8122906-5b59-509a-b745-511955be3063', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8122906-5b59-509a-b745-511955be3063'}, {'abstract': 'The White House defended President Obama’s efforts on gun violence, but he has long struggled to master his relationship with Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/us/politics/in-gun-bill-defeat-a-president-who-hesitates-to-twist-arms.html', 'snippet': 'The White House defended President Obama’s efforts on gun violence, but he has long struggled to master his relationship with Congress.', 'lead_para