 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60eced0-af0d-5aa3-b35f-b569bc913794'}, {'abstract': 'David Lee, the Golden State All-Star forward who was making the first playoff appearance of his career, tore his right hip flexor in the Warriors’ Game 1 loss to Denver and is done for the postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/sports/basketball/warriors-david-lee-ends-first-playoff-appearance-with-injury.html', 'snippet': 'David Lee, the Golden State All-Star forward who was making the first playoff appearance of his career, tore his right hip flexor in the Warriors’ Game 1 loss to Denver and is done for the postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To his credit, David Lee is not using the word “cursed.” Lee, the All-Star power forward for the Golden State Warriors, tore his right hip flexor in Saturday’s Game 1 loss to the Denver Nuggets, a quick ending to the first playoff appearance of his career. But he is trying to maintain a positive attitude about his misfortune.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/sports/LEE/LEE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/23/sports/LEE/LEE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/sports/LEE/LEE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/sports/LEE/LEE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/sports/LEE/LEE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/23/sports/LEE/LEE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/sports/LEE/LEE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Long Playoff Wait, Warrior’s Experience Is Brief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Long Playoff Wait, Warrior’s Experience Is Brief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden State Warriors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Nuggets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, David (1983- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T02:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7641fc2-a9ba-5847-b243-b455ff83d179', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7641fc2-a9ba-5847-b243-b455ff83d179'}, {'abstract': 'A debut by Severin T. Nelson.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/22/some-call-it-pop/', 'snippet': 'A debut by Severin T. Nelson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — I grew up in one of the most cosmopolitan towns in the world, New York City, and thought I had heard everything until I went off to college in upstate New York. They speak an entirely different language up there, and it soon became apparent to me that I was going to get myself in trouble if I ventured out without someone who was willing to translate for me. SODA became “pop,” sprinkles on ice cream became “jimmies” (I misheard that one, and assumed that the young man asking me if I wanted jimmies just had an odd, third-person way of coming on to women), and I’m sure there were more that I’m forgetting. My point is, never send your kids off to school in another region without a dictionary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Call It ‘Pop’', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T02:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f568a1a2-c0c1-5f72-83db-542dfb6aba20', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f568a1a2-c0c1-5f72-83db-542dfb6aba20'}, {'abstract': 'The service for a 29-year-old woman killed in the bombings drew an overflow crowd, and members of the Boston University community gathered to remember a 23-year-old graduate student from China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/us/services-held-for-boston-marathon-bombings-victims.html', 'snippet': 'The service for a 29-year-old woman killed in the bombings drew an overflow crowd, and members of the Boston University community gathered to remember a 23-year-old graduate student from China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEDFORD, Mass. — With the horror of the Boston Marathon bombings a week in the past, two communities carved out space for quiet remembrance on Monday, bidding farewell to Krystle Campbell and Lu Lingzi, the two young women claimed by the blasts at the race’s finish line. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23MEMORIAL1/23MEMORIAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23MEMORIAL1/23MEMORIAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23MEMORIAL1/23MEMORIAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23MEMORIAL1/23MEMORIAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23MEMORIAL1/23MEMORIAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23MEMORIAL1/23MEMORIAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/us/23MEMORIAL1/23MEMORIAL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hundreds Gather at Services Held for Marathon Victims', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hundreds Gather at Services Held for Marathon Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Mara