nd put on a concert performance of “Salome” by Strauss – all without a music director. The orchestra released its programs for 2013-14, which will be the third season since James Levine stepped down as its music director for health reasons after already missing a number of concerts in previous years.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Symphony Announces New Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boston Symphony Plans Asia Trip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T04:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ea330b-8ad1-56a2-a88d-c83893c46b2a', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ea330b-8ad1-56a2-a88d-c83893c46b2a'}, {'abstract': 'A closely watched monthly index added to concerns that the pace of China’s overall economic growth may be faltering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/business/global/manufacturing-growth-in-china-slows.html', 'snippet': 'A closely watched monthly index added to concerns that the pace of China’s overall economic growth may be faltering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Growth in China’s important factory sector slowed in April, a closely watched monthly index released Tuesday showed, adding to concerns that the pace of overall economic growth in China may be faltering.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype