': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T12:24:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9718ec3-b5a6-5a88-92c1-13b1a52954fd', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9718ec3-b5a6-5a88-92c1-13b1a52954fd'}, {'abstract': 'EBay is fighting efforts to require online merchants to collect state and municipal sales taxes from customers. | Andrew J. Ceresney, the new co-director of the S.E.C.’s enforcement unit, is confronting a fresh batch of challenges. | The Fed has yet to establish rules to protect taxpayers when doling out emergency loans. | Netflix reports surprising growth in its subscriber base.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/ebay-joins-sales-tax-fight/', 'snippet': 'EBay is fighting efforts to require online merchants to collect state and municipal sales taxes from customers. | Andrew J. Ceresney, the new co-director of the S.E.C.’s enforcement unit, is confronting a fresh batch of challenges. | The Fed has y...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was once Amazon that led a lobbying campaign in Washington to prevent online merchants from having to collect state and municipal sales taxes from customers. Now, eBay has taken up the cause as the issue is moving through Washington in earnest for the first time, Andrew Ross Sorkin writes in the DealBook column. A bill introducing such a tax cleared a procedural hurdle in the Senate, setting it up for a vote this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'EBay Joins Sales Tax Fight', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T12:26:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e35ba48-1f6e-5dae-8df7-7f79f5fdab2b', 'word_count': 1639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e35ba48-1f6e-5dae-8df7-7f79f5fdab2b'}, {'abstract': 'Consequences of the “cinnamon challenge,” seeking therapy late in life, replacing a computer’s hard drive and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/tuesday-reading-consequences-of-the-cinnamon-challenge/', 'snippet': 'Consequences of the “cinnamon challenge,” seeking therapy late in life, replacing a computer’s hard drive and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Consequences of the ‘Cinnamon Challenge’', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T12:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c47da5ed-fb45-522b-beba-a0fea0c44c26', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c47da5ed-fb45-522b-beba-a0fea0c44c26'}, {'abstract': 'For more than 20 years, a small group of Jewish women has been fighting against the Orthodox rule at the Western Wall. Finally, their day has come.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/women-and-the-western-wall/', 'snippet': 'For more than 20 years, a small group of Jewish women has been fighting against the Orthodox rule at the Western Wall. Finally, their day has come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The rain didn’t deter many observant Jews from visiting the Western Wall on a recent Sunday. And I wasn’t surprised to see more men than women, and more Orthodox men than other Jews. After all, the men have the luxury of access to a spacious covered area, where only they can pray, as long as they don’t stray from Orthodox customs. Women have a much smaller covered area and on rainy days many are forced to weather the elements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Separate but Equal', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Women of the Wall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western Wall (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T12:48:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37c2c619-9482-54e7-a09e-03581336cce5', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37c2c619-9482-54e7-a09e-03581336cce5'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A subway rider helped guide a family from Boston the day after the bombings at the Boston Marathon.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/strangers-from-boston/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A subway rider helped guide a family from Boston the day after the bombings at the Boston Marathon.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strangers From Boston', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T12:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Altshuler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altshuler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f3d6b10-79cc-5ec8-9fe7-1c676b0c4081', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f3d6b10-79cc-5ec8-9fe7-1c676b0c4081'}, {'abstract': 'Knowledge, not used, prejudices honored, economies destroyed.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/a-heartbreaking-work-of-staggering-folly/', 'snippet': 'Knowledge, not used, prejudices honored, economies destroyed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I have been writing a lot lately, the clean little secret of the global economic crisis is that standard economic theory actually performed pretty well. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Heartbreaking Work of Staggering Folly', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T12:49:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section