Nathaniel Rich Month at The Times. The author’s new novel was reviewed in the Arts section on April 10, then again in the Sunday Book Review on April 14. Mr. Rich also wrote an essay for the Sunday Book Review, with many references to that novel, “Odds Against Tomorrow.” In addition, the Editors’ Choice section of the Sunday Book Review listed Mr. Rich’s novel second on its list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Repeated Book Reviews and ‘the Hat Trick’', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Nathaniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T13:02:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3dc6834-bae2-56b6-94bc-4df734a01d4b', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3dc6834-bae2-56b6-94bc-4df734a01d4b'}, {'abstract': 'Dubai’s ruling family is a dominant force in the horseracing world. The revelation that some of their top thoroughbreds were administered banned streoids is being described as “hugely embarrassing.”', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/horse-doping-scandal-rocks-dubais-rulers/', 'snippet': 'Dubai’s ruling family is a dominant force in the horseracing world. The revelation that some of their top thoroughbreds were administered banned streoids is being described as “hugely embarrassing.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The horseracing world has been shaken