rs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HSBC to Cut 1,150 Additional Jobs in Britain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC.', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T17:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bde3101-1611-5e54-9379-6c6d5e1d6b13', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bde3101-1611-5e54-9379-6c6d5e1d6b13'}, {'abstract': 'The Emmy and Tony award-winning actress talks about her latest role in Richard Greenberg’s Broadway play, “The Assembled Parties.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/talking-talent-judith-light/', 'snippet': 'The Emmy and Tony award-winning actress talks about her latest role in Richard Greenberg’s Broadway play, “The Assembled Parties.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Emmy- and Tony Award-winning actress Judith Light, best remembered as the glamorous divorcée Angela Bower in the 1980s sitcom “Who’s the Boss?” stars as Faye, the matriarch of a wealthy Upper West Side family in turmoil\xa0 in “The Assembled Parties,” running through June 2 at Manhattan Theater Club’s Samuel J. Friedman Theater. Like her Tony-winning character Silda in “Other Desert Cities,” Light has clearly mastered the role of a Jewish woman facing personal and familial crisis with equal doses of wit and wisdom. Penned by Richard Greenberg and directed by Lynne Meadow, “The Assembled Parties” provides Light with a role that proves she is a Broadway force to be reckoned with.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Talent | Judith Light', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Light, Judith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T17:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Tabach-Bank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabach-Bank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/796a410a-a019-5dd7-a59a-2105ecd7c36f', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/796a410a-a019-5dd7-a59a-2105ecd7c36f'}, {'abstract': 'Sheila Birnbaum, a top product liability defense lawyer, is leaving Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom and joining Quinn Emanuel Urguhart & Sullivan.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/sheila-birnbaum-leaves-skadden-for-quinn-emanuel/', 'snippet': 'Sheila Birnbaum, a top product liability defense lawyer, is leaving Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom and joining Quinn Emanuel Urguhart & Sullivan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sheila L. Birnbaum, one of the country’s top product liability defense lawyers, is switching firms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheila Birnbaum Leaves Skadden for Quinn Emanuel', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birnbaum, Sheila L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skadden Arps Slate Meagher & Flom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T17:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc1c9677-a73a-5c01-b4b5-3c990bea2a00', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc1c9677-a73a-5c01-b4b5-3c990bea2a00'}, {'abstract': 'A band called the Upper Crust had a schtick that sounded ridiculous until you witnessed it — they dressed up as 18th-century aristocrats and played heavy metal.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/dangerous-liaisons-meets-acdc/', 'snippet': 'A band called the Upper Crust had a schtick that sounded ridiculous until you witnessed it — they dressed up as 18th-century aristocrats and played heavy metal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Lives essay I wrote for last Sunday’s magazine, a brilliant live band from Boston called the Upper Crust makes an important cameo. I knew about them because my friend Ted Widmer used to be one of their three guitarists (he also wrote for me at George magazine), and they had this shtick that sounded ridiculous until you witnessed it — they dressed up as 18th-century aristocrats and played heavy metal. Actually, it was ridiculous after you witnessed it too, but that was the point. The reason it worked, among other things, was that their songs were surprisingly great, and the band could fill a room with an energy that inspired villainy. The altercation I wrote about at a 1996 show at Brownie’s in the East Village was apparently not uncommon. “We had a lot of extremes, people who loved the humor, and then a lot of people who got out of control,” Widmer says. “It seemed to make people go crazy. There were a lot of fights breaking out at gigs in the early days.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/magazine/23-upper-crust/23-upper-crust-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 249, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/magazine/23-upper-crust/23-upper-crust-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 249, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/magazine/23-upper-crust/23-upper-crust-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/23/magazine/23-upper-crust/23-upper-crust-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/23/magazine/23-upper-crust/23-upper-crust-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dangerous Liaisons’ Meets AC/DC', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T17:17:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44c35da7-6a99-56c0-ba7f-2638f1a67c2d', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44c35da7-6a99-56c0-ba7f-2638f1a67c2d'}, {'abstract': 'Independent experts hope to get prompt, unfettered access to the site of any suspected attack, but that is very difficult in the Syrian conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/world/middleeast/key-step-in-checking-chemical-arms-use-is-also-hardest.html', 'snippet': 'Independent experts hope to get prompt, unfettered access to the site of any suspected attack, but that is very difficult in the Syrian conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most important step in conclusively determining whether chemical weapons have been used is for independent experts to get prompt, unfettered access to the site of the suspected attack, according to Physicians for Human Rights, the American organization that was one of the first to document Iraq’s use of poison gas against its Kurdish population in 1988.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Key Step in Checking Chemical-Arms Use Is Also Hardest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Physicians for Human Rights', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T17:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_