e/port-washington-li-the-town-with-a-homing-signal.html', 'snippet': 'People who grew up in Port Washington, which occupies a peninsula on the North Shore of Long Island, have a way of moving back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent afternoon at the Dolphin Bookshop, on a hilly corner of Main Street and Shore Road, Patti Vunk was gift-wrapping books. “It might be cheaper to go online; it might be easier to go online,” said Ms. Vunk, explaining the book emporium’s survival in the age of e-readers, but Port Washington residents “want us to be here.” ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/realestate/28LIVING_SPAN/Living-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/28/realestate/28LIVING_SPAN/Living-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/realestate/28LIVING_SPAN/Living-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/realestate/28LIVING_SPAN/Living-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/realestate/28LIVING_SPAN/Living-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/28/realestate/28LIVING_SPAN/Living-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im