 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Ripert and Maguy Le Coze, the owners of Le Bernardin, have signed a lease to expand their their restaurant on West 51st Street, a plan that will allow them to add more private dining rooms by early next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Le Bernardin Will Expand to Accommodate More Diners', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ripert, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Bernardin (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T19:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de27bea6-6a9a-55ca-a229-3ea1e32914a6', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de27bea6-6a9a-55ca-a229-3ea1e32914a6'}, {'abstract': 'Anne K. Small, a special assistant to President Obama, will join the Securities and Exchange Commission as its general counsel.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/at-s-e-c-white-adds-to-her-roster-of-top-officials/', 'snippet': 'Anne K. Small, a special assistant to President Obama, will join the Securities and Exchange Commission as its general counsel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after Mary Jo White shuffled the leadership of her enforcement unit, the Wall Street regulator announced on Tuesday that she hired a new lawyer to help run the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At S.E.C., White Adds to Her Roster of Top Officials', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Mary Jo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T19:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15d0611d-3933-5fdc-9ae8-d1f358c4ff73', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15d0611d-3933-5fdc-9ae8-d1f358c4ff73'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement on involvement by the United Nations cultural agency in sensitive areas of Jerusalem was a small but significant breakthrough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/world/europe/israel-and-palestinians-reach-deal-on-unesco.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement on involvement by the United Nations cultural agency in sensitive areas of Jerusalem was a small but significant breakthrough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Israel and the Palestinians agreed on Tuesday to renewed involvement by Unesco, the United Nations cultural agency, in the Old City of Jerusalem. The agreement was a small but significant breakthrough in the often highly politicized workings of the agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/UNESCO/UNESCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/24/world/UNESCO/UNESCO-arti