ibeca Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/tribeca-film-festival-dark-touch/', 'snippet': 'Talking with Marina de Van, writer and director of the grisly revenge tale “Dark Touch,” playing at the Tribeca Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From “Carrie to “Firestarter,” the horror genre is filled with girls who have special powers — to move objects, or ignite flames — that can be used for good or evil. In the film “Dark Touch,” an 11-year-old\xa0 named Neve, the only survivor of a massacre that killed her parents and brother, finds she has similar powers. What she does with them, and who she turns them against, makes the film more of a grisly revenge story than a tale of supernatural chicanery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tribeca Film Festival: ‘Dark Touch’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tribeca Film Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Van, Marina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T19:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f1eee3f-a886-54cc-867a-af77656b43b8', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f1eee3f-a886-54cc-867a-af77656b43b8'}, {'abstract': 'National Park Service sites in New York City are free to visitors from April 20 to 28, but those waiting for a chance to visit the Statue of Liberty or Ellis Island free will have to wait until next year, at least.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/23/national-park-sites-are-free-this-week-but-two-remain-closed/', 'snippet': 'National Park Service sites in New York City are free to visitors from April 20 to 28, but those waiting for a chance to visit the Statue of Liberty or Ellis Island free will have to wait until next year, at least.', 'lead_paragraph': ' This week, all of the National Park Service sites in New York City are free to visitors – except for the two best known to most of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Park Sites Are Free This Week, but Two Remain Closed', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statue of Liberty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Park Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ellis Island (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T19:35:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfc88aa9-7dec-5c51-b91b-8cb33a71fbee', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfc88aa9-7dec-5c51-b91b-8cb33a71fbee'}, {'abstract': 'A new column from Mark Bittman explores moderate, conscious eating: a diet higher in plants and lower in animal products and hyperprocessed foods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/dining/healthy-meet-delicious.html', 'snippet': 'A new column from Mark Bittman explores moderate, conscious eating: a diet higher in plants and lower in animal products and hyperprocessed foods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when few of us thought about what we ate, but that’s been turned upside down since the reigning wisdom first decried salt, then cholesterol, then saturated fat, then almost all fat, then red meat, then carbohydrates and so on. Recent culprits include so many foods and foodlike substances that at least twice a week someone asks me: “What’s left to eat? I feel like nothing is safe.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24FLEX_SPAN/24FLEX_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24FLEX_SPAN/24FLEX_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24FLEX_SPAN/24FLEX_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24FLEX_SPAN/24FLEX_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24FLEX_SPAN/24FLEX_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24FLEX_SPAN/24FLEX_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/dining/24FLEX_SPAN/24FLEX_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Healthy, Meet Delicious', 'kicker': 'The Flexitarian', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Healthy, Meet Delicious', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bittman, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T19:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b610d6fa-b2be-5269-8e91-81e63c106c25', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b610d6fa-b2be-5269-8e91-81e63c106c25'}, {'abstract': 'Hank Morris, who was an adviser to Alan G. Hevesi, a disgraced former New York State comptroller, had been in prison since March 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/nyregion/parole-granted-for-morris-ex-consultant-for-hevesi.html', 'snippet': 'Hank Morris, who was an adviser to Alan G. Hevesi, a disgraced former New York State comptroller, had been in prison since March 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Hank Morris, the onetime political adviser to disgraced former State Comptroller Alan G. Hevesi, was granted parole on Tuesday, five months after Mr. Hevesi was released.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/n