, as the Star', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cello, Big and Bowed, as the Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T20:05:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c42e54f7-9bb3-5ae2-8d29-2a0012b6b930', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c42e54f7-9bb3-5ae2-8d29-2a0012b6b930'}, {'abstract': 'Health providers are joining organizers and insurance companies to spread the word in the six months remaining before insurance becomes available under the 2010 health care law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/health/racing-to-inform-millions-unaware-of-new-health-coverage.html', 'snippet': 'Health providers are joining organizers and insurance companies to spread the word in the six months remaining before insurance becomes available under the 2010 health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST LANSING, Mich. — President Obama and the Democrats passed the 2010 health care law to make medical insurance available to more than 30 million people who do not have it. But with recent studies showing that as many as three-fourths of those people are unaware of their new options, health care providers are joining community organizers and insurance companies in an ambitious effort to spread the word in the six months remaining before the health plans become available.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racing to Spread Word About New Health Plans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racing to Spread Word About New Health Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Richard Dale', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T20:06:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa6fa7b2-f92b-5fd5-943f-1f3f54b784f7', 'word_count': 1309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa6fa7b2-f92b-5fd5-943f-1f3f54b784f7'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine Stern handed over 60 handwritten volumes that it published in 1983, mistakenly claiming they were Hitler’s undiscovered journals, to Germany’s Federal Archives for posterity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/world/europe/forged-hitler-diaries-now-part-of-germanys-archives.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine Stern handed over 60 handwritten volumes that it published in 1983, mistakenly claiming they were Hitler’s undiscovered journals, to Germany’s Federal Archives for posterity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — When the German newsweekly Stern announced in April 1983 that it had acquired Hitler’s previously undiscovered diaries, the magazine’s exclusive prompted a worldwide sensation. The editors promised to later hand over 60 handwritten volumes to West Germany’s Federal Archives for posterity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/24/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 657}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 936, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1846, 'width': 1686, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/24/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '30 Years Later, Forged Hitler Diaries Enter German Archives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '30 Years Later, Forged Hitler Diaries Enter German Archives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitler, Adolf', 'rank': 1