ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T23:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26d43253-d69d-558d-9133-a89718515816', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26d43253-d69d-558d-9133-a89718515816'}, {'abstract': 'The Environmental Protection Agency has the authority to revoke a mining permit to protect streams and wildlife, a federal appeals court ruled on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/science/earth/court-backs-epa-veto-of-mining-permit.html', 'snippet': 'The Environmental Protection Agency has the authority to revoke a mining permit to protect streams and wildlife, a federal appeals court ruled on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency has the authority to revoke a mining permit to protect streams and wildlife, a federal appeals court ruled on Tuesday. The decision was a victory for the agency, which in 2011 retroactively vetoed a permit granted by the Bush administration in 2007 to allow a subsidiary of Arch Coal of St. Louis to dump tons of mining waste into several West Virginia rivers and streams. The veto was declared illegal in a 2012 decision by Judge Amy Berman Jackson of Federal District Court, who called it an illegal power grab. But on Tuesday, a three-judge panel of the United States Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit ruled unanimously that the Clean Water Act and Congressional intent gave E.P.A. the authority to retroactively revoke a mining permit. The ruling affects a proposed mine known as Spruce No. 1, which would have involved dynamiting the tops off mountains to get at coal. Kim Link, a spokeswoman for Arch Coal, said in an e-mail: “We’re disappointed in the decision, which was related to the procedural aspects of the proceeding. The case will now go back to the district court for a decision on the merits.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Backs E.P.A. Veto of Mining Permit', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Backs E.P.A. Veto of Mining Permit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broder, John M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mountaintop Removal Mining', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Amy Berman', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCH COAL INC', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-23T23:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7f243de-9ea4-55db-ac31-00abe56182f8', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7f243de-9ea4-55db-ac31-00abe56182f8'}, {'abstract': 'Justice Carol E. Huff wrote that the plaintiffs had not proved their argument that the program was comparable to the use of two-way radios, which was banned in 1985.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/nyregion/judge-allows-pilot-program-using-smartphone-apps-to-hail-yellow-taxis.html', 'snippet': 'Justice Carol E. Huff wrote that the plaintiffs had not proved their argument that the program was comparable to the use of two-way radios, which was banned in 1985.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A State Supreme Court justice on Tuesday dismissed a lawsuit aimed at stifling New York City’s plans to allow taxi riders to hail yellow cabs using smartphone apps, ruling that a pilot program to test the apps could proceed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Allows Phone Apps for Hailing Yellow Taxis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Allows Phone Apps For Hailing Yellow Taxis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taxi and Limousine Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yas