ger train with the assistance of Al Qaeda denied the charges in court appearances on Tuesday. A lawyer for one suspect said his client, Raed Jaser, was in a state of “shock and disbelief” and described him as a legal resident for about 20 years. The other suspect, Chiheb Esseghaier, tried to deny the terrorism charges he faces before being cut off by a judge. The police say the men were aided by a group in Iran affiliated with Al Qaeda. In London, an Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesman said that there was “no shred of evidence.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Suspects Appear in Court Over Charges in Derailment Plot', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Suspects Appear in Court Over Charges in Derailment Plot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esseghaier, Chiheb', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaser, Raed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T00:44:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/54774d01-11c8-592f-8436-cabfb865cc29', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54774d01-11c8-592f-8436-cabfb865cc29'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department told Westchester County it would seek a contempt ruling and HUD warned it would revoke $7.4 million if the county did not comply with the housing pact by Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/nyregion/us-gives-westchester-deadline-to-comply-with-housing-pact.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department told Westchester County it would seek a contempt ruling and HUD warned it would revoke $7.4 million if the county did not comply with the housing pact by Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years after Westchester County entered into a landmark desegregation agreement with the federal government, relations between the two sides are hanging by a thread amid federal threats of contempt suits and revocation of money. The showdown is raising unsettling echoes of the disastrous 27-year-long court fight over housing that virtually bankrupted Yonkers, the county’s largest city.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Showdown for Westchester and U.S. Over Desegregation Agreement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showdown For County And HUD', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Applebome, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astorino, Robert P', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T00:45:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/296851ad-5fb5-58bf-99e6-9e3dfeedc197', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/296851ad-5fb5-58bf-99e6-9e3dfeedc197'}, {'abstract': 'A series of financial shocks have jolted the economy in recent decades, but the experts are no closer to understanding how such problems develop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/business/solutions-remain-elusive-after-financial-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'A series of financial shocks have jolted the economy in recent decades, but the experts are no closer to understanding how such problems develop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week the International Monetary Fund hosted a conference of some of the world’s top macroeconomists to assess how the most intense crisis to have shaken the industrialized economies since the Great Depression has changed the profession’s collective understanding of how the world economy works.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image