ion': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cc30564-2f3d-5ab6-97c4-cc6722904d54', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cc30564-2f3d-5ab6-97c4-cc6722904d54'}, {'abstract': 'A three-volume review of the prison riot and aftermath was sealed by court order decades ago. That was wrong then, and it makes even less sense now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/opinion/free-the-attica-report.html', 'snippet': 'A three-volume review of the prison riot and aftermath was sealed by court order decades ago. That was wrong then, and it makes even less sense now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The violence in 1971 at Attica resulted in 43 deaths and left many unanswered questions about what happened at the maximum security prison in western New York. The state attorney general, Eric Schneiderman, now wants a judge to allow the release of a 1975 review of the riot and the retaking of the prison by force.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free the Attica Report', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free the Attica Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Attica Correctional Facility', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T01:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2f09244-9be2-5697-b6bb-979ca293715a', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2f09244-9be2-5697-b6bb-979ca293715a'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of exacerbating historical wounds, Prime Minister Shinzo Abe should focus on enhancing its role as a leading democracy in Asia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/opinion/japans-unnecessary-nationalism.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of exacerbating historical wounds, Prime Minister Shinzo Abe should focus on enhancing its role as a leading democracy in Asia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since taking over as Japan’s prime minister in December, Shinzo Abe and his conservative Liberal Democratic Party have been juggling a packed agenda of complicated issues, including reviving the country’s economy, coping with the aftermath of the 2011 earthquake and tsunami and managing prickly relations with neighbors like North Korea. Stirring up extraneous controversy is counterproductive, but that’s exactly what he and his nationalist allies in Parliament have done.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Unnecessary Nationalism', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan’s Unnecessary Nationalism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T01:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2e0c255-f08a-57b9-a410-fa717e2f2f1c', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2e0c255-f08a-57b9-a410-fa717e2f2f1c'}, {'abstract': 'In a victory for fairness, the Supreme Court ruled that a conviction for marijuana distribution should not result in automatic deportation of noncitizens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/opinion/a-common-sense-immigration-ruling.html', 'snippet': 'In a victory for fairness, the Supreme Court ruled that a conviction for marijuana distribution should not result in automatic deportation of noncitizens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal immigration law prohibits the attorney general from letting a noncitizen stay in the United States for any reason if he is convicted of an aggravated felony. The immigration system has held that every conviction for marijuana distribution is such a felony.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Common Sense Immigration Ruling', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Common Sense Immigration Ruling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T01:23:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The E