 in a day of conflicting accounts about the fate of the pair, the most prominent clergymen drawn into Syria’s civil war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fate of Clerics Held in Syria Is Disputed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fate of Clerics Held in Syria Is Disputed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourtada, Hania', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syrian Observatory for Human Rights', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yazigi, Paul', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Yohanna', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T01:28:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hania Mourtada', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hania', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mourtada', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e758449-f633-52aa-8027-e66e2fef88ec', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e758449-f633-52aa-8027-e66e2fef88ec'}, {'abstract': 'A four-year-old company has just opened its third site in Manhattan for corporate events, offering an alternative to the hotel ballroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/realestate/commercial/convene-a-corporate-host-fills-a-need-for-meeting-space.html', 'snippet': 'A four-year-old company has just opened its third site in Manhattan for corporate events, offering an alternative to the hotel ballroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Commercial tenants have found themselves in a quandary in the last few years thanks to the make-do-with-less downturn. Some companies have shed underused office space in an effort to cut costs, but many of those same companies still require comfortable, high-tech rooms for large events like employee orientations, brainstorming sessions and shareholder meetings.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/business/SUB-CONVENE-1/SUB-CONVENE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/24/business/SUB-CONVENE-1/SUB-CONVENE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/business/SUB-CONVENE-1/SUB-CONVENE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/business/SUB-CONVENE-1/SUB-CONVENE-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1405, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/business/SUB-CONVENE-1/SUB-CONVENE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/24/business/SUB-CONVENE-1/SUB-CONVENE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'capti