b site in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/world/asia/australia-arrests-self-proclaimed-head-of-hacking-group.html', 'snippet': 'The man, who was not identified, has said he is the leader of a collective known as LulzSec, which asserted it shut down the C.I.A.’s Web site in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — The federal police in Australia have arrested the professed leader of a prominent international hacking collective known as LulzSec, which is perhaps best known for its assertions of being behind a cyberattack that shut down the Central Intelligence Agency’s public Web site in 2011.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia Arrests the Professed Head of LulzSec, Which Claims a C.I.A. Hacking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Australia Arrests the Professed Head of LulzSec, Which Claims a C.I.A. Hacking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lulz Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anonymous (Internet Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T06:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bde27c14-7b1d-5c68-bf97-be88556a95be', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bde27c14-7b1d-5c68-bf97-be88556a95be'}, {'abstract': 'The imprisoned Nobel Peace laureate Liu Xiaobo is reading about Russian intellectuals, Soviet Communism and Christianity, and has put on weight, says a lawyer who’s known his family for years.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/jailed-nobel-laureate-liu-xiaobo-reading-on-communism-christianity-gaining-weight/', 'snippet': 'The imprisoned Nobel Peace laureate Liu Xiaobo is reading about Russian intellectuals, Soviet Communism and Christianity, and has put on weight, says a lawyer who’s known his family for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Liu Xiaobo, the jailed Nobel Peace laureate serving an 11-year term for subversion after calling for an end to one-party rule and greater democracy in China, has recently been reading a popular nonfiction book about the history of Soviet Communism and Russian intellectuals in the 19th and 20th centuries, as well as Christian philosophical texts. He has also gained weight, said Mo Shaoping, a Beijing lawyer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24LiuRDV/24LiuRDV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24LiuRDV/24LiuRDV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24LiuRDV/24LiuRDV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24LiuRDV/24LiuRDV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1395, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24LiuRDV/24LiuRDV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 