itle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d29a897-ed1b-582d-9e05-c16d07723bbb', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d29a897-ed1b-582d-9e05-c16d07723bbb'}, {'abstract': 'Hertz 24/7 will extend a car-sharing model to suburban and rural areas.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/more-car-sharing-from-hertz/', 'snippet': 'Hertz 24/7 will extend a car-sharing model to suburban and rural areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The car-sharing unit of the rental car company Hertz is expanding in the coming months, the company said. The service, Hertz 24/7, will extend a car-sharing model that had been available in urban areas and college campuses in the United States, and in five other countries, to suburban and rural areas. It also will improve ease of use, with self-service features including keyless entry and a flexible rental term. Hertz said that the rollout, which will eventually provide service to “the vast majority of Americans,” will begin in late summer in the United States, followed soon after in Europe, and later in China.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Car Sharing From Hertz', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rental Cars: More Car Sharing From Hertz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hertz Global Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T15:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd174998-a23e-55b8-885c-dea31b539133', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd174998-a23e-55b8-885c-dea31b539133'}, {'abstract': 'The newly designed $100 bill is finally about to start circulating, and it is likely to be especially popular abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/made-in-america-craved-everywhere-else/', 'snippet': 'The newly designed $100 bill is finally about to start circulating, and it is likely to be especially popular abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is one of our largest exports, a product made in America from start to finish and craved by businesses and consumers around the world. And the latest edition will be released in October. We speak, of course, about the $100 bill.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Made in America. Craved Everywhere Else.', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T15:02:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e67912f-a324-52b9-9c81-0938b88481f2', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e67912f-a324-52b9-9c81-0938b88481f2'}, {'abstract': 'After an optimistic prediction for growth this week, a look back at past council projections.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/how-accurate-is-the-prime-ministers-economic-advisory-council/', 'snippet': 'After an optimistic prediction for growth this week, a look back at past council projections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, the Economic Advisory Council to the Prime Minister released its annual economic review for the financial year 2012-13. According to the report, the Indian economy is projected to grow by 6.4 percent in the coming year. “I believe we have reached the bottom. The economy will now continue to grow at a faster rate,” the council chairman, C. Rangarajan, said in releasing the report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/24/world/asia/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk/24-India-Eco-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ra