ulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quercia, Roberto G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Housing Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T18:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/571d426c-6087-5341-91b3-f28f3cd3c89b', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/571d426c-6087-5341-91b3-f28f3cd3c89b'}, {'abstract': 'Some sample questions (and answers) from tests on economic fundamentals for high-school seniors, a group whose performance changed little from 2006 to 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/test-your-economic-literacy/', 'snippet': 'Some sample questions (and answers) from tests on economic fundamentals for high-school seniors, a group whose performance changed little from 2006 to 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Education on Wednesday released its latest report on the economic proficiency of 12th graders, based on the test scores of nearly 11,000 students tested in 2012. It found little change in average economic literacy compared to test scores from 2006, although students in the lower part of the score distribution (at the 10th and 25th percentiles) made gains.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Your Economic Literacy', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': '