'abstract': 'The Big Sur Brooklyn Bridge Festival in May will include an exhibition and musical performances dedicated to the writer, who lived in Williamsburg as a child.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/a-week-to-celebrate-henry-millers-brooklyn-connections/', 'snippet': 'The Big Sur Brooklyn Bridge Festival in May will include an exhibition and musical performances dedicated to the writer, who lived in Williamsburg as a child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Henry Miller Memorial Library, a nonprofit bookstore and arts center in Big Sur, Calif., where the novelist lived between 1940 and 1962, is sending envoys east to assert Miller’s presence – in spirit, anyway (he died in 1980) – in the Williamsburg section of Brooklyn, where he spent nearly a decade. The library’s Big Sur Brooklyn Bridge Festival, which opens on May 12 and runs for a week, will include an exhibition, readings, panel discussions, comedy and musical performances.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Week to Celebrate Henry Miller’s Brooklyn Connections', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Henry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T18:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88d1b9c4-b429-5b5e-8a2c-9ddc562ea639', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88d1b9c4-b429-5b5e-8a2c-9ddc562ea639'}, {'abstract': 'Alan Cumming would reprise his Tony-winning role as the M.C.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/wilkommen-again-roundabout-planning-another-cabaret-revival/', 'snippet': 'Alan Cumming would reprise his Tony-winning role as the M.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roundabout Theater Company is planning a revival of the famed musical “Cabaret” at Studio 54 in early 2014 with Alan Cumming starring as the M.C. – the role for which he won a Tony Award in 1998 for a “Cabaret” revival by Roundabout that ended up running at Studio 54 as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Willkommen, Again? Roundabout Planning Another ‘Cabaret’ Revival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ebb, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hathaway, Anne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kander, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T18:29:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23b7aed6-d648-5d5a-9a2b-9ff1cbb1da48', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23b7aed6-d648-5d5a-9a2b-9ff1cbb1da48'}, {'abstract': 'The private equity owners behind Caesars Entertainment have been working overtime in their financial laboratory,the author says.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/caesars-blinds-market-with-science/', 'snippet': 'The private equity owners behind Caesars Entertainment have been working overtime in their financial laboratory,the author says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The private equity owners behind Caesars Entertainment have been working overtime in their financial laboratory. Apollo Global Management and TPG are following last year’s microscopic initial public offering with a spinoff and rights issue concoction. Aiming to raise $1.2 billion, the complex transaction mostly seems designed to buy still more time for the ailing $31 billion leveraged buyout.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caesars Blinds Market With Science', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apollo Global Management', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T18:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00fe0d34-9186-5ce3-a620-e058269f2c9a', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00fe0d34-9186-5ce3-a620-e058269f2c9a'}, {'abstract': 'Borrowers in need of cash can turn to short-term, high-interest loans. But these loans can become a long-term debt burden, consumer officials say.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/short-term-payday-loans-can-become-long-term-traps/', 'snippet': 'Borrowers in need of cash can turn to short-term, high-interest loans. But these loans can become a long-term debt burden, consumer officials say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Payday loans and deposit-advance loans are intended to be short-term options for emergency cash, but they can turn into long-term debt traps for borrowers, a new federal report says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Short-Term Payday Loans Can Become Long-Term Traps', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payday Loans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller of the Currency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T18:44:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d18be391-079c-5375-b643-fcf33ac14185', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d18be391-079c-5375-b643-fcf33ac14185'}, {'abstract': 'Any comparison may be fighting words, but with his guitar, harmonica and distinctive voice, 19-year-old Jake Bugg evokes the young Dylan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/booming/if-you-like-bob-dylan-try-jake-bugg.html', 'snippet': 'Any comparison may be fighting words, but with his guitar, harmonica and distinctive voice, 19-year-old Jake Bugg evokes the young Dylan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, Val Haller, a music-obsessed baby boomer and the founder of the Web site Valslist.com, matches tracks from her generation to those of her 20-something sons’ generation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/booming/24match-booming-dylan-bugg/24match-booming-dylan-bugg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/24/booming/24match-booming-dylan-bugg/24match-booming-dylan-bugg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/booming/24match-booming-dylan-bugg/24match-booming-dylan-bugg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/booming/24match-booming-dylan-bugg/24match-booming-dylan-bugg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/24/booming/24match-booming-dylan-bugg/24match-booming-dylan-bugg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/24/booming/24match-booming-dylan-bugg/24match-booming-dylan-bugg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75