 chief executive of Ovid Capital Advisors LLC. He has worked with many large international banks on regulatory capital transactions involving real risk transfer over the last decade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Defense of Regulatory Capital Trades', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Basel Committee on Banking Supervision', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T18:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Blasius', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blasius', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98a20827-aec5-5a83-b4bd-5e45082f61e6', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98a20827-aec5-5a83-b4bd-5e45082f61e6'}, {'abstract': 'Maryland Gov. Martin O’Malley said Wednesday that he would spend the second half of this year mulling whether to run for president in 2016. He seems already to have a campaign theme: jobs and innovation.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/in-israel-omalley-talks-jobs-foreign-policy-and-of-course-2016/', 'snippet': 'Maryland Gov. Martin O’Malley said Wednesday that he would spend the second half of this year mulling whether to run for president in 2016. He seems already to have a campaign theme: jobs and innovation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM – Gov. Martin O’Malley of Maryland said Wednesday that he would spend the second half of this year mulling whether to run for president in 2016. He seems already to have a campaign theme: jobs and innovation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Israel, O’Malley Talks Jobs, Foreign Policy and, of Course, 2016', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Malley, Martin J", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T18:54:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aebdf7e-240f-520a-96a9-61e65bc61424', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aebdf7e-240f-520a-96a9-61e65bc61424'}, {'abstract': 'The director Paul Verhoeven discusses his crowd-sourced film project “Tricked.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/tribeca-video-paul-verhoeven-discusses-tricked/', 'snippet': 'The director Paul Verhoeven discusses his crowd-sourced film project “Tricked.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With his latest film project “Tricked,” Paul Verhoeven worked with a list of screenwriters that rivaled the length of the script itself. In this video interview at the Tribeca Film Festival, the Dutch director, best known in America for Hollywood hits like “Robocop” and “Basic Instinct,” discusses how he and his team assembled the crowd-sourced work of multiple writers to create the screenplay for “Tricked.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '