d on the company’s plans.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/samsung-knox-delayed-july/', 'snippet': 'Samsung Electronics has delayed the release of Knox, a version of Android with security features to make its phones more suitable for businesses, until summer, according to two people briefed on the company’s plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February, Samsung Electronics introduced Knox, a version of Android with security features to make the company’s phones more suitable for businesses, expected for release this spring. But the company has delayed the release of the software until summer, according to two people briefed on the company’s plans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samsung Delays Release of Security Software for Galaxy Phones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Electronics Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T20:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/043cb9a7-9a4f-5ca0-b728-8bc5e706c84e', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/043cb9a7-9a4f-5ca0-b728-8bc5e706c84e'}, {'abstract': 'The inaugural Ballymaloe Literary Festival of Food and Wine celebrates the art of food writing.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/irelands-new-international-food-festival/', 'snippet': 'The inaugural Ballymaloe Literary Festival of Food and Wine celebrates the art of food writing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between them, the collected works of the presenters at the inaugural Ballymaloe Literary Festival of Food and Wine, taking place from May 3 to May 6, would constitute the beginnings of a library, or at least a very impressive cookbook collection. Darina Allen, arguably Ireland’s most famous cook and visible advocate of its food culture, has lured many of the world’s most revered and prolific food writers to attend the three-day event outside the Irish city of Cork. This is an international food festival with a difference. Far from being staged in the usual hotel ballroom or university lecture hall, it will take place among the bucolic surrounds of Ballymaloe, the family estate made famous first by Myrtle Allen’s seminal country house restaurant, and then by her daughter-in-law Darina’s cooking school and picturesque organic farm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ireland’s New International Food Festival', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T20:45:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Prior', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prior', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a19e8847-90ce-5d3a-b7b3-6d1c4deafdcd', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a19e8847-90ce-5d3a-b7b3-6d1c4deafdcd'}, {'abstract': 'A new study from the Kaiser Family Foundation helps sort out how much of the recent moderation in health care costs is related to causes other than the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/the-bad-economy-behind-the-health-care-slowdown/', 'snippet': 'A new study from the Kaiser Family Foundation helps sort out how much of the recent moderation in health care costs is related to causes other than the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In today’s paper, I took a look at a major innovation in health care delivery, one that Obama administration officials think might play a big role in holding down health costs in the future. It is called accountable care, and the general idea is to enlist doctors and nurses in the fight to control spending. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bad Economy Behind the Health Care Slowdown', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Advocate Health Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Cross and Blue Shield of Illinois', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser Family Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T20:46:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/160a64a0-a630-5b02-a095-41b1de0