the baritone Nathan Gunn have done things differently had he known that the concert he presented on Monday night at Zankel Hall would take place during the early blush of spring rather than the waning weeks of winter? The program, planned for February and delayed by illness, found him joined by the pianist Julie Gunn, his wife, and the Pacifica Quartet for a darkish mix of songs with English texts.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Songs Pierced With Rays of Cheer', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dark Songs Pierced With Rays of Cheer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacifica Quartet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gunn, Nathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T21:51:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f71ea03b-f20d-5b16-bcb1-dc2810fa7b2d', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f71ea03b-f20d-5b16-bcb1-dc2810fa7b2d'}, {'abstract': 'As President Obama prepares to help dedicate the George W. Bush Presidential Library and Museum on Thursday, he embarks on an awkward ritual.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/us/politics/obamas-delicate-task-at-bush-library-dedication.html', 'snippet': 'As President Obama prepares to help dedicate the George W. Bush Presidential Library and Museum on Thursday, he embarks on an awkward ritual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — President Obama has left little mystery about how he views his pr