ype_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6409dc2d-19ed-53ac-867a-39f70c340451', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6409dc2d-19ed-53ac-867a-39f70c340451'}, {'abstract': 'The alto saxophonist and composer Steve Coleman, working with his band Five Elements, began a weeklong residency at the Stone on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/arts/music/steve-coleman-and-five-elements-at-the-stone.html', 'snippet': 'The alto saxophonist and composer Steve Coleman, working with his band Five Elements, began a weeklong residency at the Stone on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The alto saxophonist and composer Steve Coleman puts his trust in systems, though he’s too rigorous to let any premise go untested. During his first set at the Stone in the East Village on Tuesday night, he kept setting up patterns and disrupting them, in variable cycles. Working as usual with Five Elements, his flagship band, he created the feeling of a meticulously honed aesthetic subjected to unrelenting pressure.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/coleman/coleman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/coleman/coleman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/coleman/coleman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/coleman/coleman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/coleman/coleman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/coleman/coleman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/coleman/coleman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All Systems Are Go, and Tested', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Systems Are Go, And Tested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleman, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T22:10:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5b0a7cf-8523-5339-a66a-afd229e79ac3', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5b0a7cf-8523-5339-a66a-afd229e79ac3'}, {'abstract': 'The New England Collection reproduces classic American hooked rugs in modern sizes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/garden/scaling-up-a-classic-american-style.html', 'snippet': 'The New England Collection reproduces classic American hooked rugs in modern sizes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People looking for vintage hooked rugs can’t always find what they want in the size they need. “Our customers were always asking for something larger,” said Ramin Hakimi, a partner with Kevin Rahmanan in Rahmanan Antique & Decorative Rugs, a dealer in antique and vintage carpets. To meet the demand, the men started an offshoot company, the New England Collection, reproducing, in modern sizes, designs taken from their inventory of classic American hooked rugs. The range now also includes rag rugs, needlepoints and flat-woven styles, including dhurries, Aubussons, and Persian-style kilims. The monochromatic design shown here was adapted from a 19th-century New England model, with tweaks to the palette and pattern. It was woven in cotton on different-size hooks to create a variation in depth. The 6-by-9-foot carpet is $3,942. Information: (212) 683-0167 or necrugs.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25RUGS/25CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1004, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25RUGS/25CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1004}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25RUGS/25CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 613, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25RUGS/25CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2046, 'width': 1223, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25RUGS/25CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25RUGS/25CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'c