materials originally intended for telescopes and lab equipment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/garden/a-table-that-is-pure-but-not-simple.html', 'snippet': 'The Frazier side table is made of materials originally intended for telescopes and lab equipment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Frazier side table, by the architecture and furniture design firm Khouri Guzman Bunce Ltd., looks old, that may be because its materials are borrowed from other industries. The top is borosilicate glass intended for telescope lenses and lab equipment. (The glass is available with a mirrored finish, which makes the subtle, character-building imperfections stand out even more.) The base is silicon bronze, with a 95 percent copper content, the most durable of all bronzes, and one that is used primarily for sculpture casting. (The base is also available in brass, blackened steel and nickel.) Rather than welded, these two pieces are screwed together, which produces a visually light effect and reveals that the frame is solid metal, rather than plated. “You can go anywhere and find a plated table,” said David Khouri, a partner in the firm. “I want people to think about how this one’s made.” A standard-size table is 22.5 inches high and 19.5 inches wide. Prices start at $7,250: (212) 420-7866 or kgb-limited.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25FURNITURE/25CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25FURNITURE/25CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 563}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25FURNITURE/25CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25FURNITURE/25CURR4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1057, 'width': 1126, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25FURNITURE/25CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25FURNITURE/25CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25FURNITURE/25CURR4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Table That Is Pure but Not Simple', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Table That Is Pure But Not Simple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tables', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Khouri Guzman Bunce Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T22:11:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Milioti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Milioti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d49e0969-53c9-5312-876b-5237563f139e', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d49e0969-53c9-5312-876b-5237563f139e'}, {'abstract': 'A store benefiting the Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center will also serve as a pop-up boutique.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/garden/brightening-up-a-cancer-centers-thrift-store.html', 'snippet': 'A store benefiting the Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center will also serve as a pop-up boutique.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February, the Society of Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center asked the textile and carpet designer Madeline Weinrib to transform its charity thrift shop on the Upper East Side into an occasional pop-up boutique for designer sample sales. “With all the consignment shops around, and people selling their furniture on eBay, it has taken a lot of business away from the charity thrift shops,” said Ms. Weinrib, who is based in Manhattan. From May 3 to 5, she will fill the 2,500-square-foot space at 1440 Third Avenue with pillows, rugs, rolls of fabric to be sold by the yard, clothing, handbags, totes, napkins and furniture. Products will be sold at 40 to 70 percent off retail. Eighteen-inch-square pillows, shown above and below, originally $350 to $575, will be $179 to $299. Home delivery is not available, but even rugs and furniture pieces will be small enough to carry. The sale will take place from 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. Information: (212) 535-1250.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25EVENTS_SPAN/25CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25EVENTS_SPAN/25CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/garden/25EVENTS_SPAN/25CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/g