 to the Big Easy, their car was stolen, with all their instruments inside. Most everything was later recovered, and so the city — coupled with the fact that they were able to borrow instruments from supportive locals to continue their tour — left a big impression on the young artist. “It’s almost like these things happened in my life that changed my course, but put me back to where I needed to be,” says Winslow-King, who then quickly moved to the Crescent City, where he started busking on Frenchmen Street while studying music at the University of New Orleans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Listening | Luke Winslow-King', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T22:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Slenske', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slenske', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b7fe637-138f-578d-b815-e600f5d2af93', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b7fe637-138f-578d-b815-e600f5d2af93'}, {'abstract': 'Osamu Nagafuchi has warned for years that a die-off among pine trees on Yakushima island is caused by pollution from China. Now he is being taken more seriously.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/world/asia/japanese-scientist-blames-china-for-yakushimas-dying-trees.html', 'snippet': 'Osamu Nagafuchi has warned for years that a die-off among pine trees on Yakushima island is caused by pollution from China. Now he is being taken more seriously.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YAKUSHIMA, Japan — A mysterious pestilence has befallen this island’s primeval forests, leaving behind the bleached, skeletal remains of dead trees that now dot the dark green mountainsides. Osamu Nagafuchi, an environmental engineer with a passion for the island and its rugged terrain, believes he knows the culprit: airborne pollutants from smog-belching China, hundreds of miles upwind. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/asia/25yakushima/25yakushima-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/world/asia/25yakushima/25yakushima-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/asia/25yakushima/25yakushima-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/asia/25yakushima/25yakushima-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/asia/25yakushima/25yakushima-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/25/world/asia/25yakushima/25yakushima-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/asia/25yakushima/25yakushima-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scientist Says Pollution From China Is Killing a Japanese Island’s Trees', 'kicker': 'Yakushima Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scientist Says Pollution From China Is Killing a Japanese Island’s Trees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nagafuchi, Osamu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yakushima (Japan)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-24T22:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d45f5675-baa0-526d-afa7-ad009e01b68d', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d45f5675-baa0-526d-afa7-ad009e01b68d'}, {'abstract': 'Shaking off an ankle that was swollen after he was hit by a comebacker Tuesday night, Jon Niese said he’d be ready to face the Phillies.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/niese-likely-to-start-on-sunday/', 'snippet': 'Shaking off an ankle that was swollen after he was hit by a comebacker Tuesday night, Jon Niese said he’d be ready to face the Phillies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day after he was knocked out of a game when he took a comebacker to his right ankle, Jon Niese said he expected to make his next scheduled start, Sunday against the Philadelphia Phillies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'so