rnia will lead a $9 million effort financed by the National Institute of Mental Health to identify promising drugs for autism and conduct early tests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/business/public-private-effort-seeks-to-expedite-discovery-of-autism-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'The University of California will lead a $9 million effort financed by the National Institute of Mental Health to identify promising drugs for autism and conduct early tests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the diagnosis of autism on the rise and drug companies facing major setbacks in developing successful treatments, the University of California, Los Angeles will lead a $9 million effort financed by the National Institute of Mental Health to find effective drugs, officials said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Drug/Drug-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Drug/Drug-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Drug/Drug-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Drug/Drug-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joint Effort Seeks Drugs for Autism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joint Effort Seeks Drugs For Autism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Katie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute of Mental Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCracken, James', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:12:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e060c8ac-711b-5cc9-898f-7c2217c8adc1', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e060c8ac-711b-5cc9-898f-7c2217c8adc1'}, {'abstract': 'On a visit to New York and Washington, Joe Oliver has a few things to say to opponents of the Keystone XL oil pipeline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/opinion/nocera-canadas-oil-minister-unmuzzled.html', 'snippet': 'On a visit to New York and Washington, Joe Oliver has a few things to say to opponents of the Keystone XL oil pipeline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time your friendly scribe sought an interview with Joe Oliver, Canada’s minister of natural resources, he was turned down flat. It was February last year. Oliver had made a series of impolitic remarks about the efforts to block the Keystone XL oil pipeline, which, if it’s ever built, would import oil from the tar sands of Alberta to refineries along the Gulf Coast — and which Canadians believe that the United States would be nuts to reject.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s Oil Minister, Unmuzzled', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada’s Oil Minister, Unmuzzled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oliver, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harper, Stephen J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/494cedd9-01fa-5128-8311-8878622518cd', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/494cedd9-01fa-5128-8311-8878622518cd'}, {'abstract': 'Forcing publicly traded corporations to disclose their political donations to their shareholders would be an enormous step toward addressing political corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/opinion/corporate-donations-and-the-securities-and-exchange-commission.html', 'snippet': 'Forcing publicly traded corporations to disclose their political donations to their shareholders would be an enormous step toward addressing political corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court’s Citizens United decision that triggered an avalanche of corporate political spending also contained a proposal for greater public disclosure from corporations that would prefer to write their checks in the shadows. Transparency, the court advised, would let voters decide for themselves “whether elected officials are ‘in the pocket’ of so-called moneyed interests.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Donations and the S.E.C.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corporate Donations and the S.E.C. ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Mary Jo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:16:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccaaf809-f3b2-5248-9630-087d0fc8ce9e', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccaaf809-f3b2-5248-9630-087d0fc8ce9e'}, {'abstract': 'An overhauling by Congress would require that search warrants be obtained for all personal e-mails and other electronic content held by a third-party service provider.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/technology/updating-an-e-mail-law-from-the-last-century.html', 'snippet': 'An overhauling by Congress would require that search warrants be obtained for all personal e-mails and other electronic content held by a third-party service provider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Warshak, a Cincinnati businessman who built an empire selling male sexual enhancement drugs, was convicted of wire fraud several years ago, based in large part on his e-mail correspondence, which authorities had extracted via a subpoena under a 1986 law governing electronic privacy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Email/Email-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Email/Email-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Email/Email-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/business/Email/Email-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Updating an E-Mail Law From the Last Century', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Updating an E-Mail Law From the Last Century', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Communications Privacy Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0976707a-32d6-507a-926a-bfdc5fb6c616', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0976707a-32d6-507a-926a-bfdc5fb6c616'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration must carefully investigate the charges before deciding how to respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/opinion/were-chemical-weapons-used-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration must carefully investigate the charges before deciding how to respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not hard to imagine that President Bashar al-Assad, desperately clinging to power, might use chemical weapons against the Syrian people. He has already pummeled them with warplanes and missiles and shows no signs of ending a bloody onslaught that has lasted more than two years. But while he may be capable of using weapons of mass destruction, there is no proof that he has done so.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Were Chemical Weapons Used in Syria?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Were Chemical Weapons Used In Syria?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f05baa0-f29e-5731-9dd5-6eb1ea3d0b13', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f05baa0-f29e-5731-9dd5-6eb1ea3d0b13'}, {'abstract': 'Though the European Union fumbled the euro crisis, the agreement it brokered between Serbia and Kosovo shows the good work it can do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/opinion/moving-past-the-last-balkan-war.html', 'snippet': 'Though the European Union fumbled the euro crisis, the agreement it brokered between Serbia and Kosovo shows the good work it can do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a time of disillusionment about the state of the European Union, a diplomatic deal between Serbia and Kosovo highlights some of the more positive features of the institution that won last year’s Nobel Peace Prize but fumbled the euro crisis. The tentative agreement signed last Friday not only shows that the European Union can perform well but also that it remains an attractive destination for countries that aspire to membership.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moving Past the Last Balkan War', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moving Past the Last Balkan War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashton, Catherine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/74e751bc-520e-55bc-a823-4f44d412cad5', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74e751bc-520e-55bc-a823-4f44d412cad5'}, {'abstract': 'John Idzik, the new general manager, has a defined sense of what he wants in a player he is about to draft, and he has plenty of openings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/sports/football/john-idzik-jets-new-general-manager-known-for-steady-approach.html', 'snippet': 'John Idzik, the new general manager, has a defined sense of what he wants in a player he is about to draft, and he has plenty of openings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Idzik worked in the Tampa Bay front office in 1997 when the Buccaneers set out in the draft to improve the N.F.L.’s lowest-scoring offense. They focused on a certain running back, and after ascertaining that another team was also in pursuit, they maneuvered to select him with the 12th pick.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/sports/jpJETS/jpJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/sports/jpJETS/jpJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 737}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/sports/jpJETS/jpJETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 834, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/sports/jpJETS/jpJETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1946, 'width': 1584, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/sports/jpJETS/jpJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/25/sports/jpJETS/jpJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/sports/jpJETS/jpJETS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets’ Remodeler Refined His Style Over the Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets’ Remodeler Refined His Style Over the Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Idzik, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b3ba12a-b764-5b95-b558-72132b5276a4', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b3ba12a-b764-5b95-b558-72132b5276a4'}, {'abstract': 'The secretary of homeland security explained how immigration reform would strengthen security at the borders and expand enforcement of the laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/opinion/on-beyond-fear-of-immigration-reform.html', 'snippet': 'The secretary of homeland security explained how immigration reform would strengthen security at the borders and expand enforcement of the laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The homeland security secretary, Janet Napolitano, testified on Tuesday before the Senate Judiciary Committee about the Senate’s bipartisan immigration bill. For hours, in a calm and methodical manner, she flipped each confrontational line of questioning on its head. No, the bill would not loosen security at borders and ports. It would tighten it. The bill would not weaken immigration enforcement, but strengthen it — adding resources and improving the government’s ability to keep unwanted people out and to catch fugitives, identify thieves and terrorists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Beyond Fear', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Beyond Fear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napolitano, Janet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '