nt. As is often the case in the broiling Muslim insurgency here in the North Caucasus, his complaints were intensely local: a police commander had announced a policy of harassing and threatening family members of suspected militants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Attack Spotlights Struggle Half a World Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boston Attack Spotlights Caucasus Strife', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dagestan (Russia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Tamerlan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T01:57:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn and Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f99feef-e401-518b-a5cc-99b8776b2715', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f99feef-e401-518b-a5cc-99b8776b2715'}, {'abstract': 'Jeffrey Wechsler tips his top hat to us.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/24/crazy-talk/', 'snippet': 'Jeffrey Wechsler tips his top hat to us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — This is the type of puzzle where the reveal hits you in two parts: first, you might have filled in enough of the four theme answers — a diverse list of items, to say the least — and noticed the payoff at 50 Across to note that certain letters in the theme answer make up a “magician’s phrase.”', 'source': 'The New York Ti