enforcement agents against Homeland Security Secretary Janet Napolitano. Judge Reed O’Connor rejected most of the administration’s arguments and found that the agents were “likely to succeed” in the case. He delayed a final ruling, asking both sides to submit more information by May 6. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Skepticism on Immigration Law', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Skepticism On Immigration Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T02:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/81a5e1b5-0a93-56a4-9ab9-a01363ced5c8', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81a5e1b5-0a93-56a4-9ab9-a01363ced5c8'}, {'abstract': 'At a fund-raiser in Dallas, the president renewed his commitment to bipartisanship despite the divisions in Washington and “even if some of you think I’m a sap.”', 'web_url': 'https: