bject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cisco Systems Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Hat Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TIBCO Software Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'English Channel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Isle of Wight', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T04:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18c6ded3-8201-5f3f-a9db-d6f86fed4602', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18c6ded3-8201-5f3f-a9db-d6f86fed4602'}, {'abstract': 'South Korea gave North Korea until Friday to respond to its proposal for dialogue on a joint industrial park or face a “grave measure” on the future of the factory complex.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/world/asia/south-korea-ultimatum-on-talks.html', 'snippet': 'South Korea gave North Korea until Friday to respond to its proposal for dialogue on a joint industrial park or face a “grave measure” on the future of the factory complex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'South Korea gave North Korea until Friday to respond to its proposal for dialogue on a joint industrial park or face a “grave measure” on the future of the factory complex, which has been the only remaining symbol of economic cooperation between the two Koreas. A statement from the South’s Unification Ministry stopped short of clarifying whether the decision it was contemplating involved pulling out 176 South Korean managers remaining in the Kaesong factory park in North Korea or even terminating the joint economic project. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea: Ultimatum on Talks', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: Ultimatum on Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kaesong (North Korea)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T04:40:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/111cdf18-ed84-58a6-935b-744135dfa226', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/111cdf18-ed84-58a6-935b-744135dfa226'}, {'abstract': 'The threats came after days of relative quiet, which followed weeks of warnings that dire consequences would ensue if the United States and South Korea provoked the North.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/world/asia/south-korea-warns-north-of-grave-measure-in-factory-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'The threats came after days of relative quiet, which followed weeks of warnings that dire consequences would ensue if the United States and South Korea provoked the North.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — On an anniversary known for military showmanship, North Korean generals on Thursday declared that their forces were ready to launch intercontinental ballistic missiles and kamikazelike nuclear attacks at the United States if threatened.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Issues Threat at Ceremony for Military', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Issues Threat At Ceremony For Military', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T04:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13326e21-29de-5d9c-9169-6cc91233694c', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13326e21-29de-5d9c-9169-6cc91233694c'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Fox Movie Channel) BLACK SWAN (2010) Natalie Portman, above, in the role that earned her an Academy Award, stars as Nina, a ballet dancer teetering on the verge of insanity as she tries to break out of the corps and into the dual lead of “Swan Lake”: the Swan Queen and her villainous black swan twin. Mila Kunis is Lily, the sultry newcomer who is everything the increasingly tormented Nina is not, as their company’s artistic director, Thomas (Vincent Cassel), points out. The result is “a witchy brew of madness and cunning,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about this film, directed by Darren Aronofsky, which also received Oscar nominations for best director, best picture and others.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T05:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cfb3f15-89b9-5d43-92f2-9d863ffd571a', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cfb3f15-89b9-5d43-92f2-9d863ffd571a'}, {'abstract': 'In Thailand, Chinese opera troupes are a study in contrasts, presenting flamboyant shows but made up of people who are often poor and living on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/world/asia/in-thailand-a-not-so-glamorous-life-on-stage.html', 'snippet': 'In Thailand, Chinese opera troupes are a study in contrasts, presenting flamboyant shows but made up of people who are often poor and living on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Sleep like dogs, eat like pigs, dress like angels.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non