', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson and John E. Parsons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Parsons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1141aee2-dc37-5eef-969e-2a9fc34c6c43', 'word_count': 1708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1141aee2-dc37-5eef-969e-2a9fc34c6c43'}, {'abstract': 'James Hill recalls recently photographing Sochi, Russia, the site of the 2014 Winter Olympics, which will be the first held in a subtropical zone.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/dreaming-of-a-white-winter-olympics/', 'snippet': 'James Hill recalls recently photographing Sochi, Russia, the site of the 2014 Winter Olympics, which will be the first held in a subtropical zone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few hours before President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia spoke at a ceremony in the Bolshoy Ice Dome in Sochi in February, marking a year to the start of the 2014 Winter Olympics, I was watching pensioners strip to the waist and bask in the midday sunshine on a beach a few miles from the Olympic Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caught Cold When Sochi Freezes Over', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sochi (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T09:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Hill'