/2013/04/25/ranking-top-5-wide-receivers-in-n-f-l-draft/', 'snippet': 'Cordarelle Patterson of Tennessee, with jaw-dropping open-field talent, gets the nod as the top receiver in the draft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt Waldman is the author of The Rookie Scouting Portfolio, a testament to his obsession with film analysis, now available for download. Examples of his work can be found at his blog. He is helping The Fifth Down rank skill position players before the draft:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ranking Top 5 Wide Receivers in N.F.L. Draft', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T09:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Waldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af6d693a-82c1-586a-b3fa-1e28d62f2993', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af6d693a-82c1-586a-b3fa-1e28d62f2993'}, {'abstract': 'In the United States, pillarless hartops have more or less gone the way of the Dodo. Cars are safer, but the style’s demise is a shame.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/why-we-should-miss-pillarless-rooflines/', 'snippet': 'In the United States, pillarless hartops have more or less gone the way of the Dodo. Cars are safer, but the style’s demise is a shame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once upon a time, automotive roof pillars were elegantly skinny. They’ve since bulked up in the interest of safety, but what have we lost in the process?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why We Should Miss Pillarless Rooflines', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cadillac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Insurance Institute for Highway Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T10:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f07314e1-71e4-57a1-83a9-5d5aa4473bcf', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f07314e1-71e4-57a1-83a9-5d5aa4473bcf'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/the-early-word-awkward/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Awkward', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T10:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a80689a-c924-5c86-b449-2df1020a6ce1', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a80689a-c924-5c86-b449-2df1020a6ce1'}, {'abstract': 'The battle to raise awareness has been won. So why aren’t more lives being saved?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/magazine/our-feel-good-war-on-breast-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'The battle to raise awareness has been won. So why aren’t more lives being saved?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I used to believe that a mammogram saved my life. I even wrote that in the pages of this magazine. It was 1996, and I had just turned 35 when my doctor sent me for an initial screening — a relatively common practice at the time — that would serve as a base line when I began annual mammograms at 40. I had no family history of breast cancer, no particular risk factors for the disease.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/magazine/28breastcancerHP/28breastcancerHP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 337, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/magazine/28breastcancerHP/28breastcancerHP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 337, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/magazine/28breastcancerHP/28breastcancerHP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/28/magazine/28breastcancerHP/28breastcancerHP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/magazine/28breastcancerHP/28breastcancerHP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Feel-Good War on Breast Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Problem With Pink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orenstein, Peggy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mammography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Komen, Susan G, for the Cure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T10:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peggy Orenstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peggy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9faf2e1-c275-55b7-87f3-ec6378fd6d77', 'word_count': 6503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9faf2e1-c275-55b7-87f3-ec6378fd6d77'}, {'abstract': 'The example you set may be more important than you realize.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/yes-you-treat-customers-well-but-how-do-you-treat-employees/', 'snippet': 'The example you set may be more important than you realize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been involved in owning and coaching businesses for about 35 years. I have gone from being one of the worst employers I have ever seen to being one that is at least pretty good. The biggest lesson I learned was that if I ever wanted my employees to treat my customers well, I had better treat my employees well. It took me 10 years to learn this lesson, but once I did, our customer service went from O.K. with lots of effort to great with minimal effort.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, You Treat Customers Well. But How Do You Treat Employees?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Patrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75800ef5-3c6c-5863-981a-f8a286027097', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75800ef5-3c6c-5863-981a-f8a286027097'}, {'abstract': 'Yahoo announced that it had acquired the exclusive rights to classic clips of “Saturday Night Live” from 1975 through 2012, Brian Stelter reports in The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/daily-report-yahoo-buys-rights-to-saturday-night-live-archive/', 'snippet': 'Yahoo announced that it had acquired the exclusive rights to classic clips of “Saturday Night Live” from 1975 through 2012, Brian Stelter reports in The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yahoo announced Wednesday that it acquired the exclusive rights to classic clips of “Saturday Night Live” from 1975 through 2012, effective in September. The clips will be removed from Hulu and NBC.com, where they currently reside, and be shown instead on Yahoo, which wants to share in the buzz the show creates, Brian Stelter reports Thursday in The New York Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None,