r’s still-radioactive support of extremism.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tea Party Caucus: It’s Baaack!', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Return of the Tea Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Tea Party Caucus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T12:35:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/229266cc-542d-5867-8b57-66acdb7f2224', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/229266cc-542d-5867-8b57-66acdb7f2224'}, {'abstract': 'Allison Moore’s comedy “Collapse” is built around a couple dealing with infertility and other serious issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/theater/reviews/collapse-at-city-center.html', 'snippet': 'Allison Moore’s comedy “Collapse” is built around a couple dealing with infertility and other serious issues.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Collapse” is quite a bold title for a play that proves so trite. Built on unbelievable situations and uninspired jokes, the script holds enough humor to sustain a sitcom. But as this comedy stretches toward an hour and a half, the only thing that the title invites is an easy attempt to sum up the show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 