s of his song “Sweet Caroline” to a fund for victims of the Boston Marathon bombing. He made the announcement on Twitter on Wednesday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neil Diamond to Donate ‘Sweet Caroline’ Royalties to Boston Bombing Charity', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diamond, Neil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T15:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04384e4b-3c26-53b0-bf6f-4bacf6254c4f', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04384e4b-3c26-53b0-bf6f-4bacf6254c4f'}, {'abstract': 'A $2 iPhone app called FocusTwist uses some software processing tricks to refocus a photo after it’s taken, similar to what the Lytro camera can do. But using it to best effect requires a tripod for your phone.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/a-2-app-that-refocuses-photos-like-a-400-lytro/', 'snippet': 'A $2 iPhone app called FocusTwist uses some software processing tricks to refocus a photo after it’s taken, similar to what the Lytro camera can do. But using it to best effect requires a tripod for your phone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographers have been wowed by the Lytro, a camera that can refocus a shot after you take it. But the Lytro costs $400 to $500, and that’s a lot to spend for a feature that is a bit of a novelty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headl