ge W. Bush Presidential Library coincides with a recent uptick in the public’s view of the 43rd president’s performance, which in turn has inspired a lot of discussion about whether Bush’s reputation could enjoy, or deserves to enjoy,\xa0a Harry Truman-style rehabilitation with historians and the public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George W. Bush in Hindsight', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Truman, Harry S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bush, George W, Presidential Library and Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T16:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2033454f-f77b-542a-a951-d4441ac1aa4f', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2033454f-f77b-542a-a951-d4441ac1aa4f'}, {'abstract': 'A species that doesn’t play well with others.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/lionfish-on-the-menu/', 'snippet': 'A species that doesn’t play well with others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Bruni, our colleague and former food critic, wrote the other day about making meals out of animals that are considered “the bullies of the