ract': 'Barbara Bush said she does not want Jeb Bush, the former governor of Florida, to run for president in 2016, even though he is “by far the best-qualified man.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/barbara-bush-on-son-jeb-in-2016-weve-had-enough-bushes/', 'snippet': 'Barbara Bush said she does not want Jeb Bush, the former governor of Florida, to run for president in 2016, even though he is “by far the best-qualified man.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'After having a husband and a son in the White House, Barbara Bush said she did not miss “one darn thing” about life there. And she does not want another reason to go back, even if it means depriving the country of the “best-qualified man.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barbara Bush on Son Jeb in 2016: ‘We’ve Had Enough Bushes’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Barbara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T16:37:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/506a05fa-d267-5e6c-8858-701ef9304ca7', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/506a05fa-d267-5e6c-8858-701ef9304ca7'}, {'abstract': 'Janet Yellen of the Federal Reserve, like many central bankers, knows her way around a metaphor to make a monetary point.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/the-gorilla-and-the-maginot-line/', 'snippet': 'Janet Yellen of the Federal Reserve, like many central bankers, knows her way around a metaphor to make a monetary point.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Janet Yellen likes metaphors. This is a common trait among central bankers, at least the ones who see value in trying to explain their work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gorilla and the Maginot Line', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Open Market Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T16:41:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8266c188-af37-51ef-aa6c-a3c8c509839c', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8266c188-af37-51ef-aa6c-a3c8c509839c'}, {'abstract': 'As delivered by the Secretary of Defense in Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates, on April 25, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/us/chuck-hagels-statement-on-syria.html', 'snippet': 'As delivered by the Secretary of Defense in Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates, on April 25, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As delivered by Secretary of Defense Chuck Hagel in Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates, on Thursday, April 25, 2013.', 'so