'uri': 'nyt://interactive/41467821-ccc2-5ec5-922c-81fbb736b75c'}, {'abstract': 'Imelda Marcos, the controversial former first lady of the Philippines and subject of David Byrne’s current musical marvel “Here Lies Love,” inspires a regal roundup of today’s ornate heels.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/market-sweep-if-the-shoe-fits/', 'snippet': 'Imelda Marcos, the controversial former first lady of the Philippines and subject of David Byrne’s current musical marvel “Here Lies Love,” inspires a regal roundup of today’s ornate heels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Byrne’s musical marvel “Here Lies Love,” now extended through June 2 at New York’s Public Theater, celebrates the splendor of Imelda Marcos, the controversial former first lady of the Philippines who was famous for her lavish collection of extravagant footwear. The once-exiled lady of leisure’s theatrical triumph inspires a regal roundup of today’s ornate heels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Sweep | If the Shoe Fits', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Ladies (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcos, Imelda R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T17:18:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68051b07-efd6-5275-af50-20660b16adac', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68051b07-efd6-5275-af50-20660b16adac'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg announced the initiative, which he said he hoped more restaurants would join.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/100-restaurants-pledge-to-halve-food-waste-sent-to-landfills/', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg announced the initiative, which he said he hoped more restaurants would join.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The next time you bite into that pork bun at Momofuku or burrito at Chipotle, you can tell yourself that you are doing something for the environment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurants Vow to Stop Tossing Out So Much Food', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restaurants to Stop Tossing Out So Much Food', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compost', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T17:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15a797dd-350f-5bb6-80f9-324a36e96834', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15a797dd-350f-5bb6-80f9-324a36e96834'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki warned on Thursday that the growing sectarian conflict in Iraq could lead to a civil war like the one raging in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/world/middleeast/iraqi-premier-urges-calm-but-vows-to-continue-military-strikes.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki warned on Thursday that the growing sectarian conflict in Iraq could lead to a civil war like the one raging in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — In the face of an armed rebellion by disgruntled Sunni Muslims against his Shiite-led government, Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki on Thursday urged dialogue to calm tensions but vowed to continue military operations in a growing sectarian conflict that he warned could lead to a civil war like the one raging in Syria.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/world/iraq/iraq-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/world/iraq/iraq-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/world/iraq/iraq-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/world/iraq/iraq-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/world/iraq/iraq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/world/iraq/iraq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/world/iraq/iraq-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'