4-25T19:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07041b7f-1a7b-5abe-8ea4-7e3b5bedfcd0', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07041b7f-1a7b-5abe-8ea4-7e3b5bedfcd0'}, {'abstract': 'Teams do have skill in picking players in the N.F.L. Draft, but chance also plays a strong role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/04/25/sports/football/picking-the-best-in-the-nfl-draft.html', 'snippet': 'Teams do have skill in picking players in the N.F.L. Draft, but chance also plays a strong role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teams do have skill in picking players in the N.F.L. Draft, but chance also plays a strong role.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Draft: How Good Are Teams at Picking the Best?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T19:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/78d585e7-d5ae-594c-8688-d15de99bce0c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/78d585e7-d5ae-594c-8688-d15de99bce0c'}, {'abstract': 'A Seoul native opens up her little black book to share her favorite things and places in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/hometown-advantage-jung-baes-seoul/', 'snippet': 'A Seoul native opens up her little black book to share her favorite things and places in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There’s so much more than PSY, bibimbap and Gangnam,” says Jung Bae, 40, of Seoul, her hometown that was recently featured in T’s travel issue. It’s understandable why Bae, an artist and self-professed “cultural mediator,” has grown weary of the global spotlight on one singer, one bowl of food, and one neighborhood. And as someone who’s juggled multiple creative professions — writer (the author of two books: “The Devil Wears Cheap Prada” in 2007 and “Shopping and the City” in 2006), the former editor in chief of Nylon Korea, the current creative director of Absolut Vodka Korea and Kiehl’s Korea, and the current publisher of the art tabloid Hello, Garosu-gil (translation: tree-lined street) — Bae doesn’t mind the mainstream. But what she really loves is seeking out neighborhoods and establishments that lie at popularity’s tipping point. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hometown Advantage | Jung Bae’s Seoul', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seoul (South Korea)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T19:18:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3475f481-f1fe-5a74-9aac-7f05eee91ab3', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3475f481-f1fe-5a74-9aac-7f05eee91ab3'}, {'abstract': 'MTV said it was working with Dimension Films to produce an hour-long pilot based on the “Scream” horror franchise, for a series that would make its debut in the summer of 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/mtv-orders-tv-pilot-based-on-scream-horror-series/', 'snippet': 'MTV said it was working with Dimension Films to produce an hour-long pilot based on the “Scream” horror franchise, for a series that would make its debut in the summer of 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you like scary movies? And do you also like scary TV shows adapted from scary movies that cleverly deconstruct the entire scary-movie genre?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/scream/scream-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/scream/scream-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/scream/scream-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/scream/scream-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/scream/scream-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/25/arts/scream/scream-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'MTV Orders TV Pilot Based on ‘Scream’ Horror Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craven, Wes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williamson, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T19:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f80d0b5c-f1c7-5cb2-89f3-71bcf5540425', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f80d0b5c-f1c7-5cb2-89f3-71bcf5540425'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s premier independent English language news source ceased publication on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/news-web-site-in-egypt-abruptly-shuts-down/', 'snippet': 'The country’s premier independent English language news source ceased publication on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Egypt Independent, the country’s premier independent English language news source, ceased publication on Thursday after four years during which its staff chronicled the waning days of the Mubarak regime, the outbreak of revolution in their own country and across the Arab world, military rule and most recently the administration of the first democratically elected Islamist leader of Egypt, Mohamed Morsi. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Web Site in Egypt Abruptly Shuts Down', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T19:22:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58fed8f0-21a0-509d-b277-23df859757cb', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58fed8f0-21a0-509d-b277-23df859757cb'}, {'abstract': 'To mark the New York screening of “The Source Family,” a new documentary about a 1970s commune, musicians will perform some of that group’s psychedelic compositions on Sunday in Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/nyregion/the-source-family-a-concert-and-film.html', 'snippet': 'To mark the New York screening of “The Source Family,” a new documentary about a 1970s commune, musicians will perform some of that group’s psychedelic compositions on Sunday in Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the late 1960s a New Age guru named Father Yod commanded a crowd of young utopia-seeking acolytes. The men grinned through robust beards and the women wore long, wispy dresses. They called themselves the Source Family. The group owned and operated a popular health-food restaurant in Hollywood and believed in the notion of the “eternal now” — until 1975, when Father Yod strapped himself to a hang glider and leapt off a cliff in Oahu. (He did not stick the landing.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26SOURCE_SPAN/26SOURCE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26SOURCE_SPAN/26SOURCE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capt