lue': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harkin, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavenner, Marilyn B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T20:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip M. Boffey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dfa2f4f-f9fb-5ace-9947-7b84c1316f43', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dfa2f4f-f9fb-5ace-9947-7b84c1316f43'}, {'abstract': 'The Times will provide live updates during the first round of the N.F.L. draft on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/live-coverage-of-the-n-f-l-draft/', 'snippet': 'The Times will provide live updates during the first round of the N.F.L. draft on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What a wild night at Radio City Music Hall. Three offensive tackles and three pass-rushers in the first six picks. Two guards in the top 10 for the first time in N.F.L. history. A 5-foot-8 receiver drafted at No. 8 over all. And that was just in the first 90 minutes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/sports/football/26class/26class-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/sports/football/26class/26class-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/sports/football/26class/26class-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/sports/football/26class/26class-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1313, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/sports/football/26class/26class-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/sports/football/26class/26class-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/sports/football/26class/26class-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights and Analysis of the N.F.L. Draft', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Top 10 Emerges From the Fog', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T20:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Bales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9bf1c3d-89bd-50fb-aea7-b104682b721a', 'word_count': 4644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9bf1c3d-89bd-50fb-aea7-b104682b721a'}, {'abstract': 'This getaway tucked into the country’s northwest corner features everything from neo-Classical buildings to a tropical cloud forest to dishes made with tender llama meat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/travel/36-hours-in-salta-argentina.html', 'snippet': 'This getaway tucked into the country’s northwest corner features everything from neo-Classical buildings to a tropical cloud forest to dishes made with tender llama meat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Argentina’s northwestern Salta Province has long been famous for its spectacular scenery of Andean peaks, red-rock valleys and vineyards, but its central metropolis, the city of Salta, has emerged only in the last few years as a bright spot on the tourist map. Founded in 1582 by the Spanish commander Hernando de Lerma, the city has traditionally served primarily as a supply center for the Spanish mining sites located in present-day Bolivia. A concerted effort to encourage new hotels, restaurants and shops is now paying off in a stream of visitors attracted to Salta’s updated colonial charm. Today, the old city center is recognized as a jewel-box-size getaway, perfect for exploring on foot and finally appreciated for its rich cultural offerings, grand neo-Classical buildings and thriving night life.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/travel/28HOURS_SPAN/28HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/28/travel/28HOURS_SPAN/28HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/travel/28HOURS_SPAN/28HOURS_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/travel/28HOURS_SPAN/28HOURS_SPAN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/travel/28HOURS_SPAN/28HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/28/travel/28HOURS_SPAN/28HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/travel/28HOURS_SPAN/28HOURS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Salta, Argentina', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Salta, Argentina', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salta (Argentina)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T20:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47c27244-c1a1-5942-9622-9da89bc0d4e1', 'word_count': 1368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47c27244-c1a1-5942-9622-9da89bc0d4e1'}, {'abstract': '“Jane Alexander: Surveys (From the Cape of Good Hope),” at the Cathedral Church of St. John the Divine, is the artist’s first New York solo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/arts/design/jane-alexanders-work-at-st-john-the-divine.html', 'snippet': '“Jane Alexander: Surveys (From the Cape of Good Hope),” at the Cathedral Church of St. John the Divine, is the artist’s first New York solo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cathedral Church of St. John the Divine in Morningside Heights is an occupied zone this spring, with a transient population of unearthly beings camped out in its chapels and aisles. They aren’t saints or angels, though some, in their odd way, do look angelic. They’re more closely related to the marginal creatures carved on high corbels and capitals in medieval churches: half-hidden, half-human, half-bestial things, refugees from the subconscious, defectors from dreams, staking claim to turf in the spiritual realm.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN/26ALEXANDER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN/26ALEXANDER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN/26ALEXANDER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN/26ALEXANDER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN/26ALEXANDER1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Beast in the Human, and Vice Versa', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Beast In the Human, And Vice Versa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cathedral Church of St John the Divine (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALEXANDER, JANE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T20:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/20ee88bf-b287-57e9-bff4-82f8508a26aa', 'word_count': 1296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20ee88bf-b287-57e9-bff4-82f8508a26aa'}, {'abstract': 'T reveals the exclusive behind-the-scenes video of Gerwig in the new Polaroid campaign for Band of Outsiders.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/behind-the-scenes-greta-gerwig-for-band-of-outsiders/', 'snippet': 'T reveals the exclusive behind-the-scenes video of Gerwig in the new Polaroid campaign for Band of Outsiders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fitting of the indie actress that she is, Greta Gerwig stars in the new Band of Outsiders spring campaign, in a series of Polaroids taken by the fashion label’s creative director Scott Sternberg. Next month, see Gerwig in theaters in “Frances Ha,” the film she co-wrote with Noah Baumbach, which had its premiere at the Telluride Film Festival last fall. Here, T reveals the exclusive behind-the-scenes video of Gerwig on location last month at the Hollywood Sports Paintball Park in Bellflower, Calif.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Scenes | Greta Gerwig for Band of Outsiders', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telluride Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gerwig, Greta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Band of Outsiders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T20:35:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3984f290-db11-53a4-96f4-751ad82edf76', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3984f290-db11-53a4-96f4-751ad82edf76'}, {'abstract': 'Three White House officials went to Capitol Hill to meet with Republican senators, but a broad compromise on the budget still seems distant.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/obama-officials-hold-early-budget-talks-with-republicans/', 'snippet': 'Three White House officials went to Capitol Hill to meet with Republican senators, but