u’ve got to be brave and believe,” one song advised, without cynicism or too much sentimentality. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26DECLAN_SPAN/DECLAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26DECLAN_SPAN/DECLAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26DECLAN_SPAN/DECLAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26DECLAN_SPAN/DECLAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26DECLAN_SPAN/DECLAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26DECLAN_SPAN/DECLAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26DECLAN_SPAN/DECLAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Irish Ballads and Solace in the Face of Sorrow', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Irish Ballads and Solace in the Face of Sorrow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Irish Arts Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Rourke, Declan", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T21:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4016716-9bfc-5b32-abc0-075364b84090', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4016716-9bfc-5b32-abc0-075364b84090'}, {'abstract': 'The Kurt Weill and Bertolt Brecht opera “Rise and Fall of the City of Mahagonny” is a sobering mirror for a culture obsessed with money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/arts/music/rise-and-fall-of-the-city-of-mahagonny-at-manhattan-school.html', 'snippet': 'The Kurt Weill and Bertolt Brecht opera “Rise and Fall of the City of Mahagonny” is a sobering mirror for a culture obsessed with money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We hope and expect that the arts can play a political role in our culture. They can’t, and shouldn’t, necessarily bear tangible fruit — they can’t elect a candidate or pass a bill — but they should cause us to reflect on our moment. They should make us angry when we need to be angry.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26FALLALT_SPAN/FALLALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26FALLALT_SPAN/FALLALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26FALLALT_SPAN/FALLALT-jumbo