e where the best players, as measured by their actual N.F.L. performance, were drafted each year.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In N.F.L. Draft, How Good Are Teams at Picking the Best?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Quealy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quealy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5217aac9-165d-5f9b-ad79-06bd584872be', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5217aac9-165d-5f9b-ad79-06bd584872be'}, {'abstract': 'In Jeff Nichols’s third feature, two Arkansas boys discover a boat on an overgrown island in the Mississippi River, and also discover the leathery loner who inhabits it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/movies/mud-stars-matthew-mcconaughey-and-reese-witherspoon.html', 'snippet': 'In Jeff Nichols’s third feature, two Arkansas boys discover a boat on an overgrown island in the Mississippi River, and also discover the leathery loner who inhabits it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The central image in “Mud,” Jeff Nichols’s deft and absorbing third feature, is of a boat in a tree. It’s the kind of phenomenon — a caprice of nature that is absurd but also wondrous — designed to enchant adventurous children like Ellis (Tye Sheridan) and Neckbone (Jacob Lofland), two Arkansas boys who discover the boat on an overgrown island in the Mississippi River. They also discover the fellow who claims to own, or at least inhabit, the vessel, a leathery loner whose name is Mud.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hiding From Trouble, Found by Innocents', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hiding From Trouble, Found by Innocents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConaughey, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witherspoon, Reese', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nichols, Jeff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mud (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2a7b929-7660-5147-a9f9-0c0a8d10fff0', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2a7b929-7660-5147-a9f9-0c0a8d10fff0'}, {'abstract': 'Jared Staal, 22, joined his brothers Eric and Jordan in the Hurricanes’ lineup Thursday night against the Rangers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/sports/hockey/carolinas-jared-staal-prepares-for-nhl-debut.html', 'snippet': 'Jared Staal, 22, joined his brothers Eric and Jordan in the Hurricanes’ lineup Thursday night against the Rangers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RALEIGH, N.C. — When the four Staal brothers were growing up in Thunder Bay, Ontario, they played two-on-two hockey on the backyard pond.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit