ion viewers, the show’s biggest audience yet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/business/media/media-decoder-duck-dynasty-finale-sets-ratings-record-for-ae.html', 'snippet': 'The finale was watched by 9.6 million viewers, the show’s biggest audience yet.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Duck Dynasty” only gets bigger. It season finale Wednesday night set new ratings records for the A&E network and in the process made even “American Idol” shrink under its growing wingspan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Media Decoder: ‘Duck Dynasty’ Finale Sets Ratings Record for A&E', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Duck Dynasty’ Soars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARTS & ENTERTAINMENT NETWORK', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Duck Dynasty (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be574889-30aa-5951-9d8b-f38559b4439b', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be574889-30aa-5951-9d8b-f38559b4439b'}, {'abstract': 'The debut of an environmentally friendly mascara.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/vain-glorious-kjaer-weis-mascara/', 'snippet': 'The debut of an environmentally friendly mascara.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The arrival of Earth Day this week was a reminder that there are more and more reusable, environmentally friendly products out there that people might actually want to use. Case in point: the debut of an organic, refillable mascara that has haute hippies rejoicing. The smudge-free formula, available for preorder on Kjaer Weis’s Web site, consists of lavender water and rose oil, which give it an appealing floral fragrance (and not a hint of patchouli). Refills, which will be offered online beginning next week, include one tube of product and a new wand, both of which easily slide into the sleek, metal case after the initial three-month supply is exhausted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Kjaer Weis Mascara', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Face', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27f0a9e5-a1ec-5831-827c-d86db795e07c', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27f0a9e5-a1ec-5831-827c-d86db795e07c'}, {'abstract': 'In “The New Digital Age” Eric Schmidt and Jared Cohen lay out a future without secrets — for the good and the bad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/books/the-new-digital-age-by-eric-schmidt-and-jared-cohen.html', 'snippet': 'In “The New Digital Age” Eric Schmidt and Jared Cohen lay out a future without secrets — for the good and the bad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Picture this rosy scenario for your high-tech future: You awaken because your curtains open automatically, your coffee maker starts brewing and your bed administers a subtle hint in the form of a back massage. Your closet, having scanned your calendar, coughs up a freshly cleaned suit for the big meeting today. You head for the kitchen while reading the day’s news as a translucent holographic display. Thanks to motion detection, it stays right in front of you as you walk.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26BOOKSCHMIDT1/26BOOKSCHMIDT1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26BOOKSCHMIDT1/26BOOKSCHMIDT1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 785}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26BOOKSCHMIDT1/26BOOKSCHMIDT1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26BOOKSCHMIDT1/26BOOKSCHMIDT1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1717, 'width': 1312, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26BOOKSCHMIDT1/JPBOOKSCHMIDT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26BOOKSCHMIDT1/JPBOOKSCHMIDT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26BOOKSCHMIDT1/JPBOOKSCHMIDT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Formatting a World With No Secrets', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Formatting a World With No Secrets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The New Digital Age: Reshaping the Future of People, Nations and Business (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Eric E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Jared', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0dda3e8-33eb-510a-a65d-afe2772baff2', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0dda3e8-33eb-510a-a65d-afe2772baff2'}, {'abstract': '“Some Were Neighbors: Collaboration & Complicity in the Holocaust” features details from people who witnessed the slaughter and persecution in Nazi Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/arts/design/some-were-neighbors-at-us-holocaust-memorial-museum.html', 'snippet': '“Some Were Neighbors: Collaboration & Complicity in the Holocaust” features details from people who witnessed the slaughter and persecution in Nazi Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Whatever larger themes are sounded when the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum commemorates its 20th anniversary here this weekend, whatever is said at a Monday ceremony by former President Bill Clinton or by the museum’s founding chairman, Elie Wiesel, and whatever assessments are made about its influence, accomplishments or limitations, it will take a visit to its new exhibition, “Some Were Neighbors,” to grasp one aspect of this imposing institution’s power. It reveals the demonic not in grand forces, but in the most minute details.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN/26HOLOCAUST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 301, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN/26HOLOCAUST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 301}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN/26HOLOCAUST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN/26HOLOCAUST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1028, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN/26HOLOCAUST_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bystanders, Not So Innocent', 'kicker': 'Exhibition Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bystanders, Not So Innocent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothstein, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Holocaust Memorial Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d49b76a6-b066-5e43-b487-595d619d2db1', 'word_count': 1376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d49b76a6-b066-5e43-b487-595d619d2db1'}, {'abstract': 'Is it “Voodoo,” or “Vodou”?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/undoing-a-spell-without-magic/', 'snippet': 'Is it “Voodoo,” or “Vodou”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As someone who uses The Times’s stylebook frequently enough to have installed it in the upper-right-hand search window in Firefox — it’s my second search-engine option, after Google — I’ve been interested in the ways that words are continually evolving at The Times. A couple of days ago, editors at the paper updated the stylebook’s guidelines on the use of “illegal immigrant”; a little more than a week before that, Margaret Sullivan, The Times’s public editor, argued that more attention should be paid to the way the paper uses the terms “torture” and “targeted killings.”', 'source': 'The New York Times