': 'nyt://article/fddadc93-0017-5e49-baa6-d456b206b8bd'}, {'abstract': 'An experiment with two-way chargers allows consumers to power their cars and also send power back to their electric company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/business/energy-environment/electric-vehicles-begin-to-earn-money-from-the-grid.html', 'snippet': 'An experiment with two-way chargers allows consumers to power their cars and also send power back to their electric company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Finally, payback for the plug-in. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Two-Way Charging, Electric Cars Begin to Earn Money From the Grid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Two-Way Charging, Electric Cars Begin to Earn Money From the Grid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Delaware', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mini Division of Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kempton, Willett M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:50:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8e277a6-74f4-5f70-9808-f116df772c15', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8e277a6-74f4-5f70-9808-f116df772c15'}, {'abstract': 'How the Lieber Code gave white and black women recourse from the conflict’s horrific sexual violence.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/rape-and-justice-in-the-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'How the Lieber Code gave white and black women recourse from the conflict’s horrific sexual violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Lincoln’s General Orders No. 100, also known as the Lieber Code of 1863, set clear rules for engaging with enemy combatants. But the code also clarified how Union soldiers should treat civilians, and in particular women. Largely forgotten today, the Lieber Code established strict laws regarding an issue that was everywhere and nowhere in the consciousness of the Civil War: wartime rape.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rape and Justice in the Civil War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Crystal N. Feimster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Crystal', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Feimster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0afc37b-d2f6-540e-96e5-088dbdcc0aab', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0afc37b-d2f6-540e-96e5-088dbdcc0aab'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s government warned that it may stop cross-border adoptions if Ireland approves a human rights measure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/world/europe/russia-using-adoption-leverage-in-ireland.html', 'snippet': 'Russia’s government warned that it may stop cross-border adoptions if Ireland approves a human rights measure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW – The Russian government has warned in a letter to Ireland’s Parliament that it may halt negotiations on an agreement for cross-border adoptions if an Irish parliamentary committee approves a resolution critical of rights abuses in Russia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Using Adoption Leverage in Ireland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Adoption Talks Used to Blunt Irish Criticism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Orphans and Orphanages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T22:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03871253-af84-5fae-a9e2-c151a650259d', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03871253-af84-5fae-a9e2-c151a650259d'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Dianne Feinstein, the California Democrat who is chairwoman of the Senate intelligence committee, said that it was time to consider lifting a ban on repatriating low-level detainees to Yemen from the prison at Guantanamo Bay, Cuba.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/25/senator-urges-transfer-of-guantanamo-detainees-to-yemen-amid-revolt/', 'snippet': 'Senator Dianne Feinstein, the California Democrat who is chairwoman of the Senate intelligence committee, said that it was time to consider lifting a ban on repatriating low-level detainees to Yemen from the prison at Guantanamo Bay, Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – Senator Dianne Feinstein, the California Democrat who is chairwoman of the Senate intelligence committee, declared on Thursday that it was time to consider lifting a ban on repatriating low-level detainees to Yemen from the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, amid rising desperation and a hunger strike among inmates there. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Urges Transfer of Guantánamo Detainees to Yemen Amid Revolt', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Dianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T23:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'S