f 2012. Though some of them grew last year over all, high unemployment rates and the prospect of a weaker German economy have raised fears of a widespread recession.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Signs of the European Union’s Weakening Economies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-25T23:52:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/34e380ba-4a95-53d1-bc18-374b2c32594e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/34e380ba-4a95-53d1-bc18-374b2c32594e'}, {'abstract': 'Though houses stand vacant while Galveston, Tex., is locked in litigation, a fight over rebuilding public housing is nearing resolution, and city leaders remain optimistic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/us/galveston-tex-picking-up-the-pieces-5-years-after-hurricane-ike.html', 'snippet': 'Though houses stand vacant while Galveston, Tex., is locked in litigation, a fight over rebuilding public housing is nearing resolution, and city leaders remain optimistic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GALVESTON — From his 18th-floor law office, Buddy Herz, the head of the Galveston Housing Authority and a lifelong resident of this city, can point out how his view has changed since Hurricane Ike slammed into the island in 2008. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04