t what use are they if they are so frequently reversed?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As any regular reader of news will know, popular media report “scientific results” nearly every day. They come delivered in news reports and opinion pieces, and are often used to make a variety of points concerning important matters like health, parenting, education, even spirituality and self-knowledge. How seriously should we take them?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do Scientific Studies Show?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T00:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5a9db4e-8e11-5501-a5f6-d0e729cd7e25', 'word_count': 1325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5a9db4e-8e11-5501-a5f6-d0e729cd7e25'}, {'abstract': 'Texas legislators are working to expand the free-breakfast program to all schoolchildren in poor areas, not just those from low-income households.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/education/considering-free-breakfasts-for-all-texas-students-in-poor-areas.html', 'snippet': 'Texas legislators are working to expand the free-breakfast program to all schoolchildren in poor areas, not just those from low-income households.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many students at Arnoldo Cantu Sr. Elementary School in San Juan, a Rio Grande Valley town just east of McAllen, do not have much. The Texas Education Agency estimates that 89 percent of the students in that school district are from low-income households. But every morning, all of the school’s 927 students can count on a federally subsidized breakfast.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/us/26ttStormschool/26ttStorm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/us/26ttStormschool/26ttStorm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/us/26ttStormschool/26ttStorm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/us/26ttStormschool/26ttStorm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/us/26ttStormschool/26ttStormschool-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/us/26ttStormschool/26ttStormschool-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/us/26ttStormschool/26ttStormschool-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aiming to Serve Free Breakfasts to All Students in Poor Areas', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aiming to Serve Free Breakf