alue': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'First Responder Network Authority (FirstNet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzgerald, Paul H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T04:23:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/476319bd-e486-5850-8e06-ac359ac2bdb8', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/476319bd-e486-5850-8e06-ac359ac2bdb8'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration asked the Supreme Court to review a decision from a federal appeals court that strictly limited recess appointments by presidents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/us/politics/white-house-seeks-review-of-ruling-on-recesses.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration asked the Supreme Court to review a decision from a federal appeals court that strictly limited recess appointments by presidents.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Obama administration on Thursday asked the Supreme Court to review a January decision from a federal appeals court in Washington that strictly limited recess appointments by presidents bypassing the Senate confirmation process. The administration’s brief said the ruling “would deem invalid hundreds of recess appointments made by presidents since early in the nation’s history” and call into question actions taken by many federal agencies. Should the Supreme Court agree to hear the case, National Labor Relations Board v. Noel Canning, it would probably be argued in the fall and decided next year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Seeks Review of Ruling on Recesses', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White House Seeks Review of Ruling On Recesses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T04:27:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5b690e-be18-540a-ae05-77fd4c92265c', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5b690e-be18-540a-ae05-77fd4c92265c'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Dianne Feinstein said Thursday that the Obama administration should consider lifting a ban on repatriating low-level detainees to Yemen from Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/us/obama-is-asked-to-reconsider-repatriation-of-yemenis.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Dianne Feinstein said Thursday that the Obama administration should consider lifting a ban on repatriating low-level detainees to Yemen from Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Senator Dianne Feinstein, the California Democrat who heads the Senate Intelligence Committee, said Thursday that the Obama administration should consider lifting a ban on repatriating low-level detainees to Yemen from Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, where a hunger strike has focused attention on a sense of desperation among inmates there. The prison has 56 detainees from Yemen who were approved for transfer more than three years ago. But President Obama halted any further transfers after the attempted bombing of a Detroit-bound airliner by a Yemeni-based branch of Al Qaeda on Dec. 25, 2009. In a letter to Mr. Obama’s national security director, Tom Donilon, Ms. Feinstein said it was time to examine whether Yemen’s president, Abdu Rabbu Mansour Hadi, who has been a strong foe of Al Qaeda since taking office last year, could provide adequate security assurances to return the inmates. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Is Asked to Reconsider Repatriation of Yemenis', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Is Asked To Reconsider Repatriation of Yemenis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Dianne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T04:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1188a6b8-d454-5317-82fc-f11b169f093a', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1188a6b8-d454-5317-82fc-f11b169f093a'}, {'abstract': 'Another trial of a potential vaccine against AIDS was halted because it was not working, a federal research agency announced Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/health/agency-halts-trial-for-aids-vaccine.html', 'snippet': 'Another trial of a potential vaccine against AIDS was halted because it was not working, a federal research agency announced Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Another trial of a potential vaccine against AIDS was halted because it was not working, a federal research agency announced Thursday. The trial, known as HVTN 505, started in 2009 with 2,504 gay male volunteers in 19 cities who got three shots over eight weeks. A recent analysis by an outside monitoring board found that more volunteers who got the vaccine became infected during a follow-up period than volunteers who got a placebo. However, the numbers of men infected — 27 vaccine recipients versus 21 placebo recipients — were statistically too close to say that the test vaccine had actually increased the chances of infection, according to the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, which sponsored the trial. Those who got the vaccine and became infected anyway also did not have less virus in their blood, the monitoring board found. The vaccine was based on an adenovirus, which causes common colds. In 2007, another trial of an adenovirus-based vaccine was halted because it was not working, and later analysis suggested that for some men — those who had previously caught adenovirus colds — the vaccine made it more likely, rather than less, that they would get infected with H.I.V. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agency Halts Trial for Aids Vaccine', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Science', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agency Halts Trial For AIDS Vaccine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k