 Australia’s GrainCorp with a sweetened buyout bid that includes cash and an additional dividend payout.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/a-d-m-in-2-7-billion-australian-takeover/', 'snippet': 'After its third attempt, Archer Daniels Midland on Friday finally won the support of the board of Australia’s GrainCorp with a sweetened buyout bid that includes cash and an additional dividend payout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The board of GrainCorp, one of the biggest Australian grain processors, accepted a sweetened takeover bid worth 3 billion Australian dollars ($3.1 billion) Friday from the American agribusiness giant Archer Daniels Midland. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.D.M. in $3.1 Billion Australian Takeover', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCHER-DANIELS-MIDLAND CO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T07:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce152329-267b-52e1-9bf9-28c903869b14', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce152329-267b-52e1-9bf9-28c903869b14'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the victims were patients who died in their beds as firefighters made the hourlong journey from the nearest station, safety officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/world/europe/fire-at-russian-psychiatric-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the victims were patients who died in their beds as firefighters made the hourlong journey from the nearest station, safety officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — When flames shot out of Psychiatric Hospital No. 14 at 2 a.m. on Friday, people in the village of Ramensky crept as close as they could, knowing that patients and medical staff were probably trapped inside. But fire raged through the 73-year-old wooden building, and there was nothing to put it out with.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/world/europe/27russia2/27russia2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/world/europe/27russia2/27russia2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/world/europe/27russia2/27russia2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/world/europe/27russia2/27russia2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/world/europe/27russia2/27russia2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/27/world/europe/27russia2/27russia2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/world/europe/27russ