here are no quick fixes for one of the world’s largest economies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank of Japan Sets Deflation Turnaround Target Date', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Looks To Meet Aim On Inflation In Two Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deflation (Economics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T11:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5338e29-ea9b-58e3-ade1-41a5ab468908', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5338e29-ea9b-58e3-ade1-41a5ab468908'}, {'abstract': 'The hedge fund manager Warren G. Lichtenstein is fighting with Andrew Cader, a former Goldman Sachs executive, over a British socialite’s child support claims. | George Soros disclosed a 7.9 percent stake in J.C. Penney, a retailer without many fans on Wall Street. | Two senators introducing a new banking bill can be thought of as punk rockers. | Though they’re now allowed to tweet, companies are being cautious.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/millionaires-duke-it-out-over-child-support/', 'snippet': 'The hedge fund manager Warren G. Lichtenstein is fighting with Andrew Cader, a former Goldman Sachs executive, over a British socialite’s child support claims. | George Soros disclosed a 7.9 percent stake in J.C. Penney, a retailer without many fa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILLIONAIRES DUKE IT OUT OVER CHILD SUPPORT \xa0|\xa0 The financier Warren G. Lichtenstein, head of the hedge fund Steel Partners, is accustomed to courtroom battles. But this one has a different flavor. Mr. Lichtenstein, who has a 5-year-old child with his former lover Annabelle Bond, a British socialite, is accusing Ms. Bond’s current boyfriend, Andrew Cader, a former Goldman Sachs executive and part-owner of the Tampa Bay Rays baseball team, of conspiring with her to hide her financial condition in order to secure more than $50,000 a month in child support payments, DealBook’s Peter Lattman reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millionaires in a Legal Skirmish Over Child Support', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T11:59:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72977883-f0d7-51b5-a5e5-fc9b4f8c31fc', 'word_count': 1675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72977883-f0d7-51b5-a5e5-fc9b4f8c31fc'}, {'abstract': 'The research library and exhibition space in Tulsa, Okla., houses Woody Guthrie’s archives.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/woody-guthrie-center-set-to-open-on-saturday/', 'snippet': 'The research library and exhibition space in Tulsa, Okla., houses Woody Guthrie’s archives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This archive is your archive. The new Woody Guthrie Center in Tulsa, Okla., is having its grand opening on Saturday, in a homecoming for Guthrie, who was born in Oklahoma. The 12,000-square-foot research library and exhibition space houses Guthrie’s archives, which were bought from Guthrie’s family by the Tulsa-based George Kaiser Family Foundation. On display will be the handwritten version of “This Land Is Your Land,” as well as photographs, notebooks, letters and musical instruments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woody Guthrie Center Opening in Tulsa', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guthrie, Nora', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guthrie, Woody', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser, George, Family Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tulsa (Okla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T12:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9fca2dd-ccb4-5b4a-b1fc-4d489f561218', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9fca2dd-ccb4-5b4a-b1fc-4d489f561218'}, {'abstract': 'Playing the lead role in “Scandal,” Kerry Washington is regarded as a star whose success can open doors for other black actresses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/movies/the-weight-those-heels-carry.html', 'snippet': 'Playing the lead role in “Scandal,” Kerry Washington is regarded as a star whose success can open doors for other black actresses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Kerry Washington starts with the shoes. To portray Olivia Pope, the tough crisis manager at the center of the hit ABC series “Scandal,” Ms. Washington is always in gravity-defying heels. How else to make that sexed-up power stalk down the White House corridors? ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/arts/28KERRY_SPAN/28KERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/28/arts/28KERRY_SPAN/28KERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/arts/28KERRY_SPAN/28KERRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/arts/28KERRY_SPAN/28KERRY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/arts/28KERRY_SPAN/28KERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/28/arts/28KERRY_SPAN/28KERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/arts/28KERRY_SPAN/28KERRY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Weight Those Heels Carry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Weight Those Heels Carry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Felicia R', 'rank'