.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d26fc81f-f3e0-54ad-ba0e-e3044404a34c', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d26fc81f-f3e0-54ad-ba0e-e3044404a34c'}, {'abstract': 'Since 2000, real weekly wages of relatively low-paid workers have declined, while for those nearer the top of the ladder, they have risen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/04/26/business/Widening-Inequality-In-Wages.html', 'snippet': 'Since 2000, real weekly wages of relatively low-paid workers have declined, while for those nearer the top of the ladder, they have risen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2000, real weekly wages of relatively low-paid workers have declined, while for those nearer the top of the ladder, they have risen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Widening Inequality In Wages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T14:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/0686f3d5-8fb5-58dc-8019-acc716613e63', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/0686f3d5-8fb5-58dc-8019-acc716613e63'}, {'abstract': 'This week our classroom collaborators decided to experiment with learning Web design via a tool that makes it easy. For each prompt, their students did an extension activity involving Web design, examples of which we’ve linked to. Try it yourself and let us know how it goes.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/common-core-practice-reading-the-times-and-responding-in-code/', 'snippet': 'This week 