hone in the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/business/26bits-smart/26bits-smart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/business/26bits-smart/26bits-smart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/business/26bits-smart/26bits-smart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/business/26bits-smart/26bits-smart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1427, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/business/26bits-smart/26bits-smart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/26/business/26bits-smart/26bits-smart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/business/26bits-smart/26bits-smart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Smartphones Finally Surpass the Feature Phone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T14:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0f0ee23-1106-5be2-8f02-4e6be2d74ef4', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0f0ee23-1106-5be2-8f02-4e6be2d74ef4'}, {'abstract': 'Football writers analyzed Thursday’s first round of the N.F.L. draft, which was heavy on linemen and low on glamour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/sports/football/quarterbacks-take-a-hit-in-the-nfl-draft.html', 'snippet': 'Football writers analyzed Thursday’s first round of the N.F.L. draft, which was heavy on linemen and low on glamour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the three massive offensive tackles taken in the top four spots of Thursday night’s N.F.L. draft really wanted to display their quarterback-protecting skills, they should have gone back into the greenroom and blocked the television cameras from filming every heartbeat of Geno Smith’s angst-a-thon. Eric Fisher, Luke Joeckel and Lane Johnson should have teamed up midway through the round, when it became painfully clear that the N.F.L. was trying to go cold turkey on its quarterback addiction, leaving poor Smith writhing in a chair fighting an existential battle with his ego. Because by the time Buffalo stunned everyone by snagging Florida State’s E.\u2009J. Manuel as the only quarterback in the first round, even Smith’s biggest critics wanted to give him a hug.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quarterbacks Take a Hit in Round 1', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joeckel, Luke', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lane', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manuel, E J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nassib, Ryan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Randolph, Zach', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Te'o, Manti", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milliner, Dee', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T14:56:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34098010-bdb4-5942-a756-716a5a92da03', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34098010-bdb4-5942-a756-716a5a92da03'}, {'abstract': 'How the government sector is contracting, as measured by gross domestic product.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/starving-the-beast-2/', 'snippet': 'How the government sector is contracting, as measured by gross domestic product.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1950s, government spending fell quickly after the Korean War ended. In the second quarter of 1956, the total government gross domestic product was $91.4 billion, at an annual rate. That was 0.4 percent lower than the $91.8 billion rate three years earlier, in the third quarter of 1953.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Starving the Beast', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T14:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29de2f01-af58-5885-8799-f7afd8001f1a', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29de2f01-af58-5885-8799-f7afd8001f1a'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/the-gun-report-april-26-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On April 8, in Toms River, N.J., a 4-year-old boy shot and killed his 6-year-old playmate “as their parents stood in the yard nearby,” the police later told CNN. We linked to this story in the Gun Report, and have been keeping an eye on it ever since. Two days later, Atlantic County Prosecutor James McClain announced that his office had taken over the investigation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: April 26, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denver (Colo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Huntsville (Ala)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Livingston (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orange (NJ)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T15:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f00933b-7b58-57d5-be5c-63aaca205395', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f00933b-7b58-57d5-be5c-63aaca205395'}, {'abstract': 'The companies that provide most of the jobs on the Continent are having trouble winning customers and getting bank loans, a survey by the European Central Bank found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/business/global/27iht-eurozone27.html', 'snippet': 'The companies that provide most of the jobs on the Continent are having trouble winning customers and getting bank loans, a survey by the European Central Bank found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Smaller companies that provide most of the jobs in Europe face an ever more difficult struggle to win customers and get bank loans, according to a survey from the European Central Bank on Friday that contributed to a picture of spreading economic stagnation in the euro zone.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/27/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "Europe's Small Businesses Continue to Struggle", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Europe’s Small Businesses, a Deepening Struggle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T15:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/180d4c7f-7f43-5f84-a93c-42b4226f3511', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/180d4c7f-7f43-5f84-a93c-42b4226f3511'}, {'abstract': 'The artist’s latest project is a result of integrating abstract forms in pure, vibrant colors.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/now-showing-simone-shubuck/', 'snippet': 'The artist’s latest project is a result of integrating abstract forms in pure, vibrant colors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though her filigree doodles of deceptively innocent-seeming flora and fauna were a fixture on the downtown gallery scene a decade ago, the artist Simone Shubuck has had only one solo show in the last six years — in 2009, at Corbett vs. Dempsey in Chicago. During that time, she married Adam Rapoport, the editor in chief of Bon Appetit magazine; became a mother; oversaw a protracted apartment renovation; and stepped away from her other career as a floral designer. Though she’s slowed her formerly frenetic output, she has continued to privately hone her technique, integrating abstract forms in pure, vibrant color. “My pace changed dramatically; I had to get to a new place in my life,” she says. “Having different identities brought me to a different place in my work.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Showing | Simone Shubuck', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Returning to Form', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T15:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a235118-584b-5f6e-80af-f654cf26e002', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a235118-584b-5f6e-80af-f654cf26e002'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph Altuzarra designed the costumes for one of the choreographer Christopher Wheeldon’s two ballets at the New York City Ballet’s spring gala.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/for-altuzarra-a-ballet-debut/', 'snippet': 'Joseph Altuzarra designed the costumes for one of the choreographer Christopher Wheeldon’s two ballets at the New York City Ballet’s spring gala.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It started in a really strange way,” said Joseph Altuzarra, recalling a day last summer on Fire Island when the choreographer Christopher Wheeldon invited him to design costumes for a new ballet that he was presenting at the New York City Ballet’s spring gala, on May 8. Although Mr. Altuzarra was friendly with the choreographer, he admitted that, out of courtesy, he had never asked too many questions and so didn’t fully know what Mr. Wheeldon did. “He said, ‘Oh, I’d love to do a ballet together,’ ” Mr. Altuzarra recalled, with a sheepish grin. “I was like, ‘Sure.’ ”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Altuzarra, a Ballet Debut', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fashion and Dance Meet Again in a New Ballet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altuzarra, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T15:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53b52328-cf44-5277-8579-81b95695900c', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53b52328-cf44-5277-8579-81b95695900c'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Mordaunt’s feature “The Rocket” won two top prizes at the Tribeca Film Festival: the Founders Award for best narrative feature, and a best actor prize for its young lead, Sitthiphon Disamoe.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/prize-winners-announced-at-tribeca-film-festival/', 'snippet': 'Kim Mordaunt’s feature “The Rocket” won two top prizes at the Tribeca Film Festival: the Founders Award for best narrative feature, and a best actor prize for its young lead, Sitthiphon Disamoe.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Rocket,” Kim Mordaunt’s feature about a 10-year-old Laotian boy who seeks refuge from his difficult life by participating in a rocket-building contest, won two top prizes at this year’s Tribeca Film Festival, claiming the festival’s Founders Award for best narrative feature and its best actor award for Sitthiphon Disamoe, who plays the film’s young protagonist.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/therocket/therocket-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/therocket/therocket-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/therocket/therocket-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/26/arts/therocket