rticle/81393088-acaa-52de-88a2-79ff157d46ca'}, {'abstract': 'Besides chicken eggs, some New Jersey farms offer duck, guinea hen, goose, pheasant, even ostrich eggs fresh from the nest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/nyregion/new-jersey-henhouses-sell-duck-goose-even-ostrich-eggs.html', 'snippet': 'Besides chicken eggs, some New Jersey farms offer duck, guinea hen, goose, pheasant, even ostrich eggs fresh from the nest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WANTAGE, N.J. — Most mornings outside the gates of Tier Haus Farms here, several cars drive up to investigate the contents of an ordinary-looking cooler. Inside are eggs, freshly collected from beyond the gates by Carolyn Gerdes, an owner of the hilly, 70-acre property. Instead of having a traditional farm stand, Ms. Gerdes accepts orders by text, e-mail and phone for eggs, then leaves them for her regular customers to pick up when she is not available to hand them off directly. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28REVDINENJ3/28REVsubDINENJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28REVDINENJ3/28REVsubDINENJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28REVDINENJ3/28REVsubDINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28REVDINENJ3/28REVsubDINENJ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28REVDINENJ3/28REVDINENJ3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28REVDINENJ3/28REVDINENJ3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28REVDINENJ3/28REVDINENJ3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Size of a Gumball, or Bigger Than Jumbo', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Eggs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Size of a Gumball, or Bigger Than Jumbo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roaming Acres Farm (Hardyston, NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Griggstown Quail Farm and Market (Princeton, NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goffle Road Poultry Farm (Wyckoff, NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tier Haus Farms (Wantage, NJ)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T22:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tammy La Gorce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tammy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3686e39-7f95-56aa-aa3d-c7ec4f6c53e2', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3686e39-7f95-56aa-aa3d-c7ec4f6c53e2'}, {'abstract': 'A concert by the Swedish Chamber Orchestra and the soprano Nina Stemme at Alice Tully Hall on Thursday dished out a feast of musical ideas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/arts/music/swedish-chamber-orchestra-and-nina-stemme-at-alice-tully-hall.html', 'snippet': 'A concert by the Swedish Chamber Orchestra and the soprano Nina Stemme at Alice Tully Hall on Thursday dished out a feast of musical ideas.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Life is uncertain. Eat dessert first.” At first glance, the program for Thursday evening’s concert at Alice Tully Hall by the Swedish Chamber Orchestra with the soprano Nina Stemme put me in mind of this much-quoted maxim by Ernestine Ulmer. The substantial fare appeared to have been reserved for the second half, which was given over to Brahms’s Symphony No. 1. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/27CHAMBER/27CHAMBER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/27CHAMBER/27CHAMBER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/27CHAMBER/27CHAMBER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/27CHAMBER/27CHAMBER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1456, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/27CHAMBER/27CHAMBER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/27CHAMBER/27CHAMBER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/27CHAMBER/27CHAMBER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Musical Buffet, the Entree Need Not Be Served First', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Musical Buffet, the Entree Need Not Be Served First', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swedish Chamber Orchestra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stemme, Nina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alice Tully Hall (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T22:53:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6bada91-b5f3-5690-b76b-2e2f873cd6e5', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6bada91-b5f3-5690-b76b-2e2f873cd6e5'}, {'abstract': 'Quadron, a Danish duo featuring the talented singer Coco O, performed with a full band at Le Poisson Rouge on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/arts/music/quadron-at-le-poisson-rouge.html', 'snippet': 'Quadron, a Danish duo featuring the talented singer Coco O, performed with a full band at Le Poisson Rouge on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Coco O could sing was not in question. For about a half-hour on Thursday night at Le Poisson Rouge, she’d been slithery, teasing, sensual, ecstatic. The carefree soul songs of Quadron, the duo for which she is the frontwoman, demand all of those things. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/SUB-27QUADRON/SUB-27QUADRON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/SUB-27QUADRON/SUB-27QUADRON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/SUB-27QUADRON/SUB-27QUADRON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/SUB-27QUADRON/SUB-27QUADRON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/SUB-27QUADRON/SUB-27QUADRON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/SUB-27QUADRON/SUB-27QUADRON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/arts/SUB-27QUADRON/SUB-27QUADRON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Electrosoul, With a Heartfelt Sweetness', 'kicker': 'M