ame': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rand Richards Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rand', 'middlename': 'Richards', 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/192c015b-c893-536f-b303-40f0e7612f65', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/192c015b-c893-536f-b303-40f0e7612f65'}, {'abstract': 'Whether or not Tim Tebow remains on the team in 2013, the Jets will have some quarterback drama. Will Geno Smith start ahead of Mark Sanchez?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/jets-picking-geno-smith-are-talk-of-the-town-again/', 'snippet': 'Whether or not Tim Tebow remains on the team in 2013, the Jets will have some quarterback drama. Will Geno Smith start ahead of Mark Sanchez?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Minutes before the Jets drafted West Virginia quarterback Geno Smith on Friday night with the 39th pick, the NFL Network analyst Mike Mayock exclaimed that he didn’t believe Smith would land in New York because he’s perhaps not a franchise quarterback and it would create “a circus.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets, Picking Geno Smith, Are Talk of the Town Again', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-26T23:27:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Bales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizati