', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Bales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e3fb2b0-c7cb-514d-86cb-4c61dbeac23b', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e3fb2b0-c7cb-514d-86cb-4c61dbeac23b'}, {'abstract': 'Ilona DeVito di Porriasa, a market analyst on Wall Street, hailed from a family of European nobles. But she rarely shared that information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/nyregion/in-new-york-the-death-of-a-countess-in-exile.html', 'snippet': 'Ilona DeVito di Porriasa, a market analyst on Wall Street, hailed from a family of European nobles. But she rarely shared that information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They knew her as the slender, straight-backed woman with an independent streak and a head for numbers. She told them she had immigrated from Hungary, and her colleagues at Merrill Lynch did not pry with more questions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/nyregion/countess/countess-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/nyregion/countess/countess-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/nyregion/countess/countess-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/nyregion/countess/countess-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2005,