has written a trenchant review of the State Department’s most recent effort to assess the consequences of building the Keystone XL pipeline. The E.P.A’.s letter, issued Monday, at the end of the public comment period on the department’s latest draft environmental impact statement, is hardly a favorable report card. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A.’s Keystone Report Card', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.P.A.’s Keystone Report Card', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T02:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0810d39c-928a-518d-9158-70b3512b9ee9', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0810d39c-928a-518d-9158-70b3512b9ee9'}, {'abstract': 'The country needs to get beyond the “drug war” approach to addiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/opinion/the-next-step-in-drug-treatment.html', 'snippet': 'The country needs to get beyond the “drug war” approach to addiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mandatory-sentencing craze that drove up the prison population tenfold, pushing state corrections costs to bankrupting levels, was rooted in New York’s infamous Rockefeller drug laws. These laws, which mandated lengthy sentences for nonviolent, first-time offenders, were approved 40 years ago next month. They did little to curtail drug use in New York or in other states that mimicked them, while they filled prisons to bursting with nonviolent addicts who would have been more effectively and more cheaply dealt with through treatment programs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Next Step in Drug Treatment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Next Step in Drug Treatment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Academy of Medicine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Policy Alliance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T02:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/75521635-cc3f-5a0b-a6d5-5404660fe087', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75521635-cc3f-5a0b-a6d5-5404660fe087'}, {'abstract': 'The poor remain shortchanged as even the president caves in to Republican ridicule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/opinion/congress-rushes-to-aid-the-powerful.html', 'snippet': 'The poor remain shortchanged as even the president caves in to Republican ridicule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congress can’t pass a budget or control guns or confirm judges on time, but this week members of both parties found something they could agree on, and in a big hurry: avoiding blame for inconveniencing air travelers. The Senate and House rushed through a bill that would avert furloughs to air traffic controllers, which were mandated by Congress’s own sequester but proved embarrassing when flights began to back up around the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Rushes to Aid the Powerful', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress Rushes to Aid the Powerful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoyer, Steny H', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T02:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d6278ab-3831-5d64-a119-ca1cf4df4648', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d6278ab-3831-5d64-a119-ca1cf4df4648'}, {'abstract': 'New games, new friends and new perceptions, cou