icle', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ee0d9a6-1c26-5137-be58-20eff71f299d', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ee0d9a6-1c26-5137-be58-20eff71f299d'}, {'abstract': 'Chien-Ming Wang has pitched in Class AAA, and could force his way into a discussion about the Yankees’ rotation.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/26/wang-is-on-the-yankees-radar/', 'snippet': 'Chien-Ming Wang has pitched in Class AAA, and could force his way into a discussion about the Yankees’ rotation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former Yankee Chien-Ming Wang — whose 2008 foot injury derailed a promising young career — continued his strong start in the minors by allowing just one run in six and two-third innings for Class AAA Scranton/Wilkes-Barre on Thursday. In 12 innings this season, Wang — who was signed to a minor league contract in the off-season — has a 0.75 earned run average.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wang Is on the Yankees’ Radar', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Chien-Ming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T03:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Arangure Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arangure', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organiz