l': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30aa50b1-60ce-5ff7-a1d6-effee966b2fa', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30aa50b1-60ce-5ff7-a1d6-effee966b2fa'}, {'abstract': 'The city’s long-anticipated program of public bicycles makes its debut in May, and as stations turn up in parts of Brooklyn and Manhattan, the war of cyclists and drivers and pedestrians is expanding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/nyregion/sharing-bikes-and-fury-in-new-york-neighborhoods.html', 'snippet': 'The city’s long-anticipated program of public bicycles makes its debut in May, and as stations turn up in parts of Brooklyn and Manhattan, the war of cyclists and drivers and pedestrians is expanding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a very short time, New Yorkers will have the opportunity to show the world that they are just as virtuous, well-intentioned and offended by sloth as people in Copenhagen or Geneva or any other of a number of cities where mindful living and wonderful yogurts reign. The city’s long-anticipated bike share program is scheduled to make its debut in May, allowing New Yorkers to pick up and deposit rental bikes at hundreds of locations, most of them, so far, in some of the wealthiest neighborhoods. Anyone waking up on a Sunday morning in TriBeCa, finding nothing in her refrigerator and hankering to go to Smorgasburg in Dumbo, Brooklyn, for instance, will now be able to do that with relative ease. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28JPBIGCITY1_SPAN/28JPBIGCITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/28/nyregion/28JPBIGCITY1_SPAN/28JPBIGCITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201