 a seaworthy replica of the Titanic says he will use his vast fortune to form a new political party to compete in federal elections scheduled for September.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Plans to Build Titanic II, Australian Billionaire Forms a New Political Party', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Plans to Build Titanic II, Australian Billionaire Forms a New Political Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Clive', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T06:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a006f2a1-2bca-5e2c-9064-a20adf1b65aa', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a006f2a1-2bca-5e2c-9064-a20adf1b65aa'}, {'abstract': 'Austerity pushback in Euyrope; U.S. weighs strategy on Syria; test for immigration overhaul, and Europe small companies face challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/iht-quick-read-april-27/', 'snippet': 'Austerity pushback in Euyrope; U.S. weighs strategy on Syria; test for immigration overhaul, and Europe small companies face challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS After years of insisting that the primary cure for Europe’s malaise is to slash spending, the champions of austerity, most notably Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany, find themselves under intensified pressure to back off from unpopular remedies and find some way to restore faltering growth to the world’s largest economic bloc. On Friday, Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy of Spain, who once promoted aggressive budget cuts, became the latest leader to reject European Union targets for reducing deficits. Andrew Higgins reports from Brussels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/americas/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/25/world/americas/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/americas/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/americas/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/americas/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/25/world/americas/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/25/world/americas/20130425BORDER-slide-9EHZ/20130425BORDER-