ations', 'value': 'Gap Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Topshop', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uniqlo', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T07:05:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4f47dbc-44bc-5a4e-971a-db62bf92e101', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4f47dbc-44bc-5a4e-971a-db62bf92e101'}, {'abstract': 'Deportivo la Coruña has fought its way off the bottom of La Liga, but there is still much work to do to get the club’s house in order.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/off-the-bottom-but-not-yet-in-the-clear-in-la-corua/', 'snippet': 'Deportivo la Coruña has fought its way off the bottom of La Liga, but there is still much work to do to get the club’s house in order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stability breeding consistency doesn’t seem to be an adage favored by La Liga clubs, although the facts should perhaps be given more thought by trigger-happy presidents. Last season’s three relegated clubs — Villarreal, Sporting Gijon and Racing Santander — all changed managers at least once during the season. One would be forgiven, then, for being unforgiving of Deportivo la Coruña’s Primera Division status when in February, languishing at bottom of the league, they appointed their third manager of the campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Bottom but Not Yet in the Clear in La Coruña', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deportivo La Coruna (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T07:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel Marsden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marsden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53c256d5-c0c6-5db9-8053-af55cde80a22', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53c256d5-c0c6-5db9-8053-af55cde80a22'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama suggests that Congressional leaders care mainly about budget cuts that affect themselves, while Republicans see political motivations behind the cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/obama-and-g-o-p-spar-over-direction-of-cuts/', 'snippet': 'President Obama suggests that Congressional leaders care mainly about budget cuts that affect themselves, while Republicans see political motivations behind the cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama sparred with Congressional Republicans on Saturday over who was to blame for long flight delays this week, but neither side moved closer to a consensus on how to minimize the broader impact of federal spending cuts on the public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and G.O.P. Spar Over Direction of Cuts', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shuster, Bill', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Meals on Wheels', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T10:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85d81ce7-4f55-504e-a0d4-17902f9f0aef', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85d81ce7-4f55-504e-a0d4-17902f9f0aef'}, {'abstract': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/newswallah-bharat-edition-84/', 'snippet': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: Four policemen were killed in a village in north Kashmir on Friday in an ambush by suspected militants, The Indian Express reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T10:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By