as a former businessman, the Right Rev. Justin Welby might be worth listening to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Church of England was once known as the Conservative Party at prayer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/blogs/27rdv-welby/27rdv-welby-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/27/blogs/27rdv-welby/27rdv-welby-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/blogs/27rdv-welby/27rdv-welby-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/blogs/27rdv-welby/27rdv-welby-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/blogs/27rdv-welby/27rdv-welby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/27/blogs/27rdv-welby/27rdv-welby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/27/blogs/27rdv-welby/27rdv-welby-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Banking Advice From Britain’s Businessman Archbishop', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welby, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of England', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T11:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8c72237-b5bf-50c6-a9cd-5fd70556a2de', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8c72237-b5bf-50c6-a9cd-5fd70556a2de'}, {'abstract': 'Very bad policy.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/american-austerity-an-update/', 'snippet': 'Very bad policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is some tendency among economic commentators to think that austerity policies in a deeply depressed economy are mainly a European thing; you even find a fair number of people imagining that the United States is still engaged in fiscal stimulus. But the truth is that federal stimulus is years behind us, while state and local governments have cut back, so the overall story is one of fiscal contraction that’s smaller than in Europe, but not by that much.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Austerity, An Update', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T11:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9967bcc9-f8c4-5141-8d89-d17f9dc46d19', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9967bcc9-f8c4-5141-8d89-d17f9dc46d19'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants seemed very pleased with their first-round draft selection, but first he had to survive a smothering of hugs by friends and family upon his selection.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/justin-pugh-one-jolly-giant-on-draft-day/', 'snippet': 'The Giants seemed very pleased with their first-round draft selection, but first he had to survive a smothering of hugs by friends and family upon his selection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Giants seemed very pleased with their first-round draft selection: offensive lineman Justin Pugh of Syracuse, at No. 19 over all. The only concern might be his health after he was smothered by fans and family  in a raucous celebration following the Giants’ phone call on Thursday night. Luckily, he’s a big boy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justin Pugh, One Jolly Giant on Draft Day', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pugh, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T12:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a929882f-279b-5055-8b46-4b75cdfd361c', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a929882f-279b-5055-8b46-4b75cdfd361c'}, {'abstract': 'One way to make an argument, I guess.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/the-ignoramus-strategy/', 'snippet': 'One way to make an argument, I guess.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A while back Noah Smith described one common strategy for arguing against Keynesian economics, and yours truly in particular: “Relentlessly pretend to be an ignorant simpleton.” Of course, as always, this strategy is most effective if you aren’t pretending, and really are an ignorant simpleton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ignoramus Strategy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T12:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d745e91-186c-5743-a89f-2a06cc0307cf', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d745e91-186c-5743-a89f-2a06cc0307cf'}, {'abstract': 'A veteran earth scientist pushes back against dystopian depictions of global warming and the human response.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/an-earth-scientist-explores-the-biggest-climate-threat-fear/', 'snippet': 'A veteran earth scientist pushes back against dystopian depictions of global warming and the human response.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a “Your Dot” contribution pushing back against apocalyptic depictions of the collision between humans and the climate system — written by Peter B. Kelemen, the Arthur D. Storke Professor and vice chair in the Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences at Columbia University. Kelemen has done a lot of interesting work on possible ways 