pe_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd45d5d1-b145-5bb6-9e97-c56de2317ba5', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd45d5d1-b145-5bb6-9e97-c56de2317ba5'}, {'abstract': 'Some of New York State’s most talented musicians poured their hearts into a country/bluegrass tune about I’ll Have Another’s stirring quest for the Triple Crown.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/ill-have-anothers-triumphs-put-to-song/', 'snippet': 'Some of New York State’s most talented musicians poured their hearts into a country/bluegrass tune about I’ll Have Another’s stirring quest for the Triple Crown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was one of many horse racing fans that fell in love last year with I’ll Have Another as he partnered with jockey Mario Gutierrez to win the Robert B. Lewis Stakes, Santa Anita Derby, Kentucky Derby and Preakness Stakes. Bettors put the odds of this achievement at about 7,500 to 1. Gutierrez’s rides were masterful, and I’ll Have Another’s come from behind victories in the Derby and Preakness left the crowds screaming for more. Like all his fans, I was disappointed that an injury the week of the Belmont Stakes led to his retirement and sale to stud.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I’ll Have Another’s Triumphs Put to Song', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "I'll Have Another (Race Horse)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T17:07:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_na