 'value': 'My Cancer Genome', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foundation Medicine Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T17:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Eisenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bb60a40-3fef-5d47-92d6-68f4076ff909', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bb60a40-3fef-5d47-92d6-68f4076ff909'}, {'abstract': 'In the aftermath of the marathon, there are any number of easy and insufficient answers, but just one inescapable conclusion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/opinion/sunday/bruni-the-lesson-of-boston.html', 'snippet': 'In the aftermath of the marathon, there are any number of easy and insufficient answers, but just one inescapable conclusion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF only it were as simple as the drones coming home to roost. That would be comforting somehow. In giving us a tidy cause, it would give us a clear remedy: rain less death in distant lands, and worry less about death in our own.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lesson of Boston', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lesson of Boston', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Tamerlan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T17:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/899e3c01-bed2-545e-8dfd-2efd6a3ae2cb', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/899e3c01-bed2-545e-8dfd-2efd6a3ae2cb'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s sensible proposals could feed millions more people worldwide, and they should be promptly enacted by Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/opinion/sunday/food-aid-reform.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s sensible proposals could feed millions more people worldwide, and they should be promptly enacted by Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Food aid is one of the most important tools of American foreign policy. Since the mid-1950s, the United States has spent nearly $2 billion annually to feed the world’s poor, saving millions of lives. But the process is so rigid and outdated that many more people who could be helped still go hungry. Reforms proposed by President Obama will go a long way toward fixing that problem and should be promptly enacted by Congress.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Aid Reform', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Aid Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T17:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'p