ar in Syria were killed in a fire that engulfed four tents in the Zaatari refugee camp near Jordan’s northern border, the aid worker who runs the camp said Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 Young Brothers Die in Fire at Camp for Syria Refugees in Jordan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 Young Brothers Die in Fire at Camp for Syria Refugees in Jordan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T22:13:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8dfdbc2-094d-5f02-a4c5-292a761fa48b', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8dfdbc2-094d-5f02-a4c5-292a761fa48b'}, {'abstract': 'Family income is now a better predictor of children’s success in school than race.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/no-rich-child-left-behind/', 'snippet': 'Family income is now a better predictor of children’s success in school than race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a fact that may not surprise you: the children of the rich perform better in school, on average, than children from middle-class or poor families. Students growing up in richer families have better grades and higher standardized test scores, on average, than poorer students; they also have higher rates of participation in extracurricular activities and school leadership positions, higher graduation rates and higher rates of college enrollment and completion.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Rich Child Left Behind', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Rich Child Left Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-27T22:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean F. Reardon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Reardon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28a32d96-f64b-54dc-b1bb-c38eeb8bd374', 'word_count': 2203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28a32d96-f64b-54dc-b1bb-c38eeb8bd374'}, {'abstract': 'Developments in the Boston Marathon attacks and the civil war in Syria dominate the Sunday shows this week.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/27/sunday-breakfast-menu-april-28/', 'snippet': 'Developments in the Boston Marathon attacks and the civil war in Syria dominate the Sunday shows this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'National security and foreign affairs share the limelight on the Sunday political shows this week, featuring conversations a