hat used to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do we do with the things people leave behind? What does it mean to move on, from the death of someone you love, or a divorce, which is a death of a different kind?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Months After Newtown, Sorting Boxes of Grief', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochsprung, Dawn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown (Conn)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T12:57:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Lawton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lawton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bd81b96-075d-5515-ae83-f7a13428d3a1', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bd81b96-075d-5515-ae83-f7a13428d3a1'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Cahill scored two goals, his first of the season, as the Red Bulls won at Toronto, 2-1, on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/red-bulls-rewind-cahill-saves-the-day/', 'snippet': 'Tim Cahill scored two goals, his first of the season, as the Red Bulls won at Toronto, 2-1, on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Cahill’s long (inter)national nightmare of answering questions about not scoring goals is over … at least for now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/sports/soccer/rbny27/rbny27-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/28/sports/soccer/rbny27/rbny27-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/sports/soccer/rbny27/rbny27-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/sports/soccer/rbny27/rbny27-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/sports/soccer/rbny27/rbny27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/28/sports/soccer/rbny27/rbny27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/sports/soccer/rbny27/rbny27-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bulls Rewind: Cahill Saves the Day', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cahill, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T13:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b92c1842-01bc-5941-875f-4830072aded3', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b92c1842-01bc-5941-875f-4830072aded3'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Never Say Die: A Kentucky Colt, the Epsom Derby, and the Rise of the Modern Thoroughbred Industry.”', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/the-rail-booklshelf-never-say-die/', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Never Say Die: A Kentucky Colt, the Epsom Derby, and the Rise of the Modern Thoroughbred Industry.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the arrival of Derby Week brings horseracing fans’ simmering anticipation for the first Saturday in May to a full boil, it also provides an opportunity for some reflection on the sport’s rich history. Below, an excerpt from “Never Say Die: A Kentucky Colt, the Epsom Derby, and the Rise of the Modern Thoroughbred Industry.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rail Bookshelf: ‘Never Say Die’', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T14:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af97aa7f-1882-5c8e-be40-448498d893c9', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af97aa7f-1882-5c8e-be40-448498d893c9'}, {'abstract': 'After a smooth test flight to test troublesome batteries, Boeing and All Nippon Airways must now turn to a more delicate task — selling passengers on the idea that the Dreamliner is safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/business/global/29iht-dreamliner29.html', 'snippet': 'After a smooth test flight to test troublesome batteries, Boeing and All Nippon Airways must now turn to a more delicate task — selling passengers on the idea that the Dreamliner is safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANEDA AIRPORT, JAPAN — Katsuhiro Ogami, a top engineer at All Nippon Airways, could not sit still Sunday on the airline’s first test flight of a Boeing 787 Dreamliner jet fitted with fortified batteries. He peered, and peered again, at a monitor hooked to the plane’s batteries for any signs of overheating.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/global/29dreamliner_2/29dreamliner_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/29/business/global/29dreamliner_2/29dreamliner_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/global/29dreamliner_2/29dreamliner_2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/global/29dreamliner_2/29dreamliner_2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'