, 'snippet': 'Lawmakers in both parties urged President Obama to step up American involvement in the Syrian civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Republicans on Capitol Hill took President Obama to task Sunday for what they characterized as dangerous inaction in Syria, while Democrats urged the White House to step up its humanitarian response to the two-year-old civil war that has killed 70,000 people and displaced hundreds of thousands more.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Call for Stronger U.S. Action in Syria', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Warn of Inaction on Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellison, Keith', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T18:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5b3e150-90ab-5555-9fcb-da653c68d40e', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5b3e150-90ab-5555-9fcb-da653c68d40e'}, {'abstract': 'The wealth gap might still be growing, experts said, further dimming the prospects for economic advancement for current and future generations of nonwhite Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/business/racial-wealth-gap-widened-during-recession.html', 'snippet': 'The wealth gap might still be growing, experts said, further dimming the prospects for economic advancement for current and future generations of nonwhite Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Millions of Americans suffered a loss of wealth during the recession and the sluggish recovery that followed. But the last half-decade has proved far worse for black and Hispanic families than for white families, starkly widening the already large gulf in wealth between non-Hispanic white Americans and most minority groups, according to a new study from the Urban Institute.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wealth Gap      Among Races     Has Widened Since     Recession', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recession Worsened Wealth Gap For Races', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowrey, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Urban Institute', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T18:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac65425b-e83a-5043-837c-7180fe309f3a', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac65425b-e83a-5043-837c-7180fe309f3a'}, {'abstract': 'The Queensboro Motorcycle Club, founded in 1910, has had its clubhouse for 70 years wedged among the auto salvage shops in the Willets Point section of Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000002196501/after-103-years-still-rolling-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'The Queensboro Motorcycle Club, founded in 1910, has had its clubhouse for 70 years wedged among the auto salvage shops in the Willets Point section of Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Queensboro Motorcycle Club, founded in 1910, has had its clubhouse for 70 years wedged among the auto salvage shops in the Willets Point section of Queens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/multimedia/video-motorcyclegang/video-motorcyclegang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/28/multimedia/video-motorcyclegang/video-motorcyclegang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/28/multimedia/video-motorcyclegang/video-motorcyclegang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail