60s in her show a the Whitney Museum of American Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1960s, when she was in her 20s, Annette Peacock figured out how to write slow, spacious, long-form, highly original piano ballads as if the notes were falling naturally from her fingers, and that sounded, when ideally replayed, as if she were composing them all over again. She sang them with the full range of her voice, making them twice as good, with a kind of severe passion, only semi-sentimental, following their unsettling, unresolving melodic trajectories. They were somewhere between rudimentary and very achieved: new lieder, or some radically decelerated soul-jazz hybrid, or melted torch numbers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinions and Feelings, Years in the Making, Play Out', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opinions and Feelings, Years in the Making, Play Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peacock, Annette', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T20:59:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/32248065-2367-5566-bb3b-e84de4e9ded6', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32248065-2367-5566-bb3b-e84de4e9ded6'}, {'abstract': 'Answer Will Shortz’s question about the future venue of the American Crossword Puzzle Tournament in the comments, or send him an email.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/american-crossword-puzzle-tournament-brooklyn-or-stamford-a-special-message-from-will-shortz/', 'snippet': 'Answer Will Shortz’s question about the future venue of the American Crossword Puzzle Tournament in the comments, or send him an email.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 37th American Crossword Puzzle Tournament will be held March 7-9, 2014, at the Brooklyn Bridge Marriott, where the event has been for the past six years. Our contract with the hotel runs through then.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Crossword Puzzle Tournament — Brooklyn or Stamford? A Special Message from Will Shortz', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shortz, Will', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T21:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Shortz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shortz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cee0061-7b0b-5932-8374-80bc88668220', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cee0061-7b0b-5932-8374-80bc88668220'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Wilson brought his progressive-rock stylings to Manhattan as part of his North American tour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/arts/music/steven-wilson-at-the-best-buy-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Steven Wilson brought his progressive-rock stylings to Manhattan as part of his North American tour.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I think it’s fair to say that I’m probably not really known for my three-minute pop songs,” the English singer and multi-instrumentalist Steven Wilson said from the stage of the Best Buy Theater during his concert there on Friday night. “However, very occasionally, I can write something that clocks in at under 15 minutes that I think, you know what?, that’s not bad,” he continued as preface to “Postcard,” a four-and-a-half-minute ballad.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/wilson/wilson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/wilson/wilson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/wilson/wilson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/wilson/wilson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/wilson/wilson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/wilson/wilson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/wilson/wilson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Brushes Off the Constraints of Chart-Friendly Songs', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Artist Brushes Off the Constraints of Chart-Friendly Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T21:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6697ca0-e3db-5781-a739-9a61ba7b62e7', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6697ca0-e3db-5781-a739-9a61ba7b62e7'}, {'abstract': 'Preview performances are set to begin in February at the Winter Garden Theater, the lead producers announced on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/rocky-musical-is-heading-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Preview performances are set to begin in February at the Winter Garden Theater, the lead producers announced on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new stage musical “Rocky,” an adaptation of the Oscar-winning film about a streetwise boxer from Philadelphia, is coming to Broadway next year, with preview performances set to begin in February at the Winter Garden Theater, the lead producers announced on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Rocky’ Musical Is Heading to Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Broadway (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T21:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifi