 the 48 States” has its New York premiere at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During one section of “Gabriel’s Guide to the 48 States,” which received its New York premiere at Carnegie Hall on Saturday evening, the Orpheus Chamber Orchestra stood and sang a sacred harp hymn, a genre of a cappella choral music that evolved in the South. The excerpt came under the heading “Alabama,” one stop on a musical voyage from the young composer Gabriel Kahane that was commissioned by Orpheus to celebrate its 40th anniversary this year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/ORPHEUS/ORPHEUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/ORPHEUS/ORPHEUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/ORPHEUS/ORPHEUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/ORPHEUS/ORPHEUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1641, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/ORPHEUS/ORPHEUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/ORPHEUS/ORPHEUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/arts/ORPHEUS/ORPHEUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Here’s to the First 48, in Lessons of Word and Song', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here’s to the First 48, in Lessons of Word and Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahane, Gabriel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orpheus Chamber Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Works Progress Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T21:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8516de3e-2436-5926-ab90-917a8aba7e82', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8516de3e-2436-5926-ab90-917a8aba7e82'}, {'abstract': 'Built on lush portraits of human pathology, subscription- and ad-supported cable channels gradually became hotbeds of quality and profits, as detailed in “Difficult Men” by Brett Martin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/business/media/cable-tvs-shift-to-darker-dramas-proves-lucrative.html', 'snippet': 'Built on lush portraits of human pathology, subscription- and ad-supported cable channels gradually became hotbeds of quality and profits, as detailed in “Difficult Men” by Brett Martin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We used to turn on the television to see people who were happier, funnier, prettier versions of ourselves. But at