atical proof into the computer age, solving a longstanding problem concerning colors on a map with the help of an I.B.M. computer making billions of decisions, died on April 19 in Dover, N.H. He was 80.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/us/appel-obit/appel-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1001, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/29/us/appel-obit/appel-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1001}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/us/appel-obit/appel-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/us/appel-obit/appel-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 915, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/us/appel-obit/appel-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/29/us/appel-obit/appel-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/us/appel-obit/appel-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenneth I. Appel, Mathematician Who Harnessed Computer Power, Dies at 80', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenneth I. Appel, 80, Dies; Computerized Higher Math', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Overbye, Dennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appel, Kenneth I (1932-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T22:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Overbye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Overbye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/6876e7f7-fa76-5145-b9b6-61ad85c1ad74', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6876e7f7-fa76-5145-b9b6-61ad85c1ad74'}, {'abstract': 'NBC really does have a batch of shows that are working, despite a rough patch this spring that even induced a presidential-level joke on Saturday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/business/media/nbc-renews-5-dramas.html', 'snippet': 'NBC really does have a batch of shows that are working, despite a rough patch this spring that even induced a presidential-level joke on Saturday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NBC really does have a batch of shows that are working, despite a rough patch this spring that even induced a presidential-level joke on Saturday night. Last week NBC announced it was renewing five drama series, including two, “Revolution” and “Chicago Fire,” that the network introduced this season. “Grimm,” arguably the network’s most reliable drama, was another show that was renewed; it holds up Friday night for the network and has experienced a ratings increase of 14 percent this season. The ratings for “Law & Order Special Victims Unit” have descended to just about survival level, but that show will return in a move that has been a ritual for the network for 15 years. “Parenthood,” the well-regarded family drama that performed well this year (up 8 percent), had been truncated to only 15 episodes, a sign that the network did not have the most faith in its endurance before this season started. That was also a sign that cost was a factor in considering its fate: “Parenthood” has a big budget and an enormous cast, with several star-name actors, including Lauren Graham, Peter Krause and Dax Shepard. A renewal order had been in some doubt until last week because of those budget concerns, but NBC announced that “Parenthood” would be back and with a full order of 22 episodes. The NBC announcement didn’t stop President Obama from taking a little shot at the network’s prime-time woes at the White House Correspondents’ Dinner on Saturday night. Joking about his recent performance at a basketball demonstration, the president said: “I took 22 shots and made 2 of them. That’s right, 2 hits and 20 misses. The executives at NBC asked, ‘What’s your secret?’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Renews 5 Dramas', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NBC Renews 5 Dramas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T22:18:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/22e3aeb4-eb9b-5586-a176-36c31410c2b6', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22e3aeb4-eb9b-5586-a176-36c31410c2b6'}, {'abstract': 'The American Academy of Arts and Sciences announced that Bruce Springsteen, Pete Seeger and Herbie Hancock would be among the 198 newly elected members of its 2013 class', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/arts/american-academy-announces-newest-class.html', 'snippet': 'The American Academy of Arts and Sciences announced that Bruce Springsteen, Pete Seeger and Herbie Hancock would be among the 198 newly elected members of its 2013 class', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Academy of Arts and Sciences announced on Wednesday that Bruce Springsteen, Pete Seeger and Herbie Hancock would be among the 198 newly elected members of its 2013 class. Among the other artists, writers, scientists and philanthropists who will be inducted in a ceremony scheduled for Oct. 12 in Cambridge, Mass., are Robert De Niro and Sally Field; the poets Annie Dillard and Natasha Trethewey; and the filmmaker Jonas Mekas, a co-founder of the Anthology Film Archives in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Academy Announces Newest Class', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Academy Announces Newest Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ACADEMY OF ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hancock, Herbie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seeger, Pete', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T22:21:46+0000', 'docum