igned a deal with Spiegel & Grau for a characteristically eclectic book, with a planned fall 2015 release.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Beastie Boys wrote a book, you might expect it to depart from standard memoir form. Rather than a strict narrative patiently winding its way from bygone days, such a book might — in keeping with the group’s hypereclectic style — be a pastiche of voices, images, irreverent humor and pop-culture reference points.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/29band/29band-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/29/business/29band/29band-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/29band/29band-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/29band/29band-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/29band/29band-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/29/business/29band/29band-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/business/29band/29band-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beastie Boys Sign a Memoir Deal', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beastie Boys Sign A Memoir Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beastie Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Janklow & Nesbit Associates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Sacha (1971- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T22:49:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8db9e79d-759b-535a-a7a9-d910ec202513', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8db9e79d-759b-535a-a7a9-d910ec202513'}, {'abstract': 'How can science, philosophy and a work of pure imagination meet to deepen our understanding of the physical world?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/28/borges-and-the-paradox-of-the-seenk/', 'snippet': 'How can science, philosophy and a work of pure imagination meet to deepen our understanding of the physical world?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1927 a young German physicist published a paper that would turn the scientific world on its head. Until that time, classical physics had assumed that when a particle’s position and velocity were known, its future trajectory could be calculated. Werner Heisenberg demonstrated that this condition was actually impossible: we cannot know with precision both a particle’s location and its velocity, and the more precisely we know the one, the less we can know the other. Five years later he was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics for having laid the foundations of quantum physics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Borges, Particles and the Paradox of the Perceived', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borges, Jorge Luis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heisenberg, Werner', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hume, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T23:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Egginton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egginton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19b7f9c0-3b25-533e-91e0-2099cad1cfa2', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19b7f9c0-3b25-533e-91e0-2099cad1cfa2'}, {'abstract': 'All but one of the channels are aligned with Sunni financial backers, and the Iraqi government said the channels were inciting sectarian conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/world/middleeast/iraq-suspends-al-jazeera-and-other-tv-channels.html', 'snippet': 'All but one of the channels are aligned with Sunni financial backers, and the Iraqi government said the channels were inciting sectarian conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Iraq’s government on Sunday revoked the operating licenses of Al Jazeera and nine other television channels, saying that they were inciting sectarian conflict. All but one of the channels are aligned with Sunni financial backers, and the move was widely perceived as a crackdown on dissent by the Shiite-led government that is facing an increasingly violent Sunni uprising.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq Revokes Licenses of Al Jazeera and 9 Other TV Channels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq Revokes Licenses of Al Jazeera and Other TV Channels Amid Sunni Uprising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arango, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barazanji, Riad', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anwar 2', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baghdad TV', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Sharqiya', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-28T23:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 