ations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T01:22:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b54c455d-262f-5f37-9d03-7f13b97bcf3d', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b54c455d-262f-5f37-9d03-7f13b97bcf3d'}, {'abstract': 'Cigarette packages are unlikely to carry graphic warning labels anytime soon as a result of actions by the Supreme Court and the F.D.A.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/opinion/wins-and-losses-in-the-fight-against-tobacco.html', 'snippet': 'Cigarette packages are unlikely to carry graphic warning labels anytime soon as a result of actions by the Supreme Court and the F.D.A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cigarette packages are unlikely to carry graphic warning labels anytime soon as a result of separate actions by the Supreme Court and the Food and Drug Administration. That is a setback, though perhaps temporary, for the federal government’s campaign to reduce the health damage caused by this highly lethal product. The silver lining is that the Supreme Court left intact most of the F.D.A.’s powers to regulate this industry. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wins and Losses in the Fight Against Tobacco', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wins and Losses in the Fight Against Tobacco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T01:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/353e7637-ca53-594f-97ed-51bdb03b43b0', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/353e7637-ca53-594f-97ed-51bdb03b43b0'}, {'abstract': 'In the age of the almighty search engine, do we have a right to be forgotten?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/opinion/keller-erasing-history.html', 'snippet': 'In the age of the almighty search engine, do we have a right to be forgotten?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of my favorite coffee-table books is an odd volume called “The Commissar Vanishes,” a portfolio of doctored photographs from Stalin’s Russia. When Stalin purged one of his fellow Bolsheviks, the comrade who fell from favor was duly cropped or airbrushed out of official photographs. “The Commissar Vanishes” juxtaposes the before and after. Here is the party stalwart grinning alongside Lenin in Red Square; and now — poof! — he’s gone. Person, un-person. History, un-history. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Erasing History', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Erasing History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reputation.com Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T01:22:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d46b305-d9a4-52c0-b2e9-b5faec5bc643', 'word_count': 1458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d46b305-d9a4-52c0-b2e9-b5faec5bc643'}, {'abstract': 'The federal firearms agency doesn’t have the resources or the power to do its job, and it’s because the gun lobby and its allies like it that way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/opinion/congressional-restraints-on-gun-safety.html', 'snippet': 'The federal firearms agency doesn’t have the resources or the power to do its job, and it’s because the gun lobby and its allies like it that way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the cynical arguments that Senate members recently invoked in ducking their responsibility to enact stronger gun controls was that the government first needed to enforce laws already on the books. The hollow, Catch-22 reality of this position has been underlined by a new inspector general’s report pointing out that a severely understaffed and underfinanced federal firearms agency failed to inspect nearly 60 percent of the nation’s 125,000 licensed gun dealers in the last five years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congressional Restraints on Gun Safety', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congressional Restraints on Gun Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T01:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e7aa4df-0df1-5073-b5d9-c146219a9cc6', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e7aa4df-0df1-5073-b5d9-c146219a9cc6'}, {'abstract': 'Addressing the underreported epidemic requires a credible prosecution system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/opinion/next-steps-on-military-sexual-assaults.html', 'snippet': 'Addressing the underreported epidemic requires a credible prosecution system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last big health survey of active-duty American military personnel, conducted in 2011 and released last week, one in five female service members said they had been subjected to unwanted sexual contact since joining the military. That shocking statistic squares with other alarming indicators of the military’s pervasive culture of sexual misconduct. It also underscores the urgent need to change that culture. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Next Steps on Military Sexual Assaults', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Next Steps on Military Sexual Assaults', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], '