bled on because of their color, but when they reach the gate, whether you like a dark bay or a gray, it’s all about the same factors: pace, form and racing luck, not whether the horse has “horrible markings.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Horses are identified by markings: Colors, like chestnut, bay, dark bay or brown, gray or roan, are the most popular ones. And white socks, stars, stripes and stockings are among the other ways that horses are identified.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Markings Matter? Not in the Starting Gate', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T03:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruno De Julio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruno', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Julio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7426591-8ed1-5f15-aa45-b3d5b52d1278', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7426591-8ed1-5f15-aa45-b3d5b52d1278'}, {'abstract': 'In the wake of their Game 4 loss in triple overtime, the Nets are seeking what they have been missing at times this season: mental toughness and physical play inside. The Bulls lead the series, 3-1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/sports/basketball/nets-must-dig-deep-to-stay-with-and-beat-the-bulls.html', 'snippet': 'In the wake of their Game 4 loss in triple overtime, the Nets are seeking what they have been missing at times this season: mental toughness and physical play inside. The Bulls lead the series, 3-1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Nets did not practice on Sunday, but most of the team was at the training complex anyway, receiving treatment on sore limbs and largely licking the wounds from a three-overtime heartbreaker in Game 4 on Saturday that put them behind by 3-1 in the first-round playoff series against the Chicago Bulls.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Triply Hard Loss, Nets Must Find  Heart to Stay With  Bulls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Triply Hard Loss, Nets Must Find the Heart to Stay With the Bulls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlesimo, P J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T03:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a28a5e09-2a73-5745-b2e1-6954f60dd75d', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a28a5e09-2a73-5745-b2e1-6954f60dd75d'}, {'abstract': 'LeBron James led the Heat with 30 points in a victory over the Bucks in Milwaukee, setting up a second-round series with the Nets or Bulls. Dwyane Wade rested a sore right knee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/sports/basketball/heat-sweep-as-dwyane-wade-sits-and-lebron-james-scores-30.html', 'snippet': 'LeBron James led the Heat with 30 points in a victory over the Bucks in Milwaukee, setting up a second-round series with the Nets or Bulls. Dwyane Wade rested a sore right knee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — LeBron James and Dwyane Wade have pushed each other on the court since James joined the Miami Heat in the summer of 2010. On Sunday, James exerted his influence off the court.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/NBA/NBA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/NBA/NBA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 785}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/NBA/NBA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/NBA/NBA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1567, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/NBA/NBA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/NBA/NBA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/NBA/NBA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Asks Wade to Sit, Then Picks Up the Slack', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'James Asks Wade to Sit, Then Picks Up the Slack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Nate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Bucks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T03:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcf42179-9e83-59d1-9a28-4127c37597c1', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcf42179-9e83-59d1-9a28-4127c37597c1'}, {'abstract': 'Center Derek Stepan led the Rangers with 44 points this season, but it was his pace over the last 30 games that proved critical to the team’s playoff run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/sports/hockey/derek-stepans-game-carries-more-weight-than-his-name.html', 'snippet': 'Center Derek Stepan led the Rangers with 44 points this season, but it was his pace over the last 30 games that proved critical to the team’s playoff run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Rangers open their first-round playoff series against the Capitals in Washington on Thursday, all eyes will be on the bigger names like Rick Nash, Ryan Callahan and, of course, Alex Ovechkin. But the key to the Rangers’ success may lie with a forward who does not have the same name recognition, but appears well on his way: center Derek Stepan.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'heig