ue': 'Cervix', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ovarian Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ovaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uterus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T04:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/757b39cd-984d-5163-b143-86f81a5fa376', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/757b39cd-984d-5163-b143-86f81a5fa376'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 111 New York Times article in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/word-of-the-day-knead/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 111 New York Times article in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'knead •\\ˈned\\• verb', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | knead', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T04:08:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89539fa8-e379-5f3a-84b5-09f0a71b23b2', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89539fa8-e379-5f3a-84b5-09f0a71b23b2'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/arts/television/tv-schedule-for-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Bravo) THE QUEEN OF VERSAILLES (2012) The director Lauren Greenfield traces the lives of David Siegel, the billionaire founder of the Westgate Resorts time-share business, and his wife, Jackie, a former model 31 years his junior, as they embark on the construction of what is to be the largest home in America. The couple, above, plan to build a 90,000-square-foot mansion with 10 kitchens, a 6,000-square-foot master suite, a bowling alley, two tennis courts and a roller rink, modeled after the palace of Versailles in France and with room for their 8 children, 19 household employees and array of pets. But their blueprints don’t take into account the financial crisis. On the eve of the Sundance Film Festival in January 2012, Mr. Siegel sued Ms. Greenfield for defamation, alleging that “The Queen of Versailles” depicted Westgate Resorts “in an array of defamatory, derogatory and damaging ways.” Ms. Greenfield won the directing award at the festival, where this documentary was nominated for the grand jury prize.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T04:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/df79228e-6d71-5341-8c89-fac43ac34b79', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df79228e-6d71-5341-8c89-fac43ac34b79'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on April 29, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/pageoneplus/c