n Las Vegas. Also, do you think you understand your own business?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in Small Business: 6,297 Chinese Restaurants', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T11:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da93352d-78ed-5608-909c-32aedb7c23c6', 'word_count': 1713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da93352d-78ed-5608-909c-32aedb7c23c6'}, {'abstract': 'There are now 6,400 international schools all over the world, with new ones opening all the time. A job fair in London is a snapshot of Western teachers desperate for a job meeting up with institutions desperate to fill their ranks. Have you studied or taught at an international school? Tell us your experiences.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/international-schools-boom-as-more-seek-education-in-english/', 'snippet': 'There are now 6,400 international schools all over the world, with new ones opening all the time. A job fair in London is a snapshot of Western teachers desperate for a job meeting up with institutions desperate to fill their ranks. Have you studi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A century ago, there were only a handful of international schools in the world, mostly set up by Western corporations so overseas employees would have a place to educate their children. (Shell has had one in Borneo since the 1920s, after it discovered oil there in the 1910s). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/blogs/educ29-rdv/educ29-rdv-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/29/blogs/educ29-rdv/educ29-rdv-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/blogs/educ29-rdv/educ29-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/blogs/educ29-rdv/educ29-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/blogs/educ29-rdv/educ29-rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/29/blogs/educ29-rdv/educ29-rdv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/29/blogs/educ29-rdv/educ29-rdv-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'International Schools Boom as More Seek Education in English', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T11:03:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20f53dcc-fe0b-50fb-bb01-f05f630ffd66', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20f53dcc-fe0b-50fb-bb01-f05f630ffd66'}, {'abstract': 'Alfredo Sáenz decided to leave the Spanish bank, which he helped lead to international prominence, after a court reversed a pardon he received in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/santanders-chief-executive-resigns/', 'snippet': 'Alfredo Sáenz decided to leave the Spanish bank, which he helped lead to international prominence, after a court reversed a pardon he received in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:29 p.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confronted by Renewed Legal Problems, Chief of Santander Resigns', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Confronted by Renewed Legal Problems, Chief of Santander Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saenz, Alfredo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Banco Santander S A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T11:08:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott and Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c112de8-a266-58b5-bf0e-223a4c524787', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c112de8-a266-58b5-bf0e-223a4c524787'}, {'abstract': 'After a Twitter hoax caused the Dow to drop temporarily by 150 points, regulators are increasingly concerned about the combination of social media and high-frequency trading.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/daily-report-hoax-on-twitter-that-moved-markets-raises-worries/', 'snippet': 'After a Twitter hoax caused the Dow to drop temporarily by 150 points, regulators are increasingly concerned about the combination of social media and high-frequency trading.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Could the global economy hinge on 140 characters?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Hoax on Twitter That Moved Markets Raises Worries', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T11:13:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ab484d-f007-5d54-a205-c5afe71d4e09', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ab484d-f007-5d54-a205-c5afe71d4e09'}, {'abstract': 'Pittsburgh’s selection of the Georgia linebacker was an illustration of the trust the Steelers have in developing players.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/why-jarvis-jones-was-perfect-pick-for-steelers/', 'snippet': 'Pittsburgh’s selection of the Georgia linebacker was an illustration of the trust the Steelers have in developing players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From a conceptual standpoint, Pittsburgh’s selection of the Georgia pass rusher\xa0 Jarvis Jones might be the best pick in the 2013 N.F.L. draft. Just about every mock draft had Pittsburgh taking the Georgia pass rusher 17th over all (which is where he wound up). We have no idea if Jones will ultimately prove those mockers and Steelers General Manager Kevin Colbert right. Many believe he will, but only time will tell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Jarvis Jones Was Perfect Pick for Steelers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T11:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d7f04bb-3b36-5b1c-a85c-42801653fb68', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d7f04bb-3b36-5b1c-a85c-42801653fb68'}, {'abstract': 'Frank J. Bisignano is leaving JPMorgan Chase for the First Data Corporation. | Alfredo Sáenz resigned from Banco Santander on Monday. | Companies offering so-called pension advances to retirees are drawing scrutiny from Congress and the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau. | Barron’s argues that Dell stock seems like an attractive investment.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/another-departure-at-jpmorgan/', 'snippet': 'Frank J. Bisignano is leaving JPMorgan Chase for the First Data Corporation. | Alfredo Sáenz resigned from Banco Santander on Monday. | Companies offering so-called pension advances to retirees are drawing scrutiny from Congress and the Consumer F...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank J. Bisignano, co-chief operating officer of JPMorgan Chase, is leaving the bank to become chief executive of the payment processing firm First Data Corporation, according to a statement on Sunday by the bank’s chief executive, Jamie Dimon. Matthew E. Zames, who shared the chief operating officer role with Mr. Bisignano, will take over all aspects of the job, effective immediately, Jessica Silver-Greenberg reports in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Departure at JPMorgan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T12:04:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/801d9288-6c67-561d-b039-625acc00ee18', 'word_count': 1978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/801d9288-6c67-561d-b039-625acc00ee18'}, {'abstract': 'Savor the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/crossing-the-tmz/', 'snippet': 'Savor the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No, not DMZ — TMZ. I don’t know how much people pay attention to Technorati these days, or even how they compile their index, but this is still fun to see:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crossing the TMZ', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T12:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a4bbc2f-4874-5f0e-aeb9-fa3050bcabbe', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a4bbc2f-4874-5f0e-aeb9-fa3050bcabbe'}, {'abstract': 'Europe’s hostels go upscale, rethinking the annual pelvic exam, why rent is so high in New York and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/monday-reading-europes-hostels-go-upscale/', 'snippet': 'Europe’s hostels go upscale, rethinking the annual pelvic exam, why rent is so high in New York and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Europe’s Hostels Go Upscale', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T12:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0220195d-dcee-5abd-8173-5bd47b929ad2', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0220195d-dcee-5abd-8173-5bd47b929ad2'}, {'abstract': 'Check out those low, low yields.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/the-italian-miracle/', 'snippet': 'Check out those low, low yields.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Italy is a mess. Yes, it has a prime minster, finally; but the chances of serious economic reform are minimal, the willingness to persist in ever-harsher austerity — which the Rehns of this world tell us is essential — is evaporating. It’s all bad. But a funny thing is happening:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Italian Miracle', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T12:27:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa6400c-f6fe-595a-8a5f-80965c2d9044', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa6400c-f6fe-595a-8a5f-80965c2d9044'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court rejected an argument by the terminally ill woman that the decriminalization of suicide in Irish law necessarily conferred a right to die.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/world/europe/woman-loses-appeal-for-assisted-death-in-ireland.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court rejected an argument by the terminally ill woman that the decriminalization of suicide in Irish law necessarily conferred a right to die.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — A terminally ill woman in the final stages of multiple sclerosis does not have the right to an assisted death, the Irish Supreme Court ruled Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Irish Woman Loses Appeal for Assisted Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Irish Woman Loses Appeal for Assisted Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalby, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleming, Marie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Multiple Sclerosis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denham, Susan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T12:37:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Dalby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/802f4ac8-3835-5e4c-abc0-94a2ad48f030', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/802f4ac8-3835-5e4c-abc0-94a2ad48f030'}, {'abstract': 'Ark, the children’s charity founded by the hedge fund manager Arpad A. Busson, is no longer holding its $15,500-a-ticket fund-raiser that had become an annual fixture for London’s top hedge fund managers and celebrities.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/financiers-charity-gala-goes-the-way-of-canaps/', 'snippet': 'Ark, the children’s charity founded by the hedge fund manager Arpad A. Busson, is no longer holding its $15,500-a-ticket fund-raiser that had become an annual fixture for London’s top hedge fund managers and celebrities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Every spring, top financiers would mingle with royalty and guests like Madonna, Bill Clinton and Kevin Spacey for a gala to raise money for programs to improve literacy in India and fight AIDS in Africa. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financiers’ Charity Gala Goes the Way of Canapés', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GLG Partners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marshall Wace LLP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T13:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95b74a7b-b159-5814-ac1f-407154a95bd5', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95b74a7b-b159-5814-ac1f-407154a95bd5'}, {'abstract': 'A Guinness world record holder tried to cross a West Bengal river using his hair.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/in-indiaa-guinness-world-record-attempt-goes-horribly-wrong/', 'snippet': 'A Guinness world record holder tried to cross a West Bengal river using his hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Year after year, stunt after stunt, Indians have had their names imprinted in the Guinness Book of World Records, that official chronicler of human achievement that is often the gatekeeper of the eclectic and the bizarre. One Indian man has the world’s longest mustache, while another was once lauded for the world’s longest fingernails. Yet another struggled to retain his records in the book by attempting all sorts of titles: from writing on a grain of rice to stacking the tallest single column of coins. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtyp