nytimes.com/2013/04/29/video-a-conversation-with-traffic-screenwriter-stephen-gaghan/', 'snippet': 'The reporter Ginger Thompson talks with Stephen Gaghan, the screenwriter who won an Academy Award for “Traffic,” about the ways in which the movie verged on real life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life imitates art in a New York Times article that looks at the events that inspired Steven Soderbergh’s movie “Traffic.” The article focuses on a former Mexican police official who helped hunt down drug traffickers, much like the character Benicio Del Toro so memorably portrayed in the Oscar-winning movie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: A Conversation With the ‘Traffic’ Screenwriter Stephen Gaghan', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T13:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginger Thompson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thompson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6603a4db-186d-5f0f-81c0-7b501f23d1e9', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6603a4db-186d-5f0f-81c0-7b501f23d1e9'}, {'abstract': 'The brand ambassadors of America’s Best Racing are seeking to bring the excitement of horse racing to the people, to expose and cultivate a new fan base and highlight that racing is a sports and entertainment experience that offers something for everyone.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/a-wire-to-wire-ride-on-the-americas-best-racing-bus/', 'snippet': 'The brand ambassadors of America’s Best Racing are seeking to bring the excitement of horse racing to the people, to expose and cultivate a new fan base and highlight that racing is a sports and entertainment experience that offers something for e...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The excitement of a horse race is legendary – the starting gate bursts open, hooves thunder, silks flash, legs claw frantically forward, the crowd roars, a horse’s nose crosses the finish line. In less than two minutes, a mini-drama is enacted. The stands are full of passionate fans, some who almost won and some who did and are on top of the world. Horse racing is a sport with a long and rich history as well as a colorful present. This kind of energy is a primal experience that most people only read about in books and watch in movies and television. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wire-to-Wire Ride on the America’s Best Racing Bus', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T14:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Garofalo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garofalo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd633c10-d02c-5d27-9478-bf2328ed58a9', 'word_count': 1189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd633c10-d02c-5d27-9478-bf2328ed58a9'}, {'abstract': 'Why not this time?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/the-protectionist-non-surge/', 'snippet': 'Why not this time?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: The paper was by Eichengreen and Irwin, not O’Rourke — sorry, Doug.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Protectionist Non-Surge', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_ki