eeks ago to stop writing a Saturday gun report and instead do a weekend roundup. One thing we’ve since discovered is that there are so many shootings on the weekends that it is hard to keep track of them all. It also makes for very discouraging reading, as you can see.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Gun Report: April 26-28, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pensacola (Fla)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wilmington (Del)', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T14:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d888f272-3e66-53c5-b6d9-032008b62b52', 'word_count': 1799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d888f272-3e66-53c5-b6d9-032008b62b52'}, {'abstract': 'Using a different brand of tires on the Honda Fit Sport appears to be the cause of a 44,000-vehicle recall.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/honda-recalls-44000-fit-sports-over-stability-control-issue/', 'snippet': 'Using a different brand of tires on the Honda Fit Sport appears to be the cause of a 44,000-vehicle recall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A switch in tire brand may be the cause of a recall of nearly 44,000 2012-13 Honda Fit Sport models. Tests conducted by the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration uncovered a problem with the cars’ electronic stability control system.\xa0 Honda said in a report filed with the safety agency that the software would be updated on the electronic stability control, which it called Vehicle Stability Assist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honda Recalls 44,000 Fit Sports Over Stability Control Issue', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major'