1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f1116c1-2e90-5e13-9c03-cf1eba63a6dd', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f1116c1-2e90-5e13-9c03-cf1eba63a6dd'}, {'abstract': 'Whether an owner supports the law is not necessarily determined by how onerous it will be. “We don’t have to be told to do it,” said one owner.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/paid-sick-leave-has-some-business-owners-feeling-ill/', 'snippet': 'Whether an owner supports the law is not necessarily determined by how onerous it will be. “We don’t have to be told to do it,” said one owner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the advocates at Family Forward Oregon sought to muster support among businesses in Portland for a local paid sick leave ordinance, they found a sympathetic ear in Tony Fuentes. Mr. Fuentes and his wife operate Milagros Boutique, which sells cloth diapers and clothing for babies and children on Portland’s northeast side.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paid Sick Leave Has Some Business Owners Feeling Ill', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paid Sick Leave\r\nIrks Some Owners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Benefits', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nutter, Michael A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'o