: 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T16:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c91ad2-fa42-5aed-a270-dbafe4f02d63', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55c91ad2-fa42-5aed-a270-dbafe4f02d63'}, {'abstract': 'The glories of spring are at a peak, and the tulips and hyacinths reflect the diversity of present-day fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/video-on-the-street-sketching-in-pastels/', 'snippet': 'The glories of spring are at a peak, and the tulips and hyacinths reflect the diversity of present-day fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The glories of spring are at a peak, and the tulips and hyacinths reflect the diversity of present-day fashion. The green of the trees is as fresh as the grass on a Swiss mountainside, forming a lacy canopy over all. Cherry blossoms are ready to bloom, and art students set up their easels in the parks. Women headed to a lecture on ecosystems at the American Museum of Natural History. On Earth Day, 100 young volunteers, all employees of Macy’s, spread mulch around the trees surrounding the museum and painted its fence. And what would spring be without balloons, their bright colors reflected in a red pleated shawl. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: On the Street, Sketching in Pastels', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T16:04:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f6fb895-3599-5d66-afb0-cf0e3d6f90eb', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f6fb895-3599-5d66-afb0-cf0e3d6f90eb'}, {'abstract': 'With an expanded budget for dividends and stock buybacks, Apple could be on track to borrow nearly $20 billion a year, putting the company in the same issuance ballpark as huge global banks.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/apple-of-the-debt-markets-eye/', 'snippet': 'With an expanded budget for dividends and stock buybacks, Apple could be on track to borrow nearly $20 billion a year, putting the company in the same issuance ballpark as huge global banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple may need to make its i.o.u.’s as desirable as iPhones. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple and the Debt Market', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T16:07:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Agnes T. Crane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/272cf4c5-ea33-51dd-bcc1-12389f27dac2', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/272cf4c5-ea33-51dd-bcc1-12389f27dac2'}, {'abstract': 'In east Midtown, among all the glass giants and the sameness, there are still some Lilliputian buildings that have held out against the tide of bigger and taller.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/nyregion/as-east-midtown-girds-for-taller-buildings-a-few-knee-high-relics-remain.html', 'snippet': 'In east Midtown, among all the glass giants and the sameness, there are still some Lilliputian buildings that have held out against the tide of bigger and taller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barbara Connolly has rented an apartment in the same slender town house for 42 years. Her neighbors include three small brownstones, two well-worn stoops, a Halal Indian restaurant wedged into a narrow storefront, and an income-tax preparation company a flight up from the street. And also the Chrysler Building.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/30/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i