s to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/triple-play-baseball-quiz-week-4-results/', 'snippet': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Marlins’ Giancarlo Stanton found his power stroke just in time to affect two of our questions last week. He hit three homers over the weekend to become the answer to No. 1. And his two home runs on Sunday helped the Marlins avoid a sweep and score 13 runs in their series against the Cubs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Triple Play: Week 4 Results', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T16:31:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/511c353d-d5fe-5e53-ba82-7c7819897b88', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/511c353d-d5fe-5e53-ba82-7c7819897b88'}, {'abstract': 'By revealing his orientation, Jason Collins became the first openly gay male athlete playing in a major team sport.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/sports/basketball/nba-center-jason-collins-comes-out-as-gay.html', 'snippet': 'By revealing his orientation, Jason Collins became the first openly gay male athlete playing in a major team sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 12 seasons as an N.B.A. player, Jason Collins has never been an All-Star or a scoring leader or even a full-time starter, but on Monday he shattered one of the last great barriers in professional sports. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cred