-in-brain-help-map-out-space.html', 'snippet': 'Grid cells, which fire when animals move through specific, regularly spaced positions, form a hexagonal pattern that spans, for each cell, the entire local space available to the animal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The \xa0grid cells that Edvard I. Moser and May-Britt Moser found in the brains of rats generate such precise patterns that a review article the couple wrote was titled “Crystals of the Brain.”\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/science/0430-sci-PROFILE/0430-sci-PROFILE-jumbo.gif', 'height': 467, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/science/0430-sci-PROFILE/0430-sci-PROFILE-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 467, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/science/0430-sci-PROFILE/0430-sci-PROFILE-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/30/science/0430-sci-PROFILE/0430-sci-PROFILE-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/science/0430-sci-PROFILE/0430-sci-PROFILE-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grid Cells: ‘Crystals of the Brain’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grid Cells: ‘Crystals of the Brain’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'maj