nsemble-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The American Soundscapes ensemble’s performance at Carnegie Hall was the culmination of a five-day workshop for young musicians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles Ives’s Symphony No. 4, performed recently by the New York Philharmonic, features music of such metrical complexity that two conductors are often used to keep order. Similarly, Elliott Carter suggested that two conductors should marshal the disparate elements of the coda of his “Double Concerto” (1961), which received an excellent performance on Wednesday evening at Zankel Hall by the American Soundscapes ensemble. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Generation Greets the Complexities of the Past', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Generation Greets the Complexities of the Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T20:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba877a5e-5f7d-5655-a219-a9305b566777', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba877a5e-5f7d-5655-a219-a9305b566777'}, {'abstract': 'Hugh Herr lost both of his legs below the knee in 1982. Today he designs computerized prostheses and artificial body parts as director of the biomechatronics research group 