y Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a228b9eb-fe3c-54ca-a7e1-c4f294685ed4', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a228b9eb-fe3c-54ca-a7e1-c4f294685ed4'}, {'abstract': 'The Montreal Alouettes have the negotiating rights to Tim Tebow, but the team has an established quarterback in Anthony Calvillo.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/tebow-to-canada-not-so-fast/', 'snippet': 'The Montreal Alouettes have the negotiating rights to Tim Tebow, but the team has an established quarterback in Anthony Calvillo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Tebow, after being released by the Jets on Monday, is without a job, and his prospects of latching on with another N.F.L. team are uncertain. The Montreal Alouettes of the Canadian Football League own Tebow’s negotiating rights. So, off to Canada he goes, right?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tebow to Canada? Not So Fast', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calvillo, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Russell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montreal Alouettes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T21:42:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/696338be-af47-59b2-91b2-0ac83f3fe3d1', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/696338be-af47-59b2-91b2-0ac83f3fe3d1'}, {'abstract': 'In “Khmeropédies III: Source/Primate,” a Cambodian troupe turned monkey impersonations into a performance that blended dance and mime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/arts/dance/khmeropedies-iii-and-amrita-performing-arts-at-the-guggenheim.html', 'snippet': 'In “Khmeropédies III: Source/Primate,” a Cambodian troupe turned monkey impersonations into a performance that blended dance and mime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty five minutes of monkey impersonations? Dressed only in undershirts and shorts, seven male dancers of the Cambodian Amrita Performing Arts institution held the audience’s attention on Sunday evening at the Guggenheim Museum with unfailing skill and charm. The dancers are all specialists in the role of the monkey from the Cambodian classical masked dance known as Lakhaon Kaol; but here only one of them ever donned a mask, and then only briefly. The production, choreographed by Emmanuèle Phuon, was called “Khmeropédies III: Source/Primate”; I’m sorry I missed the chance to see parts I and II. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/arts/season/season-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/30/arts/season/season-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/arts/season/season-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': 