aham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T21:57:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer A. Kingson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Kingson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Summary', '_id': 'nyt://article/59f1dc47-2ba0-5fec-b61f-701c2ec4f5c2', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59f1dc47-2ba0-5fec-b61f-701c2ec4f5c2'}, {'abstract': 'The N.B.A.’s relocation committee recommended that the  owners deny a request to move the Sacramento Kings to Seattle, a decision that will probably settle a bidding war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/sports/basketball/nbas-kings-likely-to-remain-in-sacramento.html', 'snippet': 'The N.B.A.’s relocation committee recommended that the  owners deny a request to move the Sacramento Kings to Seattle, a decision that will probably settle a bidding war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.B.A.’s relocation committee on Monday unanimously recommended that the league’s owners reject a request to move the Sacramento Kings to Seattle, a decision that will probably keep the team in California and settle a contentious bidding war.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sacramento Kings Are Likely to Stay Put', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Committee Advises Owners to Reject a Kings Move to Seattle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sacramento Kings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sacramento (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T22:16:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afcd227d-ad8a-5460-a328-1dbd89b96f95', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afcd227d-ad8a-5460-a328-1dbd89b96f95'}, {'abstract': 'In a legal decision, a fascinating discussion about meaning, expression and how we evaluate artistic intent.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/whose-art-is-it-anyway/', 'snippet': 'In a legal decision, a fascinating discussion about meaning, expression and how we evaluate artistic intent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Second Circuit Court of Appeals ruled last week on a copyright dispute that pitted the photographer Patrick Cariou against the artist Richard Prince. The court decided in favor of Prince, reversing a 2011 federal ruling in which he was found to have used Cariou’s photographs illegally in a series called “Canal Zones.” The case might have broad implications for photographers and artists. As a photo editor, I can sympathize both with a photographer’s desire to protect his original work and with the concerns about limiting artistic freedom through the fair-use exception.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whose Art Is It Anyway?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-29T22:17:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clinton Cargill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clinton', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cargill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43664452-690d-596b-93d6-d15e0d2aa58b', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43664452-690d-596b-93d6-d15e0d2aa58b'}, {'abstract': 'After security personnel stormed the cabin, Sachin Ahluwalia and other passengers were held in a room but not told what was going on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/business/ankasa-executive-sees-airport-security-in-action.html', 'snippet': 'After security personnel stormed the cabin, Sachin Ahluwalia and other passengers were held in a room but not told what was going on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’M a fashion designer and co-founder of Ankasa, a home furnishings company. I’m traveling all the time and really get a lot of inspiration on my trips to Asia. I’m there about every 45 days, and then travel domestically quite a bit, too. My wife thinks I’m on a plane all the time. I don’t think she’s wrong.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/30/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/business/Flier/Flier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/30/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/business/Flier/Flier-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline