55,000 feet, about 10.5 miles. More test flights will follow before the start of commercial operations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day of Firsts for a Spaceship', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Science', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Day Of Firsts For a Spaceship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgin Galactic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branson, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Spaceflight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T00:21:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f4b813b-b629-5623-999f-2c692e7be8b2', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f4b813b-b629-5623-999f-2c692e7be8b2'}, {'abstract': 'A fire on the roof deck at East Seventh Street near Avenue C in the East Village was quickly put out. Firefighters said that in summer, there would probably be more, caused by barbecues.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/29/roof-deck-blaze-on-a-warm-day-presages-summer-barbecue-fires/', 'snippet': 'A fire on the roof deck at East Seventh Street near Avenue C in the East Village was quickly put out. Firefighters said that in summer, there would probably be more, caused by barbecues.', 'lead_paragraph': ' One minute, sunshine and spring blossoms were the only things descending from the sky, the next moment it was ashes, soot and fire-hose water cascading from the first roof-deck fire of the year in Lower Manhattan on Sunday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roof-Deck Blaze on a Warm Day Presages Summer Barbecue Fires', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T00:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b707db5d-60f8-5b95-9cae-dfa5c8ce4c93', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b707db5d-60f8-5b95-9cae-dfa5c8ce4c93'}, {'abstract': 'State financing for preschool programs fell close to 10 percent in the 2011-12 school year, according to the National Institute for Early Education Research at Rutgers University.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/education/state-financing-for-preschool-fell-10-percent-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'State financing for preschool programs fell close to 10 percent in the 2011-12 school year, according to the National Institute for Early Education Research at Rutgers University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'State financing for preschool fell by more than $548 million, or close to 10 percent, in the 2011-12 school year, the largest annual drop in a decade, according to a report released Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preschool Financing Has Dropped, Study Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preschool Financing Declined, Study Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Arne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T00:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec4b7573-4163-5854-8b32-bf4bfe245eb0', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec4b7573-4163-5854-8b32-bf4bfe245eb0'}, {'abstract': 'The civilian cargo plane of a military contractor based in New York crashed at Bagram Air Base, northeast of Kabul, shortly after takeoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/world/asia/afghanistan-7-people-are-killed-in-cargo-plane-crash-near-kabul.html', 'snippet': 'The civilian cargo plane of a military contractor based in New York crashed at Bagram Air Base, northeast of Kabul, shortly after takeoff.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Seven people were killed on Monday when a civilian cargo plane crashed shortly after taking off from Bagram Air Base, northeast of Kabul, according to an international military spokesman. The police chief of the surrounding area, Ezmarai Nasiri, said the plane “crashed soon after it took off and its tail caught on fire.” There was no information late on Monday about whether the plane was carrying cargo or its intended destination. It belonged to National Air Cargo, a military contractor based in Orchard Park, N.Y., outside Buffalo. Military officials said that the cause of the crash was being investigated, but that there had been no enemy activity in the area at the time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '7 Killed in Plane Crash in  Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: 7 People Are Killed In Cargo Plane Crash Near Kabul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bagram Air Base (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Alissa Johannsen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T00:31:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2890788a-b26e-54e2-b6d7-acff12e20283', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2890788a-b26e-54e2-b6d7-acff12e20283'}, {'abstract': 'Mets third baseman David Wright, who was sidelined with spasms and stiffness in his neck in the series opener with the Marlins, hoped to return Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/sports/baseball/mets-david-wright-out-with-sore-neck.html', 'snippet': 'Mets third baseman David Wright, who was sidelined with spasms and stiffness in his neck in the series opener with the Marlins, hoped to return Tuesday.', '