rding to Kreider, pie is a perfectly acceptable breakfast,” or “Kreider would have it that pants are purely optional.” She’s making mild fun of my sporadic blips of Internet celebrity, but I think she’s more heavily amused to hear commenters citing her feckless goofball friend as though I were some eminent authority, solemnly parsing my passing opinions as though they were official policy statements. Alicia’s an artist, too, and understands how audiences tend to ascribe magisterial intention and control to artists, when more often we’re just making it up as we go, doing the best we can by deadline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Power of ‘I Don’t Know’', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T01:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Kreider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kreider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfe536bb-d26b-5d8f-93fc-4c28eb03ea93', 'word_count': 1447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfe536bb-d26b-5d8f-93fc-4c28eb03ea93'}, {'abstract': 'Westerners horrified by the latest factory disaster would make matters worse by not buying clothing made in Bangladesh. The key to improved worker safety is law enforcement and worker empowerment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/opinion/bangladesh-needs-strong-unions-not-outside-pressure.html', 'snippet': 'Westerners horrified by the latest factory disaster would make matters worse by not buying clothing made in Bangladesh. The key to improved worker safety is law enforcement and worker empowerment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGLADESH, my country, is again in tears. Last week in Savar, a suburb of Dhaka, the capital, a poorly constructed building that housed garment factories and other businesses collapsed. More than 300 have been confirmed dead, and the final death toll could well exceed 700. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bangladesh Needs Strong Unions, Not Outside Pressure', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bangladesh Needs Strong Unions, Not Outside Pressure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rana Plaza Building Collapse, Bangladesh (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T01:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fazle Hasan Abed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fazle', 'middlename': 'Hasan', 'lastname': 'Abed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec2d640-3acf-51dd-9355-543230ad35a8', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec2d640-3acf-51dd-9355-543230ad35a8'}, {'abstract': 'A genealogy of textile factory disasters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/opinion/bangladeshs-are-only-the-latest-in-textile-factory-disasters.html', 'snippet': 'A genealogy of textile factory disasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, Mass.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/opinion/0430OPEDdavis/0430