pe, the Olympic champion and American Indian whose gold medal feats mesmerized the nation a century ago. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jim Thorpe’s Place in America', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jim Thorpe’s Place in America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thorpe, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T01:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/25a0fcd0-c171-56f9-89a5-b9c3e045bbe3', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25a0fcd0-c171-56f9-89a5-b9c3e045bbe3'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court badly missed a chance to strengthen the constitutional right of all Americans to a speedy trial with adequate counsel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/opinion/the-supreme-court-rules-on-a-states-duty-to-indigent-defendants.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court badly missed a chance to strengthen the constitutional right of all Americans to a speedy trial with adequate counsel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, the Supreme Court should have said that every state has the duty to pay for counsel for indigent criminal defendants and ensure them a speedy trial. The court should also have ordered an appeals court in Louisiana to reconsider its decision to uphold a conviction for murder and armed robbery. The court did neither. Its five conservative justices simply refused to decide the case, leaving the conviction and a life sentence in place. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A State’s Duty to Indigent Defendants', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A State’s Duty to Indigent Defendants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders and Court-Appointed Lawyers (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyer, Jonathan Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T01:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a0f12a8-97bf-559b-b727-f5a4f850b8a4', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a0f12a8-97bf-559b-b727-f5a4f850b8a4'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bloomberg’s green legacy will be enhanced if he can get New York City’s recycling program as strong as it was when he first took office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/opinion/mayor-bloomberg-rethinks-recycling.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bloomberg’s green legacy will be enhanced if he can get New York City’s recycling program as strong as it was when he first took office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On recycling in New York City, Mayor Michael Bloomberg has come a long way. After taking office 11 years ago, Mr. Bloomberg eliminated a major chunk of the city’s recycling program to save money. Many New Yorkers were outraged. He was, they said, littering the earth as well as missing a chance to convert waste to energy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mayor Rethinks Recycling', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mayor Rethinks Recycling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T01:12:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e897334-6f49-5148-92bb-aab25ad68516', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e897334-6f49-5148-92bb-aab25ad68516'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s critics want a more muscular approach to Syria, but that could drag the United States into another extended and costly war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/opinion/ill-considered-advice-on-syria.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s critics want a more muscular approach to Syria, but that could drag the United States into another extended and costly war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To hear Senator John McCain of Arizona and Senator Lindsey Graham of South Carolina tell it, the way forward on Syria is clear. The United States should be doing more — directly arming the rebels seeking overthrow President Bashar al-Assad, establishing a no-fly zone. This is not a new line for these two legislators and others in Congress who share their views. But it has gathered force since the Obama administration disclosed last week that it believes Mr. Assad’s forces have used sarin gas against Syrians. ', 'print_section': 