eras trained on him, a host of microphones in his face and a cacophony of questions hurled at him. He spoke in his familiar Western Canadian accent and with the same measured tones as always.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/BLACKHAWKS/BLACKHAWKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/BLACKHAWKS/BLACKHAWKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/BLACKHAWKS/BLACKHAWKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/BLACKHAWKS/BLACKHAWKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/BLACKHAWKS/BLACKHAWKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/BLACKHAWKS/BLACKHAWKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/BLACKHAWKS/BLACKHAWKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mature From the Start, ‘Captain Serious’ of the Blackhawks Continues to Grow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mature From the Start, the Blackhawks’ ‘Captain Serious’ Continues to Grow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Blackhawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toews, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T03:37:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a45204a1-4b65-5d96-9d50-2dfe1d27e345', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a45204a1-4b65-5d96-9d50-2dfe1d27e345'}, {'abstract': 'Voters under 30, who turned out in droves to elect President Obama in 2008, are increasingly turned off by politics, according to a new Harvard poll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/us/politics/for-millennial-voters-a-tide-of-cynicism-toward-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Voters under 30, who turned out in droves to elect President Obama in 2008, are increasingly turned off by politics, according to a new Harvard poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Andy Welsh of Portland, Ore., was so enthusiastic about President Obama’s first run for the White House that he voted absentee while spending a semester abroad in Spain. But Mr. Welsh, now 26 and an aspiring diplomat, said the gridlock in Washington has been “a real bummer ever since.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For ‘Millennials,’ a Tide of Cynicism and a Partisan Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For ‘Millennials,’ a Tide of Cynicism and a Partisan Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': No