0', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T04:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/be8064c0-bcbd-5eb6-a8f6-2371955efa2a', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be8064c0-bcbd-5eb6-a8f6-2371955efa2a'}, {'abstract': 'It was not a vintage performance by Matt Harvey, the young Mets right-hander, but he showed why he has become such a threat on the mound, despite the Mets’ loss to the Marlins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/sports/baseball/mets-matt-harvey-at-less-than-best-is-still-strong-despite-loss-to-marlins.html', 'snippet': 'It was not a vintage performance by Matt Harvey, the young Mets right-hander, but he showed why he has become such a threat on the mound, despite the Mets’ loss to the Marlins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Before the right-hander Matt Harvey took the mound Monday for his sixth start of the season, he kept to himself in the visitors’ clubhouse at Marlins Park. He reclined on a big leather chair, tapped his iPad and seemed not even remotely interested in making small talk with his Mets teammates. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/baseball/30mets1-img/30mets1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/baseball/30mets1-img/30mets1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/30/sports/baseball/30mets1-img/30mets1-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height':