e': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T11:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Petrow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Petrow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/932dfd50-85e8-5e18-9725-4514adfd358f', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/932dfd50-85e8-5e18-9725-4514adfd358f'}, {'abstract': 'Israel’s new banknotes are an unhelpful reminder of lasting divisions between Ashkenazi and Sephardic Jews.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/israels-new-currency-highlights-lasting-divisions-between-european-jews-and-others/', 'snippet': 'Israel’s new banknotes are an unhelpful reminder of lasting divisions between Ashkenazi and Sephardic Jews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEL AVIV — I was impatiently waiting my turn to get on the Sunday morning radio show. The previous segment, involving two lawyers debating sexual harassment allegations against a well-known TV personality, went overtime after one of the lawyers asked, “Can I add something about the new currency bills?” “The bills?” the anchorman replied. “We will discuss the bills controversy at the second half of the show.” But the lawyer insisted: He just wanted to say that the notes’ design was an outrage. The other lawyer barged in: “We can agree on this.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Faces of Difference', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Bills, Similar Faces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T11:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f46c0b62-c1d3-552c-83fc-19d5f91f8fdf', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f46c0b62-c1d3-552c-83fc-19d5f91f8fdf'}, {'abstract': 'The online travel search business is consolidating, as two of the biggest online travel agencies, Priceline.com and Expedia.com, buy smaller search engines, Harriet Edleson reports in The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/daily-report-acquisitions-shrink-the-number-of-travel-search-sites/', 'snippet': 'The online travel search business is consolidating, as two of the biggest online travel agencies, Priceline.com and Expedia.com, buy smaller search engines, Harriet Edleson reports in The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The online travel search business is consolidating, as two of the biggest online travel agencies, Priceline.com and Expedia.com, buy smaller search engines, Harriet Edleson reports on Tuesday in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/t