.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/business/global/european-unemployment-sets-another-record.html', 'snippet': 'In a further sign of weakness in the European economy, the jobless rate in the euro zone increased in March to a record 12.1 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The euro zone jobless rate rose to a record 12.1 percent in March, a sharp reminder that unemployment remains among the region’s biggest problems.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/business/EUJOBS/EUJOBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/01/business/EUJOBS/EUJOBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/business/EUJOBS/EUJOBS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/business/EUJOBS/EUJOBS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1071, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/business/EUJOBS/EUJOBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/01/business/EUJOBS/EUJOBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/business/EUJOBS/EUJOBS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unemployment in Euro Zone Continues to Rise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Continuing Sign of Weakness, Unemployment Hits New High in the Euro Zone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolly, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T11:38:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f449919-2bea-54e1-86df-803b52ed67c1', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f449919-2bea-54e1-86df-803b52ed67c1'}, {'abstract': 'The nominations for the 67th annual Tonys were announced at 8:30 a.m., and we’ll be live-blogging throughout the morning with analysis of the picks, the snubs and their artistic and commercial importance.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/tony-awards-2013-nominations-live-blog/', 'snippet': 'The nominations for the 67th annual Tonys were announced at 8:30 a.m., and we’ll be live-blogging throughout the morning with analysis of the picks, the snubs and their artistic and commercial importance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Broadway musical “Kinky Boots” led the pack with 13 nominations for the 67th annual Tony Awards, including for best musical, director, actor, score and choreographer, while its chief rival “Matilda” had 12 nominations in many of the same categories. The nominations were announced at 8:30 a.m. on Tuesday. The revival of “Golden Boy” had the most nominations of any play, eight, with the new Tom Hanks play “Lucky Guy” close behind with six nominations. Lead acting nods went to only a handful of the Hollywood stars performing on Broadway this season – Mr. Hanks, Laurie Metcalf, Holland Taylor and Cicely Tyson; among those snubbed were Bette Midler, Jessica Chastain, Katie Holmes, Scarlett Johansson and Al Pacino. Among the surprises were snubs of “Motown” for a best musical nomination and its star, Brandon Victor Dixon, for best actor. Fill out your ballot here. A slide show of the nominees is  here. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Kinky Boots’ Leads With 13 Tony Nominations; Tom Hanks Gets Nod for ‘Lucky Guy’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T11:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b38afe06-de69-58e9-a44a-4deae5c5a18d', 'word_count': 2392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b38afe06-de69-58e9-a44a-4deae5c5a18d'}, {'abstract': 'A fresh departure at JPMorgan Chase has heightened concerns about turnover at the bank. | UBS posts strong first-quarter earnings. | An academic study highlights the dark art of leaking deals. | Berlin has transformed from a cold war relic to a fast-growing start-up community.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/turnover-at-jpmorgan/', 'snippet': 'A fresh departure at JPMorgan Chase has heightened concerns about turnover at the bank. | UBS posts strong first-quarter earnings. | An academic study highlights the dark art of leaking deals. | Berlin has transformed from a cold war relic to a fa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The departure of yet another JPMorgan Chase executive, Frank J. Bisignano, has heightened concerns about persistent executive turnover and raised questions about who might succeed Jamie Dimon, the bank’s chief executive and chairman, Susanne Craig and Jessica Silver-Greenberg write in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turnover at JPMorgan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T11:49:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63d18b8f-5602-545f-b8e7-02ffb548c386', 'word_count': 1868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63d18b8f-5602-545f-b8e7-02ffb548c386'}, {'abstract': 'Handling the play date gun debate, why patients sue doctors, fees for airline extras add up and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/tuesday-reading-handling-the-play-date-gun-debate/', 'snippet': 'Handling the play date gun debate, why patients sue doctors, fees for airline extras add up and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Handling the Play Date Gun Debate', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T12:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'ne