ce service tried to influence the recent presidential election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/world/asia/prosecutors-raid-south-korean-spy-agency.html', 'snippet': 'The state is investigating allegations that the intelligence service tried to influence the recent presidential election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — State prosecutors raided the headquarters of the National Intelligence Service of South Korea on Tuesday to investigate accusations that the spy agency used its agents and hired bloggers to influence the presidential election in December.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutors Raid South Korean Spy Agency in Presidential Election Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prosecutors Raid South Korean Spy Agency in Presidential Election Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T12:31:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7980e4a-23e0-54c2-81ab-9f7b24f10b42', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7980e4a-23e0-54c2-81ab-9f7b24f10b42'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Edward J. Markey took the Democratic primary, and the Republican nomination went to Gabriel E. Gomez, a private equity investor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/us/massachusetts-kerry-senate-replacement.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Edward J. Markey took the Democratic primary, and the Republican nomination went to Gabriel E. Gomez, a private equity investor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Representative Edward J. Markey, who has spent almost four decades in the House, has cleared the first hurdle in his drive to become a United States senator, easily defeating a fellow congressman, Stephen F. Lynch, in Massachusetts’s Democratic primary on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senior Congressman and Newcomer Win Senate Nods in Massachusetts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senior Congressman and Newcomer Win Senate Nods in Massachusetts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markey, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Stephen F (1955- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gomez, Gabriel E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winslow, Daniel B', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Michael J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T12:38:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d6165a3-444b-5687-8a5b-630b9b9fb75a', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d6165a3-444b-5687-8a5b-630b9b9fb75a'}, {'abstract': 'The interior decorator James Huniford opens a new Chelsea showroom this month, unveiling a collection that is both sophisticated and customizable.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/furniture-thats-simply-chic/', 'snippet': 'The interior decorator James Huniford opens a new Chelsea showroom this month, unveiling a collection that is both sophisticated and customizable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, the interior decorator James Huniford unveils a brand-new Chelsea showroom and a sophisticated furniture collection, made up of the type of pieces the designer previously created only as one-offs for his high-profile clients. The designs, Huniford says, are meant to be “user-friendly” — scale and contemporary livability are paramount, and dimensions, as well as upholstery, are all customizable. This is furniture that inhabits that elegant territory somewhere between modern and classic. A tufted slope-armed sofa ($7,800) is refreshed with a casual low-slung profile; a campaign-style side table ($4,800) is cheekily updated with a not-remotely-portable stone slab and chains; and a two-tiered occasional table ($5,800) has a brass base with an industrial feel. “I like the tension between contrasting materials,” the designer says. “Metal and stone, wood and glass.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Furniture That’s Simply Chic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huniford, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T13:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'fir