tly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A 15% Gain In Earnings At Sirius XM', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A 15% Gain In Earnings At Sirius XM', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sirius XM Radio Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, James E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T14:19:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d71b5e4-17a3-51d3-a6ae-da507db063f4', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d71b5e4-17a3-51d3-a6ae-da507db063f4'}, {'abstract': 'Adapted from Piper Kerman’s memoir, “Orange Is the New Black” chronicles a Brooklyn woman whose relationship with a drug runner lands her in prison for a year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/netflix-prison-series-gets-july-release-date/', 'snippet': 'Adapted from Piper Kerman’s memoir, “Orange Is the New Black” chronicles a Brooklyn woman whose relationship with a drug runner lands her in prison for a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though there was once a time when Netflix was most closely associated with its bright red DVD-return envelopes, the company — now better known as a video-streaming service — is hoping that orange will be its color this summer. On Tuesday, Netflix announced that it has scheduled its next original series, “Orange Is the New Black,” a comedy-drama set in a women’s prison, to have its premiere on July 11; and, as has become its custom, it will make all thirteen episodes of the series available for viewing at once.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix Prison Series Gets July Release Date', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kohan, Jenji', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prepon, Laura', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schilling, Taylor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T14:29:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf88e9ad-55d4-5bc9-a3e0-0b30b7adcd9f', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf88e9ad-55d4-5bc9-a3e0-0b30b7adcd9f'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/what-were-reading-682/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PBS Food: What went into William Randolph Hearst’s favorite snack, Welsh rarebit: homemade cheese and butter, home-brewed beer, freshly baked bread and enough cash to keep it all going. — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T14:30:44+0000', 'document_type': '