gs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/interior-departments-no-2-stepping-down/', 'snippet': 'David J. Hayes, the deputy interior secretary since the early days of the Obama administration, said he would leave his post at the end of June.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David J. Hayes, the deputy secretary of the interior since the early days of the Obama administration, said on Tuesday that he would leave the post at the end of June. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interior Department’s No. 2 Stepping Down', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayes, David J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jewell, Sally', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T16:24:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a45d4ed-b661-51a8-8418-dcf77da1a4a7', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a45d4ed-b661-51a8-8418-dcf77da1a4a7'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/the-gun-report-april-30-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer and I are both traveling today so we will dispense with the usual introduction. Here is our typically grim Gun Report, which, when you think about it, needs no introduction. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: April 30, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bend (Ore)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hollywood (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Providence (RI)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toledo (Ohio)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trenton (NJ)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T16:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2386430-59ed-5c58-95c4-a474a749353b', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2386430-59ed-5c58-95c4-a474a749353b'}, {'abstract': 'For one Marine, the 10th anniversary of the invasion of Iraq brings back vivid memories, not all of them unwanted, of his first firefight.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/humbled-by-the-souvenirs-of-war/', 'snippet': 'For one Marine, the 10th anniversary of the invasion of Iraq brings back vivid memories, not all of them unwanted, of his first firefight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I usually forget about most dreams right after I wake, but I never forget the ones that involve combat. I collect those dreams and save them, locking them in a fortified mental safe I rarely open because the images may turn into nightmares. The war dreams are the pictures I never took. They are the souvenirs of war, the thoughts that continue to humble me. Some people might think that remembering such experiences would have destructive side effects. But for me, the dreams are a reminder of how valuable life is. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humbled by the Souvenirs of War', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Euphrates River', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nasiriya (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T16:26:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew P. Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69d56efa-b0b6-5b68-996b-7d30e95d2579', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69d56efa-b0b6-5b68-996b-7d30e95d2579'}, {'abstract': 'This combination is about comfort and beauty.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/a-compelling-gamay-to-accompany-an-omelet/', 'snippet': 'This combination is about comfort and beauty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pairing decisions are part analytical and, importantly, part emotional. Almost nothing will go better with this creamy, pungent, savory ramp omelet by David Tanis than those two amplifiers of umami, fino sherry and Champagne. That’s the rational choice, yet what I want most is gamay, the grape of Beaujolais. Why? Back in the old days, when being able to prepare a perfect omelet was considered evidence of cooking ability, my custom for my first meal on any trip to France was to stop in at a cafe or bar à vin for an omelet, with a glass of the easygoing house Beaujolais. For me, this combination was comfort and beauty. Nowadays, I might choose a gamay from the Loire Valley, or one of the few American versions, like Edmunds St. John’s, which I think come closer to those lighthearted yet compelling wines. The rational choice? Maybe not, but it sure felt like a great one. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Compelling Gamay to Accompany an Omelet', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaujolais Wine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Loire Valley (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T16:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ea4a310-8851-5f02-b388-0236632ea5a3', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ea4a310-8851-5f02-b388-0236632ea5a3'}, {'abstract': 'An educator asks, “What makes a great teacher?” Readers are invited to reply.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/opinion/invitation-to-a-dialogue-the-art-of-teaching.html', 'snippet': 'An e