, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b6621d0-6f1f-5405-8ddc-d1efcbec3b6e', 'word_count': 1446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b6621d0-6f1f-5405-8ddc-d1efcbec3b6e'}, {'abstract': 'There are conservative ideas on health care, but there aren’t enough Republicans willing to actually vote for them.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/the-republican-health-policy-trainwreck/', 'snippet': 'There are conservative ideas on health care, but there aren’t enough Republicans willing to actually vote for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago,\xa0Ezra Klein\xa0and\xa0Ben Domenech\xa0had a fairly detailed back-and-forth\xa0— culminating in\xa0this mano-a-mano exchange\xa0—\xa0about whether a Republican or conservative alternative to Obamacare actually exists. You can read or watch them go at it and form your own judgment, but I think the answer is pretty straightforward: A conservative alternative or alternatives, yes; an alternative that Republican lawmakers are ready to vote for, no.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Republican Health Policy Trainwreck', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T19:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': '