still waiting.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/04/30/the-long-wait-for-wage-protections/', 'snippet': 'Sixteen months ago, President Obama promised to end the exclusion of home health aides from the Fair Labor Standards Act, which guarantees minimum wage and overtime to workers. The aides are still waiting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than three million home health aides — a lifeline for the elderly who are neither in institutions nor able to manage life’s mundane tasks on their own — are learning exactly how sclerotic the nation’s regulatory processes can be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long Wait for Wage Protections', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T19:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41fe5745-df80-5873-a48a-caea7d7f37ca', 'word_count': 1146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41fe5745-df80-5873-a48a-caea7d7f37ca'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg defended the Police Department and condemned two City Council bills related to law enforcement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/nyregion/bloomberg-says-critics-of-police-would-make-new-yorkers-less-safe.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg defended the Police Department and condemned two City Council bills related to law enforcement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With criticism of the police infusing the Democratic race to succeed him, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg on Tuesday offered a staunch defense of the New York Police Department, as well as a spirited attack against its critics.', 'print_section