in Theory: Pure Genius,” on Discovery, and “Brain Games,” on National Geographic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new competition show on the Discovery Channel is searching among 10 people with very good brains to find the one with the best brain of all. But over on the National Geographic Channel a peppy little audience-participation series has been demonstrating that the brain is easily fooled and not to be trusted. How are our brains supposed to process these conflicting signals about our brains?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gray Matter in Moments of Triumph and Defeat', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gray Matter In Moments Of Triumph And Defeat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Geographic Channel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T22:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e39e5e-0e16-59fd-8502-346258fd1012', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e39e5e-0e16-59fd-8502-346258fd1012'}, {'abstract': 'Traditional song-and-dance shows about scrappy underdogs dominated the Tony Award nominations on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/theater/theaterspecial/its-kinky-boots-vs-matilda-in-tony-nominations.html', 'snippet': 'Traditional song-and-dance shows about scrappy underdogs dominated the Tony Award nominations on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Traditional song-and-dance shows about scrappy underdogs dominated the Tony Award nominations on Tuesday, with four — “Kinky Boots,” “Matilda,” “Bring It On” and “A Christmas Story” — taking every slot in the race for best Broadway musical. Serious fare suffered, with the gritty “Hands on a Hardbody” edged out for best musical and “The Testament of Mary” — a monologue by the mother of Jesus — quickly announcing a closing date after its lead actress, Fiona Shaw, did not receive a Tony nomination. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/01TONY1_SPAN/01TONY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/01TONY1_SPAN/01TONY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/01TONY1_SPAN/01TONY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/01TONY1_SPAN/01TONY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 954, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/01TONY1_SPAN/01TONY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/01/arts/01TONY1_SPAN/01TONY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/