re returning to Mexico City from Zacatecas State after helping with the arrest of people suspected of being members of the Zetas, one of the country’s most violent gangs. The cause of the crash is under investigation. The plane, a Beechcraft King Air 300 built in 1985, had unspecified mechanical trouble Monday night, forcing it to return to Zacatecas and delaying the return of the group, the attorney general’s office said in a statement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plane Carrying Mexican Officials Crashes, Killing 6', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zetas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T23:27:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e771d9a6-6e03-5b57-8b98-d542c822fcdd', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e771d9a6-6e03-5b57-8b98-d542c822fcdd'}, {'abstract': 'Last May, the newspaper’s owners, Advance Publications, announced it would cut back printing of The Times-Picayune and would make major cuts to the newsroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/business/media/times-picayune-plans-a-new-print-tabloid.html', 'snippet': 'Last May, the newspaper’s owners, Advance Publications, announced it would cut back printing of The Times-Picayune and would make major cuts to the newsroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly one year after The Times-Picayune of New Orleans announced that it would print only three days a week, the paper said it planned to roll out a three-day-a-week tabloid edition. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times-Picayune Plans a New Print Tabloid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Times-Picayune Plans a New Print Tabloid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haughney, Christine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times-Picayune (New Orleans)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Advance Publications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T23:35:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/760bf229-be1d-5067-9edb-b6557a75efe4', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/760bf229-be1d-5067-9edb-b6557a75efe4'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling by the European Court of Human Rights does not oblige Ukraine’s judicial system to release former Prime Minister Yulia V. Tymoshenko.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/world/europe/tymoshenko-ukraines-jailed-ex-premier-gets-decision-in-her-favor.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling by the European Court of Human Rights does not oblige Ukraine’s judicial system to release former Prime Minister Yulia V. Tymoshenko.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Before she went to jail a year and eight months ago, Yulia V. Tymoshenko joked that she carried a toothbrush and a bottle of water in her purse in case of arrest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jailed Official in Ukraine Gets Decision in Her Favor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ruling Favors Ex-Premier Who Is Jailed In Ukraine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tymoshenko, Yulia V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Court of Human Rights', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanukovich, Viktor F', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-04-30T23:53:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a620f28-ef31-5197-b975-46911f463eda', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a620f28-ef31-5197-b975-46911f463eda'}, {'abstract': 'John Buck caught all 15 innings of the Mets’ loss Monday, and Manager Terry Collins said there was no way Buck would start on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/05/01/sports/baseball/after-15-inning-game-mets-give-catcher-john-buck-a-rest.html', 'snippet': 'John Buck caught all 15 innings of the Mets’ loss Monday, and Manager Terry Collins said there was no way Buck would start on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — John Buck arrived Tuesday afternoon in the visitors’ clubhouse at Marlins Park and declared himself rested and ready to play. Manager Terry Collins quickly scuttled those plans. There was no way Buck was starting for the Mets on Tuesday, not after he caught all 15 innings of their loss to the Marlins on Monday night, a marathon that extended into early Tuesday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/CITIFIELD/CITIFIELD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/CITIFIELD/CITIFIELD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/CITIFIELD/CITIFIELD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/CITIFIELD/CITIFIELD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1407, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/CITIFIELD/CITIFIELD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/CITIFIELD/CITIFIELD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/01/sports/CITIFIELD/CITIFIELD-thumb